{"symbols":[{"name":"DataContainer","group":"Classes","kind":"Class","signatures":["class DataContainer"],"doc":"<p>Holds the rows and tracks their edits (<code>getChanges()</code>). Every datasource has one: a new one by\ndefault, or the one given as <code>DatasourceOptions.container</code> - several datasources can share it and\nso show the same rows, each with its own filter, sort, grouping and selection. The field types for\nthe edit tracking come from the <code>fields</code> of the datasources made on it.</p>\n<p>Most of the time you do not use it directly: the datasource&#39;s methods call it and also rebuild the\ndisplayed rows and send the events. The container&#39;s own methods do neither - after changing the rows\nhere, call <code>datasource.reloadDatasource()</code> to show them.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer, Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// two datasources, e.g. two grids, on the same rows\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\nconst left = new Datasource({ container, fields: { born: 'date' } });\nconst right = new Datasource({ container, fields: { born: 'date' } });\n\nleft.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann', born: new Date(1990, 4, 17) }]);\nright.getAllData(); // the same row</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Constructors","members":[{"name":"constructor","signatures":["new DataContainer(UniqueKeyAttribute?: string): DataContainer"],"doc":"<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>UniqueKeyAttribute</code> the field that identifies a row, e.g. <code>&#39;id&#39;</code>. The selection follows it,\nso it survives replacing the rows with fresh ones from a server. Left out, every row gets a\ngenerated key (a negative number)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer, Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ container });</code></pre>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Methods","members":[{"name":"acceptChanges","signatures":["acceptChanges(options?: { newKeys?: ReadonlyMap<string | number, string | number>; rows?: Entity | Entity[] }): void"],"doc":"<p>Call it after a successful save: the changes are now on the server, so they are no changes any\nmore. For every row (or the <code>rows</code> given):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>a row marked for deletion is removed from the container, a new one too</li>\n<li>a new row becomes an ordinary row (<code>__rowState</code> <code>undefined</code>)</li>\n<li>the values a row has now become its original values: nothing counts as edited</li>\n<li>the row&#39;s error (<code>setErrors()</code>) and its validation errors are cleared</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Then <code>getChanges()</code> lists none of them, <code>hasChanges()</code> is <code>false</code> when every row was accepted,\nand <code>resetData()</code> goes back to these values. The undo history is cleared, also when only some\nrows were accepted. <code>datasource.acceptChanges()</code> calls it and also rebuilds the displayed rows -\nuse that one.</p>\n<p><strong>The keys of new rows.</strong> A new row has a temporary key, a generated negative number: in its key\nfield (<code>id: -1</code> with <code>new DataContainer(&#39;id&#39;)</code>), or without a key field as <code>__KEY</code> in\n<code>getChanges().newEntities</code>. <code>newKeys</code> maps each temporary key to the key the server gave the row.\nThe row gets it in its key field, or as its <code>__KEY</code> without a key field - setting it is no edit.</p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> when a key in <code>newKeys</code> is not the key of a new row that is accepted (and not marked\nfor deletion), or the server&#39;s key is blank (<code>null</code>, <code>undefined</code>, <code>&#39;&#39;</code>) - a map the wrong way\nround, say. Checked first: nothing is accepted then</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// saves the changes in one transaction, and answers with the id it gave each new row\ndeclare function save(changes: object): Promise&lt;{ temporaryId: number; id: number }[]&gt;;\n\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\ncontainer.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann' }]);\ncontainer.setData([{ name: 'Cid' }], { add: true, isNew: true }); // a temporary id: -1, say\ncontainer.getDataSet()[0].name = 'Anna';\n\nconst saved = await save(container.getChanges()); // newEntities: [{ name: 'Cid', id: -1 }]\ncontainer.acceptChanges({ newKeys: new Map(saved.map((row) =&gt; [row.temporaryId, row.id])) });\n\ncontainer.getDataSet().map((row) =&gt; [row.id, row.name, row.__rowState]);\n// [[1, 'Anna', undefined], [7, 'Cid', undefined]] - if the server gave Cid the id 7\ncontainer.hasChanges(); // false</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"clearMarkedForDeletion","signatures":["clearMarkedForDeletion(): void"],"doc":"<p>Removes the rows marked for deletion from the container, for good: <code>getChanges()</code> no longer lists\nthem in <code>deletedEntities</code> and <code>resetData()</code> does not bring them back, and their changes leave the\nundo history. Call it once the deletes are saved - or call <a href=\"#api/index.DataContainer\">acceptChanges</a>, which also\naccepts the new and edited rows. <code>datasource.clearMarkedForDeletion()</code> calls it and rebuilds the\ndisplayed rows.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\nconst { deletedEntities } = container.getChanges(); // send these first\ncontainer.clearMarkedForDeletion();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getChangedFields","signatures":["getChangedFields(row: Entity): string[]"],"doc":"<p>The fields of a row that differ from their original value, in the order they were first edited -\n<code>getChanges()</code>&#39;s fields of the row. <code>[]</code> for a new row (it has no original), a row not edited, and\nan object that is no row of the container</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getChangedRows","signatures":["getChangedRows(kinds?: ChangeKinds | null): Entity[]"],"doc":"<p>The rows getChanges() lists, of the kinds asked for (<a href=\"#api/index.ChangeKinds\">ChangeKinds</a>) - the rows themselves, not\ncopies, in the order of the data: to validate, select or show them</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getChanges","signatures":["getChanges(kinds?: ChangeKinds | null): Changes"],"doc":"<p>The rows added, edited and marked for deletion, as copies - see <a href=\"#api/index.Changes\">Changes</a> for what is\nin it and when an edit counts. <code>datasource.getChanges()</code> is the same, typed with the\ndatasource&#39;s row type. <code>kinds</code> picks the lists filled (<a href=\"#api/index.ChangeKinds\">ChangeKinds</a>): all by default, a kind\nnot asked for is <code>[]</code>.</p>\n<p>A <code>Date</code> is compared by its field&#39;s type from the <code>fields</code> of the datasources on this\ncontainer. Used without a datasource every field compares a <code>Date</code> to the second.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\ncontainer.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann' }, { id: 2, name: 'Bob' }]);\nconst [ann, bob] = container.getDataSet();\nann.name = 'Anna';\nbob.name = 'Robert';\nbob.name = 'Bob'; // back to the original, no edit\n\ncontainer.getChanges();\n// { newEntities: [], modifiedEntities: [{ id: 1, name: 'Anna' }], deletedEntities: [] }</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getDataSet","signatures":["getDataSet(): DataEntity[]"],"doc":"<p>Every row in the container, in the order they were set: the rows marked for deletion included,\nno filter, sort or grouping. A new array, the rows in it are the container&#39;s own (not copies).\n<code>datasource.getAllData()</code> is the same.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\ncontainer.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann' }, { id: 2, name: 'Bob' }]);\ncontainer.getDataSet().map((row) =&gt; row.name); // ['Ann', 'Bob']</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getKeyAttribute","signatures":["getKeyAttribute(): string | undefined"],"doc":"<p>The field that identifies a row, as given to the constructor. <code>undefined</code> when there is none,\nthen every row gets a generated key.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\ncontainer.getKeyAttribute(); // 'id'</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getMarkedForDeletion","signatures":["getMarkedForDeletion(): DataEntity[]"],"doc":"<p>The rows marked for deletion (<code>markForDeletion()</code> / <code>markAllForDeletion()</code>), still in the\ncontainer until <code>acceptChanges()</code> or <code>clearMarkedForDeletion()</code> removes them. New rows that are\nmarked are in it too, they are not in <code>getChanges().deletedEntities</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\ncontainer.markForDeletion(datasource.getSelectedRows());\ncontainer.getMarkedForDeletion().length; // the rows just marked</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getOriginalValue","signatures":["getOriginalValue(row: Entity, field: string): unknown"],"doc":"<p>The value a field of a row had before it was edited - the data set, or accepted last. The value it\nhas now when the field is not edited; undefined for a new row (it has no original) and for an object\nthat is no row of the container</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"hasChanges","signatures":["hasChanges(kinds?: ChangeKinds | null): boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when there is something to save: <code>getChanges()</code> would list a row - of the kinds asked for\n(<a href=\"#api/index.ChangeKinds\">ChangeKinds</a>, all by default). For an &quot;unsaved changes&quot; indicator. A new row marked for\ndeletion is no change, and neither is a field edited back to its original value.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\ncontainer.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann' }]);\ncontainer.hasChanges(); // false\n\ncontainer.getDataSet()[0].name = 'Anna';\ncontainer.hasChanges(); // true\ncontainer.hasChanges({ deleted: true }); // false</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"length","signatures":["length(): number"],"doc":"<p>The number of rows in the container, the rows marked for deletion included. Was <code>lenght()</code> in v5.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const count = datasource.getDataContainer().length(); // every row, no filter</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"markAllForDeletion","signatures":["markAllForDeletion(): void"],"doc":"<p>Marks every row for deletion, like <a href=\"#api/index.DataContainer\">markForDeletion</a> with all of them: the new rows are\nmarked too, and left out of <code>getChanges()</code>. Was <code>markForDeletion(null, true)</code> in v5.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\ncontainer.markAllForDeletion();\ncontainer.getChanges().deletedEntities; // every row that is not new</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"markForDeletion","signatures":["markForDeletion(rows: Entity | Entity[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Marks rows for deletion: <code>getChanges()</code> lists them in <code>deletedEntities</code>, <code>__rowState</code> is\n<code>&#39;D&#39;</code>. They stay in the container: <a href=\"#api/index.DataContainer\">unmarkForDeletion</a> (or <code>resetData()</code>) takes the mark\noff again, and <a href=\"#api/index.DataContainer\">acceptChanges</a> (or <code>clearMarkedForDeletion()</code>) removes them once the\ndeletes are saved.</p>\n<p>A new row (from <code>addNewEmpty()</code>) is marked too, so it can be brought back. While it is marked it\nis in none of the lists of <code>getChanges()</code>: it was never saved, there is nothing to send for it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows. Rows that are not in the container are skipped.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\nconst [first, second] = container.getDataSet();\ncontainer.markForDeletion(first);\ncontainer.markForDeletion([first, second]);</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"overrideEntityHandler","signatures":["overrideEntityHandler(entityHandler: any): void"],"doc":"<p>Replaces the class that wraps every row in a <code>Proxy</code> and tracks its edits, for the rows set from\nnow on. An advanced hook: the class gets the <a href=\"#api/index.EntityHandler\">EntityHandler</a> constructor options\n(<code>{ key, isNew, fieldType, onEdit }</code>) and must implement the proxy traps and the fields the grid\nreads (<code>__isNew</code>, <code>__isDeleted</code>, <code>__edited</code> ...). Its set trap calls <code>onEdit(row, field, oldValue)</code>\nafter a field is set, with the value the field had before: without the call the fields are not\nvalidated on edit and the edits are not in the undo history (<code>datasource.undo()</code>), and without\nthe old value undo can not put it back. <code>EntityHandler</code> is exported as a type only, so it can\nnot be extended - you write the whole handler.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>entityHandler</code> the class to use instead of <code>EntityHandler</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer, type FieldType } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// a handler class of your own, with the same constructor as EntityHandler\ndeclare const MyEntityHandler: new (options: {\n    key?: string;\n    isNew?: boolean;\n    fieldType?: (field: string) =&gt; FieldType | undefined;\n    onEdit?: (row: object, field: string, oldValue: unknown) =&gt; void;\n}) =&gt; ProxyHandler&lt;object&gt;;\n\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\ncontainer.overrideEntityHandler(MyEntityHandler);</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"removeAllData","signatures":["removeAllData(): Entity[]"],"doc":"<p>Removes every row from the container, like <a href=\"#api/index.DataContainer\">removeData</a> with all of them, and clears the\nundo history. Was <code>removeData(null, true)</code> in v5.</p>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the rows removed</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\ncontainer.removeAllData();\ncontainer.getDataSet(); // []</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"removeData","signatures":["removeData(rows: Entity | Entity[]): Entity[]"],"doc":"<p>Removes rows from the container, for good: they are not marked for deletion, <code>getChanges()</code>\ndoes not list them and <code>resetData()</code> does not bring them back. Their changes leave the undo\nhistory: undo never writes into a row that is not there.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows. Rows that are not in the container are skipped.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the rows removed</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\nconst [first] = container.getDataSet();\ncontainer.removeData(first); // [first]</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"replace","signatures":["replace(data: any[], index: number, remove: number): void"],"doc":"<p>Puts rows in at a position in the container, replacing <code>remove</code> rows there - <code>Array.splice</code> for\nthe container&#39;s rows. The new rows are wrapped and get a key like <code>setData()</code> gives them, they are\nnot new rows. The changes of the rows removed leave the undo history. Call\n<code>datasource.reloadDatasource()</code> after to show them.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>data</code> your objects</li>\n<li><code>index</code> where they go, 0 based</li>\n<li><code>remove</code> how many rows from <code>index</code> on are removed for good</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\ncontainer.replace([{ id: 9, name: 'Zed' }], 1, 1); // the second row is replaced\ndatasource.reloadDatasource();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"resetData","signatures":["resetData(): void"],"doc":"<p>Throws away every change since the data was set: edited rows get their original values back,\nrows marked for deletion are unmarked, new rows (from <code>addNewEmpty()</code>) are removed, and the\nvalidation errors are cleared - the original values are not validated. Rows removed for good\n(<code>removeData()</code>, <code>clearMarkedForDeletion()</code>) do not come back. The undo history is cleared.\n<code>datasource.resetData()</code> calls it and also rebuilds the displayed rows - use that one.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.getDataContainer().resetData();\ndatasource.getChanges(); // { newEntities: [], modifiedEntities: [], deletedEntities: [] }</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"resetDataSelection","signatures":["resetDataSelection(data: Entity[]): void"],"doc":"<p><a href=\"#api/index.DataContainer\">resetData</a> for the given rows only: their edits are undone, a row marked for deletion is\nunmarked, a new row is removed, and their validation errors are cleared.\n<code>datasource.resetDataSelectionOnly()</code> calls it with the selected rows. Does not rebuild a\ndatasource&#39;s displayed rows.</p>\n<p>It is one step of the undo history (<code>datasource.undo()</code> brings the edits and the marks back),\nbut a new row it removed does not come back: undo never adds a row.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>data</code> the rows to reset. Rows that are not in the container are skipped</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\ncontainer.resetDataSelection(datasource.getSelectedRows());\ndatasource.reloadDatasource(); // show it</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"setData","signatures":["setData(rows: any[], options?: { add?: boolean; isNew?: boolean }): Entity[]"],"doc":"<p>Sets the rows. Every row is wrapped in the proxy that tracks its edits, and gets a key. Without\n<code>add</code> the undo history is cleared, the rows start over; added rows are not in the history (undo\nnever removes a row).</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> your objects</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the rows as the container keeps them</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\ncontainer.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann' }]);\ncontainer.setData([{ id: 2, name: 'Bob' }], { add: true });\ncontainer.setData([{ id: 3, name: 'New' }], { add: true, isNew: true });</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"setErrors","signatures":["setErrors(errors: Map<string, string>): void"],"doc":"<p>Sets <code>__rowError</code> on the rows: the message for the rows whose key is in the map, <code>null</code> for every\nother row - so each call replaces the errors of the call before. For errors a server sent back\nafter saving.</p>\n<p>It is apart from the validation errors (<code>datasource.validate()</code>, <code>getErrors()</code>): this does not\nchange them, and <code>validate()</code> / <code>hasErrors()</code> do not read <code>__rowError</code>. The grid shows both on\nthe row selector - the error class, and the message as its tooltip. The rows whose error changed\nare in the <code>rows-changed</code> event, so the grid shows it without <code>gridInterface.refresh()</code>.\n<code>acceptChanges()</code> clears it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>errors</code> the error message per row, keyed by the row&#39;s key as text (<code>&#39;7&#39;</code> for <code>id: 7</code>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.getDataContainer().setErrors(new Map([['7', 'Name is already taken']]));\n\ndatasource.getAllData().filter((row) =&gt; row.__rowError); // the rows with an error</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"unmarkAllForDeletion","signatures":["unmarkAllForDeletion(): void"],"doc":"<p>Takes the mark off every row marked for deletion, like <a href=\"#api/index.DataContainer\">unmarkForDeletion</a> with all of them.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\ncontainer.markAllForDeletion();\ncontainer.unmarkAllForDeletion();\ncontainer.getMarkedForDeletion(); // []</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"unmarkForDeletion","signatures":["unmarkForDeletion(rows: Entity | Entity[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Takes the mark of <a href=\"#api/index.DataContainer\">markForDeletion</a> off rows again: undo a delete. A row is shown and\nlisted in <code>getChanges()</code> as before it was marked - a new row as a new row, an edited row with its\nedits. Unlike <code>resetData()</code>, no edit is undone.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows. Rows that are not in the container, or not marked, are skipped.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\ncontainer.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann' }]);\nconst [ann] = container.getDataSet();\n\ncontainer.markForDeletion(ann);\nann.__rowState; // 'D'\ncontainer.unmarkForDeletion(ann);\nann.__rowState; // undefined, as it was</code></pre>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"Datasource","group":"Classes","kind":"Class","signatures":["class Datasource<T = any>"],"doc":"<p>The rows of a grid, and what is done with them: the data, the fields (type, label and formatter of\neach), the filter, sorting, grouping, selection, the current row and the edits (<code>getChanges()</code>).\nIt works without a grid too.</p>\n<p>A grid shows one datasource: give it to <code>createGrid()</code>. What you do here - <code>filter()</code>, <code>sort()</code>,\n<code>setData()</code> ... - sends an event (see <a href=\"#api/index.DatasourceEvents\">DatasourceEvents</a>), and the grid shows the result.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of your rows. The rows the datasource hands out are <a href=\"#api/index.EntityUnion\">EntityUnion</a><code>&lt;T&gt;</code>:\nyour object with the key and the edit tracking fields</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ninterface Person {\n    id: number;\n    name: string;\n    born: Date;\n}\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource&lt;Person&gt;({ key: 'id', fields: { born: 'date' } });\ndatasource.setData([\n    { id: 1, name: 'Ann', born: new Date(1990, 4, 17) },\n    { id: 2, name: 'Bob', born: new Date(1985, 0, 2) }\n]);\n\ndatasource.filter(where('name', 'BEGIN_WITH', 'a'));\ndatasource.sort({ attribute: 'born', ascending: false });\ndatasource.getDataRows().map((row) =&gt; row.name); // ['Ann']</code></pre>\n","samples":["basic-grid"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Constructors","members":[{"name":"constructor","signatures":["new Datasource<T = any>(options?: DatasourceOptions): Datasource<T>"],"doc":"<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of your rows. The rows the datasource hands out are <a href=\"#api/index.EntityUnion\">EntityUnion</a><code>&lt;T&gt;</code>:\nyour object with the key and the edit tracking fields</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>options</code> the key, the fields and their formatters, the selection mode, or a data\ncontainer shared with another datasource - all optional, see <a href=\"#api/index.DatasourceOptions\">DatasourceOptions</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> when <code>key</code> and <code>container</code> are both given and <code>key</code> is not the container&#39;s key, a\nfield has a type that does not exist, a formatter id or a validator id is not registered (see\n<a href=\"#api/index.registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a> and <a href=\"#api/index.registerValidator\">registerValidator</a>), a rule&#39;s options are wrong, or a field\nhas another type or other rules than in a datasource made earlier on the same <code>container</code></p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    key: 'id',\n    fields: { born: 'date', age: { type: 'number', label: 'Age' } }\n});\ndatasource.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann', born: new Date(1990, 4, 17), age: 36 }]);</code></pre>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"currentEntity","signatures":["currentEntity: GroupRow | EntityUnion<T> | null"],"doc":"<p>The current row: the one last clicked, selected or set with <code>setRowAsCurrentEntity()</code>. Use it\nfor a detail form next to the grid. <code>null</code> until a row is made current.</p>\n<p>When grouped it can be a <a href=\"#api/index.GroupRow\">GroupRow</a>: moving the focus up from the first data row into\nthe header filter row makes row 0 current, and that is a group row when grouped.\n<code>setRowAsCurrentEntity(row)</code> does the same for a group row&#39;s index. Clicking a group row,\n<code>select()</code> and <code>selectNext()</code> ... never make one current. Check with <a href=\"#api/index.isGroupRow\">isGroupRow</a>.</p>\n<p><code>setData()</code> sets it to <code>null</code> when the current row is no longer in the data - the rows were\nreplaced by new objects, also ones with the same key - and keeps it when it still is (rows added,\nor the same row objects set again). The methods that remove rows set it to <code>null</code> when they\nremove it: <code>removeData()</code>, <code>removeAllData()</code>, <code>clearMarkedForDeletion()</code>, <code>acceptChanges()</code> (a\nrow marked for deletion), <code>resetData()</code> and <code>resetDataSelectionOnly()</code> (a new row). The\n<code>current-entity</code> event is sent when it changes.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { isGroupRow } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const detailForm: { show(row: object): void; clear(): void };\n\ndatasource.on('current-entity', () =&gt; {\n    const row = datasource.currentEntity;\n    if (row &amp;&amp; !isGroupRow(row)) {\n        detailForm.show(row);\n    } else {\n        detailForm.clear();\n    }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Accessors","members":[{"name":"type","signatures":["get type(): string"],"doc":"<p>Always <code>&#39;Datasource&#39;</code>. Tells a datasource from other objects without <code>instanceof</code>, which fails when\ntwo copies of the package are loaded.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const isDatasource = (value: any) =&gt; value?.type === 'Datasource';\nisDatasource(datasource); // true</code></pre>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Methods","members":[{"name":"acceptChanges","signatures":["acceptChanges(options?: { newKeys?: ReadonlyMap<string | number, string | number>; rows?: Entity | Entity[] }): void"],"doc":"<p>Call it after a successful save, to show what was saved: the changes are on the server now, so\nthey are no changes any more. For every row (or the <code>rows</code> given):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>a row marked for deletion is removed, a new one too</li>\n<li>a new row becomes an ordinary row (<code>__rowState</code> <code>undefined</code>)</li>\n<li>the values a row has now become its original values: nothing counts as edited</li>\n<li>the row&#39;s error (<code>setErrors()</code>) and its validation errors are cleared</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Then <code>getChanges()</code> lists none of them, <code>hasChanges()</code> is <code>false</code> when every row was accepted,\nand <code>resetData()</code> goes back to these values. The undo history is cleared - also when only some\nrows were accepted: the saved values are the originals now, undoing past them would make edits\nof them. The displayed rows are rebuilt and <code>collection-filtered</code> is sent once, with\n<code>info: &#39;acceptChanges&#39;</code>. When the current row was\nremoved, <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">currentEntity</a> is set to <code>null</code> and <code>current-entity</code> is sent after; a removed\nrow leaves the selection (<code>selection-change</code>).</p>\n<p><strong>The keys of new rows.</strong> A new row has a temporary key, a generated negative number: in its key\nfield (<code>id: -1</code> with <code>key: &#39;id&#39;</code>), or without a key field as <code>__KEY</code> in\n<code>getChanges().newEntities</code>. <code>newKeys</code> maps each temporary key to the key the server gave the row.\nThe row gets it in its key field, or as its <code>__KEY</code> without a key field - setting it is no edit,\nand a selected row stays selected.</p>\n<p>Keep the grid readonly while the save runs (<code>gridInterface.updateConfig({ readonly: true })</code>):\nan edit made in between is accepted too, without being saved.</p>\n<p>The changes are those of the data container, so of every datasource sharing it. Call\n<code>reloadDatasource()</code> on the others.</p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> when a key in <code>newKeys</code> is not the key of a new row that is accepted (and not marked\nfor deletion), or the server&#39;s key is blank (<code>null</code>, <code>undefined</code>, <code>&#39;&#39;</code>) - a map the wrong way\nround, say. Checked first: nothing is accepted then</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ninterface Person {\n    id: number;\n    name: string;\n}\n// saves the changes in one transaction, and answers with the id it gave each new row\ndeclare function save(changes: object): Promise&lt;{ temporaryId: number; id: number }[]&gt;;\n\nconst people = new Datasource&lt;Person&gt;({ key: 'id' });\npeople.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann' }, { id: 2, name: 'Bob' }]);\nconst [ann, bob] = people.getDataRows();\nann.name = 'Anna';\npeople.markForDeletion(bob);\npeople.addNewEmpty({ name: 'Cid' }); // a temporary id: -1, say\n\nconst saved = await save(people.getChanges());\npeople.acceptChanges({ newKeys: new Map(saved.map((row) =&gt; [row.temporaryId, row.id])) });\n\npeople.getDataRows().map((row) =&gt; [row.id, row.name, row.__rowState]);\n// [[1, 'Anna', undefined], [7, 'Cid', undefined]] - Bob is gone, Cid has the server's id\npeople.hasChanges(); // false\n\n// only some rows were saved\npeople.acceptChanges({ rows: people.getSelectedRows() });</code></pre>\n","samples":["saving"]},{"name":"addNewEmpty","signatures":["addNewEmpty(row?: Partial<T>, options?: { scrollTo?: boolean }): void"],"doc":"<p>Adds a new row at the end: <code>getChanges()</code> lists it in <code>newEntities</code>, its <code>__rowState</code> is <code>&#39;N&#39;</code>.\nWhen grouped it is put in its group, and the group is expanded.</p>\n<p>The row gets a generated key, a negative number: with a key field it is written there\n(<code>{ company: &#39;NEW COMPANY&#39;, id: -1 }</code>), else it is the row&#39;s <code>__KEY</code>. After the save,\n<code>acceptChanges({ newKeys })</code> gives it the key from the server, see <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">acceptChanges</a>.</p>\n<p>Adding the row is not a step of the undo history: <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">undo</a> never removes it. Its edits after\nare steps, like any edit.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code> the values of the new row, default none. The object itself becomes the row.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.addNewEmpty();\ndatasource.addNewEmpty({ company: 'NEW COMPANY' });\ndatasource.addNewEmpty({ company: 'NEW COMPANY' }, { scrollTo: false });</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"addNewRows","signatures":["addNewRows(rows: Partial<T>[], options?: { scrollTo?: boolean }): EntityUnion<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>Adds several new rows at the end at once, as <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">addNewEmpty</a> adds one: each is listed in\n<code>getChanges().newEntities</code>, its <code>__rowState</code> is <code>&#39;N&#39;</code>, and gets a generated key. The grid&#39;s import\n(<code>gridInterface.importRows()</code>, the import dialog) adds its rows with it. Much faster than\n<code>addNewEmpty()</code> in a loop: the rows are sorted and grouped once, not once per row.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The rows are shown at the end, also when the rows are sorted or filtered (as <code>addNewEmpty()</code>\nshows its row) - until the next sort or filter puts them in place. When grouped they are put in\ntheir groups, and the group of the first one is expanded.</li>\n<li>Not validated, as a new row from <code>addNewEmpty()</code>: call <code>validate(rows)</code> to check them.</li>\n<li>Adding them is not a step of the undo history, as <code>addNewEmpty()</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Sends <code>collection-changed</code> (<code>{ added: true }</code>) once, nothing for no rows.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> the values of the new rows. The objects themselves become the rows</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the new rows, as the datasource keeps them</p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when <code>rows</code> is not an array</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const added = datasource.addNewRows([{ company: 'NEW 1' }, { company: 'NEW 2' }]);\ndatasource.validate(added);</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"aggregate","signatures":["aggregate(field: string, fn: AggregateFunction, rows?: Entity[] | GroupRow): number | null"],"doc":"<p>Sums up a field over rows: its sum, average, smallest or largest number, or how many values it\nhas - see <a href=\"#api/index.AggregateFunction\">AggregateFunction</a>. Blank values are left out, <code>sum</code>, <code>avg</code>, <code>min</code> and <code>max</code>\ntake numbers only. Nothing is rounded, format the result with the field&#39;s formatter\n(<code>getFormatter(field).format(value)</code>).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>No rows given</strong>: the rows the filter lets through, <code>getDataRows()</code> - when grouped, the rows of\ncollapsed groups too. Rows marked for deletion count until they are saved, as they are rows\nof the grid until then.</li>\n<li><strong>A group row</strong>: the data rows of the group, of its sub groups - collapsed ones too.</li>\n<li><strong>A list of rows</strong>: those rows, e.g. <code>getSelectedRows()</code>. Computed on each call.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The value of the filtered rows and of a group row is kept until a value of the field changes (set\non a row: an edit, <code>undo()</code>, <code>upsert()</code> ...) or other rows are filtered (<code>filter()</code>, <code>setData()</code>,\nrows added or removed). Asking again is cheap: the grid asks on every rebuild, and for every\ngroup row it renders. A sort changes no value; a filter, sort or <code>group()</code> makes new group rows.</p>\n<p>The grid shows these in its group rows and its totals row: a column&#39;s <code>aggregate</code> in the grid\nconfig, see the aggregates guide.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>field</code> the field, the property on the row</li>\n<li><code>fn</code> <code>&#39;sum&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;avg&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;min&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;max&#39;</code> or <code>&#39;count&#39;</code></li>\n<li><code>rows</code> the rows: left out the filtered rows, a group row, or a list of data rows</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the number, <code>null</code> for the average, smallest or largest of no numbers</p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when <code>fn</code> is no aggregate function</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { isGroupRow } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndatasource.aggregate('balance', 'sum'); // 1234567.89, over the rows the filter lets through\ndatasource.aggregate('age', 'avg'); // 38.5, or null when no row has an age\ndatasource.aggregate('email', 'count'); // the rows with an email\n\n// per group, the rows of collapsed groups included\ndatasource.group([{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]);\nfor (const row of datasource.getRows()) {\n    if (isGroupRow(row)) {\n        console.log(row.__groupName, datasource.aggregate('balance', 'sum', row));\n    }\n}\n\n// the selected rows, formatted as the field shows its values\nconst sum = datasource.aggregate('balance', 'sum', datasource.getSelectedRows());\ndatasource.getFormatter('balance').format(sum);</code></pre>\n","samples":["aggregates"]},{"name":"canRedo","signatures":["canRedo(): boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when there is a step to <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">redo</a>: undo took one back, and nothing was recorded since.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>declare const redoButton: HTMLButtonElement;\n\nredoButton.disabled = !datasource.canRedo();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"canUndo","signatures":["canUndo(): boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when there is a step to <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">undo</a>. With the <code>history-changed</code> event, for an Undo button\nof your own.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>declare const undoButton: HTMLButtonElement;\ndeclare const redoButton: HTMLButtonElement;\n\ndatasource.on('history-changed', () =&gt; {\n    undoButton.disabled = !datasource.canUndo();\n    redoButton.disabled = !datasource.canRedo();\n});\nundoButton.onclick = () =&gt; datasource.undo();\nredoButton.onclick = () =&gt; datasource.redo();</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"clearHistory","signatures":["clearHistory(): void"],"doc":"<p>Empties the undo history: nothing to undo or redo. The edits stay as they are. Sends\n<code>history-changed</code> with <code>info: &#39;clear&#39;</code> when there was something in it.</p>\n<p>Done by the datasource itself where undoing past would be wrong: <code>setData()</code> without <code>add</code>,\n<code>removeAllData()</code>, <code>resetData()</code> and <code>acceptChanges()</code> - after a save the saved values are the\noriginals.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.getDataRows()[0].name = 'Changed';\ndatasource.clearHistory();\ndatasource.canUndo(); // false, the name stays 'Changed'</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"clearMarkedForDeletion","signatures":["clearMarkedForDeletion(): void"],"doc":"<p>Removes the rows marked for deletion for good, once the deletes are saved: they leave the rows,\n<code>getChanges()</code> no longer lists them in <code>deletedEntities</code>, and <code>resetData()</code> does not bring them\nback. Sends <code>collection-changed</code> with <code>{ removed: true, info: &#39;clearMarkedForDeletion&#39; }</code>. When\nthe current row is removed, <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">currentEntity</a> is set to <code>null</code> and <code>current-entity</code> is sent\nafter; a removed row leaves the selection (<code>selection-change</code>).</p>\n<p>When the new and edited rows were saved in the same go, call <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">acceptChanges</a> instead: it\nremoves the marked rows and accepts the rest. The changes of the removed rows leave the undo\nhistory.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const { deletedEntities } = datasource.getChanges();\nawait fetch('/api/people/delete', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(deletedEntities) });\ndatasource.clearMarkedForDeletion();</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"collapseGroup","signatures":["collapseGroup(id?: string): void"],"doc":"<p>Collapses a group, so only its group row is displayed, or every group with their sub groups.\nSends <code>collection-collapse</code>. Does nothing while the datasource is not grouped.</p>\n<p>The rows of a collapsed group are not in <code>getRows()</code>, but they are in <code>getDataRows()</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>id</code> the group&#39;s <code>__groupID</code> (see <a href=\"#api/index.GroupRow\">GroupRow</a>). Left out, every group is collapsed</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.collapseGroup('Norway');\ndatasource.collapseGroup(); // every group: getRows() has the group rows only</code></pre>\n","samples":["sorting-grouping"]},{"name":"deselectAll","signatures":["deselectAll(options?: { notify?: boolean }): void"],"doc":"<p>Deselects every row.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.deselectAll({ notify: true });</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"]},{"name":"expandGroup","signatures":["expandGroup(id?: string): void"],"doc":"<p>Expands a group, so its rows are displayed, or every group with their sub groups. Sends\n<code>collection-expand</code>. Does nothing while the datasource is not grouped.</p>\n<p>A sub group is only shown when the groups above it are expanded: expanding one expands the groups\nabove it too, so it is shown. An id that is no group changes nothing.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>id</code> the group&#39;s <code>__groupID</code> (see <a href=\"#api/index.GroupRow\">GroupRow</a>), e.g. <code>&#39;Norway&#39;</code> or <code>&#39;Norway-Apple&#39;</code> for a\nsub group. Left out, every group is expanded</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.group([{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]);\ndatasource.expandGroup('Norway'); // the rows of Norway are shown\ndatasource.expandGroup(); // every group</code></pre>\n","samples":["sorting-grouping"]},{"name":"filter","signatures":["filter(expression?: FilterExpression | null): void"],"doc":"<p>Sets the filter and runs it. The rows it lets through are sorted and grouped the way the\ndatasource is, and are what <code>getRows()</code> returns.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>filter(expression)</code> - filter on this, it replaces the filter there was</li>\n<li><code>filter(null)</code> - no filter, every row is shown</li>\n<li><code>filter()</code> - run the current filter again</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The root can be a group or a single condition. Conditions without a field or operator, date\nconditions without the value they need and empty groups are ignored. The datasource keeps the\nobject it is given, <code>getFilter()</code> returns it - a condition on a field that always matches case\n(<code>FieldConfig.caseSensitive</code>) is a copy with <code>caseSensitive: true</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>expression</code> a condition or a group of them, see <a href=\"#api/index.FilterExpression\">FilterExpression</a>. Build it with\n<a href=\"#api/index.and\">and</a>, <a href=\"#api/index.or\">or</a> and <a href=\"#api/index.where\">where</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { and, or, where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndatasource.filter(where('balance', 'GREATER_THAN', 2500));\n\n// country = 'Norway' AND (age &lt; 30 OR age &gt; 60)\ndatasource.filter(\n    and(where('country', 'EQUAL', 'Norway'), or(where('age', 'LESS_THAN', 30), where('age', 'GREATER_THAN', 60)))\n);\n\ndatasource.filter(); // run it again\ndatasource.filter(null); // every row</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"]},{"name":"filterChangedOnly","signatures":["filterChangedOnly(on: boolean): void"],"doc":"<p>Shows only the changed rows: the new rows, the edited ones and the ones marked for deletion -\nthe rows with a <code>__rowState</code>. On top of the filter there is: a row is shown when the filter lets\nit through AND it is changed. Runs the filter, as <code>filter()</code> does.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>It is not part of the filter</strong>: <code>getFilter()</code>, the header filters, the filter editor,\n<code>getFilterString()</code> and the grid&#39;s state (<code>GridState.filter</code>) do not have it, and setting the\nfilter (<code>filter()</code>, the header filters, the filter editor) leaves it on. It stays on until it\nis turned off: <code>filterChangedOnly(false)</code>, the grid&#39;s row menu (View › Changed rows only) or the\nfooter&#39;s Clear.</li>\n<li><strong>It is applied when the rows are filtered</strong>, as the filter is: <code>filter()</code>, a header filter,\n<code>setData()</code>, <code>reloadDatasource()</code>, marking rows for deletion, <code>acceptChanges()</code> ... An edit does\nnot filter the rows again, so a row edited back to its original values stays shown until the\nrows are filtered next - it does not disappear while the user types in it.</li>\n<li>The grid shows it in the footer, as a chip in front of the filter&#39;s.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>on</code> <code>true</code> for the changed rows only, <code>false</code> for every row the filter lets through</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndatasource.filter(where('country', 'EQUAL', 'Norway'));\ndatasource.filterChangedOnly(true); // the changed rows in Norway\ndatasource.isChangedOnly(); // true\ndatasource.getFilter(); // still { field: 'country', operator: 'EQUAL', value: 'Norway' }\ndatasource.filterChangedOnly(false); // every row in Norway again</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"getAllData","signatures":["getAllData(): EntityUnion<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>Every row in the data: no filter, sort or grouping, the rows marked for deletion included, never a\ngroup row. A new array, the rows in it are the rows themselves (not copies). Shared with every\ndatasource on the same data container.</p>\n<p><a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">getDataRows</a> has the rows that pass the filter, sorted; <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">getRows</a> what the grid shows.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndatasource.filter(where('age', 'GREATER_THAN', 60));\ndatasource.getDataRows().length; // the rows over 60\ndatasource.getAllData().length; // every row</code></pre>\n","samples":["rows-data"]},{"name":"getChangedFields","signatures":["getChangedFields(row: T): string[]"],"doc":"<p>The fields of a row that differ from their original value - the ones <code>getChanges()</code> sends for it -\nin the order they were first edited. <code>[]</code> for a new row (it has no original), a row not edited, and\nan object that is no row of the datasource&#39;s data. A field edited back to its original is not in it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const [ann] = datasource.getDataRows();\nann.name = 'Anna';\nann.city = 'Bergen';\ndatasource.getChangedFields(ann); // ['name', 'city']</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"getChangedRows","signatures":["getChangedRows(kinds?: ChangeKinds | null): T[]"],"doc":"<p>The rows <code>getChanges()</code> lists, of the kinds asked for - the rows themselves, not copies, in the order\nof the data: to validate what a save sends, select the edited rows, show them. A new row marked for\ndeletion is in none, and neither is a row whose fields are all back to their original value.</p>\n<p>The changes are those of the data container, so of every datasource sharing it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>kinds</code> the kinds of change, see <a href=\"#api/index.ChangeKinds\">ChangeKinds</a>: all when left out or <code>null</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> for kinds that are not <code>{ new?, modified?, deleted? }</code> of booleans</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>// validate only what a save sends: the new and edited rows\nconst errors = datasource.validate(datasource.getChangedRows({ deleted: false }));\n\n// how many rows are new\nconst added = datasource.getChangedRows({ new: true }).length;</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"getChanges","signatures":["getChanges(kinds?: ChangeKinds | null): Changes<T>"],"doc":"<p>The rows added, edited and marked for deletion since the data was set, as copies - what to send\nto a server. See <a href=\"#api/index.Changes\">Changes</a> for what is in it and when an edit counts: a field edited back\nto its original value is not listed, a <code>date</code> field compares on the day, a <code>datetime</code> field to\nthe second.</p>\n<p>The changes are those of the data container, so of every datasource sharing it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>kinds</code> the kinds of change listed, see <a href=\"#api/index.ChangeKinds\">ChangeKinds</a>: all when left out or <code>null</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ninterface Person {\n    id: number;\n    name: string;\n    born: Date;\n}\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource&lt;Person&gt;({ key: 'id', fields: { born: 'date' } });\ndatasource.setData([\n    { id: 1, name: 'Ann', born: new Date(1990, 4, 17) },\n    { id: 2, name: 'Bob', born: new Date(1985, 0, 2) }\n]);\nconst [ann, bob] = datasource.getDataRows();\nann.name = 'Anna';\nbob.born = new Date(1985, 0, 2, 13, 30); // the same day: no edit\ndatasource.addNewEmpty({ name: 'New' });\ndatasource.markForDeletion(bob);\n\nconst { newEntities, modifiedEntities, deletedEntities } = datasource.getChanges();\n// newEntities:      [{ name: 'New', id: -1 }] - a generated key\n// modifiedEntities: [{ id: 1, name: 'Anna' }]\n// deletedEntities:  [{ id: 2, name: 'Bob', born: ... }]\n\n// one kind, or some: the others are []\ndatasource.getChanges({ deleted: true }); // { newEntities: [], modifiedEntities: [], deletedEntities: [...] }\ndatasource.getChanges({ deleted: false }); // the new and edited rows, no deletions</code></pre>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> for kinds that are not <code>{ new?, modified?, deleted? }</code> of booleans</p>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"getConflicts","signatures":["getConflicts(rows?: Entity | Entity[]): Conflict<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>The conflicts <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">upsert</a> found: a field the server changed that the user has edited (the\nuser&#39;s value is kept), or a row the server no longer has that has changes here (the row is kept) -\nsee <a href=\"#api/index.Conflict\">Conflict</a>. Every row&#39;s, or the rows given, in the order of the rows. New objects every\ncall: <code>local</code> is the value the row has now.</p>\n<p>A conflict stays until it is resolved (<a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">resolveConflict</a>) or what it is about is gone: the\nfield is not edited any more (reverted with <code>resetField()</code> or <code>resetRows()</code>, undone, typed back\nto the server&#39;s value, saved with <code>acceptChanges()</code>), the row has no changes any more, or the row\nleaves the data (<code>removeData()</code>, <code>setData()</code> without <code>add</code> ...). <code>resetData()</code> clears every one.\n<code>conflicts-changed</code> is sent when they change.</p>\n<p>The conflicts are those of the data container, so of every datasource sharing it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows, default every row</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>declare const conflictCount: HTMLElement;\n\ndatasource.on('conflicts-changed', () =&gt; {\n    conflictCount.textContent = String(datasource.getConflicts().length);\n});\n\nfor (const conflict of datasource.getConflicts()) {\n    if (conflict.field === null) {\n        console.log(`row ${conflict.row.__KEY} was removed on the server`);\n    } else {\n        console.log(`${conflict.field}: yours ${conflict.local}, the server's ${conflict.remote}`);\n    }\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["live-data"]},{"name":"getDataContainer","signatures":["getDataContainer(): DataContainer"],"doc":"<p>The data container that holds the rows and tracks the edits: the one given as\n<code>DatasourceOptions.container</code>, or the one the datasource made. See <a href=\"#api/index.DataContainer\">DataContainer</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\ncontainer.setErrors(new Map([['7', 'Name is already taken']]));</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getDataRows","signatures":["getDataRows(): EntityUnion<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>Returns the data rows: filtered and sorted, never a <a href=\"#api/index.GroupRow\">GroupRow</a>, and when grouped the rows\nof collapsed groups included. Was <code>getRows(true)</code> in v5.</p>\n<p>It is the datasource&#39;s own list, not a copy - do not change it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.group([{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]);\ndatasource.collapseGroup();\n\ndatasource.getRows(); // the group rows only, every group is collapsed\ndatasource.getDataRows().map((row) =&gt; row.name); // every row that passes the filter</code></pre>\n","samples":["rows-data"]},{"name":"getErrors","signatures":["getErrors(rows?: Entity | Entity[]): ValidationError<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>The validation errors the rows have now, without validating: from the edits, and the last\n<a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">validate</a>. Every row&#39;s, or the rows given. Same entries as <code>validate()</code> returns. A row\nmarked for deletion has none (its errors are back when it is unmarked).</p>\n<p>The server&#39;s error of a row (<code>setErrors()</code>) is not in it, read it as <code>row.__rowError</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows, default every row</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { isGroupRow } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// the errors of the current row, for a form next to the grid\nconst row = datasource.currentEntity;\nif (row &amp;&amp; !isGroupRow(row)) {\n    for (const { field, messages } of datasource.getErrors(row)) {\n        console.log(datasource.getField(field).label, messages.join(', '));\n    }\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["validation"]},{"name":"getExpanded","signatures":["getExpanded(): string[]"],"doc":"<p>The ids (<code>__groupID</code>) of the expanded groups. It is what <code>GridState.expandedGroups</code> holds. A new\narray.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.expandGroup('Norway');\ndatasource.getExpanded(); // ['Norway']</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getField","signatures":["getField(name: string): Field"],"doc":"<p>A field as the datasource sees it: its type, label, formatter, validation rules and whether it\nis multiline, with every default filled in. A field that is not listed in <code>fields</code> is a <code>&#39;text&#39;</code>\nfield labelled with its name, without rules.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>name</code> the field name, the property on the row</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ fields: { born: { type: 'date', label: 'Born' } } });\n\ndatasource.getField('born'); // { name: 'born', type: 'date', label: 'Born', formatter: DateFormatterYYYYMMDD, validate: [], multiline: false, caseSensitive: false, clobType: false, readonly: false }\ndatasource.getField('name'); // { name: 'name', type: 'text', label: 'name', formatter: TextFormatter, validate: [], multiline: false, caseSensitive: false, clobType: false, readonly: false }\n// formatter: the formatter object, looked up by its id when the datasource was made</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getFilter","signatures":["getFilter(): FilterExpression | null"],"doc":"<p>The filter that is set: the object given to <code>filter()</code> / <code>setFilter()</code>, the header filters and\nthe filter editor&#39;s, or null when there is none. The root is a group or a single condition.</p>\n<p>It is the datasource&#39;s own object, not a copy.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndatasource.filter(where('age', 'GREATER_THAN', 18));\ndatasource.getFilter(); // { field: 'age', operator: 'GREATER_THAN', value: 18 }\n\n// typing 'x' in the header filter of name adds to it\ndatasource.getFilter();\n// { group: 'AND', children: [\n//     { field: 'age', operator: 'GREATER_THAN', value: 18 },\n//     { field: 'name', operator: 'EQUAL', value: 'x' }\n// ] }\n\ndatasource.filter(null);\ndatasource.getFilter(); // null</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"]},{"name":"getFilterFromType","signatures":["getFilterFromType(type: string): FilterOperator"],"doc":"<p>The operator a header filter of this type starts with: <code>&#39;GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO&#39;</code> for\n<code>&#39;number&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;date&#39;</code> and <code>&#39;datetime&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;EQUAL&#39;</code> for the rest - for text the whole text, <code>ann</code>\ndoes not find <code>Anna</code>. The grid uses it for a column without an <code>operator</code> in its config\n(<code>columns: { name: { operator: &#39;CONTAINS&#39; } }</code> for a contains search).</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>type</code> a field type, see <a href=\"#api/index.FieldType\">FieldType</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.getFilterFromType('number'); // 'GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO'\ndatasource.getFilterFromType('text'); // 'EQUAL'</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getFilterString","signatures":["getFilterString(label?: (field: string) => string): string"],"doc":"<p>The filter as text, e.g. <code>([NAME] &lt;&lt;EQUAL_TO&gt;&gt; &#39;X&#39;)</code>, upper case. Values are shown with the\nfield&#39;s formatter, a <code>valueField</code> as <code>[LABEL]</code>, a <code>BETWEEN</code> as <code>&#39;10&#39; &lt;&lt;AND&gt;&gt; &#39;20&#39;</code> (<code>&#39;&#39;</code> for an\nopen end). A condition that matches case (<code>caseSensitive</code>) keeps the case of its value and ends\nwith <code>&lt;&lt;MATCH_CASE&gt;&gt;</code>: <code>[NAME] &lt;&lt;EQUAL_TO&gt;&gt; &#39;Ann&#39; &lt;&lt;MATCH_CASE&gt;&gt;</code>. What the filter ignores -\nincomplete conditions, empty groups - is left out, and <code>&#39;&#39;</code> is returned when nothing is left (or\nno filter is set).</p>\n<p>The operators and AND / OR are texts, the ids <code>filterString.*</code> of <a href=\"#api/index.TEXTS\">TEXTS</a>: change them with\n<a href=\"#api/index.setTexts\">setTexts</a> (<code>&#39;filterString.operator.EQUAL&#39;: &#39;equal_to&#39;</code> is shown as <code>&lt;&lt;EQUAL_TO&gt;&gt;</code>).</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>label</code> the name to show for a field. Default the field&#39;s label (<code>FieldConfig.label</code>, else\nthe field name). The grid passes its column labels.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { and, Datasource, or, where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ fields: { born: { type: 'date', label: 'Born' } } });\ndatasource.filter(where('born', 'GREATER_THAN', new Date(1990, 0, 1)));\n\ndatasource.getFilterString(); // &quot;([BORN] &lt;&lt;GREATER_THAN&gt;&gt; '1990-01-01')&quot;\ndatasource.getFilterString((field: string) =&gt; `${field}!`); // &quot;([BORN!] &lt;&lt;GREATER_THAN&gt;&gt; '1990-01-01')&quot;\n\ndatasource.filter(and(where('a', 'EQUAL', 'x'), or(where('b', 'EQUAL', 'y'), where('b', 'EQUAL', 'z'))));\ndatasource.getFilterString(); // &quot;([A] &lt;&lt;EQUAL_TO&gt;&gt; 'X' AND ([B] &lt;&lt;EQUAL_TO&gt;&gt; 'Y' OR [B] &lt;&lt;EQUAL_TO&gt;&gt; 'Z'))&quot;\n\ndatasource.filter(where('a', 'EQUAL', 'Ann', { caseSensitive: true }));\ndatasource.getFilterString(); // &quot;([A] &lt;&lt;EQUAL_TO&gt;&gt; 'Ann' &lt;&lt;MATCH_CASE&gt;&gt;)&quot;</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"]},{"name":"getFilterTree","signatures":["getFilterTree(label?: (field: string) => string, formatterOf?: (field: string) => Formatter | undefined): FilterGroupNode | null"],"doc":"<p>Same information as <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">getFilterString</a>, but as a tree of <a href=\"#api/index.FilterNode\">FilterNode</a>s that\nkeeps the group nesting, so the footer can render grouped conditions as clusters\ninstead of a flat, ambiguous list. The root is always a group, also when the filter is a\nsingle condition. What the filter ignores is left out: incomplete conditions are, an empty\ngroup is a group with no children. Returns <code>null</code> when no filter is set or nothing of it is\nshown - when <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">getFilterString</a> returns <code>&#39;&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>label</code> the name to show for a field. Default the field&#39;s label (<code>FieldConfig.label</code>, else\nthe field name). The grid passes its column labels.</li>\n<li><code>formatterOf</code> a formatter to show the values of a field with instead of the field&#39;s own, or\nundefined for the field&#39;s own. It formats the values of <code>IN</code> / <code>NOT_IN</code> too (not <code>&#39;NULL&#39;</code>), which\nare shown as they are otherwise. The grid passes the formatters of its lookup columns\n(<code>ColumnConfig.editor</code>): the footer shows their labels, <code>Country in Norway, Sweden</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, type Formatter, TextFormatter, where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ fields: { age: { type: 'number', label: 'Age' } } });\ndatasource.filter(where('age', 'GREATER_THAN', 18));\n\ndatasource.getFilterTree();\n// { kind: 'group', group: 'AND', children: [\n//     { kind: 'condition', field: 'age', label: 'Age', operator: 'GREATER_THAN', value: '18', hasValue: true, caseSensitive: false }\n// ] }\n\n// the codes of country shown as names\nconst names: Record&lt;string, string&gt; = { NO: 'Norway', SE: 'Sweden' };\nconst countryName: Formatter = { ...TextFormatter, format: (value) =&gt; names[String(value)] ?? TextFormatter.format(value) };\ndatasource.filter(where('country', 'IN', ['NO', 'SE']));\ndatasource.getFilterTree(undefined, (field) =&gt; (field === 'country' ? countryName : undefined));\n// ... { kind: 'condition', field: 'country', label: 'country', operator: 'IN', value: 'Norway, Sweden', hasValue: true, caseSensitive: false } ...</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"]},{"name":"getFormatter","signatures":["getFormatter(field: string, type?: FieldType): Formatter"],"doc":"<p>The formatter for a field: its own (<code>FieldConfig.formatter</code>), else the datasource&#39;s default for\nits type. The formatter object, as registered under the id the options name (see\n<a href=\"#api/index.registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a>) when the datasource was made.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>field</code> the field name. A field that is not listed in <code>fields</code> is <code>&#39;text&#39;</code></li>\n<li><code>type</code> use this type instead of the field&#39;s. When it is not the field&#39;s type, the default\nformatter for <code>type</code> is returned - the field&#39;s own formatter is written for its own type. The\ngrid uses it for <code>dynamicCellTypeColumn</code>, where another column of the row decides the type.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    fields: { price: { type: 'number', formatter: 'numberComma' }, born: 'date' }\n});\n\ndatasource.getFormatter('price').format(12.5); // '12,5'\ndatasource.getFormatter('born').format(new Date(2026, 10, 20)); // '2026-11-20'\ndatasource.getFormatter('value', 'number').parse('12.5'); // 12.5, the default number formatter</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getGrouping","signatures":["getGrouping(): GroupArgument[]"],"doc":"<p>The grouping: the fields grouped on, the outer group first. <code>[]</code> when not grouped. It is what\n<code>GridState.grouping</code> holds. The datasource&#39;s own array, not a copy - change the grouping with\n<a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">group</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.group([{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]);\ndatasource.getGrouping(); // [{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]</code></pre>\n","samples":["sorting-grouping"]},{"name":"getLastSorting","signatures":["getLastSorting(): SortArgument[]"],"doc":"<p>The sort that is set: the fields and directions, the first decides. When grouped, the grouped\nfields come first. <code>[]</code> when the rows are not sorted. It is what <code>GridState.sorting</code> holds.</p>\n<p>It is the datasource&#39;s own array, not a copy - do not change it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.sort({ attribute: 'name', ascending: true });\ndatasource.getLastSorting(); // [{ attribute: 'name', ascending: true }]</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getMarkedForDeletion","signatures":["getMarkedForDeletion(): EntityUnion<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>The rows marked for deletion with <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">markForDeletion</a> / <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">markAllForDeletion</a>: still in\nthe data until <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">acceptChanges</a> or <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">clearMarkedForDeletion</a> removes them. The rows\nthemselves, not copies - the rows of <code>getChanges().deletedEntities</code>, plus the new rows that are\nmarked (they are not sent to a server).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.markForDeletion(datasource.getSelectedRows());\ndatasource.getMarkedForDeletion().length; // the rows just marked</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getMergedAt","signatures":["getMergedAt(row: Entity, field: string): number | undefined"],"doc":"<p>When the last <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">upsert</a> changed the value of a field of a row: the <code>Date.now()</code> of that upsert.\n<code>undefined</code> when no upsert changed it. A value set by the user or by code does not count, nor\ndoes a conflict (the value stays the user&#39;s). The grid flashes the cells a merge changed on its own\n(<code>GridConfig.mergeHighlight</code>); for a look of your own a <code>cellClass</code> hook can read it - the grid\nrenders the rows an upsert changed.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code> the row</li>\n<li><code>field</code> the field</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>// the cells an upsert changed in the last second get a class, with a css animation that runs once\ngridInterface.updateHooks({\n    cellClass: (row, field) =&gt; {\n        const at = datasource.getMergedAt(row, field);\n        return at !== undefined &amp;&amp; Date.now() - at &lt; 1000 ? { input: 'just-changed' } : null;\n    }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["live-data"]},{"name":"getOrderBy","signatures":["getOrderBy(): SortArgument[]"],"doc":"<p>The sort that is set, with <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">setOrderBy</a> or <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">sort</a>: the same fields and directions as\n<a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">getLastSorting</a>. The datasource&#39;s own array, not a copy.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.setOrderBy({ attribute: 'company', ascending: true });\ndatasource.getOrderBy(); // [{ attribute: 'company', ascending: true }]</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getOriginalValue","signatures":["getOriginalValue(row: T, field: keyof T & string): unknown"],"doc":"<p>The value a field of a row had before it was edited: as the data was set, or accepted last\n(<code>acceptChanges()</code>). The value it has now when the field is not edited. undefined for a new row (it\nhas no original) and for an object that is no row of the datasource&#39;s data. For a &quot;was&quot; tooltip, or a\nconflict to show both sides of.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const [ann] = datasource.getDataRows();\nann.name = 'Anna';\ndatasource.getOriginalValue(ann, 'name'); // 'Ann'\ndatasource.getOriginalValue(ann, 'city'); // the city now: not edited</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"getRow","signatures":["getRow(rowNo: number): GroupRow | EntityUnion<T> | undefined"],"doc":"<p>One row of the displayed rows, <code>getRows()[rowNo]</code>. When grouped it can be a <a href=\"#api/index.GroupRow\">GroupRow</a>, check\nwith <a href=\"#api/index.isGroupRow\">isGroupRow</a>. <code>undefined</code> out of range: no row at that index (no rows, a filter\nthat shows fewer).</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rowNo</code> the index in the displayed rows, 0 based</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { isGroupRow } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst row = datasource.getRow(0);\nif (row &amp;&amp; !isGroupRow(row)) {\n    console.log(row.name);\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getRows","signatures":["getRows(): (GroupRow | EntityUnion<T>)[]"],"doc":"<p>Returns the rows as they are displayed: filtered, sorted and grouped. When grouped, that\nis your data rows with a <a href=\"#api/index.GroupRow\">GroupRow</a> in front of each group, and the rows of a\ncollapsed group left out.</p>\n<p><a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">getDataRows</a> returns the data rows only - never a group row (was <code>getRows(true)</code> in v5).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { isGroupRow } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndatasource.group([{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]);\n\n// data rows and group rows, as the grid shows them\ndatasource.getRows().forEach((row) =&gt; {\n    if (isGroupRow(row)) {\n        console.log(row.__groupName);\n    } else {\n        console.log(row.name);\n    }\n});\n\n// data rows only, no check needed\nconst names = datasource.getDataRows().map((row) =&gt; row.name);</code></pre>\n","samples":["rows-data","sorting-grouping"]},{"name":"getSelectedRows","signatures":["getSelectedRows(): EntityUnion<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>The selected rows, in the order they are displayed. Data rows only, a group row can not be\nselected.</p>\n<p>Only displayed rows are returned: a selected row in a collapsed group, or one the filter leaves\nout, is not in it (it is selected again once it is displayed).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.on('selection-change', () =&gt; {\n    console.log(datasource.getSelectedRows().map((row) =&gt; row.name));\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"]},{"name":"getSelectionMode","signatures":["getSelectionMode(): SelectionMode"],"doc":"<p>How rows can be selected: <code>&#39;multiple&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;single&#39;</code> or <code>&#39;none&#39;</code>, see <a href=\"#api/index.SelectionMode\">SelectionMode</a>. Set\nwith <code>DatasourceOptions.selectionMode</code> or <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">setSelectionMode</a>; a grid showing the datasource\nuses it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>if (datasource.getSelectionMode() === 'multiple') {\n    datasource.selectAll();\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"group","signatures":["group(groups: GroupArgument[], options?: { add?: boolean }): void"],"doc":"<p>Groups the rows: a <a href=\"#api/index.GroupRow\">GroupRow</a> in front of each group, in <code>getRows()</code>. The rows are sorted\non the grouped fields, ascending. <code>group([])</code> removes the grouping.</p>\n<p>The groups start collapsed, apart from the ones whose id is in <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">getExpanded</a> (set with\n<a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">setExpanded</a>, or expanded before): <code>getRows()</code> has only the group rows until a group is\nexpanded. The rows are grouped on their value as the field&#39;s formatter shows it, so a <code>date</code> field\ngroups by day - in a grid, a date column shown as weeks, months, quarters or years\n(<code>ColumnFormat.date</code> <code>&#39;weekIso&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;weekUs&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;month&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;quarter&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;year&#39;</code>) groups by them; every blank value (null, undefined, <code>&#39;&#39;</code>) is one group with the id <code>&#39; blank&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>groups</code> the fields to group on, the first is the outer group</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.group([{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]);\ndatasource.group([{ attribute: 'company', title: 'Company' }], { add: true }); // country, then company\ndatasource.group([]); // no grouping</code></pre>\n","samples":["sorting-grouping"]},{"name":"hasChanges","signatures":["hasChanges(kinds?: ChangeKinds | null): boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when there is something to save: <code>getChanges()</code> would list a row - of the kinds asked for,\nsee <a href=\"#api/index.ChangeKinds\">ChangeKinds</a> (all by default). For an &quot;unsaved changes&quot; indicator, or to ask before the\nuser leaves the page. A new row marked for deletion is\nno change, and neither is a field edited back to its original value.</p>\n<p>The changes are those of the data container, so of every datasource sharing it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>kinds</code> the kinds of change, see <a href=\"#api/index.ChangeKinds\">ChangeKinds</a>: all when left out or <code>null</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>declare const saveButton: HTMLButtonElement;\n\n// the grid sends no event for an edit: check when the user is about to leave\nwindow.addEventListener('beforeunload', (event) =&gt; {\n    if (datasource.hasChanges()) {\n        event.preventDefault();\n    }\n});\nsaveButton.disabled = !datasource.hasChanges();\n// only deletions to confirm\nconst askFirst = datasource.hasChanges({ deleted: true });</code></pre>\n","samples":["saving"]},{"name":"hasConflicts","signatures":["hasConflicts(): boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when a row is in conflict, see <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">getConflicts</a>. Before a save, say: the user&#39;s values\nof a field in conflict overwrite the server&#39;s newer ones.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>declare const saveButton: HTMLButtonElement;\n\ndatasource.on('conflicts-changed', () =&gt; {\n    saveButton.title = datasource.hasConflicts() ? 'Some of your changes were also changed on the server' : '';\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["live-data"]},{"name":"hasErrors","signatures":["hasErrors(): boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when a row has a validation error now: from an edit, or the last <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">validate</a>. It does\nnot validate - before a save, call <code>validate()</code>, which also checks the fields never edited. The\nrows marked for deletion and the server&#39;s errors (<code>__rowError</code>) do not count.</p>\n<p>The errors are those of the data container, so of every datasource sharing it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>declare const saveButton: HTMLButtonElement;\n\n// the grid sends no event for an edit: check when it matters\nsaveButton.disabled = datasource.hasErrors();</code></pre>\n","samples":["validation"]},{"name":"isChangedOnly","signatures":["isChangedOnly(): boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> while only the changed rows are shown, see <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">filterChangedOnly</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.isChangedOnly(); // false\ndatasource.filterChangedOnly(true);\ndatasource.isChangedOnly(); // true</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"length","signatures":["length(): number"],"doc":"<p>The number of displayed rows, <code>getRows().length</code>: filtered, and when grouped the group rows\nincluded and the rows of collapsed groups left out. The number of data rows is\n<code>getDataRows().length</code> (was <code>length(true)</code> in v5).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.length(); // rows the grid shows\ndatasource.getDataRows().length; // data rows that pass the filter</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"markAllForDeletion","signatures":["markAllForDeletion(): void"],"doc":"<p>Marks every row for deletion, see <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">markForDeletion</a>: the new rows too. Was\n<code>markForDeletion(null, true)</code> in v5.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.markAllForDeletion();\ndatasource.getChanges().deletedEntities; // every row that is not new\ndatasource.unmarkAllForDeletion(); // unmarked again</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"markForDeletion","signatures":["markForDeletion(rows: Entity | Entity[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Marks rows for deletion, so the delete can be undone: <code>getChanges()</code> lists them in\n<code>deletedEntities</code>, and <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">unmarkForDeletion</a> (or <code>resetData()</code>) takes the mark off again.\nThey stay in the rows, with <code>__rowState</code> <code>&#39;D&#39;</code> - the grid marks them as deleted in the row\nselector. <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">acceptChanges</a> removes them once the deletes are saved.</p>\n<p>A new row (from <code>addNewEmpty()</code>) is marked too. While it is marked it is in none of the lists of\n<code>getChanges()</code> - it was never saved, there is nothing to send - and unmarked it is a new row again.</p>\n<p>In the grid, the row menu&#39;s &quot;Delete:&quot; entries mark and unmark the selected rows, see <code>MENU_IDS</code>.\nTo remove rows that are not on a server, without tracking, use <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">removeData</a>.</p>\n<p>A step of the undo history: <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">undo</a> (Ctrl+Z in the grid) takes the marks off again.</p>\n<p>Sends <code>collection-filtered</code> with <code>info: &#39;markForDeletion&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows, e.g. <code>getSelectedRows()</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.markForDeletion(datasource.getSelectedRows());</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"on","signatures":["on<Type extends keyof DatasourceEvents>(type: Type, handler: EventHandler<DatasourceEvents[Type]>): () => void"],"doc":"<p>Subscribes to an event. The handler gets the event&#39;s payload, typed from\n<a href=\"#api/index.DatasourceEvents\">DatasourceEvents</a> - see there for every event and what it sends.</p>\n<p>The handler stays subscribed until you call the function this returns. What the handler\nreturns is ignored (in v5 it had to return <code>true</code> to stay subscribed).</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>type</code> the event name</li>\n<li><code>handler</code> called with the payload every time the event is sent</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> a function that unsubscribes the handler</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const off = datasource.on('collection-filtered', (data) =&gt; {\n    console.log('filtered by', data.info, '-', datasource.getDataRows().length, 'rows');\n});\n\ndatasource.on('current-entity', () =&gt; {\n    console.log('current row', datasource.currentEntity);\n});\n\noff(); // unsubscribe</code></pre>\n","samples":["events"]},{"name":"parseRow","signatures":["parseRow<R extends object>(row: R): R"],"doc":"<p>Reads the values of a row as the types of the fields: a row as JSON gives it - from a backend, a\nstream - with the values the grid needs. Each field listed in <code>fields</code> (the others stay as they are):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>date</code>, <code>datetime</code>: ISO text a <code>Date</code> - <code>&#39;2026-11-22&#39;</code> the start of that day in local time (not\nUTC, as <code>new Date(&#39;2026-11-22&#39;)</code> reads it), <code>&#39;2026-11-22T08:30:00&#39;</code> and <code>&#39;2026-11-22 08:30:00&#39;</code>\nlocal time, with <code>Z</code> or an offset that instant - a number the milliseconds since 1970</li>\n<li><code>number</code>: text that is a number (<code>&#39;12.5&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;-3&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;1e3&#39;</code>) the number</li>\n<li><code>boolean</code>: <code>&#39;true&#39;</code> / <code>&#39;false&#39;</code>, <code>1</code> / <code>0</code>, <code>&#39;1&#39;</code> / <code>&#39;0&#39;</code> true and false</li>\n<li><code>&#39;&#39;</code> is <code>null</code> for those types; a value that can not be read as its type stays as it is</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Changes the object, and returns it: for the rows before <code>setData()</code> - a row already in the\ndatasource is a proxy, setting its values would be edits. <code>setData(rows, { parse: true })</code> does it\nto every row.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code> a plain object, as JSON gave it</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the same object</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ fields: { born: 'date', amount: 'number', active: 'boolean' } });\nconst row = datasource.parseRow({ born: '2026-11-22', amount: '12.5', active: 'true', name: 'Ann' });\n// { born: Date (22 November 2026, 00:00 local), amount: 12.5, active: true, name: 'Ann' }\n\ndeclare const rowsFromServer: object[];\ndatasource.setData(rowsFromServer, { parse: true }); // every row</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"redo","signatures":["redo(): boolean"],"doc":"<p>Does the last step <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">undo</a> took back again. Recording a new step empties what there is to\nredo. The grid does it with Ctrl+Y, Ctrl+Shift+Z (Cmd+Shift+Z), and from its row menu. Sends\n<code>history-changed</code> with <code>info: &#39;redo&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> <code>false</code> when there is nothing to redo</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>if (datasource.canRedo()) {\n    datasource.redo();\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"reloadDatasource","signatures":["reloadDatasource(): void"],"doc":"<p>Builds the displayed rows again from every row in the data container: filtered, sorted and grouped\nthe way the datasource is. Sends <code>collection-filtered</code> (<code>info: &#39;filter&#39;</code>). For rows changed in the\ndata container directly (<code>getDataContainer().setData()</code>, <code>replace()</code> ...), or by another datasource\non the same container.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.getDataContainer().setData([{ id: 3, name: 'Cid' }], { add: true });\ndatasource.reloadDatasource(); // the new row is shown, if the filter lets it through</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"removeAllData","signatures":["removeAllData(): Entity[]"],"doc":"<p>Removes every row for good, see <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">removeData</a>. Was <code>removeData(null, true)</code> in v5. Sends\nthe same <code>collection-changed</code> event, with <code>data: null</code>. The rows leave the selection and\n<a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">currentEntity</a> is set to <code>null</code>, with their events after it. The undo history is cleared.</p>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the rows removed</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.removeAllData();\ndatasource.getAllData(); // []</code></pre>\n","samples":["rows-data"]},{"name":"removeData","signatures":["removeData(rows: Entity | Entity[], options?: { refilter?: boolean }): Entity[]"],"doc":"<p>Removes rows for good: they are not marked for deletion, <code>getChanges()</code> does not list them and\n<code>resetData()</code> does not bring them back. Use <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">markForDeletion</a> to delete rows on a server.\nTheir changes leave the undo history, and a step left without changes is dropped: undo never\nwrites into a row that is gone.</p>\n<p>Sends <code>collection-changed</code>. A removed row leaves the selection (<code>selection-change</code> is sent\nafter), and when it was the current row <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">currentEntity</a> is set to <code>null</code>\n(<code>current-entity</code> is sent after).</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the rows removed</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.removeData(datasource.getSelectedRows());\n\n// many calls: rebuild the displayed rows once, at the end\nconst rows = datasource.getAllData().filter((row) =&gt; row.archived);\nrows.forEach((row, i) =&gt; datasource.removeData(row, { refilter: i === rows.length - 1 }));</code></pre>\n","samples":["rows-data"]},{"name":"removeGroup","signatures":["removeGroup(group?: GroupArgument): void"],"doc":"<p>Removes one level of grouping, or all of it. The sort is set to the grouped fields that are left\n(none: the rows keep the order they are in). Sends <code>collection-grouped</code> twice: <code>info: &#39;group&#39;</code> with\nthe grouping left, then <code>info: &#39;removeGroup&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>group</code> the level to remove, found by its field (<code>attribute</code>): the object from\n<a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">getGrouping</a> or a copy, the <code>title</code> does not matter. A field that is not grouped on changes\nnothing and sends no event. Left out, all grouping is removed</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.group([\n    { attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' },\n    { attribute: 'company', title: 'Company' }\n]);\ndatasource.removeGroup({ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }); // grouped on company only\ndatasource.removeGroup(); // not grouped</code></pre>\n","samples":["sorting-grouping"]},{"name":"resetData","signatures":["resetData(): void"],"doc":"<p>Throws away every change since the data was set: edited rows get their original values back,\nrows marked for deletion are unmarked, new rows (from <code>addNewEmpty()</code>) are removed, and the\nvalidation errors are cleared. Then the displayed rows are rebuilt. Rows removed for good\n(<code>removeData()</code>, <code>clearMarkedForDeletion()</code>) do not come back. A new row that was the current\nrow sets <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">currentEntity</a> to <code>null</code> (<code>current-entity</code> is sent after), and leaves the\nselection (<code>selection-change</code>). The undo history is cleared: there is nothing left to undo.</p>\n<p>The changes are those of the data container, so of every datasource sharing it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.getDataRows()[0].name = 'Changed';\ndatasource.addNewEmpty({ name: 'New' });\n\ndatasource.resetData();\ndatasource.getChanges(); // { newEntities: [], modifiedEntities: [], deletedEntities: [] }</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"resetDataSelectionOnly","signatures":["resetDataSelectionOnly(): void"],"doc":"<p><a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">resetData</a> for the selected rows only: their edits are undone, the ones marked for deletion\nare unmarked, the new ones are removed, and their validation errors are cleared. The other rows\nkeep their changes.</p>\n<p>Unlike <code>resetData()</code> it is a step of the undo history: <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">undo</a> brings the edits and the\ndeletion marks back - not a new row it removed, undo never adds a row. <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">resetRows</a> keeps\nthe new rows.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.select(1); // the first row\ndatasource.resetDataSelectionOnly(); // only that row gets its original values back</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"resetField","signatures":["resetField(row: Entity, field: string): void"],"doc":"<p>Reverts one cell: the field of the row gets its original value back - the value it had when the\ndata was set, or when the changes were last accepted. A field that is not edited (that\n<code>getChanges()</code> would not list) is left as it is.</p>\n<p>It is an edit like any other: validated, and one step of the undo history - <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">undo</a> brings\nthe edited value back. The grid&#39;s row menu has it as &quot;Undo cell edit&quot; (<code>row.edit.revertCell</code>). The\ngrid shows it on its own, as any value set on a row (the <code>rows-changed</code> event). A conflict of the\nfield goes with the edit, see <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">getConflicts</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code> the row, one the datasource handed out. A row that is not in the data is skipped</li>\n<li><code>field</code> the field</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const row = datasource.getDataRows()[0];\nrow.name = 'Changed';\n\ndatasource.resetField(row, 'name'); // the name it had\ndatasource.undo(); // 'Changed' again</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"resetRows","signatures":["resetRows(rows: Entity | Entity[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Reverts rows to what the server has: their fields get their original values back and a row\nmarked for deletion is unmarked - <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">resetDataSelectionOnly</a>, for the rows given.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A new row is marked for deletion</strong>: it is not on the server. Its fields get the values it was\nadded with (<code>addNewEmpty(row)</code>) and it is marked - shown struck through, left out of\n<code>getChanges()</code> and <code>hasChanges()</code>, removed with the other marked rows when the changes are\nsaved (<code>clearMarkedForDeletion()</code>) or thrown away (<code>resetData()</code>). Not removed at once as by\n<code>resetDataSelectionOnly()</code>: a revert can be undone, and undo never adds a row back - <code>undo()</code>\nbrings the new row back, unmarked, with its edits.</li>\n<li>It is one step of the undo history: <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">undo</a> brings the edits and the marks back.</li>\n<li>The fields are validated as for an edit: an error of an edit goes away with it, an original\nvalue that breaks a rule shows its error.</li>\n<li>The displayed rows are not rebuilt, the rows stay where they are. The grid&#39;s row menu has it\nas &quot;Undo row edits&quot; (<code>row.edit.revertRow</code>, the row right clicked, and <code>row.edit.revertRows</code>, the selected rows). The grid shows it on its own, as\nany value set on a row (the <code>rows-changed</code> event).</li>\n<li>The conflicts of the rows go with their changes, see <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">getConflicts</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows, e.g. <code>getSelectedRows()</code>. Rows that are not in the data are\nskipped</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.resetRows(datasource.getSelectedRows());</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"resetSort","signatures":["resetSort(defaultSortAttribute?: string): void"],"doc":"<p>Clears the sort, without sorting: the rows keep their order until the displayed rows are built\nagain (<code>filter()</code>, <code>setData()</code> ...), then they are in the order they were set - sorted on the\ngrouped fields when grouped, the groups need that. No event is sent.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>defaultSortAttribute</code> a field to sort on ascending instead, set the same way (not run)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.resetSort();\ndatasource.getLastSorting(); // []\n\ndatasource.resetSort('name');\ndatasource.sort(); // sorted on name, ascending</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"resolveConflict","signatures":["resolveConflict(row: Entity, field: string | null, take: \"local\" | \"remote\"): void"],"doc":"<p>Resolves a conflict, see <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">getConflicts</a>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&#39;local&#39;</code>: the user&#39;s value stays, still edited - <code>getChanges()</code> sends it, as an edit of the\nserver&#39;s value. For a row the server removed: the row stays with its changes, and a later\n<code>upsert(rows, { removeMissing: true })</code> gives it no conflict again (it removes it once it has no\nchanges)</li>\n<li><code>&#39;remote&#39;</code>: the field gets the server&#39;s value - its original - as <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">resetField</a> does: an\nedit, validated, a step of the undo history (<a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">undo</a> brings the user&#39;s value back). For a\nrow the server removed: the row is removed, as <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">removeData</a> does, with its events</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The grid shows it on its own (<code>rows-changed</code>). Nothing happens when there is no such conflict.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code> the row</li>\n<li><code>field</code> the field, <code>null</code> for a row the server removed</li>\n<li><code>take</code> <code>&#39;local&#39;</code> for the user&#39;s value, <code>&#39;remote&#39;</code> for the server&#39;s</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when <code>take</code> is neither</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>// the server wins every conflict\nfor (const conflict of datasource.getConflicts()) {\n    datasource.resolveConflict(conflict.row, conflict.field, 'remote');\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["live-data"]},{"name":"select","signatures":["select(row?: number, options?: { notify?: boolean }): void"],"doc":"<p>Selects a row and makes it the current entity. A group row can not be selected, the first\ndata row after it is.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code> the row number in the displayed rows, starting on 1 (not 0 like <code>getRow()</code>).\nDefault the first row</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.select(5); // the fifth displayed row, getRow(4)\ndatasource.select(5, { notify: true }); // and scroll the grid to it</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"]},{"name":"selectAll","signatures":["selectAll(): void"],"doc":"<p>Selects every displayed data row - not the rows of collapsed groups or the ones the filter leaves\nout - and sends <code>selection-change</code>. Only in the <code>&#39;multiple&#39;</code> selection mode: in <code>&#39;single&#39;</code> and\n<code>&#39;none&#39;</code> it does nothing, it selects nothing and sends no event.\nClicking the grid&#39;s top left corner does the same (ctrl+click there deselects every row).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.selectAll();\ndatasource.getSelectedRows().length; // every displayed data row</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"]},{"name":"selectFirst","signatures":["selectFirst(): void"],"doc":"<p>Selects the first displayed data row, makes it current and sends <code>select</code> (<code>info: &#39;select-first&#39;</code>),\nso the grid scrolls to it. Does nothing when no data row is displayed.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.selectFirst();\ndatasource.currentEntity; // the first data row</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"]},{"name":"selectLast","signatures":["selectLast(): void"],"doc":"<p>Selects the last displayed data row, makes it current and sends <code>select</code> (<code>info: &#39;select-last&#39;</code>),\nso the grid scrolls to it. Does nothing when no data row is displayed.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.selectLast();</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"]},{"name":"selectNext","signatures":["selectNext(): void"],"doc":"<p>Selects the data row below the current one, makes it current and sends <code>select</code>\n(<code>info: &#39;select-next&#39;</code>). From the last row it goes to the first, and without a current row it\nstarts at the first. Group rows are skipped.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>document.getElementById('next')!.onclick = () =&gt; datasource.selectNext();</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"]},{"name":"selectPrev","signatures":["selectPrev(): void"],"doc":"<p>Selects the data row above the current one, makes it current and sends <code>select</code>\n(<code>info: &#39;select-prev&#39;</code>). From the first row it goes to the last. Group rows are skipped.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>document.getElementById('prev')!.onclick = () =&gt; datasource.selectPrev();</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"]},{"name":"setData","signatures":["setData(rows: any[], options?: { add?: boolean; parse?: boolean; refilter?: boolean }): void"],"doc":"<p>Sets the rows, in the data container - so every datasource sharing it gets them. The rows are\nfiltered, sorted and grouped the way the datasource is: a filter that is set applies to the new\nrows too.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> your objects</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>declare const rowsFromServer: object[];\ndeclare const moreRows: object[];\n\ndatasource.setData(rowsFromServer); // replaces the rows, the filter applies\ndatasource.setData(moreRows, { add: true });\ndatasource.setData(moreRows, { add: true, refilter: false }); // shown even if the filter leaves them out</code></pre>\n","samples":["rows-data"]},{"name":"setExpanded","signatures":["setExpanded(x: string[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Sets which groups are expanded, by their <code>__groupID</code>, for the next <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">group</a>: those groups start\nexpanded, the rest collapsed. The groups shown now do not change.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>x</code> the group ids, e.g. <code>[&#39;Norway&#39;, &#39;Norway-Apple&#39;]</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.setExpanded(['Norway']);\ndatasource.group([{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]); // Norway is expanded</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"setFields","signatures":["setFields(fields: Record<string, FieldType | FieldConfig> | undefined): void"],"doc":"<p>Replaces the fields - their types, labels, formatters, validation rules - as <code>fields</code> of the\nconstructor gives them: for columns known only after the datasource is made (the metadata of a\nquery came). The rows stay; they are filtered, sorted and grouped again by the new types\n(<code>collection-filtered</code>), after <code>fields-change</code>. A grid on the datasource shows them: its columns\nkeep their settings, a display format the new type does not take is dropped - not the label, the\nplaceholder, read only (a warning in the console).</p>\n<p>The fields not given are text fields now. The rows that have validation errors are validated again\nwith the new rules; the other rows when <code>validate()</code> is called, or edited.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>fields</code> the fields, as <code>DatasourceOptions.fields</code>: <code>{ born: &#39;date&#39;, age: { type: &#39;number&#39; } }</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> as the constructor: a type that does not exist, a formatter or validator id that is not\nregistered, wrong rules, and a field that has another type or other rules in another datasource on\nthe same container. Nothing changes then</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ key: 'ID' });\n// ... the grid is made on it; later the metadata of the query comes\ndatasource.setFields({ ID: 'number', BORN: 'date', NAME: { type: 'text', label: 'Name' } });</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"setFilter","signatures":["setFilter(expression: FilterExpression | null): void"],"doc":"<p>Sets the filter without running it - <code>filter()</code> runs it. <code>setFilter(null)</code> removes it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>expression</code> a condition or a group, see <a href=\"#api/index.FilterExpression\">FilterExpression</a>, or null for no filter</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndatasource.setFilter(where('age', 'GREATER_THAN', 18));\ndatasource.filter(); // runs it</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"]},{"name":"setGrouping","signatures":["setGrouping(group: GroupArgument[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Sets the grouping without grouping the rows now. The next call that builds the displayed rows\ngroups them - <code>group()</code>, <code>sort()</code>, <code>filter()</code>, <code>setData()</code>, <code>reloadDatasource()</code> ... - with the rows\nsorted on the grouped fields first. Until then <code>getRows()</code> is not grouped and <code>expandGroup()</code> /\n<code>collapseGroup()</code> do nothing.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>group</code> the fields to group on, the outer group first</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.setGrouping([{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]);\ndatasource.filter(); // grouped now, the rows sorted on country first</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"setLocaleCompare","signatures":["setLocaleCompare(code: string, options?: any): void"],"doc":"<p>Sorts text with an <code>Intl.Collator</code> for a language, from the next sort on. Without it text is\nsorted with <code>localeCompare()</code> of the browser&#39;s language. Filtering is not changed.</p>\n<p>Was <code>setLocalCompare()</code> in v5.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>code</code> the language, e.g. <code>&#39;nb&#39;</code> - <code>å</code> sorts after <code>z</code></li>\n<li><code>options</code> the <code>Intl.Collator</code> options, e.g. <code>{ sensitivity: &#39;base&#39; }</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.setLocaleCompare('nb');\ndatasource.sort({ attribute: 'name', ascending: true }); // ... 'Zara', 'Øystein', 'Åse'</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"setOrderBy","signatures":["setOrderBy(param: SortArgument | SortArgument[], options?: { add?: boolean }): void"],"doc":"<p>Sets the sort without sorting, <code>sort()</code> sorts. Takes the same arguments as <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">sort</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>param</code> the field and direction, or a list of them</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.setOrderBy({ attribute: 'company', ascending: true });\ndatasource.setOrderBy({ attribute: 'age', ascending: false }, { add: true });\ndatasource.sort(); // sorts on company, then age</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"setRowAsCurrentEntity","signatures":["setRowAsCurrentEntity(row: number): void"],"doc":"<p>Makes a displayed row the current entity (<a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">currentEntity</a>) and sends <code>current-entity</code>. The\nselection is not changed. A group row&#39;s index makes the group row current, an index out of range\nmakes it <code>null</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code> the index in the displayed rows (<code>getRows()</code>), 0 based - not 1 based like <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">select</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.setRowAsCurrentEntity(0); // the first displayed row\ndatasource.currentEntity; // that row</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"setSelectionMode","signatures":["setSelectionMode(mode: SelectionMode): void"],"doc":"<p>Sets how rows can be selected: <code>&#39;multiple&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;single&#39;</code> or <code>&#39;none&#39;</code>. A blank value is <code>&#39;none&#39;</code>. The\nrows selected before stay selected.</p>\n<p>The datasource owns the selection mode: a grid showing it uses this one from the next click on, it\nhas no option of its own.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>mode</code> the selection mode, see <a href=\"#api/index.SelectionMode\">SelectionMode</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.setSelectionMode('single'); // a click selects one row, ctrl/shift+click too\ndatasource.setSelectionMode('none'); // a click makes the row current, selects nothing</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"]},{"name":"sort","signatures":["sort(args?: SortArgument | SortArgument[], options?: { add?: boolean }): void"],"doc":"<p>Sorts the rows. When grouped, the grouped fields are sorted first.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>sort(arg)</code> - sort on one field, replacing the sort there was</li>\n<li><code>sort(arg, { add: true })</code> - add the field to the sort there is, after the fields there are.\nA field that is sorted on already gets the new direction. The grid does this on shift+click.</li>\n<li><code>sort([a, b])</code> - sort on these fields, replacing the sort there was (<code>add</code> is ignored)</li>\n<li><code>sort()</code> - sort again with the current sort</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>args</code> the field and direction, or a list of them</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.sort({ attribute: 'company', ascending: true });\ndatasource.sort({ attribute: 'age', ascending: false }, { add: true }); // company, then age\ndatasource.sort([\n    { attribute: 'country', ascending: true },\n    { attribute: 'company', ascending: false }\n]);</code></pre>\n","samples":["sorting-grouping"]},{"name":"undo","signatures":["undo(): boolean"],"doc":"<p>Takes the last step of the undo history back: the values it changed get the values they had\nbefore, a row it marked for deletion is unmarked (and the other way round). The grid does it\nwith Ctrl+Z (Cmd+Z), and from its row menu.</p>\n<p><strong>What a step is</strong>: the changes made in one go - what the user typed in one cell until the focus\nleft it, a paste or a clear over the selected rows, a <code>markForDeletion()</code> call, a revert, or what\ncode sets on the rows in one synchronous run (no <code>await</code> in between). Edits from code are\nrecorded too, they are edits like the user&#39;s. New rows (<code>addNewEmpty()</code>, <code>setData(rows, { add: true })</code>) are not in the history: undo never removes or adds a row. The last 100 steps are kept.</p>\n<p>The values are set as an edit sets them: the edit tracking follows (a value back at its original\nis no edit any more) and so does the validation. The displayed rows are not rebuilt - no filter,\nsort or grouping runs, the rows stay where they are - and <code>history-changed</code> is sent with\n<code>info: &#39;undo&#39;</code>, on which the grid renders its cells again. The history is the data container&#39;s,\nshared by the datasources on it.</p>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> <code>false</code> when there is nothing to undo</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const row = datasource.getDataRows()[0];\nrow.name = 'Changed';\n\ndatasource.undo(); // true: the name it had\ndatasource.redo(); // true: 'Changed' again\ndatasource.undo();\ndatasource.undo(); // false, nothing left to undo</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"unmarkAllForDeletion","signatures":["unmarkAllForDeletion(): void"],"doc":"<p>Takes the mark off every row marked for deletion, see <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">unmarkForDeletion</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.markAllForDeletion();\ndatasource.unmarkAllForDeletion();\ndatasource.getMarkedForDeletion(); // []</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"unmarkForDeletion","signatures":["unmarkForDeletion(rows: Entity | Entity[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Undoes a delete: takes the mark of <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">markForDeletion</a> off rows again. A row is back as it\nwas before it was marked - with its edits, and a new row as a new row. Unlike <code>resetData()</code>, no\nedit is undone. A step of the undo history, like <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">markForDeletion</a>.</p>\n<p>Sends <code>collection-filtered</code> with <code>info: &#39;unmarkForDeletion&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows, e.g. <code>getSelectedRows()</code>. Rows that are not marked are skipped</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const rows = datasource.getSelectedRows();\ndatasource.markForDeletion(rows);\ndatasource.unmarkForDeletion(rows); // as they were</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"upsert","signatures":["upsert(rows: Partial<T>[], options?: UpsertOptions): UpsertResult<T>"],"doc":"<p>Merges rows from a server into the data by their key: for polling, or for changes a server\npushes. Needs a key (<code>new Datasource({ key: &#39;id&#39; })</code>).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A row whose key is in the data</strong> gets the values of the fields the incoming row has, as the\nserver&#39;s values: the value and its original - the row is not edited by them. A field the\nincoming row does not have stays as it is. Not a step of the undo history; the fields are\nvalidated as for an edit.</li>\n<li><strong>A field the user has edited</strong> keeps the user&#39;s value. The server&#39;s value becomes its original,\nso <code>getChanges()</code> sends the user&#39;s value as an edit of what the server has now. When the server\nchanged the field too, it is a conflict (see <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">getConflicts</a>); when the server has the\nuser&#39;s value, the edit is done - not edited any more. A cell the user is typing in counts as\nedited: it is never overwritten.</li>\n<li><strong>A row marked for deletion</strong> gets the values too, and keeps its mark.</li>\n<li><strong>A key that is not in the data</strong>: the row is added, a loaded row (not new, not edited) - the\nobject itself, as <code>setData()</code> adds it.</li>\n<li><strong>A new row</strong> (<code>addNewEmpty()</code>) is not on the server: its key is a generated one, it never matches.</li>\n<li><strong><code>removeMissing</code></strong>: the rows whose key is not among the rows are removed for good (their changes\nleave the undo history) - not a new row, and not a row with changes of the user&#39;s (edits, a\ndeletion mark, a cell being typed in): that one stays, in conflict (<code>field: null</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The keys are compared as text: <code>7</code> and <code>&#39;7&#39;</code> are the same key. The key field is never written. A\nkey given twice: the second row updates what the first one added or updated.</p>\n<p>Then the displayed rows are rebuilt once - filtered (see <code>refilter</code>, and <code>filterChangedOnly()</code>),\nsorted, grouped. The selection (it follows the key), the expanded groups and the grid&#39;s scroll\nposition stay; a removed row leaves the selection, and <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">currentEntity</a> is set to <code>null</code>\nwhen it is removed. <code>collection-changed</code> (<code>info: &#39;upsert&#39;</code>) is sent once when rows were added or\nremoved or the displayed rows changed - not when only values changed: the grid renders those\nfrom <code>rows-changed</code>, which follows in a microtask with the rows changed, then <code>conflicts-changed</code>\nwhen the conflicts changed.</p>\n<p>Cheap on many rows: one look up per row, by its key. The rows of the other datasources on the same\ncontainer are merged too, call <code>reloadDatasource()</code> on them to show it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> the server&#39;s rows, plain objects: each with its key, and the fields sent</li>\n<li><code>options</code> <code>removeMissing</code> and <code>refilter</code>, see <a href=\"#api/index.UpsertOptions\">UpsertOptions</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the rows added, updated and removed, and the conflicts it made, see <a href=\"#api/index.UpsertResult\">UpsertResult</a></p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when the datasource has no key, <code>rows</code> is no array, or a row has no key\n(blank) - checked first, nothing is merged then</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ninterface Stock {\n    id: number;\n    name: string;\n    price: number;\n}\ndeclare function fetchStocks(): Promise&lt;Stock[]&gt;;\n\nconst stocks = new Datasource&lt;Stock&gt;({ key: 'id', fields: { price: 'number' } });\nstocks.setData(await fetchStocks());\n\n// every second the rows the server has: gone there is gone here, unless it has changes here\nsetInterval(async () =&gt; {\n    stocks.upsert(await fetchStocks(), { removeMissing: true });\n}, 1000);\n\n// one value pushed by the server: only the fields sent change\nstocks.upsert([{ id: 7, price: 12.5 }]);</code></pre>\n","samples":["live-data"]},{"name":"validate","signatures":["validate(rows?: Entity | Entity[]): ValidationError<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>Validates the rows: every field that has rules (<code>FieldConfig.validate</code>), of every row or of the\nrows given. Call it before a save - the edits are validated as they are made, but a field that\nwas never edited (an empty field of a new row, say) only here.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The rows marked for deletion are skipped</strong>: they are not saved, they have no errors.</li>\n<li><strong>Every row is checked</strong>, also a row the filter leaves out and a row that was not edited. To\ncheck only what a save sends, pass the new and edited rows (see the example).</li>\n<li><strong>The errors are kept</strong>: <code>getErrors()</code> and <code>hasErrors()</code> read them, and the grid shows them on\nthe cells and the row selectors - this sends <code>validate</code>, the grid renders its rows again. A\nfield that passes loses its error. <code>acceptChanges()</code> and <code>resetData()</code> clear them.</li>\n<li>The server&#39;s errors (<code>setErrors()</code>, <code>__rowError</code>) are apart: not checked, not returned.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The errors are those of the data container, so of every datasource sharing it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows, default every row</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the errors, one entry per field with an error: the rows in the order of the data, the\nfields in the order they are listed in <code>fields</code>. <code>[]</code> when every row is valid</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst people = new Datasource({\n    key: 'id',\n    fields: { name: { validate: ['required'] }, age: { type: 'number', validate: [{ id: 'min', value: 0 }] } }\n});\npeople.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann', age: 36 }]);\npeople.addNewEmpty({ age: -1 }); // not validated yet\n\nconst errors = people.validate();\n// [{ row: &lt;the new row&gt;, field: 'name', messages: ['Required'] },\n//  { row: &lt;the new row&gt;, field: 'age', messages: ['Must be at least 0'] }]\nif (errors.length === 0) {\n    await fetch('/api/people/save', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(people.getChanges()) });\n}\n\n// only what a save sends: the new and edited rows\npeople.validate(people.getChangedRows({ deleted: false }));</code></pre>\n","samples":["validation"]}]}]},{"name":"DateElement","group":"Classes","kind":"Class","signatures":["class DateElement extends HTMLElement"],"doc":"<p>The <code>&lt;simple-html-date&gt;</code> element: shows the date picker or calendar of the <a href=\"#api/index.DateInterface\">DateInterface</a>\nconnected to it. Create it, connect an interface and put it on the page. Give it the\n<code>simple-html-date</code> class for the styles of <code>@simple-html/grid/date.css</code>.</p>\n<p>Removing it from the page unsubscribes the interface&#39;s <code>on()</code> handlers.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type DateElement, DateInterface, type IDateConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: IDateConfig;\n\nconst element = document.createElement('simple-html-date') as DateElement;\nelement.classList.add('simple-html-date');\nelement.connectInterface(new DateInterface(config));\nhost.appendChild(element);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Methods","members":[{"name":"connectedCallback","signatures":["connectedCallback(): void"],"doc":"<p>Called by the browser when the element is put on the page: renders the connected interface. Not for\ncalling yourself.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"connectInterface","signatures":["connectInterface(dateInterface: DateInterface): void"],"doc":"<p>Shows a date interface in this element, and renders it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>dateInterface</code> the date picker or calendar to show</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type DateElement, DateInterface, type IDateConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: IDateConfig;\n\nconst element = document.createElement('simple-html-date') as DateElement;\nelement.connectInterface(new DateInterface(config));\nhost.appendChild(element);</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"disconnectedCallback","signatures":["disconnectedCallback(): void"],"doc":"<p>Called by the browser when the element is removed from the page: disconnects the interface and\nunsubscribes its <code>on()</code> handlers. Not for calling yourself.</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"DateInterface","group":"Classes","kind":"Class","signatures":["class DateInterface"],"doc":"<p>A date picker, a range picker or a calendar: its config, the selected dates and the <code>date-select</code> and\n<code>range-select</code> events. It is shown in a <code>&lt;simple-html-date&gt;</code> element (<a href=\"#api/index.DateElement\">DateElement</a>). The grid uses\none for its date cells and date header filters; make one yourself for a date picker or calendar outside\na grid. See <a href=\"#api/index.IDateConfig\">IDateConfig</a> for the modes.</p>\n<p>Import <code>@simple-html/grid/date.css</code> for its styles. <code>@simple-html/grid/theme-tredespace.css</code> gives it\nthe TreDeSpace theme too, under <code>data-grid-theme=&quot;tredespace&quot;</code> (see the theming guide).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type DateElement, DateInterface, type IDateConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\nimport '@simple-html/grid/date.css';\n\ndeclare const config: IDateConfig; // see IDateConfig, with datepicker: true\n\nconst dateInterface = new DateInterface(config);\nconst element = document.createElement('simple-html-date') as DateElement;\nelement.classList.add('simple-html-date');\nelement.connectInterface(dateInterface);\nhost.appendChild(element);\n\ndateInterface.on('date-select', (date) =&gt; {\n    console.log(date ? date.toISOString() : 'cleared');\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Constructors","members":[{"name":"constructor","signatures":["new DateInterface(config: IDateConfig): DateInterface"],"doc":"<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>config</code> what to show, see <a href=\"#api/index.IDateConfig\">IDateConfig</a>. Not copied: a date picker sets the start\nmonth and year, the time and <code>datepickerDate</code> in it</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface, type IDateConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: IDateConfig;\nconst dateInterface = new DateInterface({ ...config, datepicker: false, monthsToShow: 3, monthColumns: 3 });</code></pre>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"config","signatures":["config: IDateConfig"],"doc":"<p>The config. The picker replaces it with a changed copy when the month or time changes\n(<code>nextMonth()</code>, <code>gotoNow()</code> ...), so read it here, not from the object you passed in.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"element","signatures":["element?: DateElement | null"],"doc":"<p>The element it is shown in: <code>undefined</code> until connected, <code>null</code> after the element left the page.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"lastSelected","signatures":["lastSelected: Date | null"],"doc":"<p>The day clicked last, the start of a shift+click range. <code>null</code> after a day was clicked off again.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"selected","signatures":["selected: Set<number>"],"doc":"<p>The selected dates, as timestamps (<code>date.getTime()</code>: the day at 00:00 for a day clicked in a\ncalendar, the picked time in a date picker, From and To in a range picker). A day is shown selected\nwhen a timestamp falls on it, whatever its time. Read it with <a href=\"#api/index.DateInterface\">getSelected</a>, set it with\n<a href=\"#api/index.DateInterface\">setSelected</a>.</p>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Methods","members":[{"name":"checkDatePicker","signatures":["checkDatePicker(): void"],"doc":"<p>Called when the element connects: in a date picker it sets the start month and year, the hour and\nthe minutes from <code>datepickerDate</code> (today when it is blank) and selects that date. In a range picker\nit makes <code>datepickerRange</code> days (see <a href=\"#api/index.IDateConfig\">IDateConfig.datepickerRange</a>), shows the month of From\nand selects From and To. Does nothing in a calendar. You do not need to call it.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"clearSelection","signatures":["clearSelection(): void"],"doc":"<p>Unselects every day and renders the picker again. In a range picker From and To too: the range\npicked is <code>[null, null]</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\ndateInterface.clearSelection();\ndateInterface.getSelected(); // []</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"connectElement","signatures":["connectElement(element: DateElement): void"],"doc":"<p>Called by the element when it is put on the page: renders the picker in it. You do not need to call\nit.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>element</code> the <code>&lt;simple-html-date&gt;</code> element</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"connectGridInterface","signatures":["connectGridInterface(element: DateElement): void"],"doc":"<p>Called by <code>element.connectInterface()</code>: shows the picker in the element. You do not need to call it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>element</code> the <code>&lt;simple-html-date&gt;</code> element</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"disconnectElement","signatures":["disconnectElement(): void"],"doc":"<p>Called by the element when it is removed from the page: forgets the element and unsubscribes every\nhandler subscribed with <a href=\"#api/index.DateInterface\">on</a>. You do not need to call it.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getSelected","signatures":["getSelected(): number[]"],"doc":"<p>The selected dates, as timestamps: the days clicked in a calendar (at 00:00), the date picked in a\ndate picker, the dates given to <a href=\"#api/index.DateInterface\">setSelected</a> (with their time). In the order they were\nselected.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\nconst dates = dateInterface.getSelected().map((time) =&gt; new Date(time));</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"gotoNow","signatures":["gotoNow(): void"],"doc":"<p>Goes to the current date and time: picks it, shows its month. What the date picker&#39;s &quot;Now&quot; button\ndoes. Does not send <code>date-select</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\ndateInterface.gotoNow();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"nextMonth","signatures":["nextMonth(): void"],"doc":"<p>Shows the next month, what the › button in the month header of a date picker does.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\ndateInterface.nextMonth();\ndateInterface.config.startMonth; // one later, 0 again after December</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"nextYear","signatures":["nextYear(): void"],"doc":"<p>Shows the same month a year later, what the » button in the month header of a date picker does.\nThe date picked stays as it is.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\ndateInterface.nextYear();\ndateInterface.config.startYear; // one later</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"on","signatures":["on<Type extends keyof DateEvents>(type: Type, handler: EventHandler<DateEvents[Type]>): () => void"],"doc":"<p>Subscribes to an event of the date picker. The handler gets the event&#39;s payload, typed\nfrom <a href=\"#api/index.DateEvents\">DateEvents</a> - see there for every event and what it sends.</p>\n<p>The handler stays subscribed until you call the function this returns, or the date element\nis removed from the dom. What the handler returns is ignored (in v5 it had to return <code>true</code>\nto stay subscribed).</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>type</code> the event name</li>\n<li><code>handler</code> called with the payload every time the event is sent</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> a function that unsubscribes the handler</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\nconst input = document.querySelector('input')!;\nconst off = dateInterface.on('date-select', (date) =&gt; {\n    input.value = date ? date.toLocaleString() : '';\n});\n\noff(); // unsubscribe</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"prevMonth","signatures":["prevMonth(): void"],"doc":"<p>Shows the month before, what the ‹ button in the month header of a date picker does.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\ndateInterface.prevMonth();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"prevYear","signatures":["prevYear(): void"],"doc":"<p>Shows the same month a year before, what the « button in the month header of a date picker does.\nThe date picked stays as it is.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\ndateInterface.prevYear();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"render","signatures":["render(): void"],"doc":"<p>Renders the picker in its element again. The methods that change what is shown call it; call it\nafter changing <code>config</code> yourself. Does nothing while no element is connected.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\ndateInterface.config.hideDimmedDates = true;\ndateInterface.render();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"selectRangeWithFromTo","signatures":["selectRangeWithFromTo(fromDate: Date, toDate: Date): void"],"doc":"<p>Not implemented: it only logs a warning.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>fromDate</code> the first date of the range</li>\n<li><code>toDate</code> the last date of the range</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"setSelected","signatures":["setSelected(newSelectedDates: Date[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Replaces the selected days and renders the picker again. A day is shown selected when one of the\ndates falls on it - the time of a date does not matter. They are kept as timestamps, see\n<a href=\"#api/index.DateInterface\">getSelected</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>newSelectedDates</code> the days to select</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\ndateInterface.setSelected([new Date(2026, 10, 20), new Date(2026, 10, 21, 9, 30)]);</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"styleRange","signatures":["styleRange(StyleArray: IStyle[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Not implemented: it only logs a warning.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>StyleArray</code> the dates to style, see <a href=\"#api/index.IStyle\">IStyle</a></li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"GridElement","group":"Classes","kind":"Class","signatures":["class GridElement extends HTMLElement"],"doc":"<p>The <code>&lt;simple-html-grid&gt;</code> element: shows the grid of the <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">GridInterface</a> connected to it.</p>\n<p><code>createGrid()</code> makes one for you, sized to fill a container, and is the easy way. Use the element\nyourself when you want to place and size it on your own: create it, connect an interface and add it\nto the page. It adds its <code>simple-html-grid</code> class itself; give it a size, e.g. width and height\n100% of a container with a height.</p>\n<p>Removing the element from the page disconnects the grid from the datasource and the document. Put\nback, it connects again and shows the rows as they are then.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type GridConfig, type GridElement, GridInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: GridConfig;\n\nconst element = document.createElement('simple-html-grid') as GridElement;\nelement.style.width = '100%';\nelement.style.height = '100%';\nelement.connectInterface(new GridInterface(config, datasource));\ndocument.getElementById('grid')!.appendChild(element);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Constructors","members":[{"name":"constructor","signatures":["new GridElement(): GridElement"],"doc":"<p>Made by <code>document.createElement(&#39;simple-html-grid&#39;)</code>, or <code>new GridElement()</code> - <code>createGrid()</code> does\nthat. Connect an interface with <a href=\"#api/index.GridElement\">connectInterface</a> before or after it is put on the page.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type GridConfig, GridElement, GridInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: GridConfig;\n\nconst element = new GridElement();\nelement.style.height = '400px';\nelement.connectInterface(new GridInterface(config, datasource));\nhost.appendChild(element);</code></pre>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Methods","members":[{"name":"connectInterface","signatures":["connectInterface(value: GridInterface<any>): void"],"doc":"<p>Shows a grid interface in this element: its config, its datasource and its state.</p>\n<p>Connecting another interface later replaces the first one, which is disconnected from its\ndatasource. The dom is kept, the grid is rebuilt for the new interface.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>value</code> the interface to show</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type GridConfig, type GridElement, GridInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: GridConfig;\n\nconst element = document.createElement('simple-html-grid') as GridElement;\nelement.connectInterface(new GridInterface(config, datasource));\nhost.appendChild(element);</code></pre>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"GridInterface","group":"Classes","kind":"Class","signatures":["class GridInterface<T>"],"doc":"<p>The grid: its config, its datasource and its state. What you call to work with a grid - read and\nset the state, change an option, subscribe to events, re-render.</p>\n<p>Make one with <a href=\"#api/index.createGrid\">createGrid</a>, which also puts the grid on the page. <code>new GridInterface()</code> is for\na <code>&lt;simple-html-grid&gt;</code> element you place yourself, see <a href=\"#api/index.GridElement\">GridElement</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of the rows, from the datasource: a <code>Datasource&lt;Person&gt;</code> gives a\n<code>GridInterface&lt;Person&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { createGrid, type GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: GridConfig;\n\nconst gridInterface = createGrid(document.getElementById('grid')!, { config, datasource });\n\ngridInterface.on('cell-click', (data) =&gt; console.log(data.attribute, data.rowData));\ngridInterface.updateConfig({ readonly: false });\ngridInterface.updateHooks({ cellClass: (row, field) =&gt; (field === 'age' &amp;&amp; row.age &lt; 18 ? { input: 'minor' } : null) });\nconst state = gridInterface.getState();\n\ngridInterface.destroy(); // done with it</code></pre>\n","samples":["basic-grid"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Constructors","members":[{"name":"constructor","signatures":["new GridInterface<T>(gridConfig: GridConfig, datasource: Datasource<T>, hooks?: GridHooks<T>): GridInterface<T>"],"doc":"<p>Most of the time <a href=\"#api/index.createGrid\">createGrid</a> makes the interface. Make it yourself for a\n<code>&lt;simple-html-grid&gt;</code> element you place on your own, and connect it with\n<code>element.connectInterface()</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of the rows, from the datasource: a <code>Datasource&lt;Person&gt;</code> gives a\n<code>GridInterface&lt;Person&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>gridConfig</code> the columns, the layout and the options, see <a href=\"#api/index.GridConfig\">GridConfig</a>. The object is\nnot changed, the grid copies the parts it changes</li>\n<li><code>datasource</code> the rows. The grid applies <code>gridConfig.initialState</code> to it: its sorting,\ngrouping and filter are replaced (left out, they are cleared). <code>null</code> is an option left out: the\ndefault - for the options of the grid, of a column and of its <code>format</code> (a config from a backend)</li>\n<li><code>hooks</code> optional: the functions - <code>isReadonly</code>, <code>cellClass</code>, <code>menus</code>, see <a href=\"#api/index.GridHooks\">GridHooks</a>.\nThe grid keeps a copy of the object, change them later with <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">updateHooks</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when <code>gridConfig</code> has <code>isReadonly</code>, <code>cellClass</code> or <code>menus</code> (those are\nhooks), a column has v5&#39;s <code>mandatory</code> (it is the field&#39;s <code>required</code> rule), <code>texts</code> is not an\nobject of strings, <code>multilineTooltipLines</code> or <code>multilineLineHeight</code> is not a whole number of 1 or\nmore, a column&#39;s <code>aggregate</code> is no aggregate function or needs a number field, a column&#39;s\n<code>format</code> does not fit its field (see <a href=\"#api/index.ColumnFormat\">ColumnFormat</a>), a column&#39;s <code>editor</code> is wrong - its\nlookup not registered, see <a href=\"#api/index.ColumnEditor\">ColumnEditor</a> - a column&#39;s <code>renderer</code> is not the id of a\nregistered cell renderer, or is given with an <code>editor</code>, or a column&#39;s <code>filterOperators</code>,\n<code>operator</code>, <code>filterCaseSensitive</code> or <code>datePresets</code> does not fit its type, see <a href=\"#api/index.ColumnConfig\">ColumnConfig</a> - when\n<code>detailForm</code> is not a <a href=\"#api/index.DetailForm\">DetailForm</a>, and when <code>edit</code> is not an object of the permissions\n<code>add</code>, <code>change</code> and <code>delete</code>, each true or false (see <a href=\"#api/index.EditPermissions\">EditPermissions</a>)</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type GridConfig, type GridElement, type GridHooks, GridInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: GridConfig;\ndeclare const hooks: GridHooks;\n\nconst gridInterface = new GridInterface(config, datasource, hooks);\nconst element = document.createElement('simple-html-grid') as GridElement;\nelement.connectInterface(gridInterface);\nhost.appendChild(element);</code></pre>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Methods","members":[{"name":"applyView","signatures":["applyView(id: string | null): void"],"doc":"<p>Shows a named view: applies its state, and it is the view shown (<a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">getCurrentView</a>) - as a\nclick on it in the views menu. What its <code>state</code> leaves out is the state the grid starts in\n(<code>GridConfig.initialState</code> and the config&#39;s <code>layout</code>): a view is all of the state, not a change of\nthe state shown. Applied again, it takes back what changed since.</p>\n<p><code>null</code> is &quot;Standard&quot;: the config&#39;s state, as <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">resetState</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>id</code> the view&#39;s <code>id</code>, see <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">getViews</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when no view has the id, and when its state does not fit the grid - aggregates\nor a display format of a field that is not of their type, a detail form that is none - as\n<code>setState()</code> throws, before anything changes</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.applyView('late'); // the view &quot;Late deliveries&quot;\ngridInterface.applyView(null); // Standard: the config's state</code></pre>\n","samples":["views"]},{"name":"autoResizeColumns","signatures":["autoResizeColumns(): void"],"doc":"<p>Fits every column to its content: the same as <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">fitColumns</a> without arguments.</p>\n<p><strong>Deprecated</strong> use <code>fitColumns()</code>. Before v6 it measured the values as they are stored, not as the\ncells show them, of every row - also the rows the filter hides</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"clearRanges","signatures":["clearRanges(): void"],"doc":"<p>Clears the ranges of cells: no cell is selected. Sends <code>range-change</code> when there were ranges.\nThe rows selected in the datasource stay selected.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>document.getElementById('clear-selection')!.onclick = () =&gt; gridInterface.clearRanges();</code></pre>\n","samples":["ranges"]},{"name":"closeFind","signatures":["closeFind(): void"],"doc":"<p>Closes the find bar, as Esc in it does: the cells are not marked any more. Its text is kept, Ctrl+F\nshows it again. &quot;Filter rows&quot; is turned off: every row the filter lets through is shown again. When\nthe focus was in the bar it goes to the cell of the current match. <code>find-change</code> is sent.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>document.getElementById('close-find')!.onclick = () =&gt; gridInterface.closeFind();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"closeMenu","signatures":["closeMenu(): void"],"doc":"<p>Closes the menu that is open: one opened with <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">openMenu</a>, or one of the grid&#39;s own right\nclick menus. Does nothing when no menu is open. The focus goes back as when the user closes it,\nsee <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">openMenu</a>.</p>\n<p>Replaces v5&#39;s <code>removeContextMenuElement()</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>// moving to another cell closes a dropdown opened from a cell\ngridInterface.on('cell-row-focus', () =&gt; gridInterface.closeMenu());</code></pre>\n","samples":["dropdown-grid"]},{"name":"deleteView","signatures":["deleteView(id: string): void"],"doc":"<p>Deletes a view - <em>Delete</em> in the views menu - and sends <code>views-change</code>. The view shown deleted, the\ngrid shows what it showed: no view is shown then (&quot;Standard&quot;, marked as changed), and <em>Save as new\nview…</em> still makes a view of it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>id</code> the view&#39;s <code>id</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when no view has the id, and when the view is <code>readonly</code></p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.deleteView('mine');</code></pre>\n","samples":["views"]},{"name":"destroy","signatures":["destroy(): void"],"doc":"<p>Removes the grid from the page and disconnects it: from the datasource, the document and the\nhandlers subscribed with <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">on</a>. For a grid made with <a href=\"#api/index.createGrid\">createGrid</a>, when you are done\nwith it. The datasource is not changed, it can be shown again in a new grid.</p>\n<p>The element is removed also when you placed it yourself (<code>element.connectInterface()</code>). Removing\nsuch an element from the page disconnects the grid as well: there <code>destroy()</code> is not needed.</p>\n<p>Do not use the interface after this: make a new one.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { createGrid, type GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: GridConfig;\n\nconst gridInterface = createGrid(host, { config, datasource });\n// ...\ngridInterface.destroy(); // host is empty again</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"downloadCsv","signatures":["downloadCsv(filename?: string, options?: CsvOptions): void"],"doc":"<p>Saves the rows as a CSV file: the browser downloads it, as from a link. The text is\n<a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">getCsv</a>&#39;s, with a UTF-8 byte order mark (BOM) first by default - Excel needs it to read\n<code>æøå</code> (<code>bom: false</code> leaves it out).</p>\n<p>For Excel in a locale with a decimal comma (Norwegian, German ...), use <code>separator: &#39;;&#39;</code>:\nExcel splits a .csv file on the list separator of the computer&#39;s locale, and with <code>&#39;,&#39;</code> every\nrow ends up in one column.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>filename</code> the name the file is saved as, default <code>&#39;export.csv&#39;</code>. Give it the <code>.csv</code>\nending yourself, it is not added</li>\n<li><code>options</code> what to export and how, see <a href=\"#api/index.CsvOptions\">CsvOptions</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when the filename is not a text (<code>downloadCsv({ rows: &#39;selected&#39; })</code>: the\nfilename comes first), for an option it does not know or a value an option does not take</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>document.getElementById('export')!.onclick = () =&gt; gridInterface.downloadCsv();\n\n// the selected rows, for Excel in Norway\ngridInterface.downloadCsv('selected.csv', { rows: 'selected', separator: ';' });</code></pre>\n","samples":["export"]},{"name":"downloadExcel","signatures":["downloadExcel(filename?: string, options?: ExcelOptions): Promise<void>"],"doc":"<p>Saves the rows as an Excel file (.xlsx): the browser downloads it, as from a link. The file is\n<a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">getExcel</a>&#39;s. The row menu&#39;s <em>Excel, all rows</em> and <em>Excel, selected rows</em> call this.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>filename</code> the name the file is saved as, default <code>&#39;export.xlsx&#39;</code>. Give it the <code>.xlsx</code>\nending yourself, it is not added</li>\n<li><code>options</code> what to export, see <a href=\"#api/index.ExcelOptions\">ExcelOptions</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> a promise that is fulfilled once the download is started</p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> (the promise rejects with) a <code>TypeError</code> when the filename is not a text\n(<code>downloadExcel({ rows: &#39;selected&#39; })</code>: the filename comes first), for an option it does not\nknow or a value an option does not take</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>document.getElementById('export')!.onclick = () =&gt; gridInterface.downloadExcel();\n\n// the selected rows, on a sheet named Orders\nawait gridInterface.downloadExcel('orders.xlsx', { rows: 'selected', sheetName: 'Orders' });</code></pre>\n","samples":["export"]},{"name":"exportConfig","signatures":["exportConfig(): ExportedGrid"],"doc":"<p>The grid as plain JSON, to save and give back to <code>importConfig()</code>: <code>{ version, config, state, views }</code></p>\n<ul>\n<li>the version of the format (<a href=\"#api/index.GRID_CONFIG_VERSION\">GRID_CONFIG_VERSION</a>), the config as the app gave it (the\nconstructor&#39;s, with what <code>updateConfig()</code> changed since), <code>getState()</code> - what the user did with it -\nand the named views (<code>getViews()</code>: the config&#39;s and the ones the user saved with the views button,\nleft out when there are none). The hooks and the datasource are not in it. See <a href=\"#api/index.ExportedGrid\">ExportedGrid</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>localStorage.setItem('my-grid', JSON.stringify(gridInterface.exportConfig()));\n// { &quot;version&quot;: 2, &quot;config&quot;: { &quot;layout&quot;: ..., &quot;columns&quot;: ... }, &quot;state&quot;: { &quot;sorting&quot;: [] ... } }</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"fillDown","signatures":["fillDown(): void"],"doc":"<p>Fill down, as Ctrl+D (Cmd+D) in a cell does: in every range the values of its top row go into the\nrows under it, a range of one row gets the values of the data row above it. Without a range, the\ncell with the focus gets the value of the cell above it. The values are copied as they are; cells\nthat can not be edited are skipped (the grid&#39;s <code>readonly</code>, the column&#39;s, the <code>isReadonly</code> hook),\ngroup rows have no cells. One step of the undo history. See the guide &quot;Selection and clipboard&quot;.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>// the status of the first row into the next four\ngridInterface.setRanges([{ fromRow: 0, fromField: 'status', toRow: 4, toField: 'status' }]);\ngridInterface.fillDown();</code></pre>\n","samples":["ranges"]},{"name":"find","signatures":["find(text: string, options?: { caseSensitive?: boolean; filterRows?: boolean }): number"],"doc":"<p>Finds a text in the cells, as Ctrl+F in the grid does: opens the find bar with the text, marks\nevery cell that shows it and scrolls to the current match. See <a href=\"#api/index.FindResult\">FindResult</a> for what a\nmatch is and their order - the text a cell shows, formatted, in any case (or as it is, with\n<code>caseSensitive</code>).</p>\n<p>The current match is the first one at or after the cell that has the focus (or the first one);\nwhile the bar is open, the current match stays while it still matches, else it is the next one.\nThe focus does not move: <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">openFind</a> puts it in the bar, as Ctrl+F does. <code>find-change</code> is\nsent. Does nothing while the grid is not on the page.</p>\n<p><strong><code>filterRows</code></strong> turns &quot;Filter rows&quot; of the find bar on or off, as its toggle does: only the rows\nwith a match are shown - on top of the filter, not part of it (<code>getFilter()</code> and the state do not\nhave it, nor <code>getServerFilter()</code>: it filters in the browser, also rows set later). Left out, it stays as it is. It is turned\noff when the bar closes (<a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">closeFind</a>, Esc), and by the footer&#39;s Clear. See\n<a href=\"#api/index.FindResult\">FindResult.filterRows</a>.</p>\n<p><strong><code>caseSensitive</code></strong> turns &quot;Match case&quot; of the find bar on or off, as its toggle <code>Aa</code> does: the\ntext is found as it is - <code>Acme</code> does not find <code>ACME</code>. The matches, the count and &quot;Filter rows&quot;\nfollow it. Left out, it stays as it is; it is kept when the bar closes. See\n<a href=\"#api/index.FindResult\">FindResult.caseSensitive</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>text</code> the text to find. <code>&#39;&#39;</code> opens the bar with no matches (and every row)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> how many cells show the text</p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when the text is not a string</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const count = gridInterface.find('acme');\nconsole.log(`${count} cells`, gridInterface.getFind().current); // { row: 3, field: 'company' }\ngridInterface.findNext();\n\n// only the rows with a cell that shows &quot;acme&quot;, then every row again with the bar still open\ngridInterface.find('acme', { filterRows: true });\ngridInterface.find('acme', { filterRows: false });\n\n// &quot;Acme&quot; as it is: not &quot;ACME&quot; or &quot;acme&quot;\ngridInterface.find('Acme', { caseSensitive: true });\ngridInterface.closeFind();</code></pre>\n","samples":["find"]},{"name":"findNext","signatures":["findNext(): { field: string; row: number } | null"],"doc":"<p>Goes to the next match, as Enter and F3 in the find bar: it is the current one, the grid scrolls\nto it. After the last one, the first. Nothing while the find bar is closed or nothing matches.</p>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the cell of the current match - its row in the displayed rows and its field - or <code>null</code></p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.find('norway');\nconst cell = gridInterface.findNext(); // { row: 12, field: 'country' }</code></pre>\n","samples":["find"]},{"name":"findPrevious","signatures":["findPrevious(): { field: string; row: number } | null"],"doc":"<p>Goes to the previous match, as Shift+Enter and Shift+F3 in the find bar. Before the first one, the\nlast. See <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">findNext</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the cell of the current match, or <code>null</code></p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.find('norway');\ngridInterface.findPrevious(); // the last match: the first one comes before it</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"fitColumns","signatures":["fitColumns(fields?: string[], options?: { rows?: EntityUnion<T>[] }): void"],"doc":"<p>Fits the width of columns to their content, like Excel&#39;s AutoFit: each column as wide as the\nwidest text of its fields - for a column with stacked fields the widest of them, every line of a\nmultiline text - and its header label. At least 25px, at most 750px. Then rebuilds the grid. A\ncolumn with nothing to measure keeps its width. The user does the same from the header menu\n(&quot;Fit column width&quot;, &quot;Fit all columns&quot;) and with a double click on a column&#39;s resize handle.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The text</strong> is what the cells show: formatted, with <code>numberOverride</code>. A checkbox cell needs\nthe room of its checkbox. By default the rows the filter lets through (the rows of collapsed\ngroups too), and the header label.</li>\n<li><strong>Measured</strong> with the grid&#39;s font (the labels with theirs) on a canvas: the 20 longest texts of\neach field, by their number of characters - every text of 100 000 rows would take the browser\nhalf a second per field. The widest text is one of the longest, unless a short text of wide\nletters is wider than 20 longer ones of narrow letters.</li>\n<li><strong><code>options.rows</code></strong>: only the text of these rows, and not the header label - a column fitted to\ncells, as the row menu&#39;s &quot;Fit column to this cell&quot; does.</li>\n<li>The widths are part of the state (<code>getState().layout</code>). <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">resetColumnWidths</a> goes back to\nthe widths of the config.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Measures with the grid&#39;s font, so call it once the grid is on the page: right after\n<a href=\"#api/index.createGrid\">createGrid</a>, or from a <code>grid-connected</code> handler for an element you connect yourself. It\ndoes nothing before the interface is connected to an element.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>fields</code> the columns that show one of these fields, every column when left out. A field\nthat is not in the layout is skipped</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when <code>fields</code> is not an array of field names, or <code>options.rows</code> not an array</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { createGrid, type GridConfig, isGroupRow } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: GridConfig;\n\nconst gridInterface = createGrid(host, { config, datasource });\ngridInterface.fitColumns(); // every column\ngridInterface.fitColumns(['name', 'notes']); // the columns of these fields\n\n// the name column as wide as the name of the current row\nconst row = datasource.currentEntity;\nif (row &amp;&amp; !isGroupRow(row)) {\n    gridInterface.fitColumns(['name'], { rows: [row] });\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["multiline","misc-options"]},{"name":"fitRows","signatures":["fitRows(rows?: EntityUnion<T> | EntityUnion<T>[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Makes rows as high as their multiline cells need to show every line, like Excel&#39;s AutoFit of a\nrow: each row as many lines as its tallest column needs - a multiline cell the lines of its text\n(the empty lines at its end left out), every other cell one line, the fields of a column with\nstacked fields added up. At most 20 lines. A row that needs no more lines than the layout gives a\nrow goes back to that height. The user does the same from the row menu: &quot;Fit row height&quot;, &quot;Fit\nall rows&quot;.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><strong>The height</strong>: the lines of the layout&#39;s row are <code>cellHeight</code> px each, every line more is a\nline of text, <code>multilineLineHeight</code> px (default 15): the lines of a note read as a paragraph. A\nrow of one field with a note of three lines is <code>cellHeight + 2 * multilineLineHeight</code> px, 52 by\ndefault.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>Cheap</strong>: it counts the line breaks of the cells&#39; text, nothing is measured. A long line is\nnot wrapped, it is cut at the cell&#39;s edge as in a row of one line.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>In a taller row</strong> a multiline cell shows as many of its lines as it has room for, the marker\nwhen there are more. Every other cell has its text on the first line. The editor of a\nmultiline cell is the same.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>Kept by the row&#39;s key</strong> (<code>__KEY</code>: the datasource&#39;s <code>key</code> field, or the key it generated), so\na row keeps its height through a sort, a filter, grouping and new data with the same keys\n(<code>setData()</code>, <code>upsert()</code>). A row whose text changes keeps its height: fit it again.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>Not part of the state</strong> (<code>getState()</code>): the heights belong to the rows loaded now.\n<a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">resetRowHeights</a> takes them back.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Works before the grid is on the page too.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> the rows to fit, a row or a list. Left out: the rows the filter lets through (the\nrows of collapsed groups too) - and the heights of rows that are no longer in the data are\ndropped. Group rows are skipped</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when <code>rows</code> is not a row or an array of rows</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { isGroupRow } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ngridInterface.fitRows(); // every row the filter lets through\ngridInterface.fitRows(datasource.getSelectedRows());\n\nconst row = datasource.currentEntity;\nif (row &amp;&amp; !isGroupRow(row)) {\n    gridInterface.fitRows(row);\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["multiline"]},{"name":"getCsv","signatures":["getCsv(options?: CsvOptions): string"],"doc":"<p>The rows as CSV text (RFC 4180): a header line with the column labels, then a line per row,\nevery line ended with CRLF. By default every row the filter lets through, in the sort order, and\nthe columns of the layout in the order the user sees them, each value as the grid shows it. See\n<a href=\"#api/index.CsvOptions\">CsvOptions</a> for what can be changed: the selected rows, the selected range of cells, the\nfields, the separator (<code>&#39;;&#39;</code> for Excel in Norway), raw values ...</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The rows</strong>: when grouped, every data row in the grouped order - the rows of collapsed groups\ntoo, no group rows. Rows marked for deletion are rows of the grid until they are saved, they\nare exported too.</li>\n<li><strong>Formulas</strong>: text starting with <code>=</code>, <code>+</code>, <code>-</code>, <code>@</code> ... gets a <code>&#39;</code> in front, so a spreadsheet\ndoes not run a formula a user typed in (<code>escapeFormulas</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>No BOM</strong> by default, unlike <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">downloadCsv</a>: the text is for code of your own.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Works without the grid on the page too: it reads the config and the datasource.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>options</code> what to export and how, see <a href=\"#api/index.CsvOptions\">CsvOptions</a>. Every option is optional</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the CSV text, <code>&#39;&#39;</code> when there are no columns</p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> for an option it does not know or a value an option does not take\n(<code>rows: &#39;some&#39;</code>)</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const text = gridInterface.getCsv(); // 'Name,Born\\r\\nAnn,2001-05-17\\r\\n...'\n\n// the selected rows, semicolons for Excel in Norway, the values as they are stored\nconst selected = gridInterface.getCsv({ rows: 'selected', separator: ';', formatted: false });\n\n// two fields, no header line\nconst names = gridInterface.getCsv({ fields: ['name', 'email'], header: false });\n\n// the cells of the range the user selected, see getRanges()\nconst range = gridInterface.getCsv({ rows: 'range' });</code></pre>\n","samples":["export"]},{"name":"getCurrentView","signatures":["getCurrentView(): GridView | null"],"doc":"<p>The named view the grid shows: the one applied last (the views menu, <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">applyView</a>, the\ndefault view when the grid was made) or saved last. A copy, null when none is - &quot;Standard&quot; in the\nviews menu, the config&#39;s state: after <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">resetState</a>, and when the view shown was deleted.</p>\n<p>A change of the state after it - a filter, a column resized, <code>setState()</code> - keeps it the view shown:\n<a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">isViewModified</a> says the state is not the view&#39;s any more.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const view = gridInterface.getCurrentView();\nconsole.log(view ? `${view.name}${gridInterface.isViewModified() ? ' *' : ''}` : 'Standard');</code></pre>\n","samples":["views"]},{"name":"getDatasource","signatures":["getDatasource(): Datasource<T>"],"doc":"<p>The datasource the grid shows: its rows, selection, sorting, filter and the events for them.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const datasource = gridInterface.getDatasource();\ndatasource.on('selection-change', () =&gt; console.log(datasource.getSelectedRows().length, 'selected'));</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getExcel","signatures":["getExcel(options?: ExcelOptions): Promise<Blob>"],"doc":"<p>The rows as an Excel workbook (.xlsx), a Blob: one sheet with a header row of the column labels\n(bold, frozen, with an autofilter over it and every row), then a row per data row. By default\nevery row the filter lets through, in the sort order, and the columns of the layout in the\norder the user sees them, as wide as in the grid. See <a href=\"#api/index.ExcelOptions\">ExcelOptions</a> for what can be\nchanged: the selected rows, the selected range of cells, the fields, the sheet name, the colours.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Typed cells</strong>, so Excel can sum, sort and filter: a number field gives numbers, a date or\ndatetime field Excel dates (the local date and time the grid shows), a boolean field TRUE /\nFALSE, text text - with wrapped lines when it has a line break. A value that is not of its\nfield&#39;s type (text in a number field) is written as the text the cell shows. Blanks are empty\ncells.</li>\n<li><strong>A flat list</strong>: when grouped, every data row in the grouped order - the rows of collapsed\ngroups too - and no group rows, no outline, no totals. Rows marked for deletion are rows of the\ngrid until they are saved, they are exported too.</li>\n<li><strong>No formulas</strong>: text is never a formula in an .xlsx file, a value a user typed\n(<code>=HYPERLINK(...)</code>) shows as the text it is.</li>\n<li><strong>The colours and formats of the columns</strong>: a display format as an Excel number format, a colour\nrule&#39;s text colour, background and bold as the cell&#39;s own, a data bar, colour scale and icon set\nas Excel&#39;s own conditional formatting - in the light look. <code>colors: false</code> leaves the colours out.</li>\n<li><strong>The values when called</strong>: the rows and values are read before the promise is returned, the\nfile is zipped after (with the browser&#39;s <code>CompressionStream</code>, so this is async).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Works without the grid on the page too: it reads the config and the datasource.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>options</code> what to export, see <a href=\"#api/index.ExcelOptions\">ExcelOptions</a>. Every option is optional</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the .xlsx file, of the type <code>application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet</code></p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> (the promise rejects with) a <code>TypeError</code> for an option it does not know or a value an\noption does not take (<code>rows: &#39;some&#39;</code>, a sheet name Excel does not take), a <code>RangeError</code> for more\nrows (1 048 576 with the header) or columns (16 384) than an Excel sheet holds</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>// the file, for code of your own: upload it, attach it to a mail ...\nconst blob = await gridInterface.getExcel();\nawait fetch('/api/reports', { method: 'POST', body: blob });\n\n// the selected rows, two fields, on a sheet named People\nconst people = await gridInterface.getExcel({ rows: 'selected', fields: ['name', 'born'], sheetName: 'People' });\n\n// the cells the user selected (the last range of cells)\nconst cells = await gridInterface.getExcel({ rows: 'range' });\n\n// the values without the grid's colours\nconst plain = await gridInterface.getExcel({ colors: false });</code></pre>\n","samples":["export"]},{"name":"getFind","signatures":["getFind(): FindResult"],"doc":"<p>What Find has found now: whether the bar is open, its text, whether &quot;Filter rows&quot; and &quot;Match case&quot;\nare on, how many cells match and the current match, see <a href=\"#api/index.FindResult\">FindResult</a>. A copy. The\n<code>find-change</code> event sends the same each time it changes.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const { open, count, position, filterRows, caseSensitive } = gridInterface.getFind();\nif (open) {\n    console.log(count ? `${position} of ${count}` : 'no matches', filterRows ? '(rows filtered)' : '');\n    console.log(caseSensitive ? 'match case' : 'any case');\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getHiddenFields","signatures":["getHiddenFields(): string[]"],"doc":"<p>The fields the grid knows that are not in the layout now: the ones the column chooser can add\nback. The grid knows the keys of <code>GridConfig.columns</code>, and every field that has been in the\nlayout.</p>\n<p>Was <code>getOptionalAttributes()</code> in v5.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { createGrid } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst gridInterface = createGrid(host, {\n    config: { columns: { phone: {} }, layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 100 }] } },\n    datasource\n});\ngridInterface.getHiddenFields(); // ['phone']</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getLayoutFields","signatures":["getLayoutFields(options?: { selectedOnly?: boolean }): string[]"],"doc":"<p>The fields in the layout now, in the order the user sees them: pinned left, center, pinned right,\nleft to right, and top to bottom within a column of stacked fields.</p>\n<p>With <code>selectedOnly</code>, only the fields of the columns the user selected - by clicking the column\nnumbers under the header filters, Ctrl/Cmd+click for more, Shift+click for the ones between, see\n<a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">getSelectedColumns</a>. None selected gives <code>[]</code>.</p>\n<p>Was <code>getAttributeColumns(filterSelectedColumns)</code> in v5, which gave the selected columns by default\nand every column when none was selected.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.getLayoutFields(); // ['name', 'age', 'born', 'company']\ngridInterface.getLayoutFields({ selectedOnly: true }); // ['age', 'born'] - one column, two fields\n\n// the selected columns, or every column when none is selected\nconst selected = gridInterface.getLayoutFields({ selectedOnly: true });\nconst toExport = selected.length ? selected : gridInterface.getLayoutFields();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getRanges","signatures":["getRanges(): CellRange[]"],"doc":"<p>The ranges of cells the user selected - by dragging over the cells, Shift+click, Ctrl/Cmd+click\nfor another one, Alt+Shift+arrows - or that <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">setRanges</a> set. See <a href=\"#api/index.CellRange\">CellRange</a>: rows\nare indexes in the displayed rows, fields are field names. The last range is the one made last,\nits <code>fromRow</code> / <code>fromField</code> is the active cell. <code>[]</code> when no cells are selected.</p>\n<p>Copies: changing them changes nothing in the grid.</p>\n<p>The ranges are cleared when the displayed rows change - a filter, a sort, grouping, a group\nexpanded or collapsed, rows added or removed (<code>setData()</code>, <code>upsert()</code> that adds or removes\nrows, rows marked for deletion) - and when the fields of the layout change: a column moved,\npinned, hidden or added. A column resized keeps them, and so does an edit: the rows stay where\nthey are. <code>range-change</code> is sent every time they change.</p>\n<p>The row selection of the datasource (<code>datasource.getSelectedRows()</code>) is something else: a\nrange does not select rows, selecting rows changes no range.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const ranges = gridInterface.getRanges();\nif (ranges.length) {\n    const { fromRow, fromField, toRow, toField } = ranges[ranges.length - 1];\n    console.log(`from row ${fromRow} ${fromField} to row ${toRow} ${toField}`);\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["ranges"]},{"name":"getSelectedColumns","signatures":["getSelectedColumns(): number[]"],"doc":"<p>The columns the user selected, by their numbers: the row of numbers under the header filters,\n1 based, counted across the pinned left, the center and the pinned right columns - a column of\nstacked fields is one number. A click on a number selects that column, Ctrl/Cmd+click adds or\nremoves one, Shift+click selects the columns from the one clicked before, as on the row numbers.\nAscending, <code>[]</code> when none is selected. <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">getLayoutFields</a> with <code>selectedOnly</code> gives their\nfields.</p>\n<p>The numbers are good for the layout they were selected in: the selection is cleared when the\nfields of the layout change - a column moved, pinned, hidden or added - and\n<code>column-selection-change</code> is sent. A column resized keeps it. It is not part of the state.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.getSelectedColumns(); // [2, 3, 4]\ngridInterface.getLayoutFields({ selectedOnly: true }); // ['city', 'age', 'born', 'active']</code></pre>\n","samples":["ranges"]},{"name":"getServerFilter","signatures":["getServerFilter(options?: { calculated?: \"strip\" | \"keep\"; fields?: readonly string[] }): FilterExpression | null"],"doc":"<p>The filter to send to a backend - what every button that loads rows from it can call: the filter\n(<code>datasource.getFilter()</code>), without the conditions the backend can not run - the calculated columns,\nand the fields it has no column for (<code>withoutFields()</code>: a condition taken out matches every row, so the\nbackend sends every row the grid shows, maybe more - load them, the datasource&#39;s filter drops the rest).\n<code>toSqlWhere()</code> (<code>@simple-html/grid/sql</code>) makes SQL of it.</p>\n<p>Find is not in it: <em>Filter rows</em> of the find bar filters the rows in the browser, also the rows loaded\nafter it was turned on.</p>\n<p>A column filtered on the text its template shows (<code>ColumnFormat.text</code>, <code>filterAsShown</code>) is kept when\nits template is a formula for the backend - send <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">getShownFormulas</a> with it - else taken out.</p>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the filter, <code>null</code> for every row</p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> for options that are wrong: <code>fields</code> that is no list of at least one field name</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { toSqlWhere } from '@simple-html/grid/sql';\n\nconst columns = { company: 'company', country: 'country', age: { column: 'age', type: 'number' as const } };\nconst filter = gridInterface.getServerFilter({ fields: Object.keys(columns) });\nconst body = JSON.stringify({ filter }); // the backend: toSqlWhere(filter, { dialect: 'postgres', columns })</code></pre>\n","samples":["sql"]},{"name":"getShownFormulas","signatures":["getShownFormulas(options?: { fields?: readonly string[] }): Record<string, string>"],"doc":"<p>The columns filtered on the text their template shows - a text column with <code>format.text</code> (<code>{first} {last}</code>, a link&#39;s text), <code>filterAsShown</code> not <code>false</code> - each as a formula of that text, for\n<code>toSqlWhere({ shown })</code> (<code>@simple-html/grid/sql</code>): a filter on the column then compares that text in\nSQL, as the grid does. Send it with the filter of <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">getServerFilter</a>.</p>\n<p>Only templates a formula writes the same (templateFormula.ts): every field in it of the default\nformatter of its type, no <code>datetime</code> field. A column whose template is not, or that reads a field\nnot in <code>fields</code>, is left out - and getServerFilter() takes its conditions out: the browser filters them.</p>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the formula of each column, by field: <code>{ order: &#39;CONCAT(&quot;order &quot;, {order})&#39; }</code></p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const fields = ['company', 'order', 'first', 'last'];\nconst body = JSON.stringify({\n    filter: gridInterface.getServerFilter({ fields }),\n    shown: gridInterface.getShownFormulas({ fields })\n});\n// the backend: toSqlWhere(body.filter, { dialect: 'postgres', columns, shown: body.shown })</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getState","signatures":["getState(): GridState"],"doc":"<p>The state of the grid now: what the user changed - column order, pinning and widths, sorting,\ngrouping, expanded groups, the filter and what the header filters show, the aggregates, the\ntotals row, the display formats of the columns and the detail form. See <a href=\"#api/index.GridState\">GridState</a>.</p>\n<p>It is a copy: changing it changes nothing in the grid, and what the user does later does not\nchange it. Give it to <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">setState</a> to go back to it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const state = gridInterface.getState();\nstate.layout.center.map((column) =&gt; column.fields); // [['name'], ['age', 'born']]\nstate.sorting; // [{ attribute: 'name', ascending: true }]\n\n// later, e.g. after the user moved columns and changed the filter\ngridInterface.setState(state);</code></pre>\n","samples":["grid-state"]},{"name":"getViews","signatures":["getViews(): GridView[]"],"doc":"<p>The named views, in their order: the views of the config and the storage (<code>GridConfig.views</code>,\n<code>viewsStorageKey</code>), with what the user saved, renamed and deleted since - or the list given to\n<a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">setViews</a>. See <a href=\"#api/index.GridView\">GridView</a>. Copies: changing them changes nothing in the grid.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.getViews().map((view) =&gt; view.name); // ['Late deliveries', 'My open orders']</code></pre>\n","samples":["views"]},{"name":"importConfig","signatures":["importConfig(saved: unknown): void"],"doc":"<p>Takes a saved grid back: one <code>exportConfig()</code> made, or an older one - a saved grid without a\n<code>version</code> is a config v5 saved (<code>saveConfig()</code>) or was written for, converted on the way in\n(<a href=\"#api/index.convertGridConfig\">convertGridConfig</a>). Its config is given to <code>updateConfig()</code> - an option it leaves out stays\nas it is - then its state to <code>setState()</code>; without a state the grid goes to the config&#39;s start\n(<code>resetState()</code>). Its views to <code>setViews()</code> - stored with <code>viewsStorageKey</code> - when it has them.</p>\n<p>A v5 column&#39;s <code>type</code> and <code>mandatory</code> are the datasource&#39;s fields&#39; in v6: they are left out, give the\ndatasource the field&#39;s type and its <code>required</code> rule.</p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> for what is no saved grid, a version newer than this grid&#39;s, and what\n<code>updateConfig()</code> and <code>setState()</code> throw for - the config is checked first: a config that throws\nchanges nothing</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const saved = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('my-grid') ?? 'null');\nif (saved) {\n    gridInterface.importConfig(saved);\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"importFile","signatures":["importFile(file: Blob, options?: ReadImportFileOptions & ImportOptions): Promise<ImportResult<T>>"],"doc":"<p>Imports a file in one call: an Excel workbook (.xlsx) or a CSV file, read by <a href=\"#api/index.readImportFile\">readImportFile</a>\nand added by <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">importRows</a> - so an app needs no reader of its own. By default the first sheet,\nand the first row that is not empty is the header: its names go to the columns&#39; labels or the\nfields&#39; names, as the import dialog matches them.</p>\n<p>The rows are new rows, one step of the undo history, see <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">importRows</a>. To replace the data\ninstead, read the file with <a href=\"#api/index.readImportFile\">readImportFile</a>.</p>\n<p>Code is not stopped by the grid&#39;s <code>readonly</code> or the edit permissions: check them yourself when the\nfile comes from the user. Works without the grid on the page too.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>file</code> the file: from an <code>&lt;input type=&quot;file&quot;&gt;</code>, a drop, <code>fetch()</code> - any <code>Blob</code></li>\n<li><code>options</code> <code>sheet</code> (its index from 0 or its name, default the first) and <code>separator</code> (a CSV\nfile&#39;s, default the one found) of <a href=\"#api/index.ReadImportFileOptions\">ReadImportFileOptions</a>, and the options of\n<a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">importRows</a> - <code>header</code> is <code>true</code> by default here</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> (a promise of) the new rows, the problems found and how many rows were skipped</p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> (the promise rejects with) an <code>ImportFileError</code> for a file it does not read (over a limit,\nan .xls file, a damaged one), a <code>RangeError</code> for a sheet the workbook has not, a <code>TypeError</code> for an\noption that is wrong</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const input = document.querySelector&lt;HTMLInputElement&gt;('#file')!;\ninput.onchange = async () =&gt; {\n    const result = await gridInterface.importFile(input.files![0]); // the first sheet, a header row\n    console.log(`${result.rows.length} rows imported, ${result.problems.length} problems`);\n};\n\n// another sheet, the rows with problems left out\nawait gridInterface.importFile(input.files![0], { sheet: 'Customers', invalidRows: 'skip' });</code></pre>\n","samples":["import"]},{"name":"importRows","signatures":["importRows(rows: ImportCell[][], options?: ImportOptions): ImportResult<T>"],"doc":"<p>Adds rows of cells as new rows - what the import dialog does, from code: rows read from a file\n(<a href=\"#api/index.readImportFile\">readImportFile</a>), from the clipboard, from an API. Each column goes to a field (<code>fields</code>, or\nthe names of a header row, or by position), each value is read as the user types it - through the\nfield&#39;s formatter, a number with its separators, a date - and the rows are validated. See\n<a href=\"#api/index.ImportOptions\">ImportOptions</a>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The rows are new rows (<code>getChanges().newEntities</code>), added at once at the end (<code>datasource.addNewRows()</code>)\nand the first one selected: the grid scrolls to it. A row with nothing in it is left out</li>\n<li><strong>One step of the undo history</strong>: undo takes the rows out again - marks them for deletion, as\nDelete takes out a new row, so they are in none of the lists of <code>getChanges()</code> - redo brings them\nback</li>\n<li><strong>Problems</strong>: a value that is not of its field&#39;s type (<code>abc</code> for a number) leaves the field\nempty and is put in the row&#39;s error (<code>__rowError</code>, shown on its row number, replaced by\n<code>setErrors()</code>); a validation rule broken shows on the cell. <code>invalidRows: &#39;skip&#39;</code> leaves those\nrows out. Every problem is in the result</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Code is not stopped by the grid&#39;s <code>readonly</code> or the edit permissions (as <code>addNewEmpty()</code> is not):\ncheck them yourself when the rows come from the user. Works without the grid on the page too.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> the rows, a cell for each column: text, a number, a boolean, a <code>Date</code> or <code>null</code> - as\n<a href=\"#api/index.readImportFile\">readImportFile</a> gives them</li>\n<li><code>options</code> the header, the fields, how numbers and dates are written, the rows with problems</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the new rows, the problems found and how many rows were skipped</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>// the first row names the columns\nconst result = gridInterface.importRows(\n    [\n        ['Name', 'Age'],\n        ['Ann', '36'],\n        ['Bob', 'abc']\n    ],\n    { header: true }\n);\nresult.rows.length; // 2\nresult.problems; // [{ row: 2, field: 'age', value: 'abc', kind: 'value', message: 'Not a number: abc' }]\n\n// no header: the columns by position\ngridInterface.importRows([['Cid', 41]], { fields: ['name', 'age'] });</code></pre>\n","samples":["import"]},{"name":"isViewModified","signatures":["isViewModified(): boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when the state changed since the view shown was applied or saved - or, with none shown,\nsince the grid started in the config&#39;s state or went back to it: the <code>*</code> after the name on the\nviews button. A filter, a column moved or resized, a sort, a format, <code>setState()</code> ... - the state\ncompared as JSON, with the expanded groups left out (opening a group changes no view). The\ncurrent row, the scroll position and Find are no state.</p>\n<p>Going back: <code>applyView(id)</code> the view again, <code>resetState()</code> with none shown. <code>true</code> too when the\nview shown was deleted: the state is no view&#39;s.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.applyView('late');\ngridInterface.isViewModified(); // false\ngridInterface.setState({ sorting: [{ attribute: 'company', ascending: true }] });\ngridInterface.isViewModified(); // true</code></pre>\n","samples":["views"]},{"name":"on","signatures":["on<Type extends keyof GridEvents>(type: Type, handler: EventHandler<GridEvents[Type]>): () => void"],"doc":"<p>Subscribes to an event of the grid: cell clicks and focus, copy/paste from the row menu ...\nThe handler gets the event&#39;s payload, typed from <a href=\"#api/index.GridEvents\">GridEvents</a> - see there for every\nevent and what it sends. Sorting, filtering, selection and data changes are events of the\ndatasource: <code>gridInterface.getDatasource().on(...)</code>, see <a href=\"#api/index.DatasourceEvents\">DatasourceEvents</a>.</p>\n<p>The handler stays subscribed until you call the function this returns. What the handler\nreturns is ignored (in v5 it had to return <code>true</code> to stay subscribed).</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>type</code> the event name</li>\n<li><code>handler</code> called with the payload every time the event is sent</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> a function that unsubscribes the handler</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const off = gridInterface.on('cell-click', (data) =&gt; {\n    if (data.attribute === 'company') {\n        console.log('company clicked:', data.rowData.company);\n    }\n});\n\noff(); // unsubscribe</code></pre>\n","samples":["events"]},{"name":"openColumnSettings","signatures":["openColumnSettings(field?: string): void"],"doc":"<p>Opens the grid config dialog on its <em>Columns</em> tab: the columns of the layout on the left, the\nsettings of the one picked on the right - its label, a date or number column&#39;s display format (as\nFormat › in the header menu), a number column&#39;s blank / 0, a text column&#39;s template and link, a text\nor number column as checkboxes, the placeholder and the operator of the header filter, with a\npreview of the current row (see <a href=\"#api/index.ColumnFormat\">ColumnFormat</a>). The user opens it with the gear at the right\nend of the footer (<code>GridConfig.settingsButton</code>) or <em>Column settings…</em> in the header menu; call this\nfrom a button of your own. Its other tabs are the detail form, see <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">openDetailFormSettings</a>,\nand Defaults: the formats by type (<code>GridState.typeFormats</code>) and the default view.</p>\n<p>Its Apply sets the formats of the state (<code>setState({ formats })</code>, <a href=\"#api/index.GridState\">GridState</a>): <code>getState()</code>\nhas them, to save. Reset column / Reset all go back to the formats the grid starts with -\n<code>ColumnConfig.format</code>, or <code>initialState.formats</code>.</p>\n<p>A modal <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code>, as the filter editor: the focus moves into it, Esc closes it (a menu open in it\nfirst), the focus goes back to where it was; the user drags it by its title bar and resizes it from\nevery edge and corner.</p>\n<p>Does nothing while the grid is not on the page.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>field</code> the column it shows first. Left out: the column of the cell with the focus, else the\nfirst column of the layout</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>document.getElementById('settings')!.onclick = () =&gt; gridInterface.openColumnSettings('company');</code></pre>\n","samples":["full-grid"]},{"name":"openDetailFormSettings","signatures":["openDetailFormSettings(): void"],"doc":"<p>Opens the grid config dialog on its <em>Detail form</em> tab: <em>Show the detail form</em>, its width, and the\nfields it shows - the columns of the layout and the other columns of the config - each with a\ncheckbox, in the order of the form: Move up / Move down (Alt+↑ / Alt+↓) change it. See\n<a href=\"#api/index.DetailForm\">DetailForm</a>.</p>\n<p>Its Apply sets the detail form of the state (<code>setState({ detailForm })</code>, <a href=\"#api/index.GridState\">GridState</a>):\n<code>getState()</code> has it, to save. <em>Reset form</em> goes back to the one the grid starts with -\n<code>GridConfig.detailForm</code>, or <code>initialState.detailForm</code>. The dialog&#39;s other tab, <em>Columns</em>, is\n<a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">openColumnSettings</a>; Apply applies both.</p>\n<p>Does nothing while the grid is not on the page.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>document.getElementById('detail-form')!.onclick = () =&gt; gridInterface.openDetailFormSettings();</code></pre>\n","samples":["detail-form"]},{"name":"openFilterEditor","signatures":["openFilterEditor(): void"],"doc":"<p>Opens the filter editor, the dialog where the user builds a filter of conditions and AND/OR\ngroups. It starts with the filter the datasource has now. The user opens it from the header\nfilter&#39;s menu (&quot;Advanced Filter&quot;) or by clicking the filter shown in the footer - or &quot;No filter&quot;\nthere while the rows are not filtered; call this from a button of your own.</p>\n<p>It is a modal <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> (<code>showModal()</code>): over everything on the page, the page behind it can\nnot be used while it is open. The focus moves to the dialog when it opens and goes back to where\nit was when it closes; Esc closes it (a menu open in it first). The user drags it by its title\nbar and resizes it from every edge and corner, with the mouse, a finger or a pen.</p>\n<p>Does nothing while the grid is not on the page.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>document.getElementById('advanced-filter')!.onclick = () =&gt; gridInterface.openFilterEditor();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"openFind","signatures":["openFind(): void"],"doc":"<p>Opens the find bar as Ctrl+F does: the focus goes into its input, with the text it had selected,\nand the matches of that text show. For a button or a menu entry of your own. Does nothing while\nthe grid is not on the page.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>document.getElementById('find-button')!.onclick = () =&gt; gridInterface.openFind();</code></pre>\n","samples":["find"]},{"name":"openImport","signatures":["openImport(source?: string | Blob): void"],"doc":"<p>Opens the import dialog: rows from a CSV or Excel (.xlsx) file, or pasted from a spreadsheet,\nbecome new rows. The user picks or drops a file - or pastes rows (Ctrl+V) - sees the first rows with\na field picked over each column (matched by the header&#39;s names, else by position), the problems\nfound (a value that is not a number, a date ..., a validation rule broken), and imports them: new\nrows, one step of the undo history. See the import guide.</p>\n<p>The grid&#39;s own menus open it with <code>GridConfig.importMenu</code>; call this from a button of your own, or\nwith a file of your own drop zone. A modal <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code>, as the filter editor.</p>\n<p>Does nothing while the grid is not on the page, in a readonly grid and when the user may not add\nrows (<code>GridConfig.edit.add</code>).</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>source</code> the rows to start with: a file (any <code>Blob</code>: a CSV file or an .xlsx workbook), or text\n(CSV or tab separated, as a spreadsheet copies it). Left out, the user picks a file</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>document.getElementById('import')!.onclick = () =&gt; gridInterface.openImport();\n\n// a file dropped on a zone of your own\nconst zone = document.getElementById('drop-zone')!;\nzone.ondragover = (event) =&gt; event.preventDefault();\nzone.ondrop = (event) =&gt; {\n    event.preventDefault();\n    const file = event.dataTransfer?.files[0];\n    if (file) {\n        gridInterface.openImport(file);\n    }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["import"]},{"name":"openMenu","signatures":["openMenu(at: HTMLElement | MouseEvent | MenuPosition, entries: MenuEntry[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Opens a menu of your own, in the grid&#39;s menu style: a value picker for a cell, the actions of a\nbutton, a second grid as a dropdown (<a href=\"#api/index.MenuBlock\">MenuBlock</a>). See <a href=\"#api/index.MenuEntry\">MenuEntry</a> for what it can\nshow, submenus too (<a href=\"#api/index.MenuSubmenu\">MenuSubmenu</a>). To change the grid&#39;s own right click menus, use the\n<code>menus</code> hook (<a href=\"#api/index.GridHooks\">GridHooks</a>).</p>\n<p>The menu is a popover: shown in the top layer, over everything on the page - a container with\n<code>overflow: hidden</code> does not cut it off, no z-index covers it. Opened from an element in a\n<code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> or a popover of your own, it is put inside that element, so it can be used there\n(everything outside a modal dialog is inert).</p>\n<p>The menu open before is closed: there is one menu at a time. The grid closes this one, as its\nown, on a click outside it, on Esc, when another menu opens, on scroll (with\n<code>autoRemoveContextMenuOnScrollEvent</code>) and when the grid leaves the page. Clicking an item closes\nit too, with its submenus, then calls the item&#39;s action; clicking in a block does not.\n<a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">closeMenu</a> closes it from code. When the focus is in the menu as it closes (an item, a\nfield in a block), it goes back to the element that had it when the menu opened.</p>\n<p>The keyboard: called after a key (a button pressed with Enter) the menu takes the focus, on its\nfirst item, and the arrows, Enter, Esc work as in the grid&#39;s menus - the WAI-ARIA menu pattern.\nCalled after a pointer press the focus stays where it is, ArrowDown gets into the menu.</p>\n<p>Called from a click handler the menu stays open: the click that opened it does not count as a\nclick outside it.</p>\n<p>The callbacks of the entries get a <a href=\"#api/index.MenuContext\">MenuContext</a> with <code>menu: &#39;custom&#39;</code>, the grid and the\ndatasource; it has no field, row or cell - your entries know what they were made for.</p>\n<p>Does nothing while the grid is not on the page.</p>\n<p>Replaces v5&#39;s <code>contextMenuCustom()</code> and <code>setContextMenuElement()</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><code>at</code> where it opens:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>a mouse event: its top left corner at the mouse</li>\n<li>a <a href=\"#api/index.MenuPosition\">MenuPosition</a> <code>{ x, y }</code>: its top left corner there, in px from the window&#39;s left and\ntop edges</li>\n<li>an element: under the element, lined up with its left edge</li>\n</ul>\n<p>It is kept in the window: opened above the point (or the element) when there is no room below,\nmoved left when it sticks out on the right.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><code>entries</code> what the menu shows, in order. Entries whose <code>visible</code> returns <code>false</code> are left out</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>// a value picker on a cell\ngridInterface.on('cell-click', (data) =&gt; {\n    if (data.attribute === 'fruit') {\n        const pick = (fruit: string) =&gt; {\n            data.rowData.fruit = fruit;\n            gridInterface.refresh();\n        };\n        gridInterface.openMenu(data.originalEvent, [\n            { type: 'section', id: 'fruit', label: 'Pick a fruit:' },\n            { id: 'fruit.apple', label: 'Apple', action: () =&gt; pick('Apple') },\n            { id: 'fruit.banana', label: 'Banana', action: () =&gt; pick('Banana') }\n        ]);\n    }\n});\n\n// an element of your own under a cell, closed with the grid's menus\ndeclare const cell: HTMLElement;\ndeclare const myPicker: HTMLElement;\ngridInterface.openMenu(cell, [{ type: 'block', id: 'picker', element: myPicker }]);</code></pre>\n","samples":["context-menu","dropdown-grid"]},{"name":"openShortcutHelp","signatures":["openShortcutHelp(): void"],"doc":"<p>Opens the keyboard shortcuts help: a dialog that lists the keys of the grid in groups, with a\nsearch - as <code>?</code> (where it types nothing) and Ctrl+/ in the grid do, and <em>Keyboard shortcuts…</em> in\nthe header menu. The keys as the platform names them, ⌘ on a Mac; a key that does nothing in this\ngrid is left out - the editing keys of a readonly grid. For a help button of your own: it opens the\nhelp also with <code>GridConfig.shortcutHelp: false</code>, which turns the grid&#39;s own ways to open it off.</p>\n<p>A modal <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code>, as the filter editor: the focus moves into it - into its search when a key\nopened it - Esc closes it, the focus goes back to where it was; the user drags it by its title bar\nand resizes it from every edge and corner. Its texts are <code>shortcuts.*</code>.</p>\n<p>Does nothing while the grid is not on the page.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>document.getElementById('keys-help')!.onclick = () =&gt; gridInterface.openShortcutHelp();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rebuild","signatures":["rebuild(): void"],"doc":"<p>Builds the grid again: sizes, rows, columns, header, grouping panel and footer, then renders the\ncells. For when more than the visible cells changed: what a formatter returns (the header\nfilters show it too), the texts of the page (<a href=\"#api/index.setTexts\">setTexts</a>), the size of the element without a\nresize event, a column&#39;s options changed in place. To change an option, use <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">updateConfig</a> - it rebuilds too. For the cells only,\n<a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">refresh</a> is cheaper.</p>\n<p>Does nothing while the grid is not on the page, it is built when it is put there.</p>\n<p>Was <code>triggerRebuild()</code> in v5.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, type Formatter, registerFormatter } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// a formatter that reads a setting of your own\nlet decimals = 2;\nconst price: Formatter = {\n    format: (value) =&gt; (typeof value === 'number' ? value.toFixed(decimals) : ''),\n    parse: (text) =&gt; (text.trim() === '' ? null : Number(text))\n};\nregisterFormatter('price', price);\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ fields: { price: { type: 'number', formatter: 'price' } } });\n// ...\ndecimals = 0;\ngridInterface.rebuild(); // the cells and the header filter show the prices without decimals</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"refresh","signatures":["refresh(): void"],"doc":"<p>Renders the visible cells again, with the values the rows have now. For when something the\ncells show changed without a row changing: what the <code>isReadonly</code> / <code>cellClass</code> hooks read, a\nvalue written to an object of your own instead of the row. A value set on a row shows on its\nown (the datasource&#39;s <code>rows-changed</code>, rendered in the next animation frame), and a scroll only\nrenders the rows that scroll in. Cheap, the columns and the header are not built again - that\nis <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">rebuild</a>.</p>\n<p>The cell input the user has typed in since it got the focus is not rendered, so its text is\nkept: it is rendered once the focus leaves it.</p>\n<p>Does nothing while the grid is not on the page.</p>\n<p>Was <code>triggerScrollEvent()</code> in v5.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>let highlighted = 'ACME CORP';\ngridInterface.updateHooks({ cellClass: (row) =&gt; (row.company === highlighted ? { input: 'highlight' } : null) });\n\nhighlighted = 'GLOBEX'; // the hook reads it, the grid does not know\ngridInterface.refresh();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"refreshDatePresets","signatures":["refreshDatePresets(): void"],"doc":"<p>Computes the quick date filters of the header filters from today again (<code>HeaderFilter.datePreset</code>:\nToday, This week ... picked in a date column&#39;s filter menu) and filters the rows again when their\ndays changed - the day changed since they filtered. Nothing when none changed. On a new day the cells\nof a column with a colour rule on a quick date (<code>ColorRule.datePreset</code>) are rendered again too.</p>\n<p>The grid calls it when the window gets the focus back and when the page is shown again: the user\nback the next morning sees today&#39;s rows. A grid that is looked at over midnight without either - a\nscreen on the wall - calls it from a timer of the app&#39;s.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>// a minute past midnight, every night\nconst msToMidnight = () =&gt; {\n    const now = new Date();\n    return new Date(now.getFullYear(), now.getMonth(), now.getDate() + 1, 0, 1).getTime() - now.getTime();\n};\nconst nightly = () =&gt; {\n    gridInterface.refreshDatePresets();\n    setTimeout(nightly, msToMidnight());\n};\nsetTimeout(nightly, msToMidnight());</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"]},{"name":"renameView","signatures":["renameView(id: string, name: string): void"],"doc":"<p>Gives a view another name - <em>Rename…</em> in the views menu - and sends <code>views-change</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>id</code> the view&#39;s <code>id</code></li>\n<li><code>name</code> its new name, its spaces at the ends taken off. It can be one another view has</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when no view has the id, when the view is <code>readonly</code>, and when <code>name</code> is no\ntext, or only spaces</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.renameView('mine', 'My orders');</code></pre>\n","samples":["views"]},{"name":"resetColumnWidths","signatures":["resetColumnWidths(fields?: string[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Gives columns back the width they start with: the width of the field&#39;s column in the layout\n<code>resetState()</code> goes back to - <code>initialState.layout</code> when the config has one, else the config&#39;s\n<code>layout</code>. A field that is not in it (added from the column chooser) gets 100px, as when it is\nadded. For a column with stacked fields, the width of its first field that is in it. Then\nrebuilds the grid. The header menu has it too: &quot;Reset column width&quot;, &quot;Reset all column widths&quot;.</p>\n<p>Only the widths change: the columns stay where the user put them.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>fields</code> the columns that show one of these fields, every column when left out</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when <code>fields</code> is not an array of field names</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.fitColumns();\ngridInterface.resetColumnWidths(['notes']); // the notes column as wide as in the config again\ngridInterface.resetColumnWidths(); // every column</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"resetRowHeights","signatures":["resetRowHeights(rows?: EntityUnion<T> | EntityUnion<T>[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Gives rows back the height the layout gives a row, after <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">fitRows</a>. The row menu has it\ntoo: &quot;Reset row height&quot;, &quot;Reset all row heights&quot;.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows. Left out: every row</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when <code>rows</code> is not a row or an array of rows</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.resetRowHeights(); // every row back to the height of the layout\ngridInterface.resetRowHeights(datasource.getSelectedRows());</code></pre>\n","samples":["multiline"]},{"name":"resetState","signatures":["resetState(): void"],"doc":"<p>Goes back to the state the grid started in: <code>GridConfig.initialState</code>, with the config&#39;s\n<code>layout</code> (unless <code>initialState</code> has one). What <code>initialState</code> leaves out is cleared - no sorting,\nno grouping, no filter, no header filters. A <code>layout</code> or <code>initialState</code> given to\n<a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">updateConfig</a> since is the one it goes back to.</p>\n<p>It is the view &quot;Standard&quot; of the views menu: no named view is shown after it\n(<a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">getCurrentView</a> is null) - also when the grid started in a default view\n(<code>GridView.default</code>). <code>applyView(id)</code> goes back to a view.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { GridInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst gridInterface = new GridInterface(\n    {\n        layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 100 }, { fields: ['age'], width: 100 }] },\n        initialState: { sorting: [{ attribute: 'name', ascending: true }] }\n    },\n    datasource\n);\n\n// the user sorts, filters and moves columns around ...\ngridInterface.resetState(); // sorted on name again, no filter, the config's columns</code></pre>\n","samples":["grid-state"]},{"name":"saveView","signatures":["saveView(): GridView"],"doc":"<p>Saves the state now over the view shown - <em>Save</em> in the views menu - and sends <code>views-change</code>. Its\nname, id and default stay as they are; it is not modified any more.</p>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the view saved, a copy</p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when no view is shown (&quot;Standard&quot;, the config&#39;s state: <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">saveViewAs</a>\nmakes a view of it) and when the view shown is <code>readonly</code></p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.applyView('mine');\ngridInterface.setState({ sorting: [{ attribute: 'dueDate', ascending: true }] });\ngridInterface.saveView(); // &quot;My open orders&quot; sorted on the due date from now on</code></pre>\n","samples":["views"]},{"name":"saveViewAs","signatures":["saveViewAs(name: string): GridView"],"doc":"<p>Saves the state now as a new view, at the end of the list - <em>Save as new view…</em> in the views menu -\nand sends <code>views-change</code>. It is the view shown from then on. Its id is made by the grid (<code>view-</code>\nand a random part), see the view returned.</p>\n<p>The name can be one another view has, the views menu does not let the user give one.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>name</code> the view&#39;s name, its spaces at the ends taken off</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the view saved, a copy</p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when <code>name</code> is no text, or only spaces</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const view = gridInterface.saveViewAs('Late deliveries');\nview.id; // 'view-mi3x0h2k-4fz9qa', for applyView(), renameView() ...</code></pre>\n","samples":["views"]},{"name":"selectColumns","signatures":["selectColumns(columns: number[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Selects columns by their numbers (see <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">getSelectedColumns</a>), replacing the ones selected:\nthe numbers show it, <code>column-selection-change</code> is sent when it changed. <code>[]</code> selects none. A\nShift+click after it selects from the last number given.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>columns</code> the numbers, 1 based as the header shows them</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> for a number that is no column: not a whole number from 1 to the number of\ncolumns of the layout</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.selectColumns([1, 2]); // the first two columns\ngridInterface.selectColumns([]); // none\n\ngridInterface.on('column-selection-change', ({ columns, fields }) =&gt; {\n    console.log(columns.length ? `columns ${columns.join(', ')}: ${fields.join(', ')}` : 'no column selected');\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["ranges"]},{"name":"setDefaultView","signatures":["setDefaultView(id: string | null): void"],"doc":"<p>Makes a view the default - the one the grid applies when it is made (<code>GridView.default</code>), <em>Default\nview</em> in the views menu - and sends <code>views-change</code>. One at a time: the default before is not any\nmore. A readonly view can be the default. Nothing is applied now.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>id</code> the view&#39;s <code>id</code>, null for none: the grid starts in the config&#39;s state (&quot;Standard&quot;)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when no view has the id</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.setDefaultView('late'); // the next time the grid is made it shows &quot;Late deliveries&quot;\ngridInterface.setDefaultView(null); // the config's state</code></pre>\n","samples":["views"]},{"name":"setRanges","signatures":["setRanges(ranges: CellRange[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Selects ranges of cells, replacing the ones there are - as if the user had selected them. See\n<a href=\"#api/index.CellRange\">CellRange</a>. The cells show them, <code>range-change</code> is sent. The focus does not move and the\ngrid does not scroll to them.</p>\n<p>The grid keeps copies, with only the four keys of a range. They are cleared when the displayed\nrows or the layout change, see <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">getRanges</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>ranges</code> the ranges, the last one is the active one. <code>[]</code> clears them, as <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">clearRanges</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> for a range with a row that is not displayed (0 to <code>datasource.length() - 1</code>)\nor a field that is not in the layout</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>// rows 0 to 4, the fields from name to age\ngridInterface.setRanges([{ fromRow: 0, fromField: 'name', toRow: 4, toField: 'age' }]);\n\n// two ranges, as Ctrl+click makes them\ngridInterface.setRanges([\n    { fromRow: 0, fromField: 'name', toRow: 0, toField: 'name' },\n    { fromRow: 5, fromField: 'age', toRow: 9, toField: 'age' }\n]);</code></pre>\n","samples":["ranges"]},{"name":"setState","signatures":["setState(state: Partial<GridState>): void"],"doc":"<p>Sets the state: column order, pinning and widths, sorting, grouping, expanded groups, the filter\nand what the header filters show, the aggregates, the totals row, the display formats of the\ncolumns and the detail form. See <a href=\"#api/index.GridState\">GridState</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Applies what is given and keeps the rest</strong>: <code>setState({ sorting })</code> changes the sort and\nnothing else. To set everything, pass a whole state, e.g. one from <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">getState</a>. Within a\npart nothing is merged: <code>layout</code> replaces the whole layout, <code>headerFilters</code> every header filter.</p>\n<p>The grid keeps a copy, the object passed in is not changed later. It must be plain data (no\nfunctions, no rows from the datasource): it is copied with <code>structuredClone</code>. A state stored as\nJSON can be given as it is; its <code>Date</code>s came back as ISO text, which is kept as text - see\n<a href=\"#api/index.GridState\">GridState</a>.</p>\n<p><code>filter</code> is what the rows are filtered by, <code>headerFilters</code> only what the header filter cells show.\nSet both to have a header filter&#39;s condition and its cell agree, as <code>getState()</code> gives them.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>state</code> the parts to set</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> for aggregates or display formats (<code>formats</code>) that do not fit their fields,\nsee <a href=\"#api/index.ColumnConfig\">ColumnConfig</a> <code>aggregate</code> and <a href=\"#api/index.ColumnFormat\">ColumnFormat</a>, and a <code>detailForm</code> that is no\n<a href=\"#api/index.DetailForm\">DetailForm</a> - before anything changes</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridState } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const savedState: GridState;\n\n// a whole state, saved before\ngridInterface.setState(savedState);\n\n// only some parts, the rest stays as it is\ngridInterface.setState({ sorting: [{ attribute: 'age', ascending: false }] });\ngridInterface.setState({ grouping: [{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }], expandedGroups: [] });\ngridInterface.setState({ filter: null, headerFilters: {} }); // no filter</code></pre>\n","samples":["grid-state"]},{"name":"setViews","signatures":["setViews(views: GridView[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Replaces the list of named views: loaded from a backend, say. The view shown stays shown when the\nlist has its id, else none is (&quot;Standard&quot;, marked as changed: the state shown is the old view&#39;s) -\nnothing is applied, the grid shows what it showed. Written to localStorage with\n<code>GridConfig.viewsStorageKey</code>. Sends no <code>views-change</code>: you gave the list.</p>\n<p>The grid keeps a copy, the list passed in is not changed later.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>views</code> the views, see <a href=\"#api/index.GridView\">GridView</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when <code>views</code> is no list of views - an id or a name that is no text, a state\nthat is no object, two views of one id, two defaults - before anything changes</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridView } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst response = await fetch('/api/settings/orders-grid-views');\nconst views: GridView[] = await response.json();\ngridInterface.setViews(views);</code></pre>\n","samples":["views"]},{"name":"updateColumns","signatures":["updateColumns(columns: readonly SourceColumn[], options?: ReconcileOptions): ColumnsReport"],"doc":"<p>The grid with the columns its source has now - a database view the grid was made from got columns\nand lost some: <a href=\"#api/index.reconcileColumns\">reconcileColumns</a> on what the grid has (<code>exportConfig()</code>), given back\n(<code>importConfig()</code>). A field that is gone leaves the layout, the sort, the grouping, the filters, the\nformats, the colour rules (a rule that needed it goes), the detail form, the views - the config&#39;s and\nthe ones the user saved (written back, <code>setViews()</code>) - and a calculated column whose formula named it\ngoes; a new field is listed by the column chooser (shown with <code>showNew</code>). Returns what changed.</p>\n<p>The datasource keeps its fields: a new field it has no type of is shown as text - make the datasource\nwith the new fields&#39; types when it can be made again.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>columns</code> the columns of the source now, in their order: <code>{ field, label?, ...ColumnConfig }</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>// the view's columns now: city is gone, region is new\nconst report = gridInterface.updateColumns([{ field: 'company' }, { field: 'country' }, { field: 'region', label: 'Region' }]);\nif (report.removed.length) {\n    alert(`Gone from the view: ${report.removed.join(', ')}`);\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["reconcile-columns"]},{"name":"updateConfig","signatures":["updateConfig(config: Partial<GridConfig>): void"],"doc":"<p>Changes options of the config while the grid is shown: <code>readonly</code>, <code>hideLabels</code>, the sizes,\n<code>tooltips</code>, <code>columns</code> ... and rebuilds the grid once. The functions - <code>isReadonly</code>, <code>cellClass</code>,\n<code>menus</code> - are not part of the config, change them with <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">updateHooks</a>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Only the keys given change</strong>, the rest stay as they are. A key given as <code>undefined</code> or <code>null</code> goes\nback to its default - <code>layout</code> excepted, a grid always has one.</li>\n<li><strong><code>columns</code> replaces the options of every column</strong>, nothing is merged: a field left out gets\nthe defaults.</li>\n<li><strong><code>layout</code> is shown right away</strong>, as <code>setState({ layout })</code> does: the column order, pinning and\nwidths the user made are replaced. It is also the layout <code>resetState()</code> goes back to from now\non (unless <code>initialState</code> has a layout).</li>\n<li><strong><code>initialState</code> changes nothing now</strong>: it is the state a later <code>resetState()</code> goes back to.\nCall <code>resetState()</code> after to apply it.</li>\n<li><strong><code>texts</code> replaces the grid&#39;s texts as a whole</strong>, the ids are not merged: an id left out shows\nthe page&#39;s text again (<code>setTexts()</code>). A menu or the filter editor shows them the next time it\nopens.</li>\n<li><strong><code>edit</code> replaces the permissions as a whole</strong>: a permission left out is allowed again -\n<code>updateConfig({ edit: { delete: false } })</code> allows adding and changing. The cells follow at\nonce; an open menu, date picker, lookup list or editor of a multiline cell is closed - what was\ntyped in the editor is not saved. See <a href=\"#api/index.EditPermissions\">EditPermissions</a>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>views</code> and <code>viewsStorageKey</code> make the list of views again</strong>, as when the grid is made: the\nconfig&#39;s and the stored ones. Nothing is applied; the view shown stays shown when the list still\nhas it. See <a href=\"#api/index.GridView\">GridView</a>. With no view shown (&quot;Standard&quot;) and the state the config&#39;s, the\ngrid still shows the config&#39;s state after a new <code>layout</code> or <code>columns</code>: not marked as changed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The rest of the state - sorting, grouping, filter, header filters - is kept, and so are the\nhandlers subscribed with <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">on</a>. The object passed in is not changed, the grid copies\n<code>columns</code>, <code>layout</code> and <code>initialState</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>config</code> the parts of the config to change</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when <code>config</code> has <code>isReadonly</code>, <code>cellClass</code> or <code>menus</code> (those are hooks),\na column has v5&#39;s <code>mandatory</code> (it is the field&#39;s <code>required</code> rule), <code>texts</code> is not an object of\nstrings, <code>multilineTooltipLines</code> or <code>multilineLineHeight</code> is not a whole number of 1 or more, a\ncolumn&#39;s <code>aggregate</code> is no aggregate function or needs a number field, a column&#39;s <code>format</code> does\nnot fit its field (see <a href=\"#api/index.ColumnFormat\">ColumnFormat</a>), a column&#39;s <code>editor</code> is wrong - its lookup not\nregistered, see <a href=\"#api/index.ColumnEditor\">ColumnEditor</a> - a column&#39;s <code>renderer</code> is not the id of a registered cell\nrenderer, or is given with an <code>editor</code>, or a column&#39;s <code>filterOperators</code>, <code>operator</code>,\n<code>filterCaseSensitive</code> or <code>datePresets</code> does not fit its type, see <a href=\"#api/index.ColumnConfig\">ColumnConfig</a> - when <code>detailForm</code> is\nnot a <a href=\"#api/index.DetailForm\">DetailForm</a>, and when <code>edit</code> is not an object of the permissions <code>add</code>, <code>change</code> and\n<code>delete</code>, each true or false (see <a href=\"#api/index.EditPermissions\">EditPermissions</a>)</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.updateConfig({ readonly: false }); // editing on\ngridInterface.updateConfig({ edit: { add: true, change: false, delete: false } }); // new rows only\ngridInterface.updateConfig({ hideFilter: true, cellHeight: 30 });\ngridInterface.updateConfig({ tooltips: undefined }); // back to the default, true\n\n// the columns the config starts with, shown now and what resetState() goes back to\ngridInterface.updateConfig({ layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 200 }] } });</code></pre>\n","samples":["misc-options"]},{"name":"updateHooks","signatures":["updateHooks(hooks: GridHooks<T>): void"],"doc":"<p>Changes the hooks while the grid is shown: <code>isReadonly</code>, <code>cellClass</code> and <code>menus</code>, see\n<a href=\"#api/index.GridHooks\">GridHooks</a>. <strong>Only the keys given change</strong>, a key given as <code>undefined</code> removes that hook -\nthe cells follow the config again, the menus show their defaults. The visible cells are rendered\nagain once (as <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">refresh</a> does); a menu uses its new function the next time it opens.</p>\n<p>The object passed in is not kept: the grid copies its keys.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>hooks</code> the hooks to set, or to remove with <code>undefined</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>// company can not be edited on an inactive row\ngridInterface.updateHooks({ isReadonly: (row, field) =&gt; (field === 'company' &amp;&amp; !row.isActive ? true : null) });\n\n// color the balance cells, the readonly rule stays\ngridInterface.updateHooks({ cellClass: (row, field) =&gt; (field === 'balance' &amp;&amp; row.balance &lt; 0 ? { input: 'red' } : null) });\n\ngridInterface.updateHooks({ isReadonly: undefined }); // removed: the column config decides again\ngridInterface.updateHooks({ menus: undefined }); // the menus show their defaults</code></pre>\n","samples":["cell-styling"]}]}]},{"name":"ImportFileError","group":"Classes","kind":"Class","signatures":["class ImportFileError extends Error"],"doc":"<p>The error <a href=\"#api/index.readImportFile\">readImportFile</a> rejects with when it does not read a file. <code>problem</code> says why, the\nmessage says it in English with the detail (which limit, which part of the workbook).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { ImportFileError, readImportFile } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const file: File;\n\ntry {\n    const table = await readImportFile(file);\n    gridInterface.importRows(table.rows, { header: true });\n} catch (error) {\n    if (error instanceof ImportFileError &amp;&amp; error.problem === 'tooLarge') {\n        alert('The file is too large');\n    }\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Constructors","members":[{"name":"constructor","signatures":["new ImportFileError(problem: ImportFileProblem, message: string): ImportFileError"],"doc":"<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>problem</code> why the file was not read</li>\n<li><code>message</code> what was wrong, in English</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"problem","signatures":["readonly problem: ImportFileProblem"],"doc":"<p>why the file was not read</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"CalculatedColumn","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface CalculatedColumn"],"doc":"<p>A calculated column: its values computed from the other fields of the row by a formula - plain JSON,\nin the state. Its field is the key it has in <code>GridConfig.calculatedColumns</code> /\n<code>GridState.calculatedColumns</code>: a letter, then letters, digits, <code>_</code> and <code>#</code> (64 at most), no field of the\ndatasource or of the rows. Put it in the layout as any field.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>formula</code></strong>: <code>{price} * {qty}</code>, <code>DAYS({due}, TODAY())</code>, <code>IF({qty} &gt; 10, &quot;bulk&quot;, &quot;single&quot;)</code> - see\nthe guide &quot;Calculated columns&quot; for the language: fields in braces, numbers, texts in quotes,\n<code>+ - * /</code>, <code>&amp;</code>, the comparisons, AND / OR / NOT and a few functions. Text, not code: nothing runs.</li>\n<li><strong><code>label</code></strong>: its label, default the field name made readable. <code>ColumnConfig.label</code> and\n<code>ColumnFormat.label</code> win over it, as over a field&#39;s label.</li>\n<li><strong><code>type</code></strong>: the type of its values. Left out, the formula&#39;s; given, it must be the formula&#39;s (a\n<code>TypeError</code> if not) - a saved state keeps saying what it holds.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Read only: its cells are not edited, a paste skips them. A row where the formula can not be computed\n(a division by 0) has an empty cell. A formula with a problem - a syntax error, a field the grid does\nnot know, a type that does not fit - throws a <code>TypeError</code> when the grid is made, or <code>setState()</code> or\n<code>updateConfig()</code> is given it; the grid config dialog shows the problem at once.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    calculatedColumns: {\n        total: { formula: '{price} * {qty}', label: 'Total' },\n        daysLate: { formula: 'MAX(0, DAYS({due}, TODAY()))', label: 'Days late', type: 'number' }\n    },\n    columns: { total: { aggregate: 'sum', format: { number: { decimals: 2 } } } },\n    layout: {\n        center: [\n            { fields: ['price'], width: 80 },\n            { fields: ['qty'], width: 60 },\n            { fields: ['total'], width: 90 },\n            { fields: ['daysLate'], width: 80 }\n        ]\n    }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["calculated-columns"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"formula","signatures":["formula: string"],"doc":"<p>the formula: <code>{price} * {qty}</code>. At most 1000 characters</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"label","signatures":["label?: string"],"doc":"<p>its label, default the field name made readable</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"type","signatures":["type?: CalculatedType"],"doc":"<p>the type of its values: left out the formula&#39;s, given it must be the formula&#39;s</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"CellClass","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface CellClass"],"doc":"<p>The css classes the <code>cellClass</code> hook (<a href=\"#api/index.GridHooks\">GridHooks</a>) adds to a cell. Each is one or more class\nnames, separated by spaces, the same as a <code>class</code> attribute.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { CellClass } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst negative: CellClass = { input: 'negative-text', background: 'negative-background' };</code></pre>\n","samples":["cell-styling"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"background","signatures":["background?: string"],"doc":"<p>added to the element behind the input, which fills the cell. The input is transparent, so this\nis the cell&#39;s background - the grid draws the readonly and required stripes there. On an\neditable cell it has no size (the grid&#39;s readonly and required classes give it one): give the\nclass <code>position: absolute; inset: 0</code>. Was <code>dimmedClass</code> in v5</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"input","signatures":["input?: string"],"doc":"<p>added to the cell&#39;s <code>&lt;input&gt;</code>: the text. Was <code>inputClass</code> in v5</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"CellRange","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface CellRange"],"doc":"<p>A range of cells: the rectangle between two cells, both included. The user makes ranges with the\nmouse and the keyboard (see guides/17-selection-and-clipboard.md); <code>gridInterface.getRanges()</code> gives\nthem, <code>setRanges()</code> sets them.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Rows</strong> are indexes in the displayed rows (<code>datasource.getRows()</code>), 0 based - the <code>row</code> of the\ngrid events. A group row in between is part of the rectangle, but it has no cells: copy, paste\nand clear skip it.</li>\n<li><strong>Fields</strong> are field names. The fields between them are the ones between them in the layout, in\nthe order of <code>gridInterface.getLayoutFields()</code>: pinned left, center, pinned right, and a column of\nstacked fields is a field each, top to bottom - the order of the CSV export and of\n<code>aria-colindex</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>from</code> is where the range starts</strong> (the anchor): the cell the mouse was pressed in, or the cell\nwith the focus when it was made with the keyboard. <strong><code>to</code> is the opposite corner</strong>, it can be\nabove or left of <code>from</code>. The last range&#39;s <code>from</code> is the active cell: where the focus is.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Plain JSON: it can be stored or sent. The indexes of the rows are only good for the rows as they\nare displayed now - the grid clears the ranges when the displayed rows change (filter, sort, group,\nexpand, collapse, rows added or removed) and when the layout changes.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { CellRange } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// the first three rows, from the name to the age (and every field between them in the layout)\nconst range: CellRange = { fromRow: 0, fromField: 'name', toRow: 2, toField: 'age' };\ngridInterface.setRanges([range]);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"fromField","signatures":["fromField: string"],"doc":"<p>the field the range starts at</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"fromRow","signatures":["fromRow: number"],"doc":"<p>the row the range starts at: an index in the displayed rows, 0 based</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"toField","signatures":["toField: string"],"doc":"<p>the field of the opposite corner, left of <code>fromField</code> too</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"toRow","signatures":["toRow: number"],"doc":"<p>the row of the opposite corner, above <code>fromRow</code> too</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"CellRenderContext","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface CellRenderContext<T = unknown>"],"doc":"<p>What the grid gives a cell renderer each time the cell shows a row: see <a href=\"#api/index.CellRendererInstance\">CellRendererInstance</a>.\nA new object every render.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of the rows, as in the datasource</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type CellRenderContext, registerCellRenderer } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nregisterCellRenderer('stock', (host) =&gt; {\n    const span = document.createElement('span');\n    host.appendChild(span);\n    return {\n        update(context: CellRenderContext) {\n            span.textContent = context.text; // the text the default cell would show\n            span.style.fontWeight = Number(context.value) &lt; 10 ? 'bold' : '';\n        }\n    };\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["custom-cells"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"field","signatures":["field: string"],"doc":"<p>the cell&#39;s field</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"gridInterface","signatures":["gridInterface: GridInterface<T>"],"doc":"<p>the grid: the registry is for the page, so a renderer can not know its grid otherwise</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"readonly","signatures":["readonly: boolean"],"doc":"<p>the cell can not be edited: the grid is readonly, the edit permissions lock the row\n(<code>GridConfig.edit</code>, <code>change: false</code>), or the cell is - the column&#39;s <code>readonly</code>, the <code>isReadonly</code>\nhook. Do not write the value then</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"row","signatures":["row: EntityUnion<T>"],"doc":"<p>the row - always a data row, a group row has no cells. A write goes through the datasource as one\nfrom code does: the edit is tracked, the field validated, it is a step of the undo history, and\nthe cell is rendered again in the next frame (<code>update()</code> gets the new value)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rowIndex","signatures":["rowIndex: number"],"doc":"<p>the index of the row in the displayed rows (<code>datasource.getRows()</code>), 0 based - as in the grid&#39;s events</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"text","signatures":["text: string"],"doc":"<p>the text the default cell would show: the value through the field&#39;s formatter, <code>numberOverride</code> applied</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"type","signatures":["type: FieldType"],"doc":"<p>the cell&#39;s type: the field&#39;s, or the one <code>dynamicCellTypeColumn</code> gives this row</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"value","signatures":["value: unknown"],"doc":"<p>the value, <code>row[field]</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"CellRendererInstance","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface CellRendererInstance<T = unknown>"],"doc":"<p>What a cell renderer returns for a cell element: the grid calls <code>update()</code> every time the cell is\nrendered, and <code>destroy()</code> when the cell element is done with it. See <a href=\"#api/index.registerCellRenderer\">registerCellRenderer</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of the rows, as in the datasource</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type CellRendererInstance, registerCellRenderer } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// the age of the row's last change, counted up every second\nregisterCellRenderer('age', (host) =&gt; {\n    let changed = 0;\n    const show = () =&gt; {\n        host.textContent = changed ? `${Math.round((Date.now() - changed) / 1000)}s ago` : '';\n    };\n    const timer = setInterval(show, 1000);\n    const instance: CellRendererInstance = {\n        update(context) {\n            changed = Number(context.value);\n            show();\n        },\n        // else the timer keeps running, and keeps the grid alive\n        destroy: () =&gt; clearInterval(timer)\n    };\n    return instance;\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["custom-cells"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Methods","members":[{"name":"destroy","signatures":["destroy?(): void"],"doc":"<p>Called once when the cell element is done with this renderer: it shows a column without it now\n(scrolled sideways), the column lost its <code>renderer</code> (<code>updateConfig()</code>), the cells are made again\n(a resize, <code>cellHeight</code>, a new layout), the grid is taken off the page or destroyed. Undo what\n<code>update()</code> and the renderer set up outside the host - an unmount, a subscription, a timer. The grid\nempties the host itself</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"edit","signatures":["edit?(typed?: string): void"],"doc":"<p>For a renderer that edits the value itself - a select, buttons, a checkbox of its own. The grid\ncalls it where it would open its editor: Enter, F2 and a character typed with the focus on the\ncell, a double click - only when the cell can be edited. Focus your control, open it, step the\nvalue ... Left out, the grid edits the cell in its text editor, and a date cell opens the date\npicker on a click</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>typed</code> the character typed, undefined for Enter, F2 and a double click</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"update","signatures":["update(context: CellRenderContext<T>): void"],"doc":"<p>Called every time the cell is rendered: another row while scrolling (the cell elements are reused),\na changed value, <code>refresh()</code>, a sort, the hooks changed ... Change what differs; the content is\nkept between the calls</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ChangeKinds","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ChangeKinds"],"doc":"<p>Which kinds of change <code>getChanges()</code>, <code>hasChanges()</code> and <code>getChangedRows()</code> look at:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>left out, or <code>null</code> - all of them</li>\n<li>kinds set to <code>true</code> - only those: <code>{ new: true }</code> the new rows, <code>{ new: true, modified: true }</code> what a\nsave of the rows sends without the deletions</li>\n<li>only kinds set to <code>false</code> - all but those: <code>{ deleted: false }</code> is the new and edited rows</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A kind left out is not asked for: with a kind <code>true</code> it is left out, with only kinds <code>false</code> it is in.\n<code>getChanges()</code> keeps its three lists, a kind not asked for is <code>[]</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ key: 'id' });\ndatasource.getChanges({ deleted: true }).deletedEntities; // only the rows marked for deletion\ndatasource.hasChanges({ new: true, modified: true }); // added or edited rows, not deletions\ndatasource.getChangedRows({ deleted: false }); // the new and edited rows themselves</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"deleted","signatures":["deleted?: boolean | null"],"doc":"<p>the rows marked for deletion (<code>&#39;D&#39;</code>) - not a new row marked: it was never saved</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"modified","signatures":["modified?: boolean | null"],"doc":"<p>the rows edited (<code>&#39;M&#39;</code>)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"new","signatures":["new?: boolean | null"],"doc":"<p>the rows added (<code>addNewEmpty()</code>, <code>__rowState</code> <code>&#39;N&#39;</code>)</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"Changes","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface Changes<T = Record<string, unknown>>"],"doc":"<p>What <code>datasource.getChanges()</code> returns: the rows added, edited and marked for deletion since the\ndata was set - what to send to a server.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>newEntities</code> - rows added with <code>addNewEmpty()</code>, edits to them included. A new row has a\ntemporary key, a generated negative number: in its key field (<code>id: -1</code>), or as <code>__KEY</code> when the\ndatasource has no key field. After the save, <code>acceptChanges({ newKeys })</code> gives the rows the\nserver&#39;s keys</li>\n<li><code>modifiedEntities</code> - one entry per edited row: its key and the changed fields, see\n<a href=\"#api/index.ModifiedEntity\">ModifiedEntity</a></li>\n<li><code>deletedEntities</code> - rows marked with <code>markForDeletion()</code> / <code>markAllForDeletion()</code>. A new row\nthat is marked for deletion is in none of the lists: it was never saved, there is nothing to send.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Every entry is a copy, a plain object: changing it does not change the row. It is a shallow copy -\na <code>Date</code> stays a <code>Date</code>, an object in a field is the row&#39;s own object.</p>\n<p>When an edit counts: a field is edited when its value differs from the original. A field set back\nto its original value is not edited any more. Setting a blank field (<code>null</code> / <code>undefined</code>) to <code>&#39;&#39;</code>\nis no edit. Two <code>Date</code>s are compared by the field&#39;s type in the datasource&#39;s <code>fields</code>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>date</code> - on the day. A date typed into a cell gets the current time of day, so typing the same\nday again is no edit.</li>\n<li><code>datetime</code>, and every other field - to the second, the milliseconds are ignored (they are not\nshown, and typing a time stamps the current ones). A time only change is an edit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ninterface Person {\n    id: number;\n    name: string;\n    born: Date | null;\n    lastLogin: Date | null;\n}\ndeclare const rowsFromServer: Person[];\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource&lt;Person&gt;({ key: 'id', fields: { born: 'date', lastLogin: 'datetime' } });\ndatasource.setData(rowsFromServer);\n// ... the user edits, adds and deletes rows in the grid\n\nconst { newEntities, modifiedEntities, deletedEntities } = datasource.getChanges();\nconst response = await fetch('/api/people', {\n    method: 'POST',\n    body: JSON.stringify({ newEntities, modifiedEntities, deletedEntities }) // a Date becomes its ISO text\n});\n\n// saved in one transaction: the server answers with the id it gave each new row\nconst saved: { temporaryId: number; id: number }[] = await response.json();\ndatasource.acceptChanges({ newKeys: new Map(saved.map((row) =&gt; [row.temporaryId, row.id])) });</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"deletedEntities","signatures":["deletedEntities: T[]"],"doc":"<p>the rows marked for deletion, with the values they have now</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"modifiedEntities","signatures":["modifiedEntities: ModifiedEntity<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>one entry per edited row: its key and the fields that changed</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"newEntities","signatures":["newEntities: (T & { __KEY?: string | number })[]"],"doc":"<p>the rows added with <code>addNewEmpty()</code> (or the container&#39;s <code>setData(rows, { add: true, isNew: true })</code>),\nwith the values they have now. Without a key field the temporary key is in <code>__KEY</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"CheckboxFormat","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface CheckboxFormat"],"doc":"<p>The checkboxes of a <code>text</code> or <code>number</code> column, <code>ColumnFormat.checkbox</code>: each cell is a checkbox, for\na field that holds a flag as <code>1</code> / <code>0</code>, <code>&#39;Y&#39;</code> / <code>&#39;N&#39;</code>. A cell is checked when its value is the\nchecked value - its text trimmed, a number equal to it. Clicked (or Space), an editable cell writes\nthe checked or the unchecked value: a number for a number field (<code>1</code>), else the text (<code>&#39;1&#39;</code>); an\nunchecked value <code>&#39;&#39;</code> empties the cell (null), as Delete does.</p>\n<p>The header filter is a checkbox, as a boolean column&#39;s: checked - the field equal to the checked value,\nas it is; not checked - any other value, a blank too; neither - no filter. Plain conditions a backend&#39;s\n<code>toSqlWhere()</code> takes. The value stays the value: copy, paste, the CSV and Excel exports, sorting,\ngrouping and the filter menu&#39;s value list have <code>1</code> and <code>0</code>, as without the checkboxes.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>format</th>\n<th>checked</th>\n<th>a click writes</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>{}</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;1&#39;</code>, <code>&#39; 1 &#39;</code>; <code>1</code> in a number field</td>\n<td><code>&#39;1&#39;</code> / <code>&#39;0&#39;</code>, <code>1</code> / <code>0</code> in a number field</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ checked: &#39;Y&#39;, unchecked: &#39;N&#39; }</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;Y&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;Y&#39;</code> / <code>&#39;N&#39;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ checked: &#39;1&#39;, unchecked: &#39;&#39; }</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;1&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;1&#39;</code> / null</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { CheckboxFormat, GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst yesNo: CheckboxFormat = { checked: 'Y', unchecked: 'N' };\nconst columns: GridConfig['columns'] = {\n    newsletter: { format: { checkbox: {} } }, // '1' / '0' (a text field) or 1 / 0 (a number field)\n    approved: { format: { checkbox: yesNo } }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"checked","signatures":["checked?: string"],"doc":"<p>the value of a checked cell, written when it is checked: text, not <code>&#39;&#39;</code>. A number for a number\nfield (<code>&#39;1&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;-1&#39;</code>). Left out: <code>&#39;1&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"unchecked","signatures":["unchecked?: string"],"doc":"<p>the value written when a cell is unchecked: text, <code>&#39;&#39;</code> empties the cell. A number or <code>&#39;&#39;</code> for a\nnumber field. Not the checked value. Left out: <code>&#39;0&#39;</code>. A cell whose value is neither is unchecked</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ColorRule","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ColorRule"],"doc":"<p>A colour rule of a column, <code>ColumnFormat.rules</code>: when its condition is true for a row, the cell has\nthe rule&#39;s text colour, background and bold. The first rule of the list that matches wins.</p>\n<p>The condition is one of three kinds - a rule has one of them:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><strong>Value</strong>, <code>operator</code> and <code>value</code>: the cell&#39;s own value, compared as the column&#39;s header filter\ncompares the same operator and text. <code>value</code> is text as it is typed there - <code>&#39;100&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;late&#39;</code>,\n<code>&#39;2026-11-22&#39;</code> - read with the field&#39;s formatter (a number, a date), a text with its wildcards (<code>*</code>,\n<code>%</code>, <code>_</code>), case ignored unless the column has <code>filterCaseSensitive</code>. A lookup column (<code>editor</code>)\ncompares the label its cells show. 0 is blank, as in the filter.</p>\n<p><strong>A date</strong> (<code>date</code>, <code>datetime</code>) takes a period as the value - a week <code>&#39;2026-W47&#39;</code>, a month <code>&#39;2026-11&#39;</code>,\na quarter <code>&#39;2026 Q4&#39;</code>, a year <code>&#39;2026&#39;</code> - or a quick date, <code>datePreset</code> (<code>&#39;thisWeek&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;lastMonth&#39;</code>,\n<code>&#39;next7Days&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;overdue&#39;</code> ...: its days today) instead of <code>value</code>. <code>EQUAL</code> is in the period,\n<code>NOT_EQUAL_TO</code> not in it (or blank), <code>LESS_THAN</code> before it, <code>LESS_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO</code> to its end,\n<code>GREATER_THAN</code> after it, <code>GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO</code> from its start, <code>BETWEEN</code> from the start of the\none to the end of the other (a <code>value</code> only). <strong><code>week</code></strong> says what a week is, for <code>&#39;2026-W47&#39;</code> and for\nthe quick dates of a week: <code>&#39;iso&#39;</code> (Monday, ISO 8601 numbers) or <code>&#39;us&#39;</code> (Sunday, week 1 has January 1).\nLeft out: the column&#39;s <code>weekUs</code> / <code>weekIso</code> format, else the date picker&#39;s <code>weekStart</code> (Sunday: <code>&#39;us&#39;</code>).</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>Conditions</strong>, <code>conditions</code> and <code>combine</code>: conditions on fields of the row, each tested as its\nfield&#39;s header filter tests it - see <a href=\"#api/index.RuleCondition\">RuleCondition</a>. <code>combine: &#39;AND&#39;</code> (the default) colours\nwhen all of them are true, <code>&#39;OR&#39;</code> when one is.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>Formula</strong>, <code>expression</code>: a formula of the language of the calculated columns that is true or false</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&#39;{balance} &lt; 0 AND {status} = &quot;late&quot;&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;DAYS({due}, TODAY()) &gt; 7&#39;</code> (see the guide &quot;Calculated\ncolumns&quot;). True colours the cell; a row where it can not be computed is not coloured.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>rule</th>\n<th>colours</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>{ operator: &#39;LESS_THAN&#39;, value: &#39;0&#39;, color: &#39;red&#39; }</code></td>\n<td>a negative number, red text</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ operator: &#39;EQUAL&#39;, value: &#39;waiting&#39;, background: &#39;orange&#39; }</code></td>\n<td>the text <code>waiting</code> (any case)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ operator: &#39;BETWEEN&#39;, value: [&#39;10&#39;, &#39;20&#39;], background: &#39;yellow&#39; }</code></td>\n<td>10 to 20, both included</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ operator: &#39;IS_BLANK&#39;, background: &#39;grey&#39; }</code></td>\n<td>an empty cell, or 0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ conditions: [{ field: &#39;status&#39;, operator: &#39;EQUAL&#39;, value: &#39;late&#39; }, { field: &#39;balance&#39;, operator: &#39;GREATER_THAN&#39;, value: &#39;0&#39; }], background: &#39;red&#39; }</code></td>\n<td>late and owing</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ conditions: [...], combine: &#39;OR&#39;, color: &#39;blue&#39; }</code></td>\n<td>one of the conditions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ expression: &#39;DAYS({due}, TODAY()) &gt; 7&#39;, background: &#39;#fde68a&#39; }</code></td>\n<td>more than a week late, a custom background</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ operator: &#39;EQUAL&#39;, datePreset: &#39;thisWeek&#39;, week: &#39;us&#39;, background: &#39;green&#39; }</code></td>\n<td>a date this week, Sunday to Saturday</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ operator: &#39;LESS_THAN&#39;, datePreset: &#39;thisWeek&#39;, week: &#39;iso&#39;, color: &#39;red&#39; }</code></td>\n<td>before this week&#39;s Monday</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ operator: &#39;EQUAL&#39;, value: &#39;2026-W47&#39;, week: &#39;iso&#39;, bold: true }</code></td>\n<td>in ISO week 47 of 2026</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Checked when the grid is made, or <code>updateConfig()</code> or <code>setState()</code> is given it - a <code>TypeError</code> for: no\nkind or two of them, an <code>operator</code> the field&#39;s type does not offer, <code>IN</code> / <code>NOT_IN</code> (a rule compares\none value - give each value a rule), a rule without the value its operator needs, a condition on a\nfield the grid does not know, a formula with a problem or that is not true / false, a rule that\ncolours nothing (no <code>color</code>, <code>background</code> or <code>bold</code>), a colour that is no colour of the palette and no\n<code>#rrggbb</code>. A value the field&#39;s formatter can not read (a date in another format) matches no cell.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { ColorRule, GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst negative: ColorRule = { operator: 'LESS_THAN', value: '0', color: 'red' };\nconst columns: GridConfig['columns'] = {\n    balance: { format: { rules: [negative] } },\n    name: {\n        format: {\n            rules: [\n                // the name of a late customer who owes: conditions on other fields\n                {\n                    conditions: [\n                        { field: 'status', operator: 'EQUAL', value: 'late' },\n                        { field: 'balance', operator: 'GREATER_THAN', value: '0' }\n                    ],\n                    background: 'red',\n                    bold: true\n                },\n                // a formula\n                { expression: 'DAYS({due}, TODAY()) &gt; 30', color: '#7c3aed' }\n            ]\n        }\n    }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"background","signatures":["background?: RuleColor"],"doc":"<p>the background of the cell, see <a href=\"#api/index.RuleColor\">RuleColor</a>. Left out: the row&#39;s</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"bold","signatures":["bold?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: the cell&#39;s text is bold</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"color","signatures":["color?: RuleColor"],"doc":"<p>the colour of the cell&#39;s text, see <a href=\"#api/index.RuleColor\">RuleColor</a>. Left out: the grid&#39;s (black or white on a custom background)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"combine","signatures":["combine?: \"AND\" | \"OR\""],"doc":"<p>with <code>conditions</code>: <code>&#39;AND&#39;</code> (the default) all of them are true, <code>&#39;OR&#39;</code> one of them is</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"conditions","signatures":["conditions?: RuleCondition[]"],"doc":"<p>the kind <em>Conditions</em>: conditions on fields of the row, one at least, see <a href=\"#api/index.RuleCondition\">RuleCondition</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datePreset","signatures":["datePreset?: DatePreset"],"doc":"<p>the kind <em>Value</em> on a date: a quick date as the value - its days today, <code>&#39;thisWeek&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;lastMonth&#39;</code>,\n<code>&#39;overdue&#39;</code> ... - compared with <code>operator</code> (not <code>BETWEEN</code>, no <code>value</code>)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"expression","signatures":["expression?: string"],"doc":"<p>the kind <em>Formula</em>: a formula that is true or false, <code>&#39;{balance} &lt; 0 AND {status} = &quot;late&quot;&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"operator","signatures":["operator?: FilterOperator"],"doc":"<p>the kind <em>Value</em>: how the cell&#39;s value is compared with <code>value</code> - an operator of the column&#39;s type,\nnot <code>IN</code> / <code>NOT_IN</code>. A lookup column takes a text&#39;s, it compares its labels</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"value","signatures":["value?: string | [string, string]"],"doc":"<p>the kind <em>Value</em>: what the value is compared with, as it is typed in the header filter: <code>&#39;100&#39;</code>,\n<code>&#39;late&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;2026-11-22&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;true&#39;</code> / <code>&#39;false&#39;</code> for a boolean column. <code>[from, to]</code> for <code>BETWEEN</code> - an\nend <code>&#39;&#39;</code> is open. Left out for <code>IS_BLANK</code> / <code>IS_NOT_BLANK</code>, they take none</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"week","signatures":["week?: RuleWeek"],"doc":"<p>the kind <em>Value</em> on a date: the weeks of <code>value</code> (<code>&#39;2026-W47&#39;</code>) and <code>datePreset</code>, see <a href=\"#api/index.RuleWeek\">RuleWeek</a></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ColorScaleFormat","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ColorScaleFormat"],"doc":"<p>A colour scale of a number column, <code>ColumnFormat.scale</code>: the cell&#39;s background is a mix of two colours\nby the value&#39;s place from the smallest value to the largest - or of three, with a colour of the\nmidpoint. The colours of the palette are its backgrounds, a custom colour is a tint of it: the grid&#39;s\ntext reads on all of them, light and dark.</p>\n<p>The range is from <code>min</code> to <code>max</code>, left out the smallest and the largest value of the rows the filter\nlets through. The midpoint is <code>mid</code>, left out halfway between them. A value out of a fixed range has\nthe colour of its end.</p>\n<p>A colour rule&#39;s background wins over the scale: such a cell has the rule&#39;s.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { ColorScaleFormat, GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// red - yellow - green, as a spreadsheet's: green for the high values\nconst heat: ColorScaleFormat = { minColor: 'red', midColor: 'yellow', maxColor: 'green' };\nconst columns: GridConfig['columns'] = {\n    margin: { format: { scale: heat } },\n    load: { format: { scale: { minColor: 'grey', maxColor: '#7c3aed', min: 0, max: 100 } } }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"max","signatures":["max?: number"],"doc":"<p>the value of <code>maxColor</code>. Left out: the largest value of the rows</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"maxColor","signatures":["maxColor: RuleColor"],"doc":"<p>the colour of the largest value</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"mid","signatures":["mid?: number"],"doc":"<p>with <code>midColor</code>, the value of the midpoint. Left out: halfway between the low and the high end</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"midColor","signatures":["midColor?: RuleColor"],"doc":"<p>the colour of the midpoint: a scale of three colours. Left out: two</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"min","signatures":["min?: number"],"doc":"<p>the value of <code>minColor</code>. Left out: the smallest value of the rows</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"minColor","signatures":["minColor: RuleColor"],"doc":"<p>the colour of the smallest value: a colour of the palette or <code>#rrggbb</code>, see <a href=\"#api/index.RuleColor\">RuleColor</a></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ColumnEditor","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ColumnEditor"],"doc":"<p>How a column&#39;s value is picked from a list, <code>ColumnConfig.editor</code>. Plain JSON: the list is a lookup\nregistered with <a href=\"#api/index.registerLookup\">registerLookup</a>, named by its id.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>type: &#39;select&#39;</code> - a list under the cell, with a search field on top: typing finds the rows whose\nlabel has the text (ignoring case), ArrowUp / ArrowDown, Home / End, PageUp / PageDown move,\nEnter or a click picks, Tab picks and goes to the next cell, Esc closes it.</li>\n<li><code>type: &#39;grid&#39;</code> - a dropdown grid under the cell: the lookup&#39;s datasource in a small grid of its\nown (<code>Lookup.config</code>), or the grid interface it links. The filter row searches as you type,\nEnter picks the highlighted row (the first one found), ArrowDown goes to it and the arrows move\nbetween the rows, Enter or a click on a row picks it, Esc closes it.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Picking writes the value, and the fields of <code>set</code>, in one go: one step of the undo history, Ctrl+Z\ntakes it back.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { ColumnEditor } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst country: ColumnEditor = { type: 'select', lookup: 'countries' };\n// the row's customerName gets the picked customer's name, its city the customer's city\nconst customer: ColumnEditor = { type: 'grid', lookup: 'customers', set: { customerName: 'name', city: 'city' } };</code></pre>\n","samples":["lookups"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"lookup","signatures":["lookup: string"],"doc":"<p>the id of the lookup, see <a href=\"#api/index.registerLookup\">registerLookup</a>. One that is not registered throws a <code>TypeError</code> when the grid is made</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"set","signatures":["set?: Record<string, string>"],"doc":"<p>more fields to copy from the picked row into the edited row: <code>{ &lt;field of the row&gt;: &lt;field of the picked row&gt; }</code>. <code>{ customerName: &#39;name&#39; }</code> gives the row&#39;s <code>customerName</code> the picked row&#39;s <code>name</code>.\nEmptying the cell empties them too. Written as data, also where those cells are readonly</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"type","signatures":["type: \"select\" | \"grid\""],"doc":"<p><code>&#39;select&#39;</code>: a list with a search field, <code>&#39;grid&#39;</code>: a dropdown grid</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ColumnFormat","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ColumnFormat"],"doc":"<p>The display format of a column, <code>ColumnConfig.format</code> and <code>GridState.formats</code>: one plain object (JSON)\nwith a part for the kind of value the column holds - <code>date</code> for a <code>date</code> or <code>datetime</code> field, <code>number</code>\nfor a <code>number</code> field, <code>text</code> for a <code>text</code>, <code>number</code>, <code>date</code> or <code>datetime</code> field, <code>link</code> for a <code>text</code> or\n<code>number</code> field. A part for another type throws a\n<code>TypeError</code>. <code>{}</code> is no format: the field&#39;s formatter.</p>\n<p>Only what the cells show changes - and what follows the cells: the aggregates of a number column, the\nsummary of the selected cells in the footer, Find, the fitted width and the dimmed repeated values.\nThe value stays as it was: a cell that is edited shows the value as the field&#39;s formatter writes it\n(its <code>formatForEdit</code>), a header filter is typed as the cells show it (<code>filterAsShown</code>, a date or\nnumber format; else as the field&#39;s formatter reads it), sorting and grouping use the value, the group rows&#39; names, copy and the CSV export the field&#39;s formatter. The\nExcel export writes the value, with an Excel number format like the display format where Excel has\none - and the colours of the rules, the bars, the scales and the icons (<code>ExcelOptions.colors</code>).</p>\n<p>The templates - <code>text</code> and <code>link.url</code> - are text with <code>{field}</code> placeholders, not\ncode: a saved state can come from anywhere, nothing in a format is run. See the formatting guide,\n&quot;Templates&quot; and &quot;Links&quot;.</p>\n<p>The rest of what the user sets in the grid config dialog is in the format too, so the state\nkeeps it with the rest: the column&#39;s <code>label</code> and the placeholder of its empty cells (<code>placeholderRow</code>),\na number column&#39;s <code>numberOverride</code> (blank as 0, 0 as blank), and <code>checkbox</code> - the cells of a text or\nnumber column as checkboxes. Each wins over the column&#39;s own option (<code>ColumnConfig.label</code>,\n<code>placeholderRow</code>, <code>numberOverride</code>). And <code>rules</code>, the colour rules of any column: a cell&#39;s text\ncolour, background and bold from its value. And for a number column a data bar (<code>bar</code>), a colour scale\n(<code>scale</code>) and an icon set (<code>icons</code>), as a spreadsheet&#39;s conditional formatting.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { ColumnFormat, GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst week: ColumnFormat = { date: 'weekIso' };\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    columns: {\n        born: { format: { date: 'norwegian' } }, // 22.11.2026\n        due: { format: week }, // 2026-W47\n        balance: { format: { number: { decimals: 2, thousands: ' ', decimal: ',' } } }, // 1 234 567,89\n        name: { format: { text: '{name} ({id})' } }, // Ann (12)\n        weight: { format: { number: { decimals: 1 }, text: '{value} kg' } }, // 72.5 kg\n        company: { format: { link: { url: 'https://duckduckgo.com/?q={company}', newTab: true } } },\n        stock: { format: { label: 'In stock', placeholderRowLabel: true, numberOverride: 'ZERO_TO_BLANK' } },\n        newsletter: { format: { checkbox: { checked: '1', unchecked: '0' } } }, // '1' is checked\n        // red text for a negative number, the first rule that matches wins\n        total: { format: { rules: [{ operator: 'LESS_THAN', value: '0', color: 'red' }] } },\n        // a data bar, a colour scale, an icon set: by the value's place among the column's numbers\n        sales: { format: { bar: { color: 'green' }, icons: { set: 'arrows' } } },\n        margin: { format: { scale: { minColor: 'red', midColor: 'yellow', maxColor: 'green' } } }\n    },\n    layout: {\n        center: [\n            { fields: ['born'], width: 100 },\n            { fields: ['due'], width: 100 },\n            { fields: ['balance'], width: 120 },\n            { fields: ['name'], width: 120 },\n            { fields: ['weight'], width: 100 },\n            { fields: ['company'], width: 150 },\n            { fields: ['stock'], width: 80 },\n            { fields: ['newsletter'], width: 80 },\n            { fields: ['total'], width: 100 },\n            { fields: ['sales'], width: 100 },\n            { fields: ['margin'], width: 100 }\n        ]\n    }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"bar","signatures":["bar?: DataBarFormat"],"doc":"<p>a data bar in the cells of a <code>number</code> column: as long as the value&#39;s place in the range of the\ncolumn&#39;s numbers, see <a href=\"#api/index.DataBarFormat\">DataBarFormat</a>: <code>{ color: &#39;green&#39; }</code>. Drawn over a rule&#39;s background.\nLeft out: none. Not with <code>checkbox</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"checkbox","signatures":["checkbox?: CheckboxFormat"],"doc":"<p>the cells of a <code>text</code> or <code>number</code> column are checkboxes, see <a href=\"#api/index.CheckboxFormat\">CheckboxFormat</a>. Not with\n<code>text</code>, <code>link</code>, <code>number</code> or <code>numberOverride</code>: a checkbox shows no text</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"date","signatures":["date?: DateFormat"],"doc":"<p>how a <code>date</code> or <code>datetime</code> column shows its dates, see <a href=\"#api/index.DateFormat\">DateFormat</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"filterAsShown","signatures":["filterAsShown?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>the header filter of a column with a <code>date</code> or <code>number</code> format takes the text as the cells show it,\nsee the filtering guide, &quot;Filter as shown&quot;. Left out (or <code>true</code>): on - <code>2026-W47</code> typed in a column\nshown as <code>weekIso</code> is the whole week, <code>≥ 2026-11</code> from November 1, <code>1 234,5</code> a number. <code>false</code>: the\nheader filter takes the text as the field&#39;s formatter reads it (<code>2026-11-16</code>), as it does without\na format. A format that shows no period of time - <code>&#39;weekday&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;time&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;timeSeconds&#39;</code> - is\nnever filtered as shown. For a <code>date</code>, <code>datetime</code> or <code>number</code> field: true or false.</p>\n<p>A <code>text</code> field with a template (<code>text: &#39;{first} {last}&#39;</code>, a link&#39;s text too) is filtered on the\ntext the template shows - its header filter, the filter menu&#39;s values, IN and every operator - by\ndefault; <code>false</code> filters it on the value. For a backend: <code>gridInterface.getShownFormulas()</code> and\n<code>toSqlWhere({ shown })</code> compare the same text in SQL</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst columns: GridConfig['columns'] = {\n    due: { format: { date: 'weekIso' } }, // `2026-W47` in the header filter is the week\n    born: { format: { date: 'norwegian', filterAsShown: false } } // typed as YYYY-MM-DD\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"icons","signatures":["icons?: IconSetFormat"],"doc":"<p>an icon before (or after) the value of a <code>number</code> column, by thresholds, see <a href=\"#api/index.IconSetFormat\">IconSetFormat</a>:\n<code>{ set: &#39;arrows&#39; }</code>. Shows with the rules&#39; colours. Left out: none. Not with <code>checkbox</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"label","signatures":["label?: string"],"doc":"<p>the column&#39;s label, any column: its header and everywhere the grid names the column - the menus,\nthe column chooser, the filter editor, the footer&#39;s filter, copy with headers and the headers of\nthe CSV and Excel exports. Wins over <code>ColumnConfig.label</code>. Left out: the column&#39;s own label. Not\n<code>&#39;&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"link","signatures":["link?: LinkFormat"],"doc":"<p>the cells of a <code>text</code> or <code>number</code> column are links, see <a href=\"#api/index.LinkFormat\">LinkFormat</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"multiline","signatures":["multiline?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>a <code>text</code> column&#39;s cells as text of several lines (<code>true</code>) - shown on their first line, edited in the\ntext editor, Enter a new line, taller with <code>fitRows()</code> - or of one line (<code>false</code>): only a value with a\nline break is shown as several lines then, as always. Wins over the field&#39;s <code>multiline</code>\n(<code>FieldConfig.multiline</code>). Left out: the field&#39;s. Not for a lookup column, not with <code>checkbox</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"number","signatures":["number?: NumberFormat"],"doc":"<p>how a <code>number</code> column shows its numbers, see <a href=\"#api/index.NumberFormat\">NumberFormat</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"numberOverride","signatures":["numberOverride?: \"NONE\" | \"BLANK_TO_ZERO\" | \"ZERO_TO_BLANK\""],"doc":"<p>what the cells of a <code>number</code> column show for a blank and for 0 - the value is not changed:\n<code>&#39;BLANK_TO_ZERO&#39;</code> a blank as <code>0</code>, <code>&#39;ZERO_TO_BLANK&#39;</code> 0 as an empty cell, <code>&#39;NONE&#39;</code> both as they\nare. Wins over <code>ColumnConfig.numberOverride</code> - <code>&#39;NONE&#39;</code> turns the column&#39;s off. Left out: the\ncolumn&#39;s <code>numberOverride</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"placeholderRow","signatures":["placeholderRow?: string"],"doc":"<p>the placeholder of the column&#39;s empty cells - the text an empty cell shows greyed, what to type in it\n(<code>&#39;Required&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;Name of the customer&#39;</code>) - any column but a <code>boolean</code> one (its cells are checkboxes).\nWins over <code>ColumnConfig.placeholderRow</code>; <code>GridConfig.placeholderRowCurrentEntityOnly</code> shows it on the\ncurrent row only. Left out: the column&#39;s own. Not <code>&#39;&#39;</code>, not with <code>placeholderRowLabel</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"placeholderRowLabel","signatures":["placeholderRowLabel?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: the placeholder of the column&#39;s empty cells is the column&#39;s label, see <code>placeholderRow</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"readonly","signatures":["readonly?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: the column&#39;s cells can not be edited, also in an editable grid; <code>false</code>: they can, as the\ngrid&#39;s other cells. Any column. Wins over <code>ColumnConfig.readonly</code>. Left out: the column&#39;s\n<code>readonly</code>. The <code>isReadonly</code> hook still has the last word, it gets this as its <code>readonly</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rules","signatures":["rules?: ColorRule[]"],"doc":"<p>the colour rules of the column, any column: when a cell&#39;s value matches a rule&#39;s condition - the\nheader filter&#39;s operator and text - the cell has its text colour, background or bold. The first\nrule that matches wins, see <a href=\"#api/index.ColorRule\">ColorRule</a>:\n<code>[{ operator: &#39;LESS_THAN&#39;, value: &#39;0&#39;, color: &#39;red&#39; }]</code>. Left out: the grid&#39;s colours</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"scale","signatures":["scale?: ColorScaleFormat"],"doc":"<p>a colour scale of a <code>number</code> column: the cell&#39;s background by the value&#39;s place from the smallest\nnumber to the largest, see <a href=\"#api/index.ColorScaleFormat\">ColorScaleFormat</a>: <code>{ minColor: &#39;red&#39;, midColor: &#39;yellow&#39;, maxColor: &#39;green&#39; }</code>. A rule&#39;s background wins over it. Left out: none. Not with <code>checkbox</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"text","signatures":["text?: string"],"doc":"<p>what the cells of a <code>text</code>, <code>number</code>, <code>date</code> or <code>datetime</code> column show: a template, text with\n<code>{field}</code> placeholders - each the value of a field of the row as its formatter writes it, <code>{value}</code>\nthe cell&#39;s own, in the column&#39;s <code>number</code> or <code>date</code> format when it has one. <code>&#39;{firstname} {lastname}&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;{value} kg&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;week {value}&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;{company}&#39;</code>. Left out: the cell&#39;s own text. The\ntext of the link too, with <code>link</code>. An edited cell shows the value, not the template. Not <code>&#39;&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ColumnsReport","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ColumnsReport"],"doc":"<p>What <a href=\"#api/index.reconcileColumns\">reconcileColumns</a> changed: for a message to the user, a log</p>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"added","signatures":["added: string[]"],"doc":"<p>the fields the source has that the grid had not: in <code>columns</code> now, the column chooser lists them</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"removed","signatures":["removed: string[]"],"doc":"<p>the fields the grid had that the source has not anymore: taken out of everything that named them</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"removedCalculated","signatures":["removedCalculated: string[]"],"doc":"<p>the calculated columns taken out: their formula named a field that is gone (or such a column)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"removedRules","signatures":["removedRules: RemovedRule[]"],"doc":"<p>the colour rules taken out, with the column they were on: a formula that named a field that is gone,\nor conditions on such fields only. A rule with a condition left keeps it, without the others</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"CreateGridOptions","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface CreateGridOptions<T>"],"doc":"<p>What <a href=\"#api/index.createGrid\">createGrid</a> needs: the config and the datasource, and the hooks if any.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of the rows</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type CreateGridOptions, createGrid, Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst options: CreateGridOptions&lt;{ name: string; locked: boolean }&gt; = {\n    config: { readonly: false, layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 150 }] } },\n    datasource: new Datasource&lt;{ name: string; locked: boolean }&gt;(),\n    hooks: { isReadonly: (row) =&gt; (row.locked ? true : null) }\n};\nconst gridInterface = createGrid(host, options);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"config","signatures":["config: GridConfig"],"doc":"<p>the columns, the layout and the options, see <a href=\"#api/index.GridConfig\">GridConfig</a>. Plain JSON</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datasource","signatures":["datasource: Datasource<T>"],"doc":"<p>the rows, see <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">Datasource</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"hooks","signatures":["hooks?: GridHooks<T>"],"doc":"<p>optional: the functions - <code>isReadonly</code>, <code>cellClass</code> and <code>menus</code>, see <a href=\"#api/index.GridHooks\">GridHooks</a>. Change\nthem later with <code>gridInterface.updateHooks()</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"CsvOptions","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface CsvOptions"],"doc":"<p>What <code>gridInterface.getCsv()</code> and <code>gridInterface.downloadCsv()</code> export, and how. Every option is\noptional, and the object is plain JSON - it can be stored, or come from a menu of your own.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>option</th>\n<th>default</th>\n<th></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>rows</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;all&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;all&#39;</code>: every row the filter lets through, in the sort order. <code>&#39;selected&#39;</code>: the selected rows. <code>&#39;range&#39;</code>: the rows of the selected range of cells</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>fields</code></td>\n<td>the layout (<code>&#39;range&#39;</code>: the range&#39;s)</td>\n<td>the fields to export, in order</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>header</code></td>\n<td><code>true</code></td>\n<td>a first line with the column labels</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>formatted</code></td>\n<td><code>true</code></td>\n<td>the values as the grid shows them; <code>false</code> the values themselves</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>separator</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;,&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;;&#39;</code> for Excel in a locale with a decimal comma</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>bom</code></td>\n<td><code>true</code> for <code>downloadCsv()</code>, <code>false</code> for <code>getCsv()</code></td>\n<td>a UTF-8 byte order mark first</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>escapeFormulas</code></td>\n<td><code>true</code></td>\n<td>text that starts with <code>=</code>, <code>+</code>, <code>-</code>, <code>@</code> ... gets a <code>&#39;</code> in front</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>An option with a value it does not know (<code>rows: &#39;some&#39;</code>, <code>separator: &#39;|&#39;</code>), or a key it does not\nknow, throws a <code>TypeError</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { CsvOptions } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// for Excel in Norway: a semicolon between the fields, and the BOM so it reads æøå\nconst forExcel: CsvOptions = { separator: ';', bom: true };\nconst text = gridInterface.getCsv(forExcel);\n\n// the selected rows, two fields, the values as they are stored\ngridInterface.downloadCsv('selected.csv', { rows: 'selected', fields: ['name', 'born'], formatted: false });\n\n// the cells the user selected (the last range), with a header line of their columns\ngridInterface.downloadCsv('range.csv', { rows: 'range' });</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"bom","signatures":["bom?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>Writes a UTF-8 byte order mark (<code>﻿</code>) first. Excel needs it to read the file as UTF-8,\nwithout it <code>æøå</code> show up garbled. Default <code>true</code> for <code>downloadCsv()</code>, <code>false</code> for <code>getCsv()</code> -\ntext for code of your own does not want it.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"escapeFormulas","signatures":["escapeFormulas?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>Default <code>true</code>: text that starts with <code>=</code>, <code>+</code>, <code>-</code>, <code>@</code>, a tab, CR or LF (or the full width\n<code>＝ ＋ － ＠</code>) gets a <code>&#39;</code> in front, so a spreadsheet shows it as text and does not run it as a\nformula. A value a user typed, <code>=HYPERLINK(&quot;http://evil.example&quot;, &quot;click&quot;)</code>, would else run on\nthe computer of whoever opens the file - &quot;CSV injection&quot;,\n<a href=\"https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/CSV_Injection\">https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/CSV_Injection</a>.</p>\n<p>Only text is escaped: a value that is text in the row (a string, or an object), and the labels.\nA number, a boolean, a <code>Date</code> and a blank never are, whatever their formatter writes - <code>-5</code>\nstays <code>-5</code>. The value decides, not the field&#39;s type: keep the numbers of a number field as\nnumbers, one holding the text <code>&#39;-5&#39;</code> is written as <code>&#39;-5</code>. Text that only looks like a formula\ngets the <code>&#39;</code> too: a phone number <code>+47 912 34 567</code> is written <code>&#39;+47 912 34 567</code>.</p>\n<p>The <code>&#39;</code> is part of the text in the file, a program that reads it gets it too. OWASP notes that\nthe escaping is not reliable in Excel once the file is saved and opened again, so treat a file\nof data users typed with care anyway.</p>\n<p><code>false</code> writes the text as it is: for a file that is read by a program, not opened in a\nspreadsheet.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"fields","signatures":["fields?: string[]"],"doc":"<p>The fields to export, in this order, a column each. Default the fields of the layout now, in\nthe order the user sees them: pinned left, center, pinned right, and a column of stacked fields\ngives a CSV column for each of its fields, top to bottom - <code>gridInterface.getLayoutFields()</code>.\nThe hidden columns (<code>getHiddenFields()</code>) are not in the layout, so they are left out. With\n<code>rows: &#39;range&#39;</code> the default is the fields of the range.</p>\n<p>Any field of the rows can be given, also one that is not in the grid.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"formatted","signatures":["formatted?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>Default <code>true</code>: each value as the grid shows it, the text of the field&#39;s formatter - <code>12,5</code> with\nthe <code>numberComma</code> formatter, a date as <code>2026-11-20</code> (or as its formatter writes it), a boolean\nas <code>true</code> / <code>false</code>. A column&#39;s <code>numberOverride</code> (<code>ZERO_TO_BLANK</code>, <code>BLANK_TO_ZERO</code>) and\n<code>dynamicCellTypeColumn</code> are followed, as in the cells.</p>\n<p><code>false</code>: the values as they are stored - a number with a dot (<code>String(12.5)</code>), a <code>Date</code> as\n<code>toISOString()</code> (UTC: a date at midnight in Norway is the day before at 23:00 or 22:00), a\nboolean as <code>true</code> / <code>false</code>, a blank (null, undefined, <code>&#39;&#39;</code>, an invalid Date) as nothing.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"header","signatures":["header?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>A first line with the label of each column, default <code>true</code>: the label the grid&#39;s header shows -\nthe column&#39;s <code>label</code>, else the datasource field&#39;s <code>label</code>, else the field name prettified\n(<code>first_name</code> is <code>First Name</code>).</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rows","signatures":["rows?: \"all\" | \"selected\" | \"range\""],"doc":"<p>Which rows, default <code>&#39;all&#39;</code>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&#39;all&#39;</code>: every row the filter lets through, in the sort order - <code>datasource.getDataRows()</code>.\nWhen grouped, every data row in the grouped order, the rows of collapsed groups included; no\ngroup rows</li>\n<li><code>&#39;selected&#39;</code>: the selected rows, in the same order - <code>datasource.getSelectedRows()</code>. That is\nthe selected rows that are displayed: a selected row in a collapsed group is left out, as the\nrow menu&#39;s actions on the selected rows leave it out. Nothing selected gives the header only</li>\n<li><code>&#39;range&#39;</code>: the selected range of cells - the last of <code>gridInterface.getRanges()</code>, the one made\nlast: its data rows top to bottom (a group row in it is left out) and, unless <code>fields</code> is\ngiven, its fields left to right. No range gives an empty text (no fields, no rows)</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"separator","signatures":["separator?: CsvSeparator"],"doc":"<p>Between the fields, default <code>&#39;,&#39;</code> (RFC 4180). Excel uses the list separator of the computer&#39;s\nlocale when it opens a .csv file: in a locale with a decimal comma (Norwegian, German ...) that\nis <code>&#39;;&#39;</code>, and a file with <code>&#39;,&#39;</code> opens with every row in one column. Use <code>&#39;;&#39;</code> for those users.\n<code>&#39;\\t&#39;</code> gives tab separated text.</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"DataBarFormat","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface DataBarFormat"],"doc":"<p>A data bar of a number column, <code>ColumnFormat.bar</code>: a bar in the cell&#39;s background as long as the value&#39;s\nplace in the range - the number stays readable over it, the bar is a light tint (a dark one in dark mode).</p>\n<p>The range is from <code>min</code> to <code>max</code>. Left out, they are the smallest and the largest value of the rows the\nfilter lets through, and 0 is in it: the bars start at 0, a negative value&#39;s bar goes to the left of\nthe axis where 0 is. A value out of a fixed range is drawn as its end.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>bar</th>\n<th>0 to 100</th>\n<th>-50 to 50</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>{}</code></td>\n<td>50 is half the cell, from the left</td>\n<td>0 is in the middle, -25 a quarter to the left of it</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ min: 0, max: 200 }</code></td>\n<td>100 is half the cell</td>\n<td>-50 no bar, 50 a quarter</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { DataBarFormat, GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst sales: DataBarFormat = { color: 'green' };\nconst columns: GridConfig['columns'] = {\n    total: { format: { bar: sales } },\n    progress: { format: { bar: { color: '#0f766e', min: 0, max: 100 } } }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"color","signatures":["color?: RuleColor"],"doc":"<p>the bar&#39;s colour: a colour of the palette - its background, see <a href=\"#api/index.PaletteColor\">PaletteColor</a> - or a custom\ncolour <code>#rrggbb</code>, drawn as a tint of it. Left out: <code>&#39;blue&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"max","signatures":["max?: number"],"doc":"<p>the value of a whole bar. Left out: the largest value of the rows, or 0 when that is below 0</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"min","signatures":["min?: number"],"doc":"<p>the value of the bar&#39;s low end. Left out: the smallest value of the rows, or 0 when that is above 0</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"DataEntity","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface DataEntity extends Entity"],"doc":"<p>A row of data, not a group row: the DataContainer wraps every one of them in an EntityHandler\nproxy, so it always has its controller. An <a href=\"#api/index.Entity\">Entity</a> with <code>__controller</code> set.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { DataEntity } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst isEdited = (row: DataEntity) =&gt; row.__controller.__edited === true;</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"__controller","signatures":["__controller: EntityHandler"],"doc":"<p>the object that tracks the row&#39;s edits: its original values, <code>__isNew</code>, <code>__isDeleted</code>,\n<code>__edited</code>. Read it, do not change it - see <a href=\"#api/index.EntityHandler\">EntityHandler</a></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"DatasourceEvents","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface DatasourceEvents"],"doc":"<p>The events of a <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">Datasource</a>: event name -&gt; the payload its handler gets.</p>\n<p>Subscribe with <code>datasource.on(name, handler)</code>, the payload is typed from this map.\n<code>on()</code> returns a function that unsubscribes. Events with nothing to tell send an empty object.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const off = datasource.on('collection-filtered', (data) =&gt; {\n    console.log(data.info, datasource.getDataRows().length, 'rows left');\n});\ndatasource.on('selection-change', () =&gt; {\n    console.log(datasource.getSelectedRows().length, 'rows selected');\n});\noff(); // unsubscribe</code></pre>\n","samples":["events"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"collection-changed","signatures":["'collection-changed': { added?: boolean; data?: Entity | Entity[] | null; info?: \"removeData\" | \"clearMarkedForDeletion\" | \"upsert\"; removed?: true }"],"doc":"<p>Rows were added, replaced or removed.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>setData()</code>: <code>{ added }</code> - <code>true</code> when rows were added, <code>false</code> when they replaced the data</li>\n<li><code>addNewEmpty()</code>: <code>{ added: true }</code></li>\n<li><code>removeData()</code>: <code>{ removed: true, info: &#39;removeData&#39;, data }</code> - <code>data</code> is what was passed in</li>\n<li><code>removeAllData()</code>: <code>{ removed: true, info: &#39;removeData&#39;, data: null }</code></li>\n<li><code>clearMarkedForDeletion()</code>: <code>{ removed: true, info: &#39;clearMarkedForDeletion&#39; }</code></li>\n<li><code>upsert()</code>: <code>{ info: &#39;upsert&#39;, added }</code>, with <code>removed: true</code> when it removed rows. Only when it\nadded or removed rows, or the displayed rows changed (the filter, the sort order or the groups).\nAn upsert that only changed values sends none: <code>rows-changed</code> has the rows</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"collection-collapse","signatures":["'collection-collapse': Record<string, never>"],"doc":"<p><code>collapseGroup()</code> collapsed one or all groups. Empty payload.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"collection-expand","signatures":["'collection-expand': Record<string, never>"],"doc":"<p><code>expandGroup()</code> expanded one or all groups. Empty payload.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"collection-filtered","signatures":["'collection-filtered': { info: \"markForDeletion\" | \"unmarkForDeletion\" | \"acceptChanges\" | \"filter\" | \"resetData\" | \"__internalUpdate, forced\" }"],"doc":"<p>The displayed rows were rebuilt. <code>info</code> says by what:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&#39;filter&#39;</code>: <code>filter()</code> or <code>reloadDatasource()</code></li>\n<li><code>&#39;resetData&#39;</code>: <code>resetData()</code> or <code>resetDataSelectionOnly()</code></li>\n<li><code>&#39;markForDeletion&#39;</code>: <code>markForDeletion()</code> or <code>markAllForDeletion()</code></li>\n<li><code>&#39;unmarkForDeletion&#39;</code>: <code>unmarkForDeletion()</code> or <code>unmarkAllForDeletion()</code></li>\n<li><code>&#39;acceptChanges&#39;</code>: <code>acceptChanges()</code> - also when it removed rows, it sends no <code>collection-changed</code></li>\n<li><code>&#39;__internalUpdate, forced&#39;</code>: <code>setData(rows, { refilter: false })</code> or <code>addNewEmpty()</code> while\nthere is no filter, sorting or grouping. Sent before their <code>collection-changed</code>. A <code>setData()</code>\nthat runs the filter (the default) sends only <code>collection-changed</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"collection-grouped","signatures":["'collection-grouped': { groupings?: GroupArgument[]; info: \"group\" | \"removeGroup\" }"],"doc":"<p>The grouping changed.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>group()</code>: <code>{ info: &#39;group&#39;, groupings }</code> - the grouping now applied</li>\n<li><code>removeGroup()</code>: <code>{ info: &#39;removeGroup&#39; }</code>, after the <code>&#39;group&#39;</code> event of the grouping that is left</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"collection-sorted","signatures":["'collection-sorted': Record<string, never>"],"doc":"<p><code>sort()</code> ran. Empty payload.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"conflicts-changed","signatures":["'conflicts-changed': Record<string, never>"],"doc":"<p>The conflicts changed: <code>upsert()</code> made one, or one went - resolved with <code>resolveConflict()</code>, the\nfield is not edited any more, the row was saved (<code>acceptChanges()</code>), reset, or left the data.\nSent once the code that changed them is done (in a microtask), after <code>rows-changed</code>. Empty\npayload, read <code>datasource.getConflicts()</code>.</p>\n<p>The conflicts are the data container&#39;s: every datasource on the same <code>DataContainer</code> sends it.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"current-entity","signatures":["'current-entity': Record<string, never>"],"doc":"<p><code>datasource.currentEntity</code> was set: a row was clicked or selected, or\n<code>setRowAsCurrentEntity()</code> was called. Also when <code>setData()</code> set it to <code>null</code> because the current\nrow is no longer in the data, and when a method that removes rows removed it (<code>removeData()</code>,\n<code>removeAllData()</code>, <code>clearMarkedForDeletion()</code>, <code>acceptChanges()</code>, <code>resetData()</code>,\n<code>resetDataSelectionOnly()</code>) - sent after their own event. Empty payload, read\n<code>datasource.currentEntity</code>.\nWas <code>currentEntity</code> in v5.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"fields-change","signatures":["'fields-change': Record<string, never>"],"doc":"<p><code>setFields()</code> replaced the fields: their types, labels, formatters and rules. Sent before the rows\nare filtered, sorted and grouped again by them (<code>collection-filtered</code>). Empty payload, read\n<code>getField()</code>.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"history-changed","signatures":["'history-changed': { info: \"edit\" | \"undo\" | \"redo\" | \"clear\" | \"remove\" }"],"doc":"<p>The undo/redo history changed: read <code>canUndo()</code> and <code>canRedo()</code>, e.g. to enable Undo and Redo\nbuttons of your own. <code>info</code> says what changed it:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&#39;edit&#39;</code>: a step was recorded - an edit, a paste, a clear, a (un)mark for deletion, a revert.\nSent once the code that made it is done (in a microtask): one event per step, also for a paste\nover many rows. Also when what the user typed in a cell went back to the value it started from,\nand its step was dropped</li>\n<li><code>&#39;undo&#39;</code>: <code>undo()</code> took a step back. The grid renders its cells again</li>\n<li><code>&#39;redo&#39;</code>: <code>redo()</code> did a step again. The grid renders its cells again</li>\n<li><code>&#39;clear&#39;</code>: the history was emptied - <code>clearHistory()</code>, <code>setData()</code> without <code>add</code>,\n<code>removeAllData()</code>, <code>resetData()</code>, <code>acceptChanges()</code>. Only when there was something in it</li>\n<li><code>&#39;remove&#39;</code>: rows were removed for good (<code>removeData()</code>, <code>clearMarkedForDeletion()</code>, a new row\nremoved by <code>resetDataSelectionOnly()</code>, <code>upsert(rows, { removeMissing: true })</code>) and their changes\nleft the history. Or <code>upsert()</code> gave fields the server&#39;s value as their original, and a change\nthat does nothing now was dropped (see <code>upsert()</code>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The history is the data container&#39;s: every datasource on the same container sends it, for a\nchange made through any of them.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rows-changed","signatures":["'rows-changed': { fields: ReadonlyMap<Entity, ReadonlySet<string>>; rows: Entity[] }"],"doc":"<p>Values of rows changed, or what the grid shows of them: sent once the code that changed them is\ndone (in a microtask) - one event however many rows and fields it set. The grid renders the rows\nof it that are on screen, in the next animation frame: a value set from code shows without\n<code>gridInterface.refresh()</code>.</p>\n<p>A row is in it when:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>a field was set on it: from code (<code>row.price = 10</code>), by the user in the grid, by <code>undo()</code> /\n<code>redo()</code>, <code>resetField()</code>, <code>resetRows()</code>, <code>resetData()</code>, <code>resolveConflict()</code>, or by <code>upsert()</code></li>\n<li>its deletion mark changed (<code>markForDeletion()</code>, undo ...) or its server error (<code>setErrors()</code>)</li>\n<li>one of its conflicts came or went</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The rows <code>upsert()</code> or <code>setData()</code> added and the rows removed are not in it: <code>collection-changed</code>\ntells those. A row in it can have left the data since it changed.</p>\n<p>The rows are the data container&#39;s: every datasource on the same <code>DataContainer</code> sends it, for a\nchange made through any of them.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"select","signatures":["select: { info: \"select-first\" | \"select-prev\" | \"select-next\" | \"select-last\"; row: number }"],"doc":"<p>A row was selected from code, the grid scrolls it into view.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code>: index in the displayed rows (<code>datasource.getRows()</code>), 0 based</li>\n<li><code>info</code>: what selected it - <code>select(row, { notify: true })</code> sends <code>&#39;select-first&#39;</code>, <code>selectFirst()</code>\n<code>&#39;select-first&#39;</code>, <code>selectPrev()</code> <code>&#39;select-prev&#39;</code>, <code>selectNext()</code> <code>&#39;select-next&#39;</code>,\n<code>selectLast()</code> <code>&#39;select-last&#39;</code></li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"selection-change","signatures":["'selection-change': Record<string, never>"],"doc":"<p>The selected rows changed. Also when a method that removes rows removed a selected one (see\n<code>current-entity</code>), sent after its own event. Empty payload, read <code>datasource.getSelectedRows()</code>.\nWas <code>selectionChange</code> in v5.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"validate","signatures":["validate: { errors: ValidationError<unknown>[] }"],"doc":"<p><code>datasource.validate()</code> ran: <code>errors</code> is what it returned. The grid renders its rows again, to\nshow the errors. An edit sends no event, though it is validated: read <code>getErrors()</code> when you\nneed them.</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"DatasourceOptions","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface DatasourceOptions"],"doc":"<p>Options for <code>new Datasource(options)</code>. All of them are optional, <code>new Datasource()</code> works.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>key</code> - the field that identifies a row. Selection follows the key, so it survives replacing\nthe data with fresh rows from the server, and <code>upsert()</code> merges rows from a server by it.</li>\n<li><code>fields</code> - the schema: the type, label and formatter of each field. A field that is not listed\nis <code>&#39;text&#39;</code>, labelled with its name. Sorting, grouping, filtering and the grid all read the\ntype from here. See <a href=\"#api/index.FieldConfig\">FieldConfig</a> and <a href=\"#api/index.FieldType\">FieldType</a>.</li>\n<li><code>formatters</code> - the default formatter per type, for the fields without a formatter of their own.\nThe types left out keep the built-in default (see <a href=\"#api/index.FieldType\">FieldType</a>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A formatter is named by its id, a built-in one or one registered with <a href=\"#api/index.registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a>:\n<code>fields</code> and <code>formatters</code> are plain JSON, they can be stored (in a backend, say) and given back\nas they are. An id that is not registered throws when the datasource is made.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>selectionMode</code> - <code>&#39;multiple&#39;</code> (default), <code>&#39;single&#39;</code> or <code>&#39;none&#39;</code>. A grid showing the datasource\nuses it, change it later with <code>setSelectionMode()</code>.</li>\n<li><code>container</code> - share the data with another datasource, each with its own filter, sort, grouping\nand selection. Rows added or removed through one show in the other after its\n<code>reloadDatasource()</code> (or a <code>filter()</code>) - they are not kept in sync on their own. Give the key to the container\n(<code>new DataContainer(&#39;id&#39;)</code>); a <code>key</code> that is not the container&#39;s throws. The edits are tracked\nby the container, with the field types of every datasource on it (a <code>date</code> field compares on\nthe day): a field listed by two of them must have the same type in both, the second datasource\nthrows if not. A field listed by one only has that one&#39;s type.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer, Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    key: 'id',\n    fields: {\n        id: 'number',\n        name: { label: 'Name' },\n        born: { type: 'date', label: 'Born' },\n        salary: { type: 'number', formatter: 'numberComma' },\n        active: 'boolean'\n    },\n    formatters: {\n        date: 'dateDDMMYYYY' // every date field without a formatter of its own\n    },\n    selectionMode: 'single'\n});\n\n// a second datasource on the same rows\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\nconst left = new Datasource({ container, fields: { born: 'date' } });\nconst right = new Datasource({ container, fields: { born: 'date' } });</code></pre>\n","samples":["formatters"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"container","signatures":["container?: DataContainer"],"doc":"<p>the data container to use, to share the rows with another datasource. Default a new one.\nA field in <code>fields</code> must have the same type as in the other datasources on the container.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"fields","signatures":["fields?: Record<string, FieldType | FieldConfig>"],"doc":"<p>the fields: <code>{ born: &#39;date&#39;, age: { type: &#39;number&#39;, label: &#39;Age&#39; } }</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"formatters","signatures":["formatters?: Partial<Record<FieldType, string>>"],"doc":"<p>the id of the default formatter for each type, used by the fields that have no formatter of\ntheir own: <code>{ number: &#39;numberComma&#39;, date: &#39;dateDDMMYYYY&#39; }</code>. See <a href=\"#api/index.registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a> for\nthe ids</p>\n","samples":["formatters"]},{"name":"key","signatures":["key?: string"],"doc":"<p>the field that identifies a row, e.g. <code>&#39;id&#39;</code>. Rows without it get a generated key. <code>upsert()</code>\nneeds it</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"selectionMode","signatures":["selectionMode?: SelectionMode"],"doc":"<p>how rows can be selected, default <code>&#39;multiple&#39;</code>. A grid showing the datasource uses it</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"DateEvents","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface DateEvents"],"doc":"<p>The events of a <a href=\"#api/index.DateInterface\">DateInterface</a>: event name -&gt; the payload its handler gets.</p>\n<p>Subscribe with <code>dateInterface.on(name, handler)</code>, the payload is typed from this map.\n<code>on()</code> returns a function that unsubscribes. Removing the date element from the dom\nunsubscribes every handler.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\nconst off = dateInterface.on('date-select', (date) =&gt; {\n    console.log(date ? date.toISOString() : 'cleared');\n});\noff(); // unsubscribe</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"date-select","signatures":["'date-select': Date | null"],"doc":"<p>A date was picked in the date picker (<code>datepicker: true</code>): the &quot;Use&quot; button sends the\npicked date and time, the &quot;Clear&quot; button sends <code>null</code>. Clicking a day only picks it, &quot;Now&quot; goes\nto the current date and time; neither sends the event. A calendar (<code>datepicker: false</code>) never\nsends it - read <code>dateInterface.getSelected()</code>.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"range-select","signatures":["'range-select': [Date | null, Date | null] | null"],"doc":"<p>A range was picked in a range picker (<code>rangepicker: true</code>): the &quot;Use&quot; button sends <code>[from, to]</code>,\nthe days picked at 00:00, From never after To. An end not picked is null - an open end: <code>[from, null]</code> after one click, <code>[null, null]</code> when no day was clicked. The &quot;Clear&quot; button sends <code>null</code>.\nClicking the days only picks them, neither sends the event.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\ndateInterface.on('range-select', (range) =&gt; {\n    if (!range) {\n        console.log('cleared');\n        return;\n    }\n    const [from, to] = range;\n    console.log(from?.toDateString() ?? 'open', to?.toDateString() ?? 'open');\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"DetailForm","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface DetailForm"],"doc":"<p>The detail form: a panel inside the grid, at the right of the rows, with the current row\n(<code>datasource.currentEntity</code>) as a form - a label and a value for each field of <code>fields</code>, in that\norder. <code>GridConfig.detailForm</code> is the one the grid starts with, <code>GridState.detailForm</code> the one it\nshows: the user changes it in the grid config dialog (the gear in the footer, tab <em>Detail form</em>).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The values</strong> are what the cells show: the display format, a template, a lookup&#39;s label. A text of\nseveral lines (<code>FieldConfig.multiline</code>, or a value with a line break) has a tall field with all of\nit. A row with a link (<code>ColumnFormat.link</code>) has the link beside the value.</li>\n<li><strong>Editing</strong>: in an editable grid a field is edited as its cell is - the same readonly rules\n(<code>readonly</code>, <code>edit</code>, <code>ColumnConfig.readonly</code>, the <code>isReadonly</code> hook, <code>allowPasteClearOnly</code>), the value\nparsed by the field&#39;s formatter and validated, the errors under the field, and what is typed in a\nfield is one step of the undo history. A lookup column (<code>ColumnConfig.editor</code>) is shown, not edited:\nits cell picks the value.</li>\n<li><strong>It follows the grid</strong>: another current row, a value changed (an edit, undo, <code>upsert()</code>, code), a\nfilter or a sort. Without a current row - or one that is filtered out - it says so.</li>\n<li><strong>A narrow grid</strong> - where the rows would get less room than the form beside it, or the scrolling\ncolumns less than 150px (a phone, wide pinned columns) - has the form under the rows instead, 40 % of\nthe grid&#39;s height.</li>\n<li><strong>Collapsed</strong> (<code>expanded: false</code>) it is a narrow strip at the right of the rows - a bar over the\nfooter under them - with its title: the button of its title bar expands it, and collapses it again.</li>\n<li><strong>Its width</strong>: the user drags the form&#39;s left edge (or its arrow keys) between <code>minWidth</code> and\n<code>maxWidth</code>, and sets all three in the grid config dialog. The width dragged is <code>width</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Plain JSON, part of the state: <code>getState()</code> gives it, <code>setState({ detailForm })</code> sets it - what the user\nchanged with it: the fields, the width dragged, collapsed or expanded.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { DetailForm } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst detailForm: DetailForm = { show: true, fields: ['company', 'notes', 'orderDate'], width: 300 };\ngridInterface.setState({ detailForm });\ngridInterface.getState().detailForm; // { show: true, fields: ['company', 'notes', 'orderDate'], width: 300 }\n\n// collapsed to a strip, between 200 and 500px when the user drags it wider\ngridInterface.setState({ detailForm: { ...detailForm, expanded: false, minWidth: 200, maxWidth: 500 } });</code></pre>\n","samples":["detail-form"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"expanded","signatures":["expanded?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>false</code>: collapsed, a narrow strip with the form&#39;s title - the button in its title bar expands it.\nDefault <code>true</code>. The button changes it, so a saved state keeps what the user made it last; the grid\nconfig dialog has it too (<em>Expanded</em>)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"fieldOptions","signatures":["fieldOptions?: Record<string, DetailFormFieldOptions>"],"doc":"<p>the options of the fields of <code>fields</code>, under the field&#39;s name - the lines of a multiline field, the\nroom above and under it. See <a href=\"#api/index.DetailFormFieldOptions\">DetailFormFieldOptions</a>. Default none: a field without an entry\nis a label and a value</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"fields","signatures":["fields: (string | DetailFormSection)[]"],"doc":"<p>the fields it shows, in this order: fields of the columns, or any field of the rows - and sections\nbetween them (<a href=\"#api/index.DetailFormSection\">DetailFormSection</a>): a section has the fields after it, up to the next one</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"maxWidth","signatures":["maxWidth?: number"],"doc":"<p>the most width in px a drag (and <code>width</code>) gives the form, default none - the rows keep their room</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"minWidth","signatures":["minWidth?: number"],"doc":"<p>the least width in px a drag (and <code>width</code>) gives the form, default and at least 150</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"show","signatures":["show: boolean"],"doc":"<p>shows the form</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"width","signatures":["width?: number"],"doc":"<p>its width in px, default 300 - laid out between <code>minWidth</code> and <code>maxWidth</code>. The user changes it by\ndragging the form&#39;s left edge</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"DetailFormFieldOptions","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface DetailFormFieldOptions"],"doc":"<p>The options of one field of the detail form, in <code>DetailForm.fieldOptions</code> under the field&#39;s name. Every\noption is optional. The grid config dialog (tab <em>Detail form</em>) sets them for the field picked in its list.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>minRows</code></strong> - the least lines a field of several lines (<code>FieldConfig.multiline</code>, or a value with a\nline break) has, 1 to 30, default 3. It grows with its text. Ignored on a field of one line</li>\n<li><strong><code>paddingTop</code></strong>, <strong><code>paddingBottom</code></strong> - room in px above and under the field, default 0</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Sections are entries of <code>DetailForm.fields</code>, see <a href=\"#api/index.DetailFormSection\">DetailFormSection</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { DetailForm } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst detailForm: DetailForm = {\n    show: true,\n    fields: ['company', 'notes'],\n    fieldOptions: { company: { paddingBottom: 8 }, notes: { minRows: 6 } }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"minRows","signatures":["minRows?: number"],"doc":"<p>the least lines of a field of several lines, 1 to 30, default 3</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"paddingBottom","signatures":["paddingBottom?: number"],"doc":"<p>room in px under the field, default 0</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"paddingTop","signatures":["paddingTop?: number"],"doc":"<p>room in px above the field, default 0</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"DetailFormSection","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface DetailFormSection"],"doc":"<p>A section of the detail form: an entry of <code>DetailForm.fields</code> between the field names. It has the\nfields after it, up to the next section; the fields before the first section are in none.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>section</code></strong> - its name, in its header. The header is a button that collapses the section and\nexpands it again</li>\n<li><strong><code>panel</code></strong> - <code>true</code>: a panel - a frame around its header and its fields, on a background of its own.\nDefault <code>false</code>: a header with a line under it</li>\n<li><strong><code>collapsed</code></strong> - <code>true</code>: it starts collapsed, its header only. Default <code>false</code>: it starts open. The\nheader&#39;s button opens and closes it while the form shows these fields and sections - the user&#39;s, not\nthe state&#39;s: <code>collapsed</code> stays the default, and a detail form set again (<code>setState</code>, the dialog&#39;s\nApply, <code>resetState()</code>) starts from it</li>\n<li><strong><code>paddingTop</code></strong>, <strong><code>paddingBottom</code></strong> - room in px above and under the section, default 0</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The grid config dialog (tab <em>Detail form</em>) adds sections to the list of the fields (<em>Add section</em>), they\nare moved as the fields are, and sets these for the section picked.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { DetailForm } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst detailForm: DetailForm = {\n    show: true,\n    fields: [\n        'company',\n        { section: 'Address', panel: true, paddingTop: 8 },\n        'country',\n        'city',\n        { section: 'Notes', collapsed: true },\n        'notes'\n    ],\n    fieldOptions: { notes: { minRows: 6 } }\n};\ngridInterface.setState({ detailForm });</code></pre>\n","samples":["detail-form"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"collapsed","signatures":["collapsed?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: it starts collapsed, its header only - default <code>false</code>, open. The header&#39;s button opens and closes it</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"paddingBottom","signatures":["paddingBottom?: number"],"doc":"<p>room in px under it, default 0</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"paddingTop","signatures":["paddingTop?: number"],"doc":"<p>room in px above it, default 0</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"panel","signatures":["panel?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: a frame around it, on a background of its own - default a header with a line under it</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"section","signatures":["section: string"],"doc":"<p>its name, in its header</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"EditPermissions","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface EditPermissions"],"doc":"<p>What the user may do in an editable grid, <code>GridConfig.edit</code>: each permission <code>true</code> (the default) or\n<code>false</code>. They are about the grid&#39;s own ways of editing - the user&#39;s typing, the menus, the keys. Code\nof yours that sets a value, <code>datasource.addNewEmpty()</code>, <code>markForDeletion()</code> ... is not stopped: an\n&quot;Add row&quot; or &quot;Delete&quot; button of your own follows these as you make it. <code>gridInterface.fillDown()</code>\ngoes through the grid, it follows them.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>change: false</code></strong> - the values of the rows that were there can not be changed: no typing, no\neditor (text, date picker, lookup list or grid, a custom cell&#39;s), no checkbox, no paste, no clear, no\nfill down (Ctrl+D, the fill handle), nothing in the detail form. The cells look as in a readonly\ngrid - no stripes. <strong>A new row</strong> (added and not saved yet, <code>__rowState</code> <code>&#39;N&#39;</code>) can be filled in when\n<code>add</code> is allowed: who may add a row may fill it in. Once <code>acceptChanges()</code> takes it in, it is a row\nthat was there.</li>\n<li><strong><code>delete: false</code></strong> - the rows that were there can not be marked for deletion: the row menu&#39;s\n<em>Delete ›</em> entries are greyed out on them, Delete on a row number leaves them. A new row can still\nbe taken out: it is not on the server, nothing is deleted - it is the undo of an add.</li>\n<li><strong><code>add: false</code></strong> - the grid has no way of its own to add a row, so this is for your add button,\nand for the new rows your code adds: with <code>change: false</code> too they can not be filled in.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>What still works</strong>, whatever they say: undo and redo (Ctrl+Z, the row menu) - the history has only\nwhat the user was allowed to do, and your code&#39;s edits; the reverts (<em>Undo cell edit</em>, <em>Undo row\nedits</em>, a click on the marker of an edited cell); taking the deletion mark off. They put back what\nwas, they make nothing new. A permission taken away while the grid is shown leaves the history as it\nis: call <code>datasource.clearHistory()</code> too when a redo must not bring back what was done before.</p>\n<p>The column&#39;s <code>readonly</code>, the <code>isReadonly</code> hook and <code>allowPasteClearOnly</code> still make cells readonly\nwhere a permission allows the change. Unlike them, the hook can not make a cell editable that a\npermission locks - and the user can not either: a column&#39;s readonly is a default the user changes\nin the grid config dialog (<em>Read only</em>), the permissions are not in it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { EditPermissions } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const user: { canDelete: boolean };\n\n// values and new rows, deleting for some users only\nconst edit: EditPermissions = { delete: user.canDelete };\ngridInterface.updateConfig({ readonly: false, edit });\n\n// look, and delete rows - nothing else\ngridInterface.updateConfig({ edit: { add: false, change: false, delete: true } });\n\ngridInterface.updateConfig({ edit: undefined }); // all three again</code></pre>\n","samples":["edit-permissions"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"add","signatures":["add?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>the user may add rows, default <code>true</code>. The grid adds none itself: this is for your add button.\nWhile it is allowed a new row can be filled in with <code>change: false</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"change","signatures":["change?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>the user may change the values of the rows that were there, default <code>true</code>: typing, the editors,\npaste, clear, fill down, the detail form. A new row follows <code>add</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"delete","signatures":["delete?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>the user may mark the rows that were there for deletion, default <code>true</code>: the row menu&#39;s <em>Delete ›</em>,\nDelete on a row number. A new row can always be taken out</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"Entity","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface Entity"],"doc":"<p>A data row: one of your objects, as the datasource hands it out. Group header rows are not\nentities, see <a href=\"#api/index.GroupRow\">GroupRow</a>.</p>\n<p>The row is your object wrapped in a <code>Proxy</code>. Your own fields are read and set as usual, setting one\nis an edit (<code>datasource.getChanges()</code>). The <code>__</code> fields below are not stored on your object: the\nproxy answers them, so <code>Object.keys(row)</code> and <code>JSON.stringify(row)</code> show your fields only.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const row = datasource.getDataRows()[0];\nrow.name = 'Anna'; // an edit\nrow.__rowState; // 'M'\nrow.__KEY; // the key, e.g. the row's id</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"__controller","signatures":["__controller?: EntityHandler"],"doc":"<p>the object that tracks the row&#39;s edits: its original values, <code>__isNew</code>, <code>__isDeleted</code>,\n<code>__edited</code>. Read it, do not change it - see <a href=\"#api/index.EntityHandler\">EntityHandler</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__group","signatures":["__group?: undefined"],"doc":"<p>A data row never has <code>__group</code>, only a <a href=\"#api/index.GroupRow\">GroupRow</a> has it (<code>true</code>). Declared so the two\ntypes stay apart: a group row can not be passed where an entity is expected, and\n<code>row.__group</code> tells them apart. <a href=\"#api/index.isGroupRow\">isGroupRow</a> is the readable way to check.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupLvl","signatures":["__groupLvl?: number"],"doc":"<p>Written by grouping: how many group levels the row sits under, the number of fields grouped on -\n0 when the rows are not grouped. A row in the container of two datasources (<code>container</code>) has the\nlevel of the one that grouped or ungrouped it last. The grid shows nothing from it on a data row.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__KEY","signatures":["__KEY?: string | number"],"doc":"<p>the row&#39;s key: the value of the key field (<code>new Datasource({ key: &#39;id&#39; })</code>), which reading and\nsetting <code>__KEY</code> go to. Without a key field a generated negative number. The selection and\n<code>setErrors()</code> use it</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__rowError","signatures":["__rowError?: string | null"],"doc":"<p>an error message for the row from a server, set with <code>datasource.getDataContainer().setErrors()</code>.\n<code>null</code> or <code>undefined</code> for no error. Apart from the validation errors (<code>datasource.getErrors()</code>).\nThe grid shows it on the row selector, with the validation errors: the error class, and the\nmessage as the tooltip</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__rowState","signatures":["__rowState?: string"],"doc":"<p>the row&#39;s state: <code>&#39;N&#39;</code> new (<code>addNewEmpty()</code>), <code>&#39;D&#39;</code> marked for deletion (a new row too), <code>&#39;M&#39;</code>\nedited - a field differs from its original value. <code>undefined</code> for a row as it was set, or as\n<code>acceptChanges()</code> left it. Read only, setting it does nothing</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"EntityHandler","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface EntityHandler"],"doc":"<p>The <code>Proxy</code> handler every row is wrapped in: it keeps the row&#39;s original values and tracks which\nfields were edited, whether the row is new or marked for deletion, and answers the row&#39;s <code>__</code> fields\n(<code>__KEY</code>, <code>__rowState</code> ...). The data container makes one per row.</p>\n<p>Exported as a type only: it is the type of <code>Entity.__controller</code>. Read its fields, do not change them -\nuse the datasource&#39;s methods (<code>markForDeletion()</code>, <code>resetData()</code> ...).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const row = datasource.getDataRows()[0];\nrow.name = 'Anna';\nrow.__controller?.__edited; // true\nrow.__controller?.__originalValues.name; // the name before the edit</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"__controller","signatures":["__controller?: EntityHandler"],"doc":"<p>not used: reading <code>row.__controller</code> gives the handler itself</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__currentValues","signatures":["__currentValues: Record<string, any>"],"doc":"<p>the value last set, per field that was set</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__edited","signatures":["__edited?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> while a field differs from its original value</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__editedProps","signatures":["__editedProps: Record<string, boolean>"],"doc":"<p>per property set on the row: <code>true</code> while its value differs from the original, <code>false</code> once\nit was set back to it. <code>getChanges()</code> reports the <code>true</code> ones</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__group","signatures":["__group?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>not used on a data row, it is never a group row</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupChildren","signatures":["__groupChildren?: Entity[]"],"doc":"<p>not used on a data row</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupExpanded","signatures":["__groupExpanded?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>not used on a data row</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupID","signatures":["__groupID?: string"],"doc":"<p>not used on a data row</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupLvl","signatures":["__groupLvl?: number"],"doc":"<p>how many grouping levels the row sits under, 0 when not grouped. Read as <code>row.__groupLvl</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupName","signatures":["__groupName?: string"],"doc":"<p>not used on a data row</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupTotal","signatures":["__groupTotal?: number"],"doc":"<p>not used on a data row</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__isDeleted","signatures":["__isDeleted?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> while the row is marked for deletion, see <code>markForDeletion()</code> / <code>unmarkForDeletion()</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__isNew","signatures":["__isNew?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> for a new row: <code>addNewEmpty()</code>, or the container&#39;s <code>setData(rows, { isNew: true })</code>. Until\n<code>acceptChanges()</code> makes it an ordinary row. Stays <code>true</code> while a new row is marked for deletion</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__KEY","signatures":["__KEY?: string | number"],"doc":"<p>the row&#39;s generated key, when the container has no key field</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__KEYSTRING","signatures":["__KEYSTRING?: string | number"],"doc":"<p>the container&#39;s key field, <code>undefined</code> when there is none</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__newprops","signatures":["__newprops: Record<string, any>"],"doc":"<p>the fields set on the row since it was made (or its changes were accepted), <code>true</code> each</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__originalValues","signatures":["__originalValues: Record<string, any>"],"doc":"<p>the value each field had before its first edit, per field that was set</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__rowError","signatures":["__rowError?: string | null"],"doc":"<p>the row&#39;s error, read as <code>row.__rowError</code>, see <code>DataContainer.setErrors()</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__rowState","signatures":["__rowState?: string"],"doc":"<p>not used: <code>row.__rowState</code> is computed from <code>__isNew</code>, <code>__isDeleted</code> and <code>__edited</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Methods","members":[{"name":"get","signatures":["get(target: any, prop: string, receiver: Entity): any"],"doc":"<p>The proxy&#39;s get trap, called by the <code>Proxy</code> when a field of the row is read. Not for calling\nyourself.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"set","signatures":["set(obj: any, prop: string, value: any, receiver: Entity): boolean"],"doc":"<p>The proxy&#39;s set trap, called by the <code>Proxy</code> when a field of the row is set: it records the edit,\nand the container records it for undo and validates the field. Not for calling yourself.</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ExcelOptions","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ExcelOptions"],"doc":"<p>What <code>gridInterface.getExcel()</code> and <code>gridInterface.downloadExcel()</code> export. Every option is\noptional, and the object is plain JSON - it can be stored, or come from a menu of your own.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>option</th>\n<th>default</th>\n<th></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>rows</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;all&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;all&#39;</code>: every row the filter lets through, in the sort order. <code>&#39;selected&#39;</code>: the selected rows. <code>&#39;range&#39;</code>: the rows of the selected range of cells</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>fields</code></td>\n<td>the layout (<code>&#39;range&#39;</code>: the range&#39;s)</td>\n<td>the fields to export, in order</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>sheetName</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;Sheet1&#39;</code></td>\n<td>the name of the sheet</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>colors</code></td>\n<td><code>true</code></td>\n<td>the colours of the columns: the colour rules&#39; as the cells&#39; own, the data bars, colour scales and icon sets as Excel&#39;s conditional formatting. <code>false</code>: none</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The file always has the header row (the column labels, bold), frozen, with an autofilter over it\nand every row, and is always a flat list: a row per data row, no group rows, no outline, no totals.</p>\n<p>An option with a value it does not know (<code>rows: &#39;some&#39;</code>, <code>sheetName: &#39;a/b&#39;</code>), or a key it does\nnot know (<code>header</code>: the header row is always there), throws a <code>TypeError</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { ExcelOptions } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// the selected rows, two fields, on a sheet named People\nconst options: ExcelOptions = { rows: 'selected', fields: ['name', 'born'], sheetName: 'People' };\nawait gridInterface.downloadExcel('people.xlsx', options);\n\n// the cells the user selected (the last range), with a header row of their columns\nawait gridInterface.downloadExcel('range.xlsx', { rows: 'range' });\n\n// the values without the colours of the grid\nawait gridInterface.downloadExcel('plain.xlsx', { colors: false });</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"colors","signatures":["colors?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>The colours of the columns, default <code>true</code> - as the grid shows them in its light look (a sheet has\nno dark mode):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>the <strong>colour rules</strong> (<code>ColumnFormat.rules</code>): the text colour, background and bold of the rule that\nmatches a cell, as the cell&#39;s own style - fixed, Excel does not test the rule again</li>\n<li>a <strong>data bar</strong>, a <strong>colour scale</strong> and an <strong>icon set</strong> of a number column (<code>ColumnFormat.bar</code>,\n<code>scale</code>, <code>icons</code>): Excel&#39;s own conditional formatting, Excel draws them from the values - and\nagain when they change in Excel. A rule&#39;s background wins over a scale, as in the grid: the scale\nis not on those cells</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>false</code>: the values only. The number formats of the columns are written either way.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"fields","signatures":["fields?: string[]"],"doc":"<p>The fields to export, in this order, a column each. Default the fields of the layout now, in\nthe order the user sees them: pinned left, center, pinned right, and a column of stacked fields\ngives an Excel column for each of its fields, top to bottom - <code>gridInterface.getLayoutFields()</code>.\nThe hidden columns (<code>getHiddenFields()</code>) are not in the layout, so they are left out. With\n<code>rows: &#39;range&#39;</code> the default is the fields of the range.</p>\n<p>Any field of the rows can be given, also one that is not in the grid: it gets Excel&#39;s default\nwidth, a field of the layout the width of its column.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rows","signatures":["rows?: \"all\" | \"selected\" | \"range\""],"doc":"<p>Which rows, default <code>&#39;all&#39;</code> - the same rows as the CSV export:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&#39;all&#39;</code>: every row the filter lets through, in the sort order - <code>datasource.getDataRows()</code>.\nWhen grouped, every data row in the grouped order, the rows of collapsed groups included; no\ngroup rows</li>\n<li><code>&#39;selected&#39;</code>: the selected rows, in the same order - <code>datasource.getSelectedRows()</code>. That is\nthe selected rows that are displayed: a selected row in a collapsed group is left out, as the\nrow menu&#39;s actions on the selected rows leave it out. Nothing selected gives the header row only</li>\n<li><code>&#39;range&#39;</code>: the selected range of cells - the last of <code>gridInterface.getRanges()</code>, the one made\nlast: its data rows top to bottom (a group row in it is left out) and, unless <code>fields</code> is\ngiven, its fields left to right. No range gives an empty sheet (no columns, no rows)</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"sheetName","signatures":["sheetName?: string"],"doc":"<p>The name of the sheet, default <code>&#39;Sheet1&#39;</code>. Excel&#39;s rules: 1 to 31 characters, none of\n<code>[ ] : * ? / \\</code>, not starting or ending with <code>&#39;</code>, not <code>History</code>. A name that breaks one\nthrows a <code>TypeError</code>.</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ExportedGrid","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ExportedGrid"],"doc":"<p>A grid saved as plain JSON: <code>gridInterface.exportConfig()</code> makes it, <code>importConfig()</code> takes it back</p>\n<ul>\n<li>also a saved grid of an older version, converted on the way in (<code>convertGridConfig()</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The hooks and the datasource are not in it: they are code and data of the app.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { ExportedGrid } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst saved: ExportedGrid = gridInterface.exportConfig();\nlocalStorage.setItem('my-grid', JSON.stringify(saved)); // { &quot;version&quot;: 2, &quot;config&quot;: {...}, &quot;state&quot;: {...} }\n\ngridInterface.importConfig(JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('my-grid') ?? 'null'));</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"config","signatures":["config: GridConfig"],"doc":"<p>the config: options, columns, layout, <code>initialState</code> ... - as the app gave it, and changed it with <code>updateConfig()</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"state","signatures":["state?: Partial<GridState>"],"doc":"<p>what the user did with it: <code>getState()</code> - left out, the config&#39;s <code>initialState</code> is what it starts with</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"version","signatures":["version: number"],"doc":"<p>the version of the saved grid: <a href=\"#api/index.GRID_CONFIG_VERSION\">GRID_CONFIG_VERSION</a> when it is written</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"views","signatures":["views?: GridView[]"],"doc":"<p>the named views: every one - the config&#39;s (<code>config.views</code>) and the ones the user saved, renamed and\ndeleted since with the views button (<code>viewsStorageKey</code>) - as <code>gridInterface.getViews()</code> has them, in\ntheir order. <code>importConfig()</code> gives them back with <code>setViews()</code>. Left out: the grid keeps the views it has</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"Field","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface Field"],"doc":"<p>A field as the datasource resolved it: every default filled in. Returned by <code>datasource.getField()</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const { type, label, formatter, validate } = datasource.getField('born');\nformatter.format(new Date(2026, 10, 20)); // '2026-11-20' for a date field with the default formatter\nconst required = validate.some((rule) =&gt; rule.id === 'required');</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"caseSensitive","signatures":["caseSensitive: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when <code>fields</code> gave the field <code>caseSensitive: true</code>: every filter on it matches case</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"clobType","signatures":["clobType: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when <code>fields</code> gave the field <code>clobType: true</code>: a long text filtered with <code>LIKE</code> only</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"formatter","signatures":["formatter: Formatter"],"doc":"<p>the field&#39;s own formatter, else the datasource&#39;s default for its type</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"label","signatures":["label: string"],"doc":"<p>the label from <code>fields</code>, else the field name</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"multiline","signatures":["multiline: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when <code>fields</code> gave the field <code>multiline: true</code>. The grid also shows a value with a line\nbreak as multiline text, in any text field</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"name","signatures":["name: string"],"doc":"<p>the field name, the property on the row</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"readonly","signatures":["readonly: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when <code>fields</code> gave the field <code>readonly: true</code>: no grid lets the user edit it. A calculated\ncolumn of a grid is <code>true</code> too, it is computed</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"type","signatures":["type: FieldType"],"doc":"<p>the type from <code>fields</code>, <code>&#39;text&#39;</code> when the field is not listed</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"validate","signatures":["validate: readonly ValidationRuleObject[]"],"doc":"<p>the field&#39;s validation rules, each written out as an object: <code>&#39;required&#39;</code> is <code>{ id: &#39;required&#39; }</code>.\n<code>[]</code> when the field has none. The datasource&#39;s own list, do not change it</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"FieldConfig","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface FieldConfig"],"doc":"<p>How one field of the datasource is described in <code>DatasourceOptions.fields</code>. All of it is\noptional, and writing just the type (<code>born: &#39;date&#39;</code>) is the same as <code>born: { type: &#39;date&#39; }</code>.</p>\n<p>It is plain JSON: the formatter and the validators are named by their ids (see\n<a href=\"#api/index.registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a> and <a href=\"#api/index.registerValidator\">registerValidator</a>), so the fields can be stored, e.g. in a\nbackend.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    fields: {\n        born: 'date',\n        age: { type: 'number', label: 'Age (years)', validate: ['required', { id: 'min', value: 0 }] },\n        price: { type: 'number', formatter: 'numberComma' }, // a built-in formatter, by its id\n        company: { label: 'Company name', validate: ['required'] }, // a text field with a label\n        notes: { label: 'Notes', multiline: true } // a text of several lines\n    }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["custom-formatter","validation"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"caseSensitive","signatures":["caseSensitive?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: every filter on the field matches case - <code>ABC-1</code> does not find <code>abc-1</code>. For a column the\ndatabase has an index on (a project code): <code>&quot;PROJECT_CODE&quot; = :1</code> uses it, <code>LOWER(&quot;PROJECT_CODE&quot;)</code>\nwould not. Set in the fields only, by code - not in the grid&#39;s config, and the user can not turn it\noff: &quot;Match case&quot; is on and greyed out in the header filter&#39;s menu, the filter editor and the grid\nconfig dialog. A condition on the field set without <code>caseSensitive</code> (<code>datasource.filter()</code>, a saved\nstate) is kept with <code>caseSensitive: true</code>, and <code>toSqlWhere()</code> compares the column with its case\n(<code>SqlColumn.caseSensitive</code>, which <code>sqlColumnsFromFields()</code> copies). Text fields only: <code>true</code> on another\ntype throws when the datasource is made. Default <code>false</code></p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ fields: { projectCode: { caseSensitive: true } } });</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"clobType","signatures":["clobType?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: the field is a long text the database holds as a LOB - an Oracle <code>CLOB</code> or <code>NCLOB</code> - that SQL\ncompares with <code>LIKE</code> only. LOB columns are not supported as such; this lets a grid filter one as plain\ntext: its filters offer Equal, Not equal, Contains, Does not contain, Begins with, Ends with and Blank</p>\n<ul>\n<li>no value list (<code>IN</code>), no &quot;compare with another field&quot; - and a formula (a calculated column, a colour\nrule&#39;s) can not read it: <code>{notes}</code> is a problem of the formula. A template that reads it is filtered on\nthe value, not on the text it shows. <code>toSqlWhere()</code> writes each condition with <code>LIKE</code>\n(<code>SqlColumn.clobType</code>, which <code>sqlColumnsFromFields()</code> copies). Set in the fields only, by code. Text\nfields only: <code>true</code> on another type throws when the datasource is made. Default <code>false</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ fields: { notes: { clobType: true, multiline: true } } });</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"formatter","signatures":["formatter?: string"],"doc":"<p>the id of the field&#39;s formatter: a built-in one (<code>&#39;numberComma&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;dateDDMMYYYY&#39;</code> ...) or one\nregistered with <a href=\"#api/index.registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a>. Default the datasource&#39;s formatter for the field&#39;s\ntype (see <code>DatasourceOptions.formatters</code>). An id that is not registered throws when the\ndatasource is made</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"label","signatures":["label?: string"],"doc":"<p>the field&#39;s name for people, default the field name. The grid&#39;s column label falls back to it\nwhen the column has no <code>label</code> of its own, and <code>getFilterString()</code> / <code>getFilterTree()</code> use it.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"multiline","signatures":["multiline?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>a text of several lines: notes, an address. The grid shows the first line of the cell, with a\nmarker when there is more, and the whole text in its tooltip. Enter, F2, a double click or\ntyping opens an editor over the cell, a bigger textarea: Ctrl+Enter saves, Esc cancels. See the\nediting guide.</p>\n<p>A text cell whose value has a line break is shown and edited like this without the option too:\nthe input of a cell can not hold a line break (the browser strips them). The option is for a\nfield of several lines whose values have none yet. Text fields only: <code>true</code> on another type\nthrows when the datasource is made. Default <code>false</code>. A grid&#39;s column can turn it on or off for its\ncells (<code>ColumnFormat.multiline</code>, Multiline in the grid config dialog)</p>\n","samples":["multiline"]},{"name":"readonly","signatures":["readonly?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: no grid on the datasource lets the user edit the field - its cells, paste, fill down, the\ndetail form and the import leave it as it is, also in an editable grid. Set in the fields only, by\ncode - not in the grid&#39;s config, and the user can not turn it off: &quot;Read only&quot; is on and greyed out\nin the grid config dialog. The column&#39;s own <code>readonly</code> (<code>ColumnConfig.readonly</code>) is a default the\nuser can change, this is not; the <code>isReadonly</code> hook is not asked for the field either. Code still\nsets its values (<code>row.status = &#39;Closed&#39;</code>, <code>setData()</code>, <code>upsert()</code>). Any type. Default <code>false</code></p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// the id from the database: shown, never edited\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ key: 'id', fields: { id: { type: 'number', readonly: true } } });</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"type","signatures":["type?: FieldType"],"doc":"<p>the field&#39;s type, default <code>&#39;text&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"validate","signatures":["validate?: ValidationRule[]"],"doc":"<p>the field&#39;s validation rules, checked when the field is edited and by <code>datasource.validate()</code>:\nthe id of a validator (<code>&#39;required&#39;</code>), or the id with options and a message\n(<code>{ id: &#39;min&#39;, value: 0, message: &#39;at least {value}&#39; }</code>), see <a href=\"#api/index.ValidationRule\">ValidationRule</a>. The\nbuilt-ins are <code>required</code>, <code>min</code>, <code>max</code>, <code>minLength</code>, <code>maxLength</code> and <code>pattern</code>, register your\nown with <a href=\"#api/index.registerValidator\">registerValidator</a>. An id that is not registered throws when the datasource is\nmade. A field with <code>&#39;required&#39;</code> gets the grid&#39;s required stripes while it is empty.</p>\n","samples":["validation"]}]}]},{"name":"FilterCondition","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface FilterCondition"],"doc":"<p>One test on one field: <code>field</code> <code>operator</code> <code>value</code>. The field&#39;s type comes from the datasource&#39;s\n<code>fields</code> (<code>&#39;text&#39;</code> when it is not listed), the condition has none of its own.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>field</code> - the property on the row</li>\n<li><code>operator</code> - how to compare, see <a href=\"#api/index.FilterOperator\">FilterOperator</a></li>\n<li><code>value</code> - what to compare with. Left out for <code>IS_BLANK</code> / <code>IS_NOT_BLANK</code>, an array for <code>IN</code> /\n<code>NOT_IN</code>, <code>[from, to]</code> for <code>BETWEEN</code>, a <code>Date</code> for date fields. A number value compares as a\nnumber and a <code>Date</code> as a date, also on a field that is not listed</li>\n<li><code>valueField</code> - compare with another field of the same row instead of <code>value</code> (not <code>BETWEEN</code>)</li>\n<li><code>caseSensitive</code> - <code>true</code>: a text is compared with upper and lower case as they are</li>\n<li><code>literal</code> - <code>true</code>: <code>*</code>, <code>%</code> and <code>_</code> in a text value are characters, not wildcards</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A condition without <code>field</code> or <code>operator</code> is ignored: it does not filter out anything. So is one\nwithout the value it needs: a blank <code>value</code> (null, undefined, <code>&#39;&#39;</code>, an invalid Date) and no\n<code>valueField</code>, or a <code>BETWEEN</code> without a <code>[from, to]</code> that has an end.</p>\n<p><a href=\"#api/index.where\">where</a> builds one. A <code>valueField</code> condition is written out:</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nwhere('age', 'GREATER_THAN', 18); // { field: 'age', operator: 'GREATER_THAN', value: 18 }\nwhere('name', 'EQUAL', 'Ann', { caseSensitive: true }); // finds Ann, not ANN\n\n// rows changed after they were approved\ndatasource.filter({ field: 'changed', operator: 'GREATER_THAN', valueField: 'approved' });</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"caseSensitive","signatures":["caseSensitive?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: a text is compared with upper and lower case as they are - <code>&#39;Ann&#39;</code> does not find <code>&#39;ANN&#39;</code>\nor <code>&#39;ann&#39;</code>. Default <code>false</code>: case is ignored, the two texts are compared in lower case (<code>IN</code> /\n<code>NOT_IN</code>: in upper case). Only <code>true</code> turns it on.</p>\n<p>For the conditions that compare text: on a <code>text</code> field (also a field that is not listed),\nwith a value that is no number and no <code>Date</code>. Every text operator takes it: <code>EQUAL</code> and\n<code>NOT_EQUAL_TO</code> (wildcards too), <code>CONTAINS</code>, <code>DOES_NOT_CONTAIN</code>, <code>BEGIN_WITH</code>, <code>END_WITH</code>, <code>IN</code> /\n<code>NOT_IN</code> (the list as it is, write a blank as <code>&#39;NULL&#39;</code>), and the <code>LESS_THAN</code> ... a text field\ndoes not offer. Ignored on a number, date, datetime and boolean field - their <code>IN</code> compares the\nformatted text ignoring case - and by <code>IS_BLANK</code> / <code>IS_NOT_BLANK</code>.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"field","signatures":["field: string"],"doc":"<p>the field to test, the property on the row</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"literal","signatures":["literal?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: the text of <code>value</code> is matched as it is - <code>*</code>, <code>%</code> and <code>_</code> are characters like any other,\nnot wildcards: <code>&#39;50%&#39;</code> with <code>CONTAINS</code> finds <code>&#39;50% off&#39;</code>, not <code>&#39;500&#39;</code>. Default <code>false</code>: they are\nwildcards (see <a href=\"#api/index.FilterOperator\">FilterOperator</a>). Only <code>true</code> turns it on.</p>\n<p>For the conditions that match a pattern on text: <code>EQUAL</code>, <code>NOT_EQUAL_TO</code>, <code>CONTAINS</code>,\n<code>DOES_NOT_CONTAIN</code>, <code>BEGIN_WITH</code>, <code>END_WITH</code> on a <code>text</code> field (also a field that is not listed),\nwith a text value. Ignored by the others - <code>IN</code> / <code>NOT_IN</code> and the comparisons have no wildcards -\nand on the other types. <code>toSqlWhere()</code> escapes the wildcards of the database&#39;s pattern for it.</p>\n<p>Made by code: the row menu&#39;s <em>Filter</em> on a cell&#39;s value makes it. The header filters and the filter editor do not make it, and the filter editor\nleaves it out when it applies a filter it edited.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"operator","signatures":["operator: FilterOperator"],"doc":"<p>how to compare, see <a href=\"#api/index.FilterOperator\">FilterOperator</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"value","signatures":["value?: unknown"],"doc":"<p>what to compare with, not used by <code>IS_BLANK</code> / <code>IS_NOT_BLANK</code> or when <code>valueField</code> is set. An\narray for <code>IN</code> / <code>NOT_IN</code>, <code>[from, to]</code> for <code>BETWEEN</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"valueField","signatures":["valueField?: string"],"doc":"<p>the name of another field: the row&#39;s value of that field is what is compared with. Not used\nby <code>BETWEEN</code>, it takes its ends from <code>value</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"FilterConditionNode","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface FilterConditionNode"],"doc":"<p>One condition of <a href=\"#api/index.FilterGroupNode\">FilterGroupNode</a>, ready to show: the field&#39;s label and the value as text.\nPart of what <code>getFilterTree()</code> returns.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { FilterConditionNode } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst describe = (node: FilterConditionNode) =&gt; (node.hasValue ? `${node.label} ${node.operator} ${node.value}` : `${node.label} ${node.operator}`);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"caseSensitive","signatures":["caseSensitive: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when the condition compares text with upper and lower case as they are: it has\n<code>caseSensitive: true</code> and compares text, see <a href=\"#api/index.FilterCondition\">FilterCondition</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"field","signatures":["field: string"],"doc":"<p>the field of the condition, its name: <code>label</code> is what is shown</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"hasValue","signatures":["hasValue: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>false</code> for <code>IS_BLANK</code> / <code>IS_NOT_BLANK</code>, they take no value</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"kind","signatures":["kind: \"condition\""],"doc":"<p>always <code>&#39;condition&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"label","signatures":["label: string"],"doc":"<p>the field&#39;s label, or what the <code>label</code> function given to <code>getFilterTree()</code> returns</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"operator","signatures":["operator: string"],"doc":"<p>the operator&#39;s name, e.g. <code>&#39;EQUAL&#39;</code>, see <a href=\"#api/index.FilterOperator\">FilterOperator</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"value","signatures":["value: string"],"doc":"<p>the value as text: formatted with the field&#39;s formatter, the values of <code>IN</code> / <code>NOT_IN</code> joined by\n<code>&#39;, &#39;</code>, a <code>valueField</code> as <code>[label]</code>. <code>&#39;&#39;</code> for <code>IS_BLANK</code> / <code>IS_NOT_BLANK</code>. For <code>BETWEEN</code> the\nstart, <code>from</code>, and <code>valueTo</code> the end - <code>&#39;&#39;</code> for an open end</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"valueTo","signatures":["valueTo?: string"],"doc":"<p>the end of a <code>BETWEEN</code> as text, <code>&#39;&#39;</code> for an open end. Only on a <code>BETWEEN</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"FilterGroup","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface FilterGroup"],"doc":"<p>Conditions and groups joined by AND (every child must match) or OR (one is enough). Groups nest,\nso any mix of AND and OR can be written. A group without children is ignored.</p>\n<p><a href=\"#api/index.and\">and</a> and <a href=\"#api/index.or\">or</a> build one.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { and, type FilterGroup, or, where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// age &gt;= 18 AND (country = 'Norway' OR country = 'Sweden')\nconst filter: FilterGroup = {\n    group: 'AND',\n    children: [\n        { field: 'age', operator: 'GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO', value: 18 },\n        {\n            group: 'OR',\n            children: [\n                { field: 'country', operator: 'EQUAL', value: 'Norway' },\n                { field: 'country', operator: 'EQUAL', value: 'Sweden' }\n            ]\n        }\n    ]\n};\n// the same, with the builders\nand(where('age', 'GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO', 18), or(where('country', 'EQUAL', 'Norway'), where('country', 'EQUAL', 'Sweden')));</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"children","signatures":["children: FilterExpression[]"],"doc":"<p>the conditions and groups in the group</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"group","signatures":["group: \"AND\" | \"OR\""],"doc":"<p><code>&#39;AND&#39;</code>: every child must match, <code>&#39;OR&#39;</code>: one is enough</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"FilterGroupNode","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface FilterGroupNode"],"doc":"<p>A group of filter nodes joined by one logical operator, as <code>getFilterTree()</code> returns it. It keeps the\nnesting of the filter, so the grouping can be shown, not flattened away - the grid&#39;s footer draws\nthese as bracketed chips.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { FilterNode } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// the filter as text: (age GREATER_THAN 18 AND (country EQUAL Norway OR country EQUAL Sweden))\nconst toText = (node: FilterNode): string =&gt;\n    node.kind === 'group'\n        ? `(${node.children.map(toText).join(` ${node.group} `)})`\n        : `${node.label} ${node.operator} ${node.value}`;\n\nconst tree = datasource.getFilterTree();\nconst text = tree ? toText(tree) : 'no filter';</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"children","signatures":["children: FilterNode[]"],"doc":"<p>the conditions and groups in it. The conditions the filter ignores are left out</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"group","signatures":["group: \"AND\" | \"OR\""],"doc":"<p>how the children are joined: <code>&#39;AND&#39;</code>, or <code>&#39;OR&#39;</code> - named as in the filter (<code>FilterGroup.group</code>)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"kind","signatures":["kind: \"group\""],"doc":"<p>always <code>&#39;group&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"FindResult","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface FindResult"],"doc":"<p>What Find (Ctrl+F in the grid, <code>gridInterface.find()</code>) has found: the text, how many cells show it\nand which of them is the current one. <code>gridInterface.getFind()</code> gives it, and the <code>find-change</code> event\nsends it each time it changes. See guides/19-find.md.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A match</strong> is a cell whose text - as the cell shows it, through the field&#39;s formatter - holds the\ntext searched for, in any case - as it is with &quot;Match case&quot; (<code>caseSensitive</code>). The cells are the\nfields of the layout in the displayed rows (after the filter, sorted): not the rows of a collapsed\ngroup, not a group row, not a checkbox.</li>\n<li><strong>The order</strong> is the rows top to bottom, and in a row the fields in the order of\n<code>gridInterface.getLayoutFields()</code>: pinned left, center, pinned right.</li>\n<li><strong>&quot;Filter rows&quot;</strong> (<code>filterRows</code>) shows only the rows with a match. The matches are the same, in\nfewer rows.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Plain JSON. The row of <code>current</code> is an index in the displayed rows as they are now, as the <code>row</code> of\nthe grid events.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.on('find-change', ({ open, count, position, current, filterRows, caseSensitive }) =&gt; {\n    if (open &amp;&amp; current) {\n        console.log(`match ${position} of ${count}: row ${current.row}, ${current.field}`);\n    }\n    console.log(filterRows ? 'only the rows with a match' : 'every row', caseSensitive ? '(match case)' : '');\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"caseSensitive","signatures":["caseSensitive: boolean"],"doc":"<p>&quot;Match case&quot; is on: the text is found as it is, <code>Acme</code> does not find <code>ACME</code> - the toggle <code>Aa</code> of the\nfind bar (Alt+C), or <code>find(text, { caseSensitive: true })</code>. The matches, the count and &quot;Filter rows&quot;\nfollow it. It is kept when the bar closes, as the text</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"count","signatures":["count: number"],"doc":"<p>how many cells show the text. 0 for an empty text, and while the bar is closed</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"current","signatures":["current: { field: string; row: number } | null"],"doc":"<p>the cell of the current match: its row, an index in the displayed rows (<code>datasource.getRows()</code>, 0\nbased), and its field. <code>null</code> when there is no match</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"filterRows","signatures":["filterRows: boolean"],"doc":"<p>&quot;Filter rows&quot; is on: only the rows with a match are shown - the toggle of the find bar, or\n<code>find(text, { filterRows: true })</code>. With an empty text every row is shown. <code>false</code> while the bar\nis closed: closing it turns it off</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"open","signatures":["open: boolean"],"doc":"<p>the find bar is open: Ctrl+F, <code>find()</code> or <code>openFind()</code> opened it. The matches show while it is</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"position","signatures":["position: number"],"doc":"<p>which match is the current one, 1 to <code>count</code> - 0 when there is none</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"text","signatures":["text: string"],"doc":"<p>the text searched for, as it was typed. It is kept when the bar closes, Ctrl+F shows it again</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"Formatter","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface Formatter"],"doc":"<p>Turns the values of a field into text and back. Every field has one: its own (<code>FieldConfig.formatter</code>),\nor the datasource&#39;s default for the field&#39;s type (<code>DatasourceOptions.formatters</code>). The options name\na formatter by its id: register yours with <a href=\"#api/index.registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a>, the built-in ones are\nregistered from the start.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>format</code> is used for everything shown as text: the cells, the edit and filter inputs, the group\nheaders, the value list of the filter menu, the footer&#39;s filter and <code>getFilterString()</code>. Booleans\nare the exception, the grid&#39;s checkbox shows the raw value.</li>\n<li><code>formatForEdit</code> (optional) is what a cell shows while it is edited - the text the user starts from:\nthe plain value where <code>format</code> is hard to type over (thousands separators, a currency sign).</li>\n<li><code>parse</code> turns what the user typed or pasted into the value stored in the row.</li>\n<li><code>parseFilter</code> turns what the user typed into a filter input into the value filtered on. Left out,\n<code>parse</code> is used.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The grid always calls <code>parse</code> and <code>parseFilter</code> with text. The built-in formatters are plain\nobjects, so a variant is a spread away: <code>{ ...NumberFormatterDot, format: (value) =&gt; ... }</code>.\nDo not use <code>this</code> in a formatter&#39;s methods, the datasource may call them detached.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, type Formatter, registerFormatter } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// money with two decimals and a space between the thousands: 12345.6 -&gt; '12 345.60', edited as '12345.6'\nconst money: Formatter = {\n    format: (value) =&gt; (typeof value === 'number' ? value.toFixed(2).replace(/\\B(?=(\\d{3})+(?!\\d))/g, ' ') : ''),\n    formatForEdit: (value) =&gt; (typeof value === 'number' ? String(value) : ''),\n    parse: (text) =&gt; (text.trim() === '' ? null : Number(text.replaceAll(' ', ''))),\n    placeholder: '0.00'\n};\nregisterFormatter('money', money);\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    fields: {\n        price: { type: 'number', formatter: 'money' }\n    }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["custom-formatter","formatters"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"placeholder","signatures":["placeholder?: string"],"doc":"<p>Optional: shown in an empty header filter input when the column has no <code>placeholderFilter</code>,\ne.g. <code>&#39;YYYY-MM-DD&#39;</code>.</p>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Methods","members":[{"name":"format","signatures":["format(value: unknown): string"],"doc":"<p>A value of the field as text. Give <code>&#39;&#39;</code> for a blank value (null, undefined).</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>value</code> the value in the row, can be anything the row holds</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"formatForEdit","signatures":["formatForEdit?(value: unknown): string"],"doc":"<p>Optional: a value of the field as text while its cell is edited - what the input shows when it\ngets the focus, and the text the editor over a cell starts from. Left out, <code>format</code> is used.\nGive the plain value where <code>format</code> is hard to type over: <code>&#39;12 345.60&#39;</code> is edited as <code>&#39;12345.6&#39;</code>.\n<code>parse</code> must read it back. When the cell loses the focus it shows <code>format</code> again.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>value</code> the value in the row</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"parse","signatures":["parse(text: string): unknown"],"doc":"<p>Text the user typed or pasted into a cell, as the value to store in the row.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>text</code> what the user typed</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"parseFilter","signatures":["parseFilter?(text: string): unknown"],"doc":"<p>Optional: text typed into a filter input, as the value to filter on. Left out, <code>parse</code> is used.\nThe built-in date formatters use it to make a filter boundary start at 00:00:00, where <code>parse</code>\nkeeps the current time of day.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>text</code> what the user typed</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"GridCellEventData","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface GridCellEventData"],"doc":"<p>The cell a grid event happened on. Most <a href=\"#api/index.GridEvents\">GridEvents</a> send this, some with more fields.\n<code>cell-header-focus</code> sends it with a different <code>rowData</code>, see there.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { EventHandler, GridCellEventData } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst logCell: EventHandler&lt;GridCellEventData&gt; = (data) =&gt; console.log(data.attribute, data.row, data.rowData);\ngridInterface.on('copy-cell', logCell);\ngridInterface.on('clear', logCell);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"attribute","signatures":["attribute: string"],"doc":"<p>the attribute (field) of the cell</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"cell","signatures":["cell: HTMLCellElement"],"doc":"<p>the cell element</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"cellType","signatures":["cellType: string"],"doc":"<p><code>&#39;row-cell&#39;</code> for a data cell, <code>&#39;filter&#39;</code> for a header filter cell</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"celno","signatures":["celno: number"],"doc":"<p>index of the cell in the column, a column can have more than one row of cells. 0 based</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"colType","signatures":["colType: ColType"],"doc":"<p>the section of the grid the cell is in</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"column","signatures":["column: number"],"doc":"<p>index of the column in its section (<code>colType</code>), 0 based</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"row","signatures":["row: number"],"doc":"<p>index of the row in the displayed rows (<code>datasource.getRows()</code>), 0 based. 0 for header cells</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rowData","signatures":["rowData: Entity"],"doc":"<p>the data row of the cell. Never a group row, a group row has no cells</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"GridEvents","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface GridEvents"],"doc":"<p>The events of a <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">GridInterface</a>: event name -&gt; the payload its handler gets.\nThe datasource has its own events, see <a href=\"#api/index.DatasourceEvents\">DatasourceEvents</a>.</p>\n<p>Subscribe with <code>gridInterface.on(name, handler)</code>, the payload is typed from this map.\n<code>on()</code> returns a function that unsubscribes.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const off = gridInterface.on('cell-click', (data) =&gt; {\n    console.log('clicked', data.attribute, 'in row', data.row, data.rowData);\n});\ngridInterface.on('grid-connected', () =&gt; {\n    gridInterface.fitColumns();\n});\noff(); // unsubscribe</code></pre>\n","samples":["events"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"cell-click","signatures":["'cell-click': GridCellEventData & { originalEvent: MouseEvent }"],"doc":"<p>A data cell was clicked. Sent in a <code>setTimeout</code> after the click, so the row is already the\ncurrent entity. <code>originalEvent</code> is the click. Not sent for a boolean (checkbox) cell.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"cell-dblclick","signatures":["'cell-dblclick': GridCellEventData & { originalEvent: MouseEvent }"],"doc":"<p>A data cell was double-clicked: the payload of <code>cell-click</code>, <code>originalEvent</code> the dblclick. Sent in a\n<code>setTimeout</code> after it, so after the <code>cell-click</code> of each of its two clicks. A cell with a renderer\nand a link cell send it too; a boolean (checkbox) cell does not. What the grid does with a double\nclick is done first - a multiline cell&#39;s editor, a lookup&#39;s list are open - and the text of a link\nopened it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.on('cell-dblclick', ({ attribute, rowData }) =&gt; {\n    if (attribute === 'report') {\n        window.open(`/reports/${String(rowData.id)}`);\n    }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"cell-focus-button-click","signatures":["'cell-focus-button-click': GridCellEventData & { originalEvent: FocusEvent | KeyboardEvent; target: HTMLElement }"],"doc":"<p>The focus button of a cell was clicked, or Space pressed in the cell. The button is shown\nby <code>focusButton</code> on the column (<code>ColumnConfig.focusButton</code>).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>target</code>: the cell&#39;s input, focus it to give the focus back to the cell</li>\n<li><code>originalEvent</code>: the focus event of the cell (button clicked) or the keydown (Space)</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"cell-header-focus","signatures":["'cell-header-focus': Omit<GridCellEventData, \"rowData\"> & { rowData: Entity | GroupRow | undefined }"],"doc":"<p>A header filter cell got focus. <code>cellType</code> is <code>&#39;filter&#39;</code>, <code>row</code> is 0.</p>\n<p><code>rowData</code> is not the header&#39;s own: it is the first displayed row (<code>datasource.getRow(0)</code>)\nwhen the header filter got the focus. That is a <a href=\"#api/index.GroupRow\">GroupRow</a> when the datasource is\ngrouped, and <code>undefined</code> when no rows are displayed - check with <code>isGroupRow()</code> before\nreading it as a data row.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"cell-row-focus","signatures":["'cell-row-focus': GridCellEventData & { originalEvent: FocusEvent }"],"doc":"<p>A data cell got focus, by click or keyboard. <code>originalEvent</code> is the focus event. Not sent for a\nboolean (checkbox) cell.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"clear","signatures":["clear: GridCellEventData"],"doc":"<p>Cleared from the row menu (Clear: Cell): the column, in the selected rows.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"column-selection-change","signatures":["'column-selection-change': { columns: number[]; fields: string[] }"],"doc":"<p>The selected columns changed: the user clicked a column number (the row of numbers under the\nheader filters), pressed Esc on one, or <code>selectColumns()</code> was called. Also when the grid cleared\nthem because the fields of the layout changed - a column moved, pinned, hidden or added. Not sent\nwhen nothing changed.</p>\n<p><code>columns</code> is what <code>gridInterface.getSelectedColumns()</code> gives now - the numbers, 1 based, <code>[]</code> when\nnone is selected - and <code>fields</code> their fields, <code>getLayoutFields({ selectedOnly: true })</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.on('column-selection-change', ({ columns, fields }) =&gt; {\n    console.log(columns.length ? `columns ${columns.join(', ')}: ${fields.join(', ')}` : 'no column selected');\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["ranges"]},{"name":"copy-cell","signatures":["'copy-cell': GridCellEventData"],"doc":"<p>Copied from the row menu (Copy: Cell Value): the value of the cell.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"copy-column","signatures":["'copy-column': GridCellEventData"],"doc":"<p>Copied from the row menu (Copy: Column): the column, in the selected rows.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"copy-row","signatures":["'copy-row': GridCellEventData"],"doc":"<p>Copied from the row menu (Copy: Row): all columns, in the selected rows.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"copy-row-col","signatures":["'copy-row-col': GridCellEventData"],"doc":"<p>Copied from the row menu (Copy: Row, selected rows/col): the selected columns (all when none\nare selected), in the selected rows.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"filter-operator-change","signatures":["'filter-operator-change': { column: ColumnConfig; field: string; operator: FilterOperator; rebuildHeader: () => void }"],"doc":"<p>An operator was picked for a header filter - in the filter menu&#39;s Filter › Operator ›, another one\napplied with the range block of a number or date column, or picked in the choice the header\nfilter&#39;s operator indicator opens (<code>GridConfig.filterOperatorIndicator</code>) - and the filter ran with\nit. The operator is state, <code>getState().headerFilters[field].operator</code>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>field</code>: the column&#39;s field</li>\n<li><code>operator</code>: the operator picked</li>\n<li><code>column</code>: the options of the column as the grid uses them (from <code>GridConfig.columns</code>). Change\nthem to change what the header shows, e.g. <code>placeholderFilter</code></li>\n<li><code>rebuildHeader()</code>: renders the header again, call it after changing <code>column</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Was <code>{ cellConfig, rebuildHeader }</code> in v5, with the operator in <code>cellConfig.operator</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.on('filter-operator-change', (data) =&gt; {\n    data.column.placeholderFilter = data.operator; // show the operator in the empty filter cell\n    data.rebuildHeader();\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["filter-operator-header"]},{"name":"find-change","signatures":["'find-change': FindResult"],"doc":"<p>What Find (Ctrl+F in the grid) has found changed: the find bar opened or closed, the text was\ntyped (sent when the typing stops), the current match moved (Enter, F3, <code>findNext()</code> ...), or the\nmatches were found again after the data changed. Not sent when nothing changed.</p>\n<p>The payload is what <code>gridInterface.getFind()</code> gives now, see <a href=\"#api/index.FindResult\">FindResult</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.on('find-change', ({ open, text, count, current }) =&gt; {\n    console.log(open ? `&quot;${text}&quot;: ${count} cells, the current at ${JSON.stringify(current)}` : 'find closed');\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["find"]},{"name":"grid-connected","signatures":["'grid-connected': Record<string, never>"],"doc":"<p>A grid element connected to this interface: <code>element.connectInterface(gridInterface)</code>,\nor the element was put back in the dom. Empty payload. Was <code>gridConnected</code> in v5.</p>\n<p><code>createGrid()</code> connects before it returns: a handler subscribed after it hears this only when\nthe element is put back in the dom.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"paste","signatures":["paste: Omit<GridCellEventData, \"rowData\"> & { entity: Entity }"],"doc":"<p>Pasted from the row menu (Paste: Cell). Sent once per selected row pasted into, <code>entity</code>\nis that row. The other fields are the cell the menu was opened on.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"range-change","signatures":["'range-change': { ranges: CellRange[] }"],"doc":"<p>The ranges of cells changed: the user dragged over the cells, Shift+clicked, Ctrl/Cmd+clicked,\npressed Alt+Shift+arrows or Esc, moved to another cell, or <code>setRanges()</code> / <code>clearRanges()</code> were\ncalled. Also when the grid cleared them: the displayed rows or the layout changed, see\n<code>gridInterface.getRanges()</code>. While the mouse drags it is sent each time the range reaches another\ncell. Not sent when nothing changed.</p>\n<p><code>ranges</code> is what <code>getRanges()</code> gives now, <code>[]</code> when they were cleared.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.on('range-change', ({ ranges }) =&gt; {\n    console.log(ranges.length ? `${ranges.length} ranges, the last ends at row ${ranges[ranges.length - 1].toRow}` : 'no cells selected');\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["ranges"]},{"name":"views-change","signatures":["'views-change': { views: GridView[] }"],"doc":"<p>The list of named views changed: a view was saved (over the one shown, or as a new one), renamed,\ndeleted or made the default - in the views menu of the footer, or by <code>saveView()</code>, <code>saveViewAs()</code>,\n<code>renameView()</code>, <code>deleteView()</code>, <code>setDefaultView()</code>. Store <code>views</code> - in a backend, say - and give it\nback as <code>GridConfig.views</code> next time. Not sent by <code>setViews()</code> and <code>updateConfig({ views })</code>: you\ngave the list, you have it. Nor when the user only switches to another view.</p>\n<p><code>views</code> is what <code>gridInterface.getViews()</code> gives now: copies, plain JSON - the readonly views of\nyours are in it too, leave them out when you store the user&#39;s. See <a href=\"#api/index.GridView\">GridView</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.on('views-change', async ({ views }) =&gt; {\n    const own = views.filter((view) =&gt; !view.readonly);\n    await fetch('/api/settings/orders-grid-views', {\n        method: 'PUT',\n        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n        body: JSON.stringify(own)\n    });\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["views"]}]}]},{"name":"GridHooks","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface GridHooks<T = unknown>"],"doc":"<p>The functions of a grid: what can not be written as data. They are kept apart from the\n<a href=\"#api/index.GridConfig\">GridConfig</a>, so the config is plain JSON and can be stored - in a backend, say - while the\nhooks stay in your code.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>isReadonly</code> - makes a cell readonly, or editable, from the values of its row</li>\n<li><code>cellClass</code> - adds css classes to a cell, from the values of its row</li>\n<li><code>rowClass</code> - adds css classes to a row, from its values: a late order, a blocked customer</li>\n<li><code>menus</code> - changes the grid&#39;s right click menus, see <a href=\"#api/index.GridMenus\">GridMenus</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Give them to <code>createGrid(host, { config, datasource, hooks })</code> (or <code>new GridInterface(config, datasource, hooks)</code>), and change them while the grid is shown with <code>gridInterface.updateHooks()</code>.\nAll of them are optional.</p>\n<p>Do not use <code>this</code> in them: the grid calls them on its own copy of the hooks object.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of the rows, from the datasource: the row the hooks get is an\n<a href=\"#api/index.EntityUnion\">EntityUnion</a><code>&lt;T&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { createGrid, type GridConfig, type GridHooks } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ninterface Account {\n    company: string;\n    balance: number;\n    isActive: boolean;\n}\n\n// the config is plain JSON: it can come from a backend\nconst config: GridConfig = JSON.parse(\n    '{&quot;readonly&quot;: false, &quot;layout&quot;: {&quot;center&quot;: [{&quot;fields&quot;: [&quot;company&quot;], &quot;width&quot;: 150}, {&quot;fields&quot;: [&quot;balance&quot;], &quot;width&quot;: 100}]}}'\n);\n\n// the hooks are code\nconst hooks: GridHooks&lt;Account&gt; = {\n    // company can not be edited on an inactive row, every other cell follows the config\n    isReadonly: (row, field) =&gt; (field === 'company' &amp;&amp; !row.isActive ? true : null),\n    // .negative { position: absolute; inset: 0; background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.25); }\n    cellClass: (row, field) =&gt; (field === 'balance' &amp;&amp; row.balance &lt; 0 ? { background: 'negative' } : null),\n    // no summary in the row menu\n    menus: { row: (defaults) =&gt; defaults.filter((entry) =&gt; !entry.id.startsWith('row.export')) }\n};\n\nconst gridInterface = createGrid(host, { config, datasource, hooks });</code></pre>\n","samples":["cell-styling","context-menu"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"menus","signatures":["menus?: GridMenus"],"doc":"<p>Changes the grid&#39;s right click menus: hide entries, reorder them, change their labels, add your\nown. One function per menu - <code>row</code> (a cell), <code>header</code> (a header label), <code>filter</code> (a header\nfilter), <code>column</code> (a column number, under the header filters) - that gets the grid&#39;s own entries\nand what the menu was opened on, and returns the entries to show. Called every time the menu opens. A menu without a function shows its defaults.</p>\n<p>The ids of the grid&#39;s own entries are listed in <code>MENU_IDS</code>, see <a href=\"#api/index.GridMenus\">GridMenus</a> and\n<a href=\"#api/index.MenuEntry\">MenuEntry</a>. Set or remove the functions later with <code>gridInterface.updateHooks({ menus })</code>.</p>\n<p>Replaces v5&#39;s <code>contextMenuCustom()</code> for the grid&#39;s own menus; a menu of your own is opened with\n<code>gridInterface.openMenu()</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type GridHooks, isGroupRow } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst hooks: GridHooks = {\n    menus: {\n        // no &quot;Clear:&quot; in the row menu, and an entry of your own at the end\n        row: (defaults, context) =&gt; [\n            ...defaults.filter((entry) =&gt; entry.id !== 'row.clear' &amp;&amp; entry.id !== 'row.clear.cell'),\n            { type: 'section', id: 'my.section', label: 'Row:' },\n            {\n                id: 'my.logRow',\n                label: 'Log row',\n                visible: () =&gt; !isGroupRow(context.row),\n                action: () =&gt; console.log(context.field, context.row)\n            }\n        ],\n        // the header menu without the grouping part\n        header: (defaults) =&gt; defaults.filter((entry) =&gt; !entry.id.startsWith('header.grouping'))\n    }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["context-menu"]}]},{"title":"Methods","members":[{"name":"cellClass","signatures":["cellClass?(row: EntityUnion<T>, field: string): CellClass | null | undefined"],"doc":"<p>Adds css classes to a cell, from the values of its row: to color a cell by its value, say. Called\nevery time a cell is rendered, keep it fast. See <a href=\"#api/index.CellClass\">CellClass</a> for where each class goes.</p>\n<p>Return <code>null</code> or <code>undefined</code> for no classes of your own.</p>\n<p>Replaces v5&#39;s <code>gridInterface.cellAppendClassSetter(callback)</code>: <code>inputClass</code> is <code>input</code>,\n<code>dimmedClass</code> is <code>background</code>, the row comes first and the third argument (readonly) is gone.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code> the cell&#39;s row. Always a data row: a group row has no cells</li>\n<li><code>field</code> the cell&#39;s field</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridHooks } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// .low { position: absolute; inset: 0; background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.25); }\nconst hooks: GridHooks = {\n    cellClass: (row, field) =&gt; {\n        if (field === 'balance' &amp;&amp; row.balance &lt; 0) {\n            return { background: 'low', input: 'bold-text' };\n        }\n        return null;\n    }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["cell-styling"]},{"name":"isReadonly","signatures":["isReadonly?(row: EntityUnion<T>, field: string, readonlyByConfig: boolean): boolean | null | undefined"],"doc":"<p>Makes a cell readonly, or editable, from the values of its row. Called every time a cell is\nrendered, and by the row menu&#39;s paste, clear and delete for each selected row.</p>\n<p>Return <code>true</code> (readonly) or <code>false</code> (editable). <code>null</code> or <code>undefined</code> leaves it to the config:\nthe column&#39;s <code>readonly</code> option, which is passed in as <code>readonlyByConfig</code>. The grid&#39;s own\n<code>readonly: true</code> makes every cell readonly, whatever this returns - and so do a locked field\n(<code>FieldConfig.readonly</code>, the hook is not asked for it), a calculated column and the edit\npermissions on a row they lock (<code>GridConfig.edit</code>: <code>change: false</code> and a row that is not new).</p>\n<p>A row it returns <code>true</code> for in every column of the layout is locked: the row menu&#39;s delete\n(<code>row.delete.rows</code>) skips it. The column&#39;s <code>readonly</code> option does not lock a row.</p>\n<p>Called often: keep it fast. When what it reads changes, call <code>gridInterface.refresh()</code> to render\nthe cells again.</p>\n<p>Replaces v5&#39;s <code>gridInterface.readonlySetter(callback)</code>; the row comes first now.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code> the cell&#39;s row. Always a data row: a group row has no cells</li>\n<li><code>field</code> the cell&#39;s field</li>\n<li><code>readonlyByConfig</code> the column&#39;s <code>readonly</code> option, <code>false</code> when it is not set</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridHooks } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// company can not be edited on an inactive row, every other cell follows the config\nconst hooks: GridHooks = {\n    isReadonly: (row, field) =&gt; (field === 'company' &amp;&amp; row.isActive === false ? true : null)\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["cell-styling"]},{"name":"rowClass","signatures":["rowClass?(row: EntityUnion<T>, rowIndex: number): string | null | undefined"],"doc":"<p>Adds css classes to a whole row, from its values: a late order, a blocked customer, a row to look\nat. Return one or more class names separated by spaces, or <code>null</code> / <code>undefined</code> / <code>&#39;&#39;</code> for none.</p>\n<p>The classes go on the row&#39;s element in every section - the row number, the pinned left, middle\nand pinned right columns - so a selector like <code>.late .simple-html-grid-col-cell</code> reaches every\ncell of the row, and <code>.late</code> alone the row (it is behind its cells: the cells&#39; inputs are\ntransparent, so a background on the row shows). They follow the row: called every time the row\nis rendered - scrolled in, <code>refresh()</code>, and after its values changed (an edit, an upsert, an undo),\nin the next frame. Not called for a group row.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code> the row. Always a data row</li>\n<li><code>rowIndex</code> its index in the displayed rows, as in the grid&#39;s events</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridHooks } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ninterface Order {\n    due: Date;\n    shipped: boolean;\n}\n\n// .late .simple-html-grid-col-cell { box-shadow: inset 0 -2px 0 #dc2626; }\nconst hooks: GridHooks&lt;Order&gt; = {\n    rowClass: (row) =&gt; (!row.shipped &amp;&amp; row.due &lt; new Date() ? 'late' : null)\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["cell-styling"]}]}]},{"name":"GridLayout","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface GridLayout"],"doc":"<p>Where the columns go. Each list is a list of columns from left to right; a column shows one field,\nor several stacked on top of each other.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>left</code> - pinned to the left, does not scroll sideways</li>\n<li><code>center</code> - scrolls sideways</li>\n<li><code>right</code> - pinned to the right</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridLayout } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst layout: GridLayout = {\n    left: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 150 }],\n    center: [\n        { fields: ['age', 'born'], width: 100 }, // two fields stacked in one column\n        { fields: ['company'], width: 200 }\n    ],\n    right: [] // the same as leaving it out\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["column-layout"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"center","signatures":["center: LayoutColumn[]"],"doc":"<p>the columns that scroll sideways</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"left","signatures":["left?: LayoutColumn[]"],"doc":"<p>the columns pinned to the left, default none</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"right","signatures":["right?: LayoutColumn[]"],"doc":"<p>the columns pinned to the right, default none</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"GridMenus","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface GridMenus"],"doc":"<p>Changes the grid&#39;s right click menus: the <code>menus</code> hook (<a href=\"#api/index.GridHooks\">GridHooks</a>). Each function gets the\ngrid&#39;s own entries for that menu (<code>defaults</code>, the tree shown in <a href=\"#api/index.MENU_IDS\">MENU_IDS</a>) and what the menu\nwas opened on, and returns the entries to show - hide some, reorder them, change them, add your\nown. Called every time the menu opens.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code>: right click on a cell or a row number - the submenus undo, select, copy, paste, clear,\ndelete, filter, view, size, export</li>\n<li><code>header</code>: right click on a header label - pin, hide, remove sorting, column chooser, then the\nsubmenus size, format (a date or number column), aggregate, grouping</li>\n<li><code>filter</code>: right click on a header filter - clear, the submenus blank and operator, the filter\neditor, the value list (text) or the range block (numbers and dates)</li>\n<li><code>column</code>: right click on a column number (the row of numbers under the header filters) - the\nselect submenu, the copies of the column, of the selected columns and of their header names</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>defaults</code> is a tree: most entries are in a submenu (<a href=\"#api/index.MenuSubmenu\">MenuSubmenu</a>), whose id is the start of\ntheirs - <code>row.copy.cell</code> is in <code>row.copy</code>. A filter on <code>defaults</code> sees the top of the menu: hiding\n<code>row.copy</code> hides the submenu with what is in it. An entry in a submenu is changed in its\nsubmenu&#39;s <code>entries</code>, with <code>map</code>.</p>\n<p>The grid&#39;s own entries are new objects every time, change them as you like. Left out, a menu shows\nits defaults. Change the functions while the grid is shown with <code>gridInterface.updateHooks({ menus })</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridMenus, MenuEntry } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// createGrid(host, { config, datasource, hooks: { menus } })\nconst menus: GridMenus = {\n    row: (defaults, context) =&gt; [\n        // no export: the submenu and what is in it\n        ...defaults.filter((entry) =&gt; !entry.id.startsWith('row.export')),\n        { id: 'my.logRow', label: 'Log row', action: () =&gt; console.log(context.field, context.row) }\n    ],\n    // the value list first, then the rest\n    filter: (defaults) =&gt; [\n        ...defaults.filter((entry) =&gt; entry.id === 'filter.values'),\n        ...defaults.filter((entry) =&gt; entry.id !== 'filter.values')\n    ],\n    // in the size submenu: one entry less, and one of your own\n    header: (defaults, context) =&gt;\n        defaults.map((entry): MenuEntry =&gt; {\n            if (entry.type !== 'submenu' || entry.id !== 'header.size') {\n                return entry;\n            }\n            return {\n                ...entry,\n                entries: [\n                    ...entry.entries.filter((inner) =&gt; inner.id !== 'header.size.resetAll'),\n                    { id: 'my.wide', label: 'Wide', action: () =&gt; console.log('wide', context.field) }\n                ]\n            };\n        })\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["context-menu"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"column","signatures":["column?: (defaults: MenuEntry[], context: MenuContext) => MenuEntry[]"],"doc":"<p>the menu of a column number, under the header filters</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"filter","signatures":["filter?: (defaults: MenuEntry[], context: MenuContext) => MenuEntry[]"],"doc":"<p>the menu of a header filter</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"header","signatures":["header?: (defaults: MenuEntry[], context: MenuContext) => MenuEntry[]"],"doc":"<p>the menu of a header label</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"row","signatures":["row?: (defaults: MenuEntry[], context: MenuContext) => MenuEntry[]"],"doc":"<p>the menu of a cell and of a row number</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"GridState","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface GridState"],"doc":"<p>What the user changes while working with the grid: <code>gridInterface.getState()</code> reads it,\n<code>setState()</code> sets it, <code>resetState()</code> goes back to the one the grid started with\n(<code>GridConfig.initialState</code>, and the config&#39;s <code>layout</code>).</p>\n<p>It is plain data, so it can be stored, e.g. as JSON. The one value JSON changes is a <code>Date</code> in the\nfilter or a header filter: it comes back as its ISO text, and <code>setState()</code> keeps it as text. A\n<code>date</code> or <code>datetime</code> field reads the text as the same moment - the same rows, the same date in the\nheader filter. A field not listed as <code>date</code> / <code>datetime</code> in the datasource&#39;s <code>fields</code> filters on a\n<code>Date</code> as a date only while it is a <code>Date</code>, after JSON it compares the text: list its type.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridState } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// keep what the user did, and give it back next time\nlocalStorage.setItem('my-grid', JSON.stringify(gridInterface.getState()));\n\nconst saved: GridState | null = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('my-grid') ?? 'null');\nif (saved) {\n    gridInterface.setState(saved);\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["grid-state"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"aggregates","signatures":["aggregates: Record<string, AggregateFunction[]>"],"doc":"<p>the aggregate functions of the columns, keyed by field - what <code>ColumnConfig.aggregate</code> starts\nwith and the header menu changes: <code>{ balance: [&#39;sum&#39;, &#39;avg&#39;] }</code>. Only the fields that have some are\nlisted; a field left out has none. See <code>ColumnConfig.aggregate</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"calculatedColumns","signatures":["calculatedColumns: Record<string, CalculatedColumn>"],"doc":"<p>the calculated columns, by field name - what <code>GridConfig.calculatedColumns</code> starts with and the\nuser adds, changes and removes in the grid config dialog: <code>{ total: { formula: &#39;{price} * {qty}&#39;, label: &#39;Total&#39; } }</code>. Their formulas are text, not code: a state from storage runs nothing. A column\nleft out that the grid had is taken out of the layout, the sort, the grouping, the filter and the\ndetail form. See <a href=\"#api/index.CalculatedColumn\">CalculatedColumn</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"detailForm","signatures":["detailForm: DetailForm"],"doc":"<p>the detail form - whether it is shown, its fields in their order, its width (dragged too), whether\nit is expanded or collapsed - what <code>GridConfig.detailForm</code> starts with and the user changes: the\ngrid config dialog (tab <em>Detail form</em>), the form&#39;s edge and its title bar. See <a href=\"#api/index.DetailForm\">DetailForm</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"expandedGroups","signatures":["expandedGroups: string[]"],"doc":"<p>the ids of the expanded groups, <code>datasource.getExpanded()</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"filter","signatures":["filter: FilterExpression | null"],"doc":"<p>the filter, <code>datasource.getFilter()</code>: the header filters&#39; conditions are part of it</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"formats","signatures":["formats: Record<string, ColumnFormat>"],"doc":"<p>the display formats of the columns, keyed by field - what <code>ColumnConfig.format</code> starts with and\nthe header menu (Format ›) and the grid config dialog change:\n<code>{ born: { date: &#39;weekIso&#39; }, balance: { number: { decimals: 2 } }, email: { link: { url: &#39;mailto:{email}&#39; } } }</code>.\nOnly the fields that have one are listed; a field left out shows its field&#39;s formatter. With the\nrest of the column settings: the label, the placeholder, blank / 0, the checkboxes\n(<code>{ company: { label: &#39;Firm&#39; }, newsletter: { checkbox: {} } }</code>). See <a href=\"#api/index.ColumnFormat\">ColumnFormat</a>. Its\ntemplates are text, not code: a state from storage runs nothing</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"grouping","signatures":["grouping: GroupArgument[]"],"doc":"<p>the grouping, <code>datasource.getGrouping()</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"headerFilters","signatures":["headerFilters: Record<string, HeaderFilter>"],"doc":"<p>what the header filter cells show, keyed by field: the value typed or picked, the operator\npicked in the header filter&#39;s menu, whether its &quot;Match case&quot; is on and its filter as you type.\nOnly the columns that have one of them are listed.</p>\n<p>The rows are filtered by <code>filter</code>: these are what the header shows, the conditions they made are\nin <code>filter</code> already. A state from <code>getState()</code> has both. The one exception is a quick date\n(<code>datePreset</code>): it is computed from today when the state is set, and its condition replaces the\ncolumn&#39;s in <code>filter</code> - see <code>HeaderFilter.datePreset</code>.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"layout","signatures":["layout: GridLayout"],"doc":"<p>column order, pinning and widths</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"sorting","signatures":["sorting: SortArgument[]"],"doc":"<p>the sort, <code>datasource.getLastSorting()</code>. When grouped, the grouped fields come first</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"totalsRow","signatures":["totalsRow: boolean"],"doc":"<p>whether the totals row is shown, <code>GridConfig.totalsRow</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"typeFormats","signatures":["typeFormats: TypeFormats"],"doc":"<p>the formats of the columns by type - what <code>GridConfig.typeFormats</code> starts with and the Defaults tab\nof the grid config dialog changes: <code>{ date: &#39;norwegian&#39;, number: { decimals: 2 } }</code>. A column with a\ndate or number format of its own (<code>formats</code>) shows that one. See <a href=\"#api/index.TypeFormats\">TypeFormats</a></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"GridView","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface GridView"],"doc":"<p>A named view: a snapshot of the grid&#39;s state - its columns, widths and pinning, the filter and the\nheader filters, sorting, grouping, the formats and colour rules of the columns, the aggregates, the\ntotals row, the detail form ... what <code>gridInterface.getState()</code> gives - under a name the user picked,\n&quot;My open orders&quot;. The user switches between them in the views menu, the button at the left end of the\nfooter, see <code>GridConfig.views</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>It is plain JSON</strong>: store it anywhere and give it back - <code>GridConfig.views</code>, <code>setViews()</code>. Where the\nviews are kept is the app&#39;s choice: the grid sends <code>views-change</code> with the list when the user saves,\nrenames or deletes one, or <code>GridConfig.viewsStorageKey</code> keeps them in the browser&#39;s localStorage. A\n<code>Date</code> in the filter comes back from JSON as its ISO text, as for a <a href=\"#api/index.GridState\">GridState</a>.</p>\n<p>Applied (<code>applyView()</code>, a click in the menu), what <code>state</code> leaves out is the state the grid starts in -\n<code>GridConfig.initialState</code> and the config&#39;s <code>layout</code> - so a view of a few parts (a filter and a sort)\nis the config&#39;s columns with that filter and sort, and a view saved before a part was added to the\nstate gets the config&#39;s.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type GridView, where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst views: GridView[] = [\n    {\n        id: 'late',\n        name: 'Late deliveries',\n        // the parts it sets, the rest is the config's\n        state: {\n            filter: where('dueDate', 'LESS_THAN', '2026-11-22'),\n            sorting: [{ attribute: 'dueDate', ascending: true }]\n        },\n        // shared: the user can apply it, not change, rename or delete it\n        readonly: true\n    },\n    { id: 'mine', name: 'My open orders', state: gridInterface.getState(), default: true }\n];\ngridInterface.setViews(views);</code></pre>\n","samples":["views"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"default","signatures":["default?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: the view the grid applies when it is made - instead of <code>initialState</code>, on top of it. One\nview of the list at most. The user sets it with <em>Default view</em> in the views menu\n(<code>setDefaultView()</code>). Default <code>false</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"id","signatures":["id: string"],"doc":"<p>unique in the list, never shown. A view the user saves gets one made by the grid (<code>view-</code> and a\nrandom part); a view of yours can have any text</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"name","signatures":["name: string"],"doc":"<p>what the views menu and the footer&#39;s button show: &quot;My open orders&quot;</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"readonly","signatures":["readonly?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: a view of yours the user can apply and save as a new view of their own, but not save over,\nrename or delete - a view shared by the company, say. The views menu shows it with the hint\n&quot;shared&quot;. Default <code>false</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"state","signatures":["state: Partial<GridState>"],"doc":"<p>the state the view applies, what <code>getState()</code> gave when it was saved. It can leave parts out: they\nare the state the grid starts in (<code>GridConfig.initialState</code>, the config&#39;s <code>layout</code>)</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"GroupArgument","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface GroupArgument"],"doc":"<p>One level of grouping: the field to group on and its title. <code>datasource.group()</code> takes a list of\nthem, the first is the outer group. It is what <code>GridState.grouping</code> holds.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GroupArgument } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst grouping: GroupArgument[] = [\n    { attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' },\n    { attribute: 'company', title: 'Company' } // inside each country\n];\ndatasource.group(grouping);</code></pre>\n","samples":["sorting-grouping"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"attribute","signatures":["attribute: string"],"doc":"<p>the field to group on</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"title","signatures":["title: string"],"doc":"<p>shown in the group rows (<code>&#39;Country: Norway&#39;</code>, its first letter made upper case) and in the\ngrouping panel above the grid. The grid uses the column&#39;s label when the user groups by dragging\na column to the panel</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"GroupRow","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface GroupRow"],"doc":"<p>A group header row. When the datasource is grouped, the displayed rows\n(<code>datasource.getRows()</code>) mix your data rows with these headers - one per group, in front of\nits rows. A group row is made by the datasource, it is not one of your objects: it can not be\nselected, edited or marked for deletion, and <code>getDataRows()</code>, <code>getSelectedRows()</code> and\n<code>getAllData()</code> never contain one. Tell the two kinds apart with <a href=\"#api/index.isGroupRow\">isGroupRow</a>.</p>\n<p>Read the fields, do not change them - expand and collapse with <code>datasource.expandGroup(id)</code> /\n<code>collapseGroup(id)</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { isGroupRow } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndatasource.group([{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]);\ndatasource.expandGroup();\n\nfor (const row of datasource.getRows()) {\n    if (isGroupRow(row)) {\n        console.log(row.__groupName, row.__groupTotal, row.__groupExpanded ? 'open' : 'closed');\n    } else {\n        console.log('  ', row.name);\n    }\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["sorting-grouping"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"__group","signatures":["__group: true"],"doc":"<p>always <code>true</code>, the mark of a group row - see <a href=\"#api/index.isGroupRow\">isGroupRow</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupChildren","signatures":["__groupChildren: (Entity | GroupRow)[]"],"doc":"<p>the rows in the group: data rows, or the group rows of the next level when grouped on more than one attribute</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupExpanded","signatures":["__groupExpanded: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when the group is expanded and its rows are displayed</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupID","signatures":["__groupID: string"],"doc":"<p>id of the group, for <code>expandGroup(id)</code> / <code>collapseGroup(id)</code>: the grouped value as the field&#39;s\nformatter shows it, <code>&#39;Norway&#39;</code>. On a sub group the ids of the groups above it come first, joined\nby <code>-</code>: <code>&#39;Norway-Apple&#39;</code>. The group of the blank values is <code>&#39; blank&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupLvl","signatures":["__groupLvl: number"],"doc":"<p>the grouping level, 0 for the first <code>group()</code> attribute. The grid indents the row by it</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupName","signatures":["__groupName: string"],"doc":"<p>the text the grid shows: the group&#39;s title (its first letter in upper case) and the value,\n<code>&#39;Country: Norway&#39;</code>. The group of the blank values shows the text <code>grouping.blank</code>,\n<code>&#39;Country: blank&#39;</code> - see <a href=\"#api/index.TEXTS\">TEXTS</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupTotal","signatures":["__groupTotal: number"],"doc":"<p>number of data rows in the group, the ones in its sub groups included</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"HeaderFilter","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface HeaderFilter"],"doc":"<p>The header filter of one column, see <code>GridState.headerFilters</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { HeaderFilter } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst headerFilters: Record&lt;string, HeaderFilter&gt; = {\n    name: { value: 'Ann*', caseSensitive: true }, // typed in the name column, &quot;Match case&quot; on\n    age: { value: 30, operator: 'LESS_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO' }, // the operator picked in the menu\n    balance: { value: [1000, 5000], operator: 'BETWEEN' }, // typed as 1000..5000\n    active: { value: true }, // a boolean column's checkbox\n    city: { value: 'Os*', filterOnType: true }, // filter as you type turned on\n    due: { value: new Date(2026, 10, 16), operator: 'EQUAL' }, // `2026-W47` typed, the column shown as weekIso\n    orderDate: { value: null, datePreset: 'thisMonth' } // Quick dates › This month: this month when it is set\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["grid-state"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"caseSensitive","signatures":["caseSensitive?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when &quot;Match case&quot; is on in the header filter&#39;s menu, see <code>ColumnConfig.filterCaseSensitive</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datePreset","signatures":["datePreset?: DatePreset"],"doc":"<p>the quick date filter picked in the column&#39;s filter menu (<em>Quick dates</em>: <code>&#39;thisMonth&#39;</code> ...), see\n<a href=\"#api/index.DatePreset\">DatePreset</a>. It is <strong>relative</strong>: the grid computes its days from today whenever it filters -\nwhen it is picked, when a state with it is set (<code>setState()</code>, <code>initialState</code>, <code>resetState()</code>) and\nwhen the window gets the focus back on another day (<code>gridInterface.refreshDatePresets()</code>). So a\nstate saved with This month filters on the month it is set in.</p>\n<p>With it, <code>operator</code> is <code>&#39;BETWEEN&#39;</code> and <code>value</code> the <code>[from, to]</code> it was computed to last (a\n<code>datetime</code>&#39;s To at 23:59:59, an open start null for <code>&#39;overdue&#39;</code>): set it with <code>value: null</code>, the\ngrid fills them in. Its condition - a plain <code>BETWEEN</code> of those days - replaces the column&#39;s in\n<code>GridState.filter</code> when the state is set: <code>filter</code> and <code>toSqlWhere()</code> never see the quick date.\nThe cell shows its name (<em>This month</em>). A value typed, picked or cleared replaces it, and so does\nanother operator. Left out for a column that can not take it (no date column, no <code>BETWEEN</code>)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"filterOnType","signatures":["filterOnType?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>filter as you type, as the user turned it on (<code>true</code>) or off (<code>false</code>) in the operator choice, the\nfilter menu or the grid config dialog. Left out: the column&#39;s <code>filterOnType</code>, else the grid&#39;s -\nlisted only when the user&#39;s differs from it. See <code>ColumnConfig.filterOnType</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"operator","signatures":["operator?: FilterOperator"],"doc":"<p>the operator picked in the header filter&#39;s menu. Left out, the column&#39;s <code>operator</code> is used - and\nso it is when the column does not offer this one (<code>filterOperators</code>)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"value","signatures":["value: unknown"],"doc":"<p>what the header filter cell shows: the text typed, the date picked, <code>true</code>/<code>false</code> for a\ncheckbox, <code>[from, to]</code> for <code>BETWEEN</code> (an open end null). null is empty.</p>\n<p>A number or a date typed is stored as its value: a number, a <code>Date</code>. In a column that filters as\nshown (<code>ColumnFormat.filterAsShown</code>) the date is the start of the period typed - <code>2026-W47</code> is\nstored as Monday 2026-11-16 00:00, <code>2026-W40..2026-W47</code> as <code>[Monday of week 40, Monday of week 47]</code></p>\n<ul>\n<li>and the cell shows it in the column&#39;s format again: <code>2026-W47</code>. The conditions of the whole week\nare in <code>GridState.filter</code></li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"HTMLCellElement","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface HTMLCellElement extends HTMLElement"],"doc":"<p>A cell element of the grid: the <code>cell</code> the grid events and the menu context give you. The grid\nreuses these elements while scrolling, so the <code>$</code> fields say what the cell shows now - read them\nin the handler, do not keep the element for later.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.on('cell-click', (data) =&gt; {\n    console.log(data.cell.$attribute, data.cell.$row); // the same as data.attribute, data.row\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"$attribute","signatures":["$attribute: string | null"],"doc":"<p>the field of the cell. null on group and selector cells, they have no field</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"$celno","signatures":["$celno: number"],"doc":"<p>index of the cell in the column (a column can stack several fields), 0 based</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"$coltype","signatures":["$coltype: ColType"],"doc":"<p>the section of the grid the cell is in</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"$column","signatures":["$column: number"],"doc":"<p>index of the column in its section (<code>$coltype</code>), 0 based</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"$focused","signatures":["$focused: boolean"],"doc":"<p>helper to know if cell is focused</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"$row","signatures":["$row: number"],"doc":"<p>index of the row in the displayed rows, 0 based</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"IconSetFormat","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface IconSetFormat"],"doc":"<p>An icon set of a number column, <code>ColumnFormat.icons</code>: an icon before (or after) each value, by two\nthresholds - a value from the second has the high icon, from the first the middle one, below it the\nlow one (as a spreadsheet&#39;s: &quot;from&quot; is <code>&gt;=</code>).</p>\n<p>The thresholds are percent of the range from the smallest value to the largest of the rows the filter\nlets through (<code>unit: &#39;percent&#39;</code>, the default: <code>[33, 67]</code>, the thirds), or numbers (<code>unit: &#39;number&#39;</code>).\nFor a screen reader the cell says <em>High</em>, <em>Middle</em> or <em>Low</em> after its value (the texts\n<code>cell.icon.high</code> ...).</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>icons</th>\n<th>0 to 100</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>{ set: &#39;arrows&#39; }</code></td>\n<td>▲ from 67, ► from 33, ▼ below</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ set: &#39;traffic&#39;, thresholds: [50, 90] }</code></td>\n<td>a green light from 90, amber from 50</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ set: &#39;symbols&#39;, thresholds: [0, 1000], unit: &#39;number&#39; }</code></td>\n<td>✓ from 1000, ! from 0, ✕ for a negative value</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ set: &#39;arrows&#39;, reverse: true }</code></td>\n<td>▼ red from 67: the high values are the bad ones (costs, days late)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig, IconSetFormat } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst trend: IconSetFormat = { set: 'arrows' };\nconst columns: GridConfig['columns'] = {\n    growth: { format: { icons: trend } },\n    stock: { format: { icons: { set: 'traffic', thresholds: [10, 50], unit: 'number', position: 'after' } } }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"position","signatures":["position?: \"before\" | \"after\""],"doc":"<p><code>&#39;before&#39;</code> (the default): the icon at the left of the cell, <code>&#39;after&#39;</code> at its right</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"reverse","signatures":["reverse?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: the icons the other way round - the low values have the high icon (▲ green)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"set","signatures":["set: IconSetName"],"doc":"<p>the icons, see <a href=\"#api/index.IconSetName\">IconSetName</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"thresholds","signatures":["thresholds?: [number, number]"],"doc":"<p>the two thresholds, the first not above the second: from the first the middle icon, from the second\nthe high one. Left out: <code>[33, 67]</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"unit","signatures":["unit?: \"number\" | \"percent\""],"doc":"<p><code>&#39;percent&#39;</code> (the default): the thresholds are percent of the range, 0 to 100. <code>&#39;number&#39;</code>: they are\nvalues of the column</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"IDateConfig","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface IDateConfig"],"doc":"<p>The config of a <a href=\"#api/index.DateInterface\">DateInterface</a>: a date picker (<code>datepicker: true</code> - one month, one date with a\ntime, and Clear / Now / Use buttons) or a calendar (<code>datepicker: false</code> - one or more months, click\ndays to select them).</p>\n<p>A range picker is a date picker with <code>rangepicker: true</code>: two months side by side, From and To picked\nwith two clicks, and Clear / Use buttons that send the <code>range-select</code> event - see <code>rangepicker</code>.</p>\n<p>The type requires every field but <code>texts</code>, <code>datepickerDate</code>, <code>datepickerHour</code>, <code>datepickerMinute</code>,\n<code>datepickerHeight</code>, <code>rangepicker</code> and <code>datepickerRange</code>.</p>\n<p>The names of the months and days and the buttons are texts, the ids <code>datePicker.*</code> of <a href=\"#api/index.TEXTS\">TEXTS</a>:\nset with <a href=\"#api/index.setTexts\">setTexts</a>, or with <code>texts</code> for this picker.</p>\n<p>The grid&#39;s date picker (<code>GridConfig.datePickerConfig</code>) takes a <code>Partial&lt;IDateConfig&gt;</code>: the fields to\nchange. It reads only <code>showWeek</code>, <code>isoWeek</code>, <code>weekStart</code>, <code>rowHeight</code>, <code>monthWidth</code>, <code>monthMargin</code>,\n<code>hideDimmedDates</code>, <code>showYearInMonth</code> and <code>datepickerHeight</code>, each with a default; the others it sets\nitself - <code>texts</code> to the grid&#39;s texts. Its range picker (a date header filter with Between) takes the\nsame fields.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type DateElement, DateInterface, type IDateConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\nimport '@simple-html/grid/date.css';\n\nconst config: IDateConfig = {\n    datepicker: true,\n    datepickerDate: new Date(), // the date it opens on\n    monthsToShow: 1,\n    monthColumns: 1,\n    startMonth: 0, // set from datepickerDate in a date picker\n    startYear: 2026,\n    weekStart: 1, // the week starts on monday\n    showWeek: true,\n    isoWeek: true,\n    rowHeight: 22,\n    monthWidth: 230,\n    monthMargin: 10,\n    hideDimmedDates: false,\n    showYearInMonth: false,\n    headerTitle: ''\n};\n\nconst dateInterface = new DateInterface(config);\nconst element = document.createElement('simple-html-date') as DateElement;\nelement.classList.add('simple-html-date');\nelement.connectInterface(dateInterface);\nhost.appendChild(element);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"datepicker","signatures":["datepicker: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: a date picker - one month, one date and its time, and Clear / Now / Use buttons that\nsend the <code>date-select</code> event; with <code>rangepicker: true</code> a range picker, see there. <code>false</code>: a\ncalendar - click days to select them, shift+click a range, read them with <code>getSelected()</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datepickerDate","signatures":["datepickerDate?: Date | null"],"doc":"<p>the date the date picker opens on and shows picked. null or undefined: the datepicker opens on today.\nThe picker changes this date in place (seconds and milliseconds set to 0)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datepickerHeight","signatures":["datepickerHeight?: number"],"doc":"<p>grid only: the height of the date picker in px - by default 282 (its height with rows of 22px, 277,\nand a gap of 5) and 7px more for every px a row is taller (<code>rowHeight</code>). The grid opens the picker\nabove the cell when there is no room for this below it. Set it when you change <code>monthMargin</code>. The range picker (<code>rangepicker</code>) is\nmeasured, this is not used for it</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datepickerHour","signatures":["datepickerHour?: number"],"doc":"<p>the hour of the picked time, set from <code>datepickerDate</code> by the date picker</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datepickerMinute","signatures":["datepickerMinute?: number"],"doc":"<p>the minutes of the picked time, set from <code>datepickerDate</code> by the date picker</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datepickerRange","signatures":["datepickerRange?: [Date | null, Date | null] | null"],"doc":"<p>The From and To a range picker (<code>rangepicker: true</code>) opens on and shows picked: it opens on the\nmonth of From (of To when From is null, today when both are). null, undefined or a null end: not\npicked. The times are dropped: the picker keeps days, at 00:00.</p>\n<p>The picker sets it to the days picked as they are clicked - new dates, the ones you gave are not\nchanged - so it is the range picked so far, <code>[from, null]</code> after the first click.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"headerTitle","signatures":["headerTitle: string"],"doc":"<p>the title above the months of a calendar. Not shown by a date picker</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"hideDimmedDates","signatures":["hideDimmedDates: boolean"],"doc":"<p>hides the days of the month before and after, which are shown dimmed</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"isoWeek","signatures":["isoWeek: boolean"],"doc":"<p>ISO week numbers (weeks start on monday, week 1 has the year&#39;s first thursday), else US week numbers\nas Excel&#39;s <code>WEEKNUM</code> (weeks start on sunday, week 1 has January 1). The same numbers as a date\ncolumn&#39;s week formats</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"monthColumns","signatures":["monthColumns: number"],"doc":"<p>how many months a calendar shows side by side, before it starts a new row. A date picker sets 1, a\nrange picker as many as it shows</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"monthMargin","signatures":["monthMargin: number"],"doc":"<p>the space on each side of a month, in px</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"monthsToShow","signatures":["monthsToShow: number"],"doc":"<p>how many months a calendar shows. A date picker shows 1, whatever this is - a range picker 2, 1 in a\nwindow too narrow for two</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"monthWidth","signatures":["monthWidth: number"],"doc":"<p>the width of a month, in px</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rangepicker","signatures":["rangepicker?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>, with <code>datepicker: true</code>: a range picker - pick a From and a To day. Ignored by a calendar\n(<code>datepicker: false</code>).</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Two months side by side, one when the window is too narrow for two (a phone): the « ‹ › »\nbuttons once, around the pair. <code>monthsToShow</code> and <code>monthColumns</code> are set to 1 or 2</li>\n<li>The first day clicked is From, the next one To - swapped when it is before From - and a third\nclick starts again with a new From. From and To are shown selected\n(<code>simple-html-date-day-selected</code>), the days between them <code>simple-html-date-day-in-range</code></li>\n<li>A line under the months shows the From and To picked, and the buttons Clear and Use: Use sends\nthe <code>range-select</code> event with <code>[from, to]</code>, Clear with <code>null</code>. No hours and minutes, no Now:\nFrom and To are days, at 00:00</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The range it opens on is <code>datepickerRange</code>. The grid opens one for a date header filter with the\nBETWEEN operator, and for From and To of the filter menu&#39;s Between.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type DateElement, DateInterface, type IDateConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: IDateConfig;\n\nconst dateInterface = new DateInterface({\n    ...config,\n    datepicker: true,\n    rangepicker: true,\n    datepickerRange: [new Date(2026, 10, 22), new Date(2026, 10, 28)]\n});\nconst element = document.createElement('simple-html-date') as DateElement;\nelement.classList.add('simple-html-date');\nelement.connectInterface(dateInterface);\nhost.appendChild(element);\n\ndateInterface.on('range-select', (range) =&gt; {\n    console.log(range ? range.map((day) =&gt; day?.toDateString() ?? 'open') : 'cleared');\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rowHeight","signatures":["rowHeight: number"],"doc":"<p>the height of a row of days, in px. The grid&#39;s date picker: 22 by default, 28 on a touch screen\n(<code>pointer: coarse</code>) - room for a finger</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"showWeek","signatures":["showWeek: boolean"],"doc":"<p>shows the week numbers in front of each week</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"showYearInMonth","signatures":["showYearInMonth: boolean"],"doc":"<p>a calendar shows the year after the month&#39;s name: <code>November-2026</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"startMonth","signatures":["startMonth: number"],"doc":"<p>the first month shown, 0 (January) to 11. A date picker sets it from <code>datepickerDate</code>, a range\npicker from <code>datepickerRange</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"startYear","signatures":["startYear: number"],"doc":"<p>the year of the first month shown. A date picker sets it from <code>datepickerDate</code>, a range picker from\n<code>datepickerRange</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"texts","signatures":["texts?: Texts"],"doc":"<p>The texts of this picker, by id: the ones to change, they win over the page&#39;s (<a href=\"#api/index.setTexts\">setTexts</a>).\nThe ids are <code>datePicker.*</code> of <a href=\"#api/index.TEXTS\">TEXTS</a>: <code>datePicker.month.january</code> ..., <code>datePicker.day.sunday</code>\n... (<code>&#39;Su&#39;</code>), and the buttons and labels. The grid sets it to its own <code>texts</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { IDateConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst texts: IDateConfig['texts'] = { 'datePicker.month.january': 'Januar', 'datePicker.day.monday': 'Ma' };</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"weekStart","signatures":["weekStart: number"],"doc":"<p>the first day of the week: 0 Sunday, 1 Monday ... The days are shown from it on</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ImportOptions","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ImportOptions"],"doc":"<p>How <code>gridInterface.importRows()</code> reads the rows. Every option is optional.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>option</th>\n<th>default</th>\n<th></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>header</code></td>\n<td><code>false</code></td>\n<td>the first row that is not empty names the columns, it is not imported</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>fields</code></td>\n<td>by the header&#39;s names, or by position</td>\n<td>the field of each column, <code>null</code> skips it</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>decimalMark</code></td>\n<td>each number column&#39;s own</td>\n<td>how numbers in text are written: <code>&#39;.&#39;</code> 1,234.5 or <code>&#39;,&#39;</code> 1 234,5</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>dateOrder</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;DMY&#39;</code></td>\n<td>how a date with <code>/</code> is written: <code>&#39;DMY&#39;</code> 31/12/2026, <code>&#39;MDY&#39;</code> 12/31/2026</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>invalidRows</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;import&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;skip&#39;</code> leaves out the rows with problems</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { ImportOptions } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// the first row names the columns; a column named Notes is skipped, there is no such field\nconst byName: ImportOptions = { header: true };\n\n// no header: the first column is the name, the third the age, the second is skipped\nconst byPosition: ImportOptions = { fields: ['name', null, 'age'], decimalMark: ',', invalidRows: 'skip' };</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"dateOrder","signatures":["dateOrder?: \"DMY\" | \"MDY\""],"doc":"<p>How a date written with <code>/</code> is ordered: <code>&#39;DMY&#39;</code> (31/12/2026, default) or <code>&#39;MDY&#39;</code> (12/31/2026, the\nUS). <code>2026-12-31</code> and <code>31.12.2026</code> are always read, with a time <code>13:45</code> or <code>13:45:12</code> after them; a\ndate in any other form is read by the field&#39;s formatter. A date cell of a workbook is a date already.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"decimalMark","signatures":["decimalMark?: \",\" | \".\""],"doc":"<p>How a number written as text has its decimals: <code>&#39;.&#39;</code> (<code>1234.5</code>, <code>1,234.5</code>) or <code>&#39;,&#39;</code> (<code>1234,5</code>,\n<code>1 234,5</code>, <code>1.234,5</code>). Spaces and <code>&#39;</code> between the digits are left out, and so is the other mark,\nbetween groups of three digits. Default each number field&#39;s own: <code>&#39;,&#39;</code> when its formatter writes\n1.5 as <code>1,5</code> (<code>numberComma</code>), else <code>&#39;.&#39;</code>. A number cell of a workbook is a number already.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"fields","signatures":["fields?: (string | null)[]"],"doc":"<p>The field of each column, by position: <code>[&#39;name&#39;, null, &#39;age&#39;]</code> - <code>null</code> (or a field that can not\nbe imported, below) skips the column. Default: with <code>header</code>, the fields the header names; without,\nthe fields of the layout from the first one on, as a paste of a block of cells.</p>\n<p>A field can be imported when a user could type into it on a new row: any field of the datasource\nbut a column that is readonly (<code>ColumnConfig.readonly</code>, the user&#39;s <code>format.readonly</code>). The\n<code>isReadonly</code> hook is not asked: it decides about the rows that are there.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"header","signatures":["header?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: the first row that is not empty is a header - its cells name the columns, it is not\nimported. Without <code>fields</code> each column goes to the field it names: the label of a column of the\ngrid, or the name or the label of a field of the datasource, in any case, spaces around it\nignored. A name that is none of them is skipped, and so is a second column with the name of the\nsame field. Default <code>false</code>: every row is data.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"invalidRows","signatures":["invalidRows?: \"import\" | \"skip\""],"doc":"<p>The rows with problems - a value that is not of its field&#39;s type, a validation rule a value breaks:\n<code>&#39;import&#39;</code> (default) adds them - a value that could not be read is left empty and listed in the\nrow&#39;s error, the validation errors show on the cells - or <code>&#39;skip&#39;</code>, which leaves them out.</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ImportProblem","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ImportProblem"],"doc":"<p>A problem of a cell of the rows given to <code>gridInterface.importRows()</code>: a value that is not of its\nfield&#39;s type, or a validation rule the value breaks.</p>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"field","signatures":["field: string"],"doc":"<p>the field the cell went to</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"kind","signatures":["kind: \"value\" | \"rule\""],"doc":"<p><code>&#39;value&#39;</code>: the cell is not a value of the field&#39;s type - the new row has the field empty.\n<code>&#39;rule&#39;</code>: the value breaks a validation rule of the field (<code>FieldConfig.validate</code>)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"message","signatures":["message: string"],"doc":"<p>what is wrong, in the grid&#39;s texts: <code>Not a number: abc</code>, a validation message</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"row","signatures":["row: number"],"doc":"<p>the row, an index into the rows given: <code>rows[row]</code>. For a sheet, Excel&#39;s row number is <code>row + 1</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"value","signatures":["value: ImportCell"],"doc":"<p>the cell as it was given</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ImportResult","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ImportResult<T>"],"doc":"<p>What <code>gridInterface.importRows()</code> did.</p>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"problems","signatures":["problems: ImportProblem[]"],"doc":"<p>every problem found, of the rows added and of the rows skipped, in the order of the rows</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rows","signatures":["rows: EntityUnion<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>the new rows, in the order of the rows given</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"skipped","signatures":["skipped: number"],"doc":"<p>how many rows with problems were left out, with <code>invalidRows: &#39;skip&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ImportTable","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ImportTable"],"doc":"<p>A file read by <a href=\"#api/index.readImportFile\">readImportFile</a>: its rows, and what it was read as.</p>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"format","signatures":["format: \"csv\" | \"xlsx\""],"doc":"<p><code>&#39;csv&#39;</code> for text (<code>.csv</code>, <code>.tsv</code>, <code>.txt</code> ...), <code>&#39;xlsx&#39;</code> for an Excel workbook</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rows","signatures":["rows: ImportCell[][]"],"doc":"<p>The rows, a cell for each column - see <a href=\"#api/index.ImportCell\">ImportCell</a>. A CSV file gives a text for every\nfield, <code>&#39;&#39;</code> for an empty one. A workbook gives the cells typed (text, numbers, booleans, a <code>Date</code>\nfor a cell with a date format), <code>null</code> for an empty cell; its rows are the sheet&#39;s rows,\n<code>rows[4]</code> is Excel&#39;s row 5 - a row with nothing in it is <code>[]</code>.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"separator","signatures":["separator: CsvSeparator | null"],"doc":"<p>the separator of a CSV file: the one given, else the one found (<a href=\"#api/index.ReadImportFileOptions\">ReadImportFileOptions</a>); <code>null</code> for a workbook</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"sheet","signatures":["sheet: number"],"doc":"<p>the sheet read, an index into <code>sheets</code>; 0 for CSV</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"sheets","signatures":["sheets: string[]"],"doc":"<p>the names of the worksheets of a workbook, in the order of its tabs; <code>[]</code> for CSV</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"IStyle","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface IStyle"],"doc":"<p>The style of one date in a calendar, for <a href=\"#api/index.DateInterface\">DateInterface.styleRange</a> - which is not implemented\nyet: it only logs a warning.</p>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"addClass","signatures":["addClass?: string | string[]"],"doc":"<p>css classes to add</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"backgroundColor","signatures":["backgroundColor?: string"],"doc":"<p>the background color, a css color</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"bold","signatures":["bold?: string"],"doc":"<p>a css font weight</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"borderColor","signatures":["borderColor?: string"],"doc":"<p>the border color, a css color</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"date","signatures":["date: Date"],"doc":"<p>the date to style</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"fontColor","signatures":["fontColor?: string"],"doc":"<p>the text color, a css color</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"LayoutColumn","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface LayoutColumn"],"doc":"<p>One column of the <a href=\"#api/index.GridLayout\">GridLayout</a>: the fields it shows, stacked from top to bottom, and its\nwidth. The options of a field (label, placeholders, readonly ...) are in <code>GridConfig.columns</code>, its\ntype and default label in the datasource&#39;s <code>fields</code>.</p>\n<p>Every column gets as many cells as the column with the most fields; a column with fewer fields\nleaves the rest empty. A column without fields is left out.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { LayoutColumn } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst single: LayoutColumn = { fields: ['name'], width: 150 };\nconst stacked: LayoutColumn = { fields: ['firstName', 'lastName'], width: 120 };</code></pre>\n","samples":["column-layout"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"fields","signatures":["fields: string[]"],"doc":"<p>the fields shown in this column, top to bottom</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"width","signatures":["width: number"],"doc":"<p>width in px</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"LinkFormat","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface LinkFormat"],"doc":"<p>The link of a text or number column, <code>ColumnFormat.link</code>: its cells are links, the text they show (the cell&#39;s\nown, or <code>ColumnFormat.text</code>) is the link&#39;s text. The address is a template: text with <code>{field}</code>\nplaceholders, each the value of a field of the row - encoded, so a value can not change where the\nlink goes. Templates, not code: nothing in it is run.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><code>url</code></th>\n<th>links to</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>&#39;https://crm.example.com/customer/{id}&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>https://crm.example.com/customer/12</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;https://duckduckgo.com/?q={company}&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>https://duckduckgo.com/?q=Acme%20Corp</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;mailto:{email}&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>mailto:ann@example.com</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;tel:{phone}&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>tel:+47%2012345678</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;{website}&#39;</code></td>\n<td>the address the field holds, as it is: one placeholder alone is a whole address</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;https://shop.example.com/order/{value}&#39;</code> on a number column</td>\n<td><code>https://shop.example.com/order/1042</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The address starts with <code>https://</code>, <code>http://</code>, <code>mailto:</code> or <code>tel:</code>, or is one placeholder - else the\nformat throws a <code>TypeError</code> (<code>javascript:</code>, <code>data:</code>, a relative <code>/customer/{id}</code>). A row whose address\nis no absolute address of those four schemes - a field&#39;s <code>javascript:alert(1)</code>, an empty <code>{id}</code> - shows\nits text, no link. See the formatting guide, &quot;Links&quot;.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig, LinkFormat } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst customer: LinkFormat = { url: 'https://crm.example.com/customer/{id}', newTab: true };\nconst columns: GridConfig['columns'] = {\n    company: { format: { link: customer } },\n    email: { format: { link: { url: 'mailto:{email}' } } }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"newTab","signatures":["newTab?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>opens the link in a new tab (<code>target=&quot;_blank&quot;</code>, <code>rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;</code>). Left out: <code>false</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"url","signatures":["url: string"],"doc":"<p>the address: <code>https://</code>, <code>http://</code>, <code>mailto:</code> or <code>tel:</code> and <code>{field}</code> placeholders - their values\nencoded - or one placeholder alone, a field that holds the whole address (<code>&#39;{website}&#39;</code>)</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"LookupFromDatasource","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface LookupFromDatasource"],"doc":"<p>A <a href=\"#api/index.Lookup\">Lookup</a> of the rows of a datasource.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, type LookupFromDatasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst customers = new Datasource({ fields: { id: 'number' } });\nconst lookup: LookupFromDatasource = {\n    datasource: customers,\n    valueField: 'id',\n    labelField: 'name',\n    config: {\n        layout: { center: [{ fields: ['id'], width: 60 }, { fields: ['name'], width: 180 }, { fields: ['city'], width: 120 }] }\n    }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["lookups"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"config","signatures":["config?: GridConfig"],"doc":"<p>the dropdown grid (<code>type: &#39;grid&#39;</code>): its columns and options, plain JSON. Default one column of\n<code>labelField</code>, or <code>valueField</code> and <code>labelField</code> when they differ. Left out of it: no grouping\npanel (<code>panelHeight: 0</code>), no footer, no row state, and the header filters of the text columns\nsearch anywhere in the text (<code>operator: &#39;CONTAINS&#39;</code> for a text column without an operator). The\nselect does not use it</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datasource","signatures":["datasource: Datasource<any>"],"doc":"<p>the rows to pick from. The select shows the rows it displays (<code>getDataRows()</code>: its filter and\nsort). The dropdown grid filters and sorts it: give the lookup a datasource of its own, or one\nthat shares the rows of another through a <code>DataContainer</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"gridInterface","signatures":["gridInterface?: undefined"],"doc":"<p>a lookup of a datasource has no grid interface</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"labelField","signatures":["labelField?: string"],"doc":"<p>the field the cell and the list show, e.g. <code>&#39;name&#39;</code>. Default <code>valueField</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"valueField","signatures":["valueField: string"],"doc":"<p>the field of the picked row that is stored in the cell, e.g. <code>&#39;id&#39;</code> or <code>&#39;code&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"LookupFromGridInterface","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface LookupFromGridInterface"],"doc":"<p>A <a href=\"#api/index.Lookup\">Lookup</a> that shows a grid interface of your own as the dropdown grid: its config, its hooks\nand its datasource. The select shows the rows of its datasource.</p>\n<p><strong>Show it in the dropdown only</strong>: an interface shows one grid at a time. While the dropdown is open\nthe interface is connected to it, and disconnected when it closes - a grid on the page with the same\ninterface would stop following its datasource. Each time the dropdown opens, the interface goes back\nto the state it started in (<code>resetState()</code>): the filter typed the last time is gone.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, GridInterface, type LookupFromGridInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst customers = new Datasource({ fields: { id: 'number' } });\nconst picker = new GridInterface(\n    {\n        columns: { name: { operator: 'CONTAINS' } },\n        layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 200 }] },\n        panelHeight: 0\n    },\n    customers,\n    { cellClass: (row) =&gt; (row.blocked ? { input: 'blocked' } : null) }\n);\nconst lookup: LookupFromGridInterface = { gridInterface: picker, valueField: 'id', labelField: 'name' };</code></pre>\n","samples":["lookups"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"config","signatures":["config?: undefined"],"doc":"<p>the interface has its own config</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datasource","signatures":["datasource?: undefined"],"doc":"<p>the interface has its own datasource</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"gridInterface","signatures":["gridInterface: GridInterface<any>"],"doc":"<p>the grid interface the dropdown grid shows, made with <code>new GridInterface()</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"labelField","signatures":["labelField?: string"],"doc":"<p>the field the cell and the list show. Default <code>valueField</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"valueField","signatures":["valueField: string"],"doc":"<p>the field of the picked row that is stored in the cell</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"MenuBlock","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface MenuBlock"],"doc":"<p>An element shown in the menu as it is. The grid adds it to the menu and does nothing else with it:\nthe element handles its own clicks, input and keys, and clicking in it does not close the menu -\ncall <code>gridInterface.closeMenu()</code> for that. The arrow keys of the menu pass it by: Tab gets into it,\nfrom an item of its menu.</p>\n<p>The header filter menu&#39;s value list (search box, checkboxes, &quot;Cancel&quot; and &quot;Apply&quot;) is a block of the grid&#39;s\nown, <code>&#39;filter.values&#39;</code>: hide or move it as one entry, it is not built from items. So is the range block\nof a number or date column (its operators, an input, &quot;Cancel&quot; and &quot;Apply&quot;), <code>&#39;filter.range&#39;</code>, and the\nquick dates of a date column (Today, This week ...), <code>&#39;filter.dates&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p>Also for something bigger than a list of items in a menu of your own: a second grid as a dropdown,\nwhich then closes with the grid&#39;s menus (outside click, scroll, another menu opening).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, type GridConfig, type GridElement, GridInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const cell: HTMLElement;\ndeclare const dropdownConfig: GridConfig;\nconst dropdownDatasource = new Datasource();\n\n// a grid to pick from, opened under a cell\nconst dropdown = document.createElement('simple-html-grid') as GridElement;\ndropdown.style.width = '300px';\ndropdown.style.height = '250px';\ndropdown.connectInterface(new GridInterface(dropdownConfig, dropdownDatasource));\ngridInterface.openMenu(cell, [{ type: 'block', id: 'company-picker', element: dropdown }]);</code></pre>\n","samples":["dropdown-grid"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"element","signatures":["element: HTMLElement"],"doc":"<p>the element shown</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"id","signatures":["id: string"],"doc":"<p>a name for the entry, unique in its menu. See <a href=\"#api/index.MENU_IDS\">MENU_IDS</a> for the grid&#39;s own</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"type","signatures":["type: \"block\""],"doc":"<p>always <code>&#39;block&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"visible","signatures":["visible?: (context: MenuContext) => boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>false</code> leaves the block out of the menu. Called when the menu opens, left out it is shown</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"MenuContext","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface MenuContext"],"doc":"<p>What a menu was opened on, handed to every callback of its entries (<code>action</code>, <code>visible</code>, <code>disabled</code>,\n<code>selected</code>) and to the <a href=\"#api/index.GridMenus\">GridMenus</a> functions.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { isGroupRow, type MenuItem } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst copyKey: MenuItem = {\n    id: 'my.copyKey',\n    label: 'Copy key',\n    visible: (context) =&gt; context.row !== undefined &amp;&amp; !isGroupRow(context.row),\n    action: (context) =&gt; {\n        if (context.row &amp;&amp; !isGroupRow(context.row)) {\n            navigator.clipboard.writeText(String(context.row.id));\n        }\n    }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"cell","signatures":["cell: HTMLElement | undefined"],"doc":"<p>the cell the menu was opened on - the row number&#39;s in the row menu of a row number -\n<code>undefined</code> in a menu opened with <code>openMenu()</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datasource","signatures":["datasource: Datasource<unknown>"],"doc":"<p>the grid&#39;s datasource, <code>gridInterface.getDatasource()</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"field","signatures":["field: string"],"doc":"<p>the field of the cell the menu was opened on: in the column menu the column&#39;s first field (a\ncolumn of stacked fields has more). <code>&#39;&#39;</code> in the row menu of a row number - it has no cell - and\nin a menu opened with <code>openMenu()</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"gridInterface","signatures":["gridInterface: GridInterface<unknown>"],"doc":"<p>the grid</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"menu","signatures":["menu: \"filter\" | \"header\" | \"row\" | \"column\" | \"custom\""],"doc":"<p>which menu: <code>&#39;row&#39;</code> (right click on a cell or a row number), <code>&#39;header&#39;</code> (on a header label),\n<code>&#39;filter&#39;</code> (on a header filter), <code>&#39;column&#39;</code> (on a column number, under the header filters) or\n<code>&#39;custom&#39;</code> (opened with <code>gridInterface.openMenu()</code>)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"row","signatures":["row: Entity | GroupRow | undefined"],"doc":"<ul>\n<li>row menu: the row of the cell or the row number, always a data row (a group row has no cells,\nits number no menu)</li>\n<li>header, filter and column menus: the first displayed row, a <a href=\"#api/index.GroupRow\">GroupRow</a> when the\ndatasource is grouped and <code>undefined</code> when no rows are shown - as <code>cell-header-focus</code> sends it</li>\n<li><code>openMenu()</code>: <code>undefined</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Check with <code>isGroupRow()</code> before reading it as a data row.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rowIndex","signatures":["rowIndex: number"],"doc":"<p>the index of <code>row</code> in the displayed rows (<code>datasource.getRows()</code>): 0 in the header, filter and\ncolumn menus, -1 in a menu opened with <code>openMenu()</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"MenuItem","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface MenuItem"],"doc":"<p>An entry to click. Clicking it - or Enter or Space on it - closes the menu and its submenus, then\ncalls <code>action</code>.</p>\n<p><code>type</code> can be left out, an entry without one is an item.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { isGroupRow, type MenuItem } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst logRow: MenuItem = {\n    id: 'my.logRow',\n    label: 'Log row',\n    hint: 'console',\n    action: (context) =&gt; console.log(context.field, context.row),\n    // only on data rows, and greyed out while nothing is selected\n    visible: (context) =&gt; !isGroupRow(context.row),\n    disabled: (context) =&gt; context.datasource.getSelectedRows().length === 0\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["context-menu"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"action","signatures":["action: (context: MenuContext) => void"],"doc":"<p>called when the item is clicked, after the menu is closed</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"disabled","signatures":["disabled?: (context: MenuContext) => boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> shows the item greyed out, and clicking it does nothing. The keyboard still gets to it,\nas the ARIA menu pattern has it. Called when the menu opens</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"hint","signatures":["hint?: string"],"doc":"<p>shown after the label, in italics and in parentheses: <code>Paste cell (selected rows)</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"id","signatures":["id: string"],"doc":"<p>a name for the entry, unique in its menu. See <a href=\"#api/index.MENU_IDS\">MENU_IDS</a> for the grid&#39;s own</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"label","signatures":["label: string"],"doc":"<p>the text shown</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"selected","signatures":["selected?: (context: MenuContext) => boolean"],"doc":"<p>A toggle or a choice: <code>true</code> shows a ✓ in front of the label - the aggregates of the header\nmenu, the operator in use in the filter menu. With it the item is a <code>menuitemcheckbox</code> for a\nscreen reader, <code>aria-checked</code> says whether it is on. Called when the menu opens</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"tooltip","signatures":["tooltip?: string"],"doc":"<p>what the item does, longer than a label: shown as a tooltip while the pointer rests on it, and read\nby a screen reader as the item&#39;s description (<code>aria-description</code>). The formula fields&#39; function\nmenu has one for each function</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"type","signatures":["type?: \"item\""],"doc":"<p><code>&#39;item&#39;</code>, or left out</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"visible","signatures":["visible?: (context: MenuContext) => boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>false</code> leaves the item out of the menu. Called when the menu opens, left out it is shown</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"MenuPosition","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface MenuPosition"],"doc":"<p>Where <code>gridInterface.openMenu()</code> opens a menu: a point in the window, in px from its left and top\nedges - the same as a mouse event&#39;s <code>clientX</code> / <code>clientY</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { MenuEntry, MenuPosition } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const button: HTMLButtonElement;\ndeclare const entries: MenuEntry[];\n\nconst rect = button.getBoundingClientRect();\nconst position: MenuPosition = { x: rect.left, y: rect.bottom };\ngridInterface.openMenu(position, entries);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"x","signatures":["x: number"],"doc":"<p>px from the left edge of the window</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"y","signatures":["y: number"],"doc":"<p>px from the top edge of the window</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"MenuSection","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface MenuSection"],"doc":"<p>A section header, &quot;Pick a fruit:&quot;, with a line under it. Not clickable, the keyboard passes it by.\nThe grid&#39;s own menus have submenus instead of sections.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { MenuSection } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst section: MenuSection = { type: 'section', id: 'my.export', label: 'Export:' };</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"id","signatures":["id: string"],"doc":"<p>a name for the entry, unique in its menu. See <a href=\"#api/index.MENU_IDS\">MENU_IDS</a> for the grid&#39;s own</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"label","signatures":["label: string"],"doc":"<p>the text shown</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"type","signatures":["type: \"section\""],"doc":"<p>always <code>&#39;section&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"visible","signatures":["visible?: (context: MenuContext) => boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>false</code> leaves the header out of the menu. Called when the menu opens, left out it is shown</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"MenuSeparator","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface MenuSeparator"],"doc":"<p>A dashed line between two entries. Not clickable, the keyboard passes it by.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { MenuSeparator } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst separator: MenuSeparator = { type: 'separator', id: 'my.separator' };</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"id","signatures":["id: string"],"doc":"<p>a name for the entry, unique in its menu. See <a href=\"#api/index.MENU_IDS\">MENU_IDS</a> for the grid&#39;s own</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"type","signatures":["type: \"separator\""],"doc":"<p>always <code>&#39;separator&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"visible","signatures":["visible?: (context: MenuContext) => boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>false</code> leaves the line out of the menu. Called when the menu opens, left out it is shown</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"MenuSubmenu","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface MenuSubmenu"],"doc":"<p>An entry that opens a menu of its own: shown with a <code>›</code> after the label, its <code>entries</code> open beside\nit - on its right, on its left when there is no room on the right, kept in the window. It opens when\nthe pointer rests on it (150ms, so moving the pointer across it to an open submenu does not swap\nthem), on a click, and with ArrowRight, Enter or Space. ArrowLeft and Esc close it again.</p>\n<p>One submenu is open at a time in a menu: moving to another entry closes it. A click on an item in\na submenu closes the whole menu, then calls its action. Submenus can hold submenus.</p>\n<p>A submenu with nothing to show - every item, submenu and block in it hidden by <code>visible</code> - is left\nout of the menu.</p>\n<p>The grid&#39;s own menus have their entries in submenus (<code>row.copy</code>, <code>header.size</code>, ...): change one\nwith <code>map</code>, see <a href=\"#api/index.GridMenus\">GridMenus</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { MenuSubmenu } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const exportAs: (format: string) =&gt; void;\n\nconst exportMenu: MenuSubmenu = {\n    type: 'submenu',\n    id: 'my.export',\n    label: 'Export as',\n    entries: [\n        { id: 'my.export.csv', label: 'CSV', action: () =&gt; exportAs('csv') },\n        { id: 'my.export.json', label: 'JSON', action: () =&gt; exportAs('json') }\n    ]\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["context-menu"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"entries","signatures":["entries: MenuEntry[]"],"doc":"<p>what the submenu shows, in order: the same entries a menu has</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"id","signatures":["id: string"],"doc":"<p>a name for the entry, unique in its menu. See <a href=\"#api/index.MENU_IDS\">MENU_IDS</a> for the grid&#39;s own</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"label","signatures":["label: string"],"doc":"<p>the text shown, a <code>›</code> is put after it</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"type","signatures":["type: \"submenu\""],"doc":"<p>always <code>&#39;submenu&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"visible","signatures":["visible?: (context: MenuContext) => boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>false</code> leaves the submenu out of the menu. Called when the menu opens, left out it is shown</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"NumberFormat","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface NumberFormat"],"doc":"<p>How a <code>number</code> column shows its numbers: <code>ColumnFormat.number</code> - the decimals, the thousands\nseparator and the decimal mark. Every part is optional, <code>{}</code> is <code>1234567.891</code>. What 1234567.891 is\nshown as:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>format</th>\n<th>shows</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>{ thousands: &#39; &#39;, decimal: &#39;,&#39; }</code></td>\n<td><code>1 234 567,891</code> - Norwegian</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ thousands: &#39;,&#39; }</code></td>\n<td><code>1,234,567.891</code> - English</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ thousands: &quot;&#39;&quot; }</code></td>\n<td><code>1&#39;234&#39;567.891</code> - Swiss</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ decimals: 2, thousands: &#39; &#39;, decimal: &#39;,&#39; }</code></td>\n<td><code>1 234 567,89</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ decimals: 0 }</code></td>\n<td><code>1234568</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>{ decimals: 1, percent: true }</code> on 0.256</td>\n<td><code>25.6 %</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The same character can not be both separators: <code>{ thousands: &#39;.&#39; }</code> (the decimal mark is <code>.</code> too)\nthrows a <code>TypeError</code>, give it <code>decimal: &#39;,&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig, NumberFormat } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst norwegian: NumberFormat = { decimals: 2, thousands: ' ', decimal: ',' }; // 1 234 567,89\nconst columns: GridConfig['columns'] = { balance: { format: { number: norwegian } } };</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"decimal","signatures":["decimal?: \",\" | \".\""],"doc":"<p>the decimal mark, <code>&#39;.&#39;</code> or <code>&#39;,&#39;</code>. Left out: <code>&#39;.&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"decimals","signatures":["decimals?: 0 | 2 | 1 | 3 | 4"],"doc":"<p>the decimals shown, 0 to 4: rounded half away from zero, of the number as it is written\n(<code>1.005</code> is <code>1.01</code>) - the decimals a number has are padded with 0. Left out: the decimals the\nnumber has, as the field&#39;s formatter shows them (at most 20)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"percent","signatures":["percent?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: the number times 100, with <code> %</code> after it - 0.256 is <code>25.6 %</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"thousands","signatures":["thousands?: \" \" | \",\" | \".\" | \"'\""],"doc":"<p>between the thousands: <code>&#39; &#39;</code> a space, <code>&#39;,&#39;</code> a comma, <code>&#39;.&#39;</code> a dot or <code>&quot;&#39;&quot;</code> an apostrophe. Left\nout: none. The space is a plain space (U+0020), not the no-break space <code>Intl.NumberFormat(&#39;nb-NO&#39;)</code>\nwrites: a cell is one line, and Find finds a space typed</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ReadImportFileOptions","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ReadImportFileOptions"],"doc":"<p>How <a href=\"#api/index.readImportFile\">readImportFile</a> reads a file. Every option is optional.</p>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"separator","signatures":["separator?: CsvSeparator"],"doc":"<p>the separator of a CSV file: <code>&#39;,&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;;&#39;</code> or <code>&#39;\\t&#39;</code>. Default the one that splits the first lines evenly, see the import guide</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"sheet","signatures":["sheet?: string | number"],"doc":"<p>the sheet of a workbook to read: its index (from 0) or its name. Default the first. Not used for CSV</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ReconciledGrid","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ReconciledGrid"],"doc":"<p>What <a href=\"#api/index.reconcileColumns\">reconcileColumns</a> returns</p>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"grid","signatures":["grid: ExportedGrid"],"doc":"<p>the saved grid with the source&#39;s columns: a new one, the one given is not changed</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"report","signatures":["report: ColumnsReport"],"doc":"<p>what changed</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ReconcileOptions","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ReconcileOptions"],"doc":"<p>How <a href=\"#api/index.reconcileColumns\">reconcileColumns</a> brings a grid up to date</p>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"showNew","signatures":["showNew?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: a new column is shown - at the end of the scrolling columns, <code>width</code> px wide. Default <code>false</code>:\nit is hidden, the column chooser lists it</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"width","signatures":["width?: number"],"doc":"<p>the width in px of a new column shown, default 100</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"RemovedConflict","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface RemovedConflict<T = any>"],"doc":"<p>A row in conflict as a whole: <code>datasource.upsert(rows, { removeMissing: true })</code> did not get it from\nthe server, but the row has local changes - edits, a deletion mark, or the user is typing in it. It\nis kept, with this conflict, instead of being removed.</p>\n<p>Part of <a href=\"#api/index.Conflict\">Conflict</a>, see there.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of the rows, the <code>T</code> of <code>Datasource&lt;T&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { RemovedConflict } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst describe = (conflict: RemovedConflict) =&gt; `row ${conflict.row.__KEY} is no longer on the server`;</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"field","signatures":["field: null"],"doc":"<p>always <code>null</code>: the row as a whole, not a field. Tells it from a <a href=\"#api/index.ValueConflict\">ValueConflict</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"remote","signatures":["remote: \"removed\""],"doc":"<p>always <code>&#39;removed&#39;</code>: the server no longer has the row</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"row","signatures":["row: EntityUnion<T>"],"doc":"<p>the row, the one the datasource handed out</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"RemovedRule","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface RemovedRule"],"doc":"<p>A colour rule <a href=\"#api/index.reconcileColumns\">reconcileColumns</a> took out</p>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"field","signatures":["field: string"],"doc":"<p>the column the rule was on</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rule","signatures":["rule: ColorRule"],"doc":"<p>the rule as it was</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"RuleCondition","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface RuleCondition"],"doc":"<p>A condition of a colour rule of the kind <em>Conditions</em> (<code>ColorRule.conditions</code>): a field of the row - the\ncolumn&#39;s own, another, a calculated column - an operator and a value, tested as the header filter of\nthat field tests what is typed in it (the field&#39;s type, its formatter, a lookup column&#39;s label, its\n<code>filterCaseSensitive</code>).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { RuleCondition } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst late: RuleCondition = { field: 'status', operator: 'EQUAL', value: 'late' };\nconst big: RuleCondition = { field: 'balance', operator: 'GREATER_THAN', value: '1000' };</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"datePreset","signatures":["datePreset?: DatePreset"],"doc":"<p>a date field: a quick date as the value - the days of <code>thisWeek</code> ... - see <a href=\"#api/index.ColorRule\">ColorRule</a> <code>datePreset</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"field","signatures":["field: string"],"doc":"<p>the field: a field of the datasource, a column of the grid, a calculated column</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"operator","signatures":["operator: FilterOperator"],"doc":"<p>an operator the field&#39;s type offers, not <code>IN</code> / <code>NOT_IN</code> - a lookup column takes a text&#39;s</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"value","signatures":["value?: string | [string, string]"],"doc":"<p>the value as typed in the field&#39;s header filter, <code>[from, to]</code> for <code>BETWEEN</code>, none for <code>IS_BLANK</code> / <code>IS_NOT_BLANK</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"week","signatures":["week?: RuleWeek"],"doc":"<p>a date field: the weeks of <code>value</code> (<code>2026-W47</code>) and of <code>datePreset</code> - see <a href=\"#api/index.ColorRule\">ColorRule</a> <code>week</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"SortArgument","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface SortArgument"],"doc":"<p>One field to sort on, and the direction. <code>datasource.sort()</code> takes one or a list of them, the first\nin the list decides first. It is what <code>GridState.sorting</code> holds.</p>\n<p>Blank values (null, undefined, <code>&#39;&#39;</code>) come first when ascending, last when descending.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { SortArgument } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst byAge: SortArgument = { attribute: 'age', ascending: false };\ndatasource.sort([{ attribute: 'country', ascending: true }, byAge]);</code></pre>\n","samples":["sorting-grouping"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"ascending","signatures":["ascending: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> for A-Z / 0-9 / oldest first, <code>false</code> for the other way round</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"attribute","signatures":["attribute: string"],"doc":"<p>the field to sort on</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"TypeFormats","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface TypeFormats"],"doc":"<p>The formats of the columns by type: how a column of a type shows its values when it has no date or\nnumber format of its own - <code>GridConfig.typeFormats</code>, <code>GridState.typeFormats</code>, the Defaults tab of the\ngrid config dialog. A type left out shows the field&#39;s formatter.</p>\n<p>A column&#39;s own format wins (<code>ColumnFormat.date</code>, <code>.number</code>); one shown as checkboxes shows no number,\nand a lookup column shows its labels. The rest of a column&#39;s format - its label, its template, its\nblank / 0 - stays: <code>{value}</code> of a template is the value in the type&#39;s format.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig, TypeFormats } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// every date as 22.11.2026, every number as 1 234 567,89 - a column can still have its own\nconst typeFormats: TypeFormats = { date: 'norwegian', number: { decimals: 2, thousands: ' ', decimal: ',' } };\nconst config: Partial&lt;GridConfig&gt; = { typeFormats };</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"date","signatures":["date?: DateFormat"],"doc":"<p>the format of a <code>date</code> column, see <a href=\"#api/index.DateFormat\">DateFormat</a>: no time of day (<code>&#39;isoTime&#39;</code> ...)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datetime","signatures":["datetime?: DateFormat"],"doc":"<p>the format of a <code>datetime</code> column, see <a href=\"#api/index.DateFormat\">DateFormat</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"number","signatures":["number?: NumberFormat"],"doc":"<p>the format of a <code>number</code> column, see <a href=\"#api/index.NumberFormat\">NumberFormat</a></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"UpsertOptions","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface UpsertOptions"],"doc":"<p>The options of <code>datasource.upsert(rows, options)</code>. Both are optional.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { UpsertOptions } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const rowsFromServer: object[];\n\n// the server sent every row: the rows it did not send are gone there\nconst options: UpsertOptions = { removeMissing: true };\ndatasource.upsert(rowsFromServer, options);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"refilter","signatures":["refilter?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>false</code> to leave the filter out, default <code>true</code>: the filter runs on the rows, so a row whose new\nvalues the filter leaves out is no longer shown. With <code>false</code> the rows shown stay shown (the\nrows added are shown too) until the filter runs again - the sorting and grouping still run, as\nfor <code>setData(rows, { refilter: false })</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"removeMissing","signatures":["removeMissing?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when the rows are every row there is (a full poll): a row whose key is not among them\nis removed. Default <code>false</code>, the rows are changes only (a push of what changed). A row with\nlocal changes is not removed, it gets a <a href=\"#api/index.RemovedConflict\">RemovedConflict</a>; a new row (<code>addNewEmpty()</code>)\nis never removed, the server does not have it yet</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"UpsertResult","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface UpsertResult<T = any>"],"doc":"<p>What <code>datasource.upsert()</code> did, the rows themselves (not copies).</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of the rows, the <code>T</code> of <code>Datasource&lt;T&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>declare const rowsFromServer: object[];\n\nconst { added, updated, removed, conflicts } = datasource.upsert(rowsFromServer, { removeMissing: true });\nconsole.log(`${added.length} new, ${updated.length} changed, ${removed.length} removed, ${conflicts.length} conflicts`);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"added","signatures":["added: EntityUnion<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>the rows of keys that were not in the data: added, as loaded rows (not new, not edited)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"conflicts","signatures":["conflicts: Conflict<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>the conflicts this upsert made, or gave a newer server value. <code>getConflicts()</code> has every one</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"removed","signatures":["removed: EntityUnion<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>the rows <code>removeMissing</code> removed</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"updated","signatures":["updated: EntityUnion<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>the rows a value of the server changed, or that got a conflict - each once</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"V5Filter","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface V5Filter"],"doc":"<p>A filter as v5 had it: <code>datasource.filter()</code>, <code>GridConfig.filter</code>, <code>getFilter()</code>. A group has\n<code>type: &#39;GROUP&#39;</code> and <code>filterArguments</code>, a condition <code>attribute</code>, <code>operator</code>, <code>value</code> - <code>valueType: &#39;ATTRIBUTE&#39;</code> when the value is the name of another field. <code>attributeType</code> is the datasource&#39;s field\ntype in v6, it is dropped.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { V5Filter } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst v5: V5Filter = {\n    type: 'GROUP',\n    logicalOperator: 'AND',\n    filterArguments: [{ type: 'CONDITION', attribute: 'age', operator: 'GREATER_THAN', value: 18, valueType: 'VALUE' }]\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"attribute","signatures":["attribute?: string | null"],"doc":"<p>a condition&#39;s field</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"attributeType","signatures":["attributeType?: string | null"],"doc":"<p>the field&#39;s type: dropped, the datasource&#39;s <code>fields</code> have it in v6</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"filterArguments","signatures":["filterArguments?: V5Filter[]"],"doc":"<p>a group&#39;s conditions and groups</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"logicalOperator","signatures":["logicalOperator?: \"AND\" | \"OR\" | \"NONE\""],"doc":"<p>a group&#39;s: <code>&#39;OR&#39;</code> is an OR group, anything else AND</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"operator","signatures":["operator?: string | null"],"doc":"<p>a condition&#39;s operator: the names of v6</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"type","signatures":["type?: \"GROUP\" | \"CONDITION\""],"doc":"<p><code>&#39;GROUP&#39;</code> for a group, <code>&#39;CONDITION&#39;</code> for a condition</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"value","signatures":["value?: unknown"],"doc":"<p>a condition&#39;s value - the name of another field with <code>valueType: &#39;ATTRIBUTE&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"valueType","signatures":["valueType?: \"VALUE\" | \"ATTRIBUTE\" | null"],"doc":"<p><code>&#39;ATTRIBUTE&#39;</code>: <code>value</code> is another field, a <code>valueField</code> in v6</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ValidationError","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ValidationError<T = unknown>"],"doc":"<p>The validation errors of one field of one row, what <code>datasource.validate()</code> and <code>getErrors()</code>\nreturn a list of.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of your rows, the <code>T</code> of <code>Datasource&lt;T&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { ValidationError } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst errors: ValidationError[] = datasource.validate();\nfor (const { row, field, messages } of errors) {\n    console.log(row.__KEY, datasource.getField(field).label, messages.join(', '));\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["validation"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"field","signatures":["field: string"],"doc":"<p>the field</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"messages","signatures":["messages: string[]"],"doc":"<p>a message per rule the value fails, in the order of the field&#39;s rules</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"row","signatures":["row: Entity & T"],"doc":"<p>the row itself, not a copy</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ValidationRuleObject","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ValidationRuleObject"],"doc":"<p>A validation rule written out: the id of its validator, its options, and a message of its own.\nThe validator gets it as its <code>rule</code> argument - a rule given as text (<code>&#39;required&#39;</code>) is\n<code>{ id: &#39;required&#39; }</code> there.</p>\n<p>The built-in validators take their option as <code>value</code> (see <a href=\"#api/index.registerValidator\">registerValidator</a>). A validator\nof your own can take any options: they are what the rule has besides <code>id</code> and <code>message</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { ValidationRuleObject } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst atLeastZero: ValidationRuleObject = { id: 'min', value: 0 };\nconst notTooOld: ValidationRuleObject = { id: 'max', value: 150, message: 'too old, at most {value}' };</code></pre>\n","samples":["validation"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"id","signatures":["id: string"],"doc":"<p>the id of the validator: a built-in one (<code>&#39;required&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;min&#39;</code> ...) or one registered with <a href=\"#api/index.registerValidator\">registerValidator</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"message","signatures":["message?: string"],"doc":"<p>the message when the value fails the rule, instead of the validator&#39;s: the message itself, or a\ntext id - a text set with <code>setTexts()</code>, so it can be translated. <code>{name}</code> in it is replaced by\nthe rule&#39;s option <code>name</code>: <code>&#39;at most {value}&#39;</code> is <code>&#39;at most 150&#39;</code> for <code>{ id: &#39;max&#39;, value: 150 }</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ValueConflict","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ValueConflict<T = any>"],"doc":"<p>A field in conflict: <code>datasource.upsert()</code> brought a new value from the server for a field the user\nhas edited and not saved (or is typing in). The user&#39;s value is kept in the row, the server&#39;s is\nthe field&#39;s original now - so <code>getChanges()</code> sends the user&#39;s value, as an edit of what the server\nhas now.</p>\n<p>Part of <a href=\"#api/index.Conflict\">Conflict</a>, see there. <code>getConflicts()</code> makes the objects: <code>local</code> is the value the row\nhas when it is called.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of the rows, the <code>T</code> of <code>Datasource&lt;T&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { ValueConflict } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst describe = (conflict: ValueConflict) =&gt;\n    `${conflict.field}: yours ${conflict.local}, the server's ${conflict.remote} (it was ${conflict.original})`;</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"field","signatures":["field: string"],"doc":"<p>the field in conflict</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"local","signatures":["local: unknown"],"doc":"<p>the user&#39;s value: the value the row has, kept by the merge</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"original","signatures":["original: unknown"],"doc":"<p>the value the user&#39;s edit started from: the original before the server changed it. A second\nmerge that changes the field again keeps it, it gives <code>remote</code> the newer value</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"remote","signatures":["remote: unknown"],"doc":"<p>the server&#39;s value: the field&#39;s original now, what <code>resolveConflict(row, field, &#39;remote&#39;)</code> takes</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"row","signatures":["row: EntityUnion<T>"],"doc":"<p>the row, the one the datasource handed out</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"AggregateFunction","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type AggregateFunction = \"sum\" | \"avg\" | \"min\" | \"max\" | \"count\""],"doc":"<p>How <a href=\"#api/index.Datasource\">Datasource.aggregate</a> sums up the values of a field over rows. Blank values (<code>null</code>,\n<code>undefined</code>, <code>&#39;&#39;</code>, an invalid <code>Date</code>) are left out by all of them; <code>0</code> and <code>false</code> are values.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>function</th>\n<th>the result</th>\n<th>of no values</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>&#39;sum&#39;</code></td>\n<td>the sum of the numbers</td>\n<td><code>0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;avg&#39;</code></td>\n<td>the average of the numbers: their sum / how many there are</td>\n<td><code>null</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;min&#39;</code></td>\n<td>the smallest number</td>\n<td><code>null</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;max&#39;</code></td>\n<td>the largest number</td>\n<td><code>null</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;count&#39;</code></td>\n<td>how many values are not blank, of any type</td>\n<td><code>0</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><code>sum</code>, <code>avg</code>, <code>min</code> and <code>max</code> take numbers only: a value that is no number (text, even <code>&#39;12&#39;</code>, a\n<code>Date</code>, <code>NaN</code>, <code>Infinity</code>) is left out, as a blank is. Nothing is rounded: format the result with the field&#39;s\nformatter. The sum is added up with a compensated sum (Neumaier), so it does not drift away over\nmany rows: 100 000 times <code>0.1</code> is <code>10000</code>.</p>\n<p>It is what a column&#39;s <code>aggregate</code> in the grid config shows, in the group rows and the totals row.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { AggregateFunction } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst fn: AggregateFunction = 'sum';\ndatasource.aggregate('balance', fn); // over the rows the filter lets through</code></pre>\n","samples":["aggregates"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"CalculatedType","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type CalculatedType = \"number\" | \"text\" | \"date\" | \"boolean\""],"doc":"<p>The type of the values of a calculated column: a number, a text, a date or true / false - the type\nits formula gives. A <code>boolean</code> column shows checkboxes, a <code>date</code> column its day.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { CalculatedType } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst type: CalculatedType = 'number';</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"CellRenderer","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type CellRenderer<T = unknown> = (host: HTMLElement) => CellRendererInstance<T>"],"doc":"<p>A cell renderer: called once per cell element that shows a column with this renderer. Render into\n<code>host</code>, keep what you need, and return what the grid calls from then on, see <a href=\"#api/index.CellRendererInstance\">CellRendererInstance</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of the rows, as in the datasource</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type CellRenderer, registerCellRenderer } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ninterface Task {\n    done: boolean;\n}\n\n// typed rows: context.row is a Task\nconst doneMark: CellRenderer&lt;Task&gt; = (host) =&gt; ({\n    update(context) {\n        host.textContent = context.row.done ? 'yes' : 'no';\n    }\n});\nregisterCellRenderer('done', doneMark);</code></pre>\n","samples":["custom-cells"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"ColType","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type ColType = \"group\" | \"selector\" | \"left-pinned\" | \"middle-pinned\" | \"right-pinned\""],"doc":"<p>Which section of the grid a cell is in, the <code>colType</code> of the grid events:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&#39;left-pinned&#39;</code> - the columns pinned left (<code>GridLayout.left</code>)</li>\n<li><code>&#39;middle-pinned&#39;</code> - the columns that scroll sideways (<code>GridLayout.center</code>)</li>\n<li><code>&#39;right-pinned&#39;</code> - the columns pinned right (<code>GridLayout.right</code>)</li>\n<li><code>&#39;selector&#39;</code> - the row selector at the far left, with the row numbers</li>\n<li><code>&#39;group&#39;</code> - the cells of a group row</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.on('cell-click', (data) =&gt; {\n    if (data.colType === 'left-pinned') {\n        console.log('a pinned column', data.attribute);\n    }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"ColumnConfig","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type ColumnConfig"],"doc":"<p>The options of one column, in <code>GridConfig.columns</code> under the field&#39;s name. Every option is\noptional, a field without an entry gets the defaults.</p>\n<p>The type of the column comes from the datasource (<code>datasource.getField(field).type</code>), set it in the\ndatasource&#39;s <code>fields</code>, not here. So do the validation rules: a value the user has to fill in is the\nfield&#39;s <code>required</code> rule (<code>fields: { company: { validate: [&#39;required&#39;] } }</code>), which also gives its\nempty editable cells the grid&#39;s blue stripes (<code>simple-html-mandatory</code>). It replaces v5&#39;s\n<code>mandatory</code> column option.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { ColumnConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst columns: Record&lt;string, ColumnConfig&gt; = {\n    company: { label: 'Company', placeholderRow: 'required' },\n    age: { operator: 'EQUAL', numberOverride: 'ZERO_TO_BLANK' },\n    born: { placeholderFilter: 'from date', readonly: true },\n    country: { focusButton: 'ALWAYS', allowPasteClearOnly: true }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["basic-grid"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"aggregate","signatures":["aggregate?: AggregateFunction | AggregateFunction[]"],"doc":"<p>sums the column up: <code>&#39;sum&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;avg&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;min&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;max&#39;</code> or <code>&#39;count&#39;</code> - one, or a list of them\n(<code>[&#39;sum&#39;, &#39;avg&#39;]</code>), see <a href=\"#api/index.AggregateFunction\">AggregateFunction</a>. The grid shows each in the column&#39;s place in\neach group row (<code>GridConfig.groupAggregates</code>, on by default) and in the totals row\n(<code>GridConfig.totalsRow</code>), a line each in the order sum, avg, min, max, count: the label at the\nleft, the value at the right - <code>Sum        1 234,50</code> (the texts <code>aggregate.*</code>). The datasource\ncomputes them: <code>datasource.aggregate(field, fn)</code>.</p>\n<p>These are where the grid starts: the user turns functions on and off in the header menu (right\nclick a column label, &quot;Aggregate:&quot;), and they are part of the grid&#39;s state\n(<code>GridState.aggregates</code>), <code>resetState()</code> goes back to these.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>sum</code>, <code>avg</code>, <code>min</code> and <code>max</code> are for a <code>number</code> field (the datasource&#39;s <code>fields</code>), anything\nelse throws a <code>TypeError</code> when the grid is made or <code>updateConfig()</code> is given the column. They\ntake the numbers, blanks and what is no number are left out. The value is shown with the\nfield&#39;s formatter, not rounded: give the field a formatter with the decimals you want, or the\ncolumn a display format with them (<code>format: { number: { decimals: 2 } }</code>).</li>\n<li><code>count</code> counts the values that are not blank, in a field of any type. Shown as a whole number.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    columns: {\n        balance: { aggregate: ['sum', 'avg'] },\n        age: { aggregate: 'avg' },\n        email: { aggregate: 'count' }\n    },\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['email'], width: 200 }, { fields: ['age'], width: 80 }, { fields: ['balance'], width: 120 }] },\n    totalsRow: true\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["aggregates"]},{"name":"allowPasteClearOnly","signatures":["allowPasteClearOnly?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>the cells can not be typed in, only changed by the row menu&#39;s paste and clear (and by your own\ncode, e.g. a dialog from <code>focusButton</code>). Typed text is undone right away. A column with an\n<code>editor</code> is never typed in, its list opens as without this option</p>\n","samples":["misc-options"]},{"name":"datePresets","signatures":["datePresets?: DatePreset[] | false"],"doc":"<p>the quick date filters the column&#39;s filter menu offers - <em>Quick dates</em>, one click each: Today,\nYesterday, This week, Last week, This month ... in the order given. Left out: every one but\n<code>&#39;overdue&#39;</code> (see <a href=\"#api/index.DATE_PRESETS\">DATE_PRESETS</a>, <a href=\"#api/index.DatePreset\">DatePreset</a>). <code>false</code> (or <code>[]</code>): none, the menu has\nno Quick dates.</p>\n<p>For a <code>date</code> or <code>datetime</code> column whose header filter offers <code>BETWEEN</code> (a quick date is a range of\ndays). A <code>TypeError</code> when the grid is made or <code>updateConfig()</code> is given the column: an id that is no\nquick date, or the option on another type (a lookup column filters as text). It limits what the\nuser picks: a state from <code>setState()</code> can hold any quick date.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    columns: {\n        dueDate: { datePresets: ['today', 'next7Days', 'thisMonth', 'overdue'] },\n        born: { datePresets: false } // no quick dates\n    },\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['dueDate'], width: 110 }, { fields: ['born'], width: 110 }] }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"]},{"name":"dynamicCellTypeColumn","signatures":["dynamicCellTypeColumn?: string"],"doc":"<p>the name of another column whose value in the row is the type of this cell -\n<code>&#39;text&#39; | &#39;number&#39; | &#39;boolean&#39; | &#39;date&#39; | &#39;datetime&#39;</code>. A number/text/date etc in the same\ncolumn, for property/value style data. Only for a <code>text</code> field (the default), and a value that\nis no type leaves the cell <code>text</code>.\nPS! sorting, grouping and filtering still use the field&#39;s own type</p>\n","samples":["dynamic-cell-types"]},{"name":"editor","signatures":["editor?: ColumnEditor"],"doc":"<p>the value is picked from a list: a select or a dropdown grid, of the rows of a lookup registered\nwith <a href=\"#api/index.registerLookup\">registerLookup</a> - see <a href=\"#api/index.ColumnEditor\">ColumnEditor</a>. The cell stores the value of the picked\nrow (the lookup&#39;s <code>valueField</code>) and shows its label (<code>labelField</code>). For a <code>text</code> or <code>number</code>\nfield.</p>\n<p>The cell is not typed in: a character opens the list with it as the search, so do the button at\nits right, Alt+ArrowDown, F4, F2, Space and a double click. Delete and Backspace empty the cell.\nNot in a readonly grid or cell: there it shows the label only.</p>\n<p>Sorting the column sorts on the labels, typing in its header filter finds the rows whose label\nmatches, the filter menu&#39;s value list lists the labels, the CSV export and copy write the labels -\nsee the lookups guide.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// registerLookup('countries', ...) and registerLookup('customers', ...) when the page loads\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    readonly: false,\n    columns: {\n        country: { label: 'Country', editor: { type: 'select', lookup: 'countries' } },\n        customerId: { label: 'Customer', editor: { type: 'grid', lookup: 'customers', set: { customerName: 'name' } } }\n    },\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['country'], width: 120 }, { fields: ['customerId'], width: 180 }] }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["lookups","dropdown-grid"]},{"name":"filterCaseSensitive","signatures":["filterCaseSensitive?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: the grid&#39;s conditions on the column match case - <code>Ann</code> does not find <code>ANN</code>. The header\nfilter (the value typed and the value list) and the row menu&#39;s filter give their conditions\n<code>caseSensitive: true</code>, the filter editor&#39;s toggle (Aa) is on for it and can not be turned off,\nand so is the header menu&#39;s &quot;Match case&quot;. Default <code>false</code>: the user turns &quot;Match case&quot; on per\ncolumn in the header filter&#39;s menu (<code>GridState.headerFilters[field].caseSensitive</code>). For a text\ncolumn (and a lookup column), <code>true</code> on another type throws a <code>TypeError</code> when the grid is made.\nSee <a href=\"#api/index.FilterCondition\">FilterCondition</a> <code>caseSensitive</code></p>\n","samples":["filtering"]},{"name":"filterOnType","signatures":["filterOnType?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: the column&#39;s header filter filters as you type, after a short pause (300ms) - no Enter\nneeded. A number or date column filters when the text is a number or a date, not while one is half\ntyped. Left out: the grid&#39;s <code>filterOnType</code>, else <code>false</code>. The user turns it on and off in the\noperator choice of the header filter, Filter › in its menu and the grid config dialog - state,\n<code>GridState.headerFilters[field].filterOnType</code>. Ignored on a boolean column: its checkbox filters on\na click</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    columns: { name: { operator: 'CONTAINS', filterOnType: true } }, // a search as you type\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 150 }] }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"filterOperators","signatures":["filterOperators?: FilterOperator[]"],"doc":"<p>the operators the column offers in the grid: in the header filter&#39;s menu (Operator ›, Blank ›,\nthe value list needs <code>IN</code>) and the filter editor&#39;s operator picker. A list of operators of the\ncolumn&#39;s type (see <a href=\"#api/index.operatorsFor\">operatorsFor</a>), shown in the type&#39;s order. Default: every operator of\nthe type.</p>\n<p>A <code>TypeError</code> when the grid is made or <code>updateConfig()</code> is given the column: an operator the type\ndoes not have, an empty list, or one without an operator the header filter&#39;s input takes (any\nbut <code>IN</code>, <code>NOT_IN</code>, <code>IS_BLANK</code>, <code>IS_NOT_BLANK</code>). <code>operator</code> must be one of them. A lookup column\n(<code>editor</code>) filters as text in its header; in the filter editor a lookup on a number field offers\nthe number operators. It limits what the user picks, not the filter: <code>datasource.filter()</code> and a\nstate from <code>setState()</code> can hold any condition.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    columns: {\n        name: { filterOperators: ['CONTAINS', 'BEGIN_WITH', 'IS_BLANK'] }, // starts with CONTAINS\n        age: { filterOperators: ['EQUAL', 'BETWEEN'], operator: 'BETWEEN' }\n    },\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 150 }, { fields: ['age'], width: 80 }] }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"]},{"name":"focusButton","signatures":["focusButton?: \"SHOW_IF_GRID_NOT_READONLY\" | \"SHOW_IF_GRID_AND_CELL_NOT_READONLY\" | \"ALWAYS\""],"doc":"<p>shows a <code>...</code> button at the right of the cell while it has focus; clicking it, or Space in the cell,\nsends the <code>cell-focus-button-click</code> event - open a dialog or a dropdown of your own from there. When\nit is shown: <code>&#39;SHOW_IF_GRID_NOT_READONLY&#39;</code> the grid is editable, <code>&#39;SHOW_IF_GRID_AND_CELL_NOT_READONLY&#39;</code>\nthe grid and the cell are editable, <code>&#39;ALWAYS&#39;</code> always. Not on a boolean (checkbox) cell.</p>\n<p>To pick the value from a list, <code>editor</code> does it all - its button, the keys, writing the value.\nA column has one of the two: both throw a <code>TypeError</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"format","signatures":["format?: ColumnFormat"],"doc":"<p>how the column&#39;s cells show the value - a display format, see <a href=\"#api/index.ColumnFormat\">ColumnFormat</a>: an object with\n<code>date</code> for a <code>date</code> or <code>datetime</code> field, a <a href=\"#api/index.DateFormat\">DateFormat</a> (<code>{ date: &#39;norwegian&#39; }</code> 22.11.2026,\n<code>{ date: &#39;weekIso&#39; }</code> 2026-W47, <code>{ date: &#39;daysUntil&#39; }</code> ...), <code>number</code> for a <code>number</code> field, a\n<a href=\"#api/index.NumberFormat\">NumberFormat</a> (<code>{ number: { decimals: 2, thousands: &#39; &#39;, decimal: &#39;,&#39; } }</code> 1 234 567,89),\n<code>text</code> and <code>link</code> for a <code>text</code> field - a template of the text shown (<code>{ text: &#39;{name} ({id})&#39; }</code>)\nand a link, see <a href=\"#api/index.LinkFormat\">LinkFormat</a> (<code>{ link: { url: &#39;mailto:{email}&#39; } }</code>). Left out: the field&#39;s\nformatter.</p>\n<p>The rest of what the grid config dialog sets is here too: <code>label</code>, the empty cells&#39;\n<code>placeholderRow</code> / <code>placeholderRowLabel</code>, a number column&#39;s <code>numberOverride</code>, and <code>checkbox</code> - the cells\nof a text or number column as checkboxes, see <a href=\"#api/index.CheckboxFormat\">CheckboxFormat</a>\n(<code>{ checkbox: { checked: &#39;1&#39;, unchecked: &#39;0&#39; } }</code>).</p>\n<p>Only the text shown changes: the cells, the aggregates of the column, the summary of the selected\ncells, Find. The value is not changed, and editing, the header filter, sorting, grouping, copy and\nthe CSV export keep to the field&#39;s formatter - a cell shown as <code>2026-W47</code> is edited as\n<code>2026-11-22</code>, a link&#39;s cell as its value. The Excel export writes the value with an Excel number\nformat like it, where Excel has one.</p>\n<p>This is where the grid starts: the user picks another one in the header menu (right click a column\nlabel, &quot;Format&quot;) or the grid config dialog (the gear in the footer), and it is part of the\ngrid&#39;s state (<code>GridState.formats</code>) - <code>resetState()</code> goes back to this one, and so does the dialog&#39;s\n&quot;Reset column&quot;. A format that does not fit the field&#39;s type, and a format on a lookup column\n(<code>editor</code>), throw a <code>TypeError</code> when the grid is made or <code>updateConfig()</code> is given the column.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    columns: {\n        born: { format: { date: 'norwegian' } }, // 22.11.2026\n        due: { format: { date: 'daysUntil' } }, // 3: due in 3 days\n        balance: { format: { number: { decimals: 2, thousands: ' ', decimal: ',' } } }, // 1 234 567,89\n        email: { format: { link: { url: 'mailto:{email}' } } }, // a link that writes an email\n        newsletter: { format: { label: 'News', checkbox: {} } } // '1' / '0' as checkboxes\n    },\n    layout: {\n        center: [\n            { fields: ['born'], width: 100 },\n            { fields: ['due'], width: 80 },\n            { fields: ['balance'], width: 120 },\n            { fields: ['email'], width: 180 },\n            { fields: ['newsletter'], width: 80 }\n        ]\n    }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["full-grid"]},{"name":"label","signatures":["label?: string"],"doc":"<p>the column&#39;s header text. Left out, the label of the datasource field (<code>FieldConfig.label</code>) is\nused, and without that the field name prettified (<code>first_name</code> is <code>First Name</code>). The grid shows\nthe same label everywhere: header, column chooser, group chip, filter editor, footer filter, the\nheaders of the exports. The label the user gives the column in the grid config dialog\n(<code>format.label</code>, <a href=\"#api/index.ColumnFormat\">ColumnFormat</a>) wins</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"numberOverride","signatures":["numberOverride?: \"ZERO_TO_BLANK\" | \"BLANK_TO_ZERO\""],"doc":"<p>for a number field, what a cell shows - the value is not changed: <code>&#39;ZERO_TO_BLANK&#39;</code> shows 0 as an\nempty cell, <code>&#39;BLANK_TO_ZERO&#39;</code> shows an empty value as <code>0</code>. Default: the value as the formatter\nshows it. The user&#39;s from the grid config dialog (<code>format.numberOverride</code>, Show blank as 0,\nShow 0 as blank) wins - its <code>&#39;NONE&#39;</code> turns this off</p>\n","samples":["misc-options"]},{"name":"operator","signatures":["operator?: FilterOperator"],"doc":"<p>the operator the column&#39;s header filter starts with. Default <code>&#39;GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO&#39;</code> for\nnumber and date fields, <code>&#39;EQUAL&#39;</code> for the rest (the first of <code>filterOperators</code> when they do not\nhave it). For text <code>&#39;EQUAL&#39;</code> is the whole text, ignoring case: <code>ann</code> finds <code>Ann</code>, not <code>Anna</code>. Set\n<code>&#39;CONTAINS&#39;</code> for a search anywhere in the text, <code>&#39;BEGIN_WITH&#39;</code> for the start. The operator the\nuser picks in the header filter&#39;s menu is state: <code>GridState.headerFilters[field].operator</code>.</p>\n<p>One the header filter&#39;s input can take, of the column&#39;s operators (<code>filterOperators</code>, else the\ntype&#39;s, see <a href=\"#api/index.operatorsFor\">operatorsFor</a>) - not <code>IN</code>, <code>NOT_IN</code>, <code>IS_BLANK</code> or <code>IS_NOT_BLANK</code>, those are\nthe value list&#39;s and the Blank submenu&#39;s. Anything else throws a <code>TypeError</code> when the grid is made\nor <code>updateConfig()</code> is given the column. A lookup column (<code>editor</code>) filters as text.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    columns: { name: { operator: 'CONTAINS' } }, // `ann` finds Ann, Anna and Joanna\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 150 }] }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["filter-operator-header"]},{"name":"placeholderFilter","signatures":["placeholderFilter?: string"],"doc":"<p>shown in the empty header filter. Default: the formatter&#39;s placeholder (date fields), else the field&#39;s type: <code>Text</code> or <code>Number</code> (texts <code>filter.placeholder.*</code>).</p>\n","samples":["required-placeholders"]},{"name":"placeholderRow","signatures":["placeholderRow?: string"],"doc":"<p>shown in an empty cell, see <code>GridConfig.placeholderRowCurrentEntityOnly</code>. The user&#39;s from the grid\nconfig dialog (<code>format.placeholderRow</code>, or the column&#39;s label with <code>format.placeholderRowLabel</code>) wins</p>\n","samples":["required-placeholders"]},{"name":"readonly","signatures":["readonly?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>makes the column&#39;s cells readonly while the grid is editable (<code>GridConfig.readonly: false</code>). The\ngrid draws red stripes behind them. The <code>isReadonly</code> hook (<a href=\"#api/index.GridHooks\">GridHooks</a>) can decide per row\ninstead. The user&#39;s from the grid config dialog (<code>format.readonly</code>, Read only) wins - so it is a\ndefault the user can change, <code>GridConfig.edit</code> (<a href=\"#api/index.EditPermissions\">EditPermissions</a>) is what they may not. A\nfield that is never edited is locked in the datasource&#39;s fields (<code>FieldConfig.readonly</code>)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"renderer","signatures":["renderer?: string"],"doc":"<p>draws the column&#39;s cells with a renderer of your own - a badge, a progress bar, a link, a select:\nthe id it was registered under with <a href=\"#api/index.registerCellRenderer\">registerCellRenderer</a>, so the config stays plain JSON.\nAn id that is not registered throws a <code>TypeError</code> when the grid is made or <code>updateConfig()</code> is\ngiven the column: register the renderer when the page loads, before the grid. So does a column\nwith an <code>editor</code> too: a lookup column draws its own cell.</p>\n<p>The cell keeps what the grid does on a cell: the keys, the focus ring, copy and paste, errors, the\nedited marker, ranges, Find, the stripes and the <code>cellClass</code> hook. In a cell that can be edited,\nEnter, F2, typing and a double click open the grid&#39;s text editor (a date cell&#39;s click the date\npicker), unless the renderer edits the value itself. Not the default cell&#39;s <code>placeholderRow</code>,\n<code>focusButton</code> and the lines of a multiline cell; <code>fitColumns()</code> measures the text of the field&#39;s\nformatter, not what the renderer draws. See the guide &quot;Custom cells&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    columns: { status: { renderer: 'badge' }, progress: { renderer: 'progress', readonly: true } },\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['status'], width: 100 }, { fields: ['progress'], width: 120 }] }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["custom-cells"]},{"name":"validate","signatures":["validate?: ValidationRule[]"],"doc":"<p>the column&#39;s validation rules, as a field&#39;s (<code>FieldConfig.validate</code>, see <a href=\"#api/index.ValidationRule\">ValidationRule</a>):\n<code>&#39;required&#39;</code>, <code>{ id: &#39;maxLength&#39;, value: 50 }</code>, <code>{ id: &#39;pattern&#39;, value: &#39;^[A-Z]{2}-\\\\d+$&#39; }</code>,\n<code>{ id: &#39;min&#39;, value: 0 }</code>, <code>&#39;integer&#39;</code>, <code>{ id: &#39;oneOf&#39;, value: [&#39;Open&#39;, &#39;Closed&#39;] }</code>, <code>&#39;email&#39;</code> ... or\nthe id of one registered with <code>registerValidator()</code>. Added after the field&#39;s own rules: an edit of\nthe cell, the detail form, an import and <code>datasource.validate()</code> check both, a required cell gets its\nstripes. <strong>Set by code, the user can not change them</strong>: they are not in the state (<code>GridState</code>), a\nview or the grid config dialog - <code>updateConfig({ columns })</code> replaces them. An id that is not\nregistered, or wrong options, throw a <code>TypeError</code> when the grid is made. Not for a calculated column,\nit is not edited. Two grids on one datasource: the rules of the last one made (or given its columns) that\nhas some are used, and its <code>destroy()</code> gives the other&#39;s back - a grid without any leaves the other&#39;s</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    columns: {\n        projectCode: { validate: ['required', { id: 'pattern', value: '^[A-Z]{2}-\\\\d{3}$', message: 'Like AB-123' }] },\n        hours: { validate: [{ id: 'min', value: 0 }, { id: 'max', value: 24 }, { id: 'decimals', value: 1 }] },\n        status: { validate: [{ id: 'oneOf', value: ['Open', 'Closed'] }] }\n    },\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['projectCode'], width: 120 }, { fields: ['hours'], width: 80 }, { fields: ['status'], width: 100 }] }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["validation"]}]}]},{"name":"Conflict","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type Conflict<T = any> = ValueConflict<T> | RemovedConflict<T>"],"doc":"<p>What <code>datasource.getConflicts()</code> lists: a server value that <code>upsert()</code> did not write because the user\nchanged the same thing. Tell the two kinds apart by <code>field</code>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"#api/index.ValueConflict\">ValueConflict</a> (<code>field</code> is the field&#39;s name): the server changed a field the user has\nedited. The user&#39;s value stays, the server&#39;s is the original now</li>\n<li><a href=\"#api/index.RemovedConflict\">RemovedConflict</a> (<code>field</code> is <code>null</code>): the server no longer has a row that has local\nchanges, <code>upsert(rows, { removeMissing: true })</code> kept it</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Resolve one with <code>datasource.resolveConflict(row, field, &#39;local&#39; | &#39;remote&#39;)</code>. A conflict also goes\nwhen what it is about goes: the field is not edited any more (reverted, undone, typed back to the\nserver&#39;s value, saved with <code>acceptChanges()</code>), the row has no local changes any more, or it leaves\nthe data.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of the rows, the <code>T</code> of <code>Datasource&lt;T&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>for (const conflict of datasource.getConflicts()) {\n    if (conflict.field === null) {\n        console.log(`row ${conflict.row.__KEY} was removed on the server, it has changes here`);\n    } else {\n        console.log(`${conflict.field}: yours ${conflict.local}, the server's ${conflict.remote}`);\n    }\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["live-data"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"CsvSeparator","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type CsvSeparator = \",\" | \";\" | \"\\t\""],"doc":"<p>The separators <a href=\"#api/index.CsvOptions\">CsvOptions</a> can use: <code>&#39;,&#39;</code> (RFC 4180), <code>&#39;;&#39;</code> (what Excel expects in a locale\nwith a decimal comma, Norwegian for one) and <code>&#39;\\t&#39;</code> (tab separated text).</p>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"DateFormat","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type DateFormat = \"iso\" | \"norwegian\" | \"norwegianShort\" | \"us\" | \"uk\" | \"medium\" | \"long\" | \"full\" | \"weekday\" | \"weekIso\" | \"weekUs\" | \"month\" | \"quarter\" | \"year\" | \"daysUntil\" | \"isoTime\" | \"isoSeconds\" | \"norwegianTime\" | \"norwegianSeconds\" | \"time\" | \"timeSeconds\""],"doc":"<p>How a <code>date</code> or <code>datetime</code> column shows its dates: <code>ColumnFormat.date</code>. What 2026-11-22 13:45:12 (a\nSunday) is shown as:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>format</th>\n<th>shows</th>\n<th></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>&#39;iso&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>2026-11-22</code></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;norwegian&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>22.11.2026</code></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;norwegianShort&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>22.11.26</code></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;us&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>11/22/2026</code></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;uk&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>22/11/2026</code></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;medium&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>Nov 22, 2026</code> - <code>22. nov. 2026</code> in <code>nb-NO</code></td>\n<td>the names in the language of the text <code>format.locale</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;long&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>November 22, 2026</code> - <code>22. november 2026</code></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;full&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>Sunday, November 22, 2026</code> - <code>søndag 22. november 2026</code></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;weekday&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>Sunday</code> - <code>søndag</code></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;weekIso&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>2026-W47</code></td>\n<td>ISO 8601: weeks start on Monday, week 1 has the year&#39;s first Thursday. The year is the week&#39;s: 2027-01-01 is <code>2026-W53</code>. Written as the text <code>format.weekIso</code> says, <code>&#39;{year}-W{week}&#39;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;weekUs&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>2026-W48</code></td>\n<td>weeks start on Sunday, week 1 has January 1 (Excel&#39;s <code>WEEKNUM</code>): 2026-12-31 is <code>2026-W53</code>, 2027-01-01 <code>2027-W01</code>. The text <code>format.weekUs</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;month&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>2026-11</code></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;quarter&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>2026 Q4</code></td>\n<td>the text <code>format.quarter</code>, <code>&#39;{year} Q{quarter}&#39;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;year&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>2026</code></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;daysUntil&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>0</code></td>\n<td>whole days from today: <code>1</code> tomorrow, <code>-1</code> yesterday. Today is the day the cell is rendered</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;isoTime&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>2026-11-22 13:45</code></td>\n<td>a <code>datetime</code> column only</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;isoSeconds&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>2026-11-22 13:45:12</code></td>\n<td>a <code>datetime</code> column only</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;norwegianTime&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>22.11.2026 13:45</code></td>\n<td>a <code>datetime</code> column only</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;norwegianSeconds&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>22.11.2026 13:45:12</code></td>\n<td>a <code>datetime</code> column only</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;time&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>13:45</code></td>\n<td>a <code>datetime</code> column only</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;timeSeconds&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>13:45:12</code></td>\n<td>a <code>datetime</code> column only</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The date&#39;s local day and time are shown, as the field&#39;s formatter shows them.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { DateFormat, GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst week: DateFormat = 'weekIso'; // 2026-W47\nconst columns: GridConfig['columns'] = { due: { format: { date: week } } };</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"DatePreset","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type DatePreset = \"today\" | \"yesterday\" | \"thisWeek\" | \"lastWeek\" | \"thisMonth\" | \"lastMonth\" | \"thisQuarter\" | \"lastQuarter\" | \"thisYear\" | \"lastYear\" | \"last7Days\" | \"last30Days\" | \"next7Days\" | \"overdue\""],"doc":"<p>A quick date filter of a date or datetime column: one click in the column&#39;s filter menu, <em>Quick\ndates</em>. Each is a range of whole days, computed from today when it filters:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>id</th>\n<th>the days</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>&#39;today&#39;</code></td>\n<td>today</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;yesterday&#39;</code></td>\n<td>yesterday</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;thisWeek&#39;</code></td>\n<td>the week of today, from its first day (<code>datePickerConfig.weekStart</code>, Monday by default) for 7 days</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;lastWeek&#39;</code></td>\n<td>the 7 days before that</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;thisMonth&#39;</code></td>\n<td>the 1st to the last day of this month</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;lastMonth&#39;</code></td>\n<td>the month before</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;thisQuarter&#39;</code></td>\n<td>the quarter of today: January-March, April-June, July-September or October-December</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;lastQuarter&#39;</code></td>\n<td>the quarter before</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;thisYear&#39;</code></td>\n<td>1 January to 31 December</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;lastYear&#39;</code></td>\n<td>last year</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;last7Days&#39;</code></td>\n<td>today and the 6 days before</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;last30Days&#39;</code></td>\n<td>today and the 29 days before</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;next7Days&#39;</code></td>\n<td>today and the 6 days after</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;overdue&#39;</code></td>\n<td>every day before today (an open start) - not offered unless a column lists it, see <code>ColumnConfig.datePresets</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { DatePreset, GridState } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst preset: DatePreset = 'thisMonth';\n// a saved state with it filters on the month it is set in, not the month it was saved in\nconst headerFilters: GridState['headerFilters'] = { orderDate: { value: null, datePreset: preset } };\ngridInterface.setState({ headerFilters });</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"EntityUnion","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type EntityUnion<T> = Entity & T"],"doc":"<p>A data row as the datasource hands it out: your object <code>T</code> and the fields of an <a href=\"#api/index.Entity\">Entity</a> - the\nkey, the row state, the error and the edit tracking controller. <code>getDataRows()</code>, <code>getSelectedRows()</code>,\n<code>getAllData()</code> ... return these.</p>\n<p>The row is your own object, wrapped in a <code>Proxy</code> that tracks the edits: setting a field on it is an\nedit (<code>getChanges()</code>).</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of your rows, the <code>T</code> of <code>Datasource&lt;T&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, type EntityUnion } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ninterface Person {\n    id: number;\n    name: string;\n}\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource&lt;Person&gt;({ key: 'id' });\ndatasource.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann' }]);\nconst ann: EntityUnion&lt;Person&gt; = datasource.getDataRows()[0];\nann.name; // 'Ann'\nann.__rowState; // undefined: not edited</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"EventHandler","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type EventHandler<Payload> = (data: Payload) => void"],"doc":"<p>A handler for one event: it gets the event&#39;s payload. What it returns is ignored, a handler\nstays subscribed until you call the function <code>on()</code> returned.</p>\n<p>Only needed when you write a handler on its own, before passing it to <code>on()</code>.\nThe payload type comes from the event map: <a href=\"#api/index.DatasourceEvents\">DatasourceEvents</a>, <a href=\"#api/index.GridEvents\">GridEvents</a>,\n<a href=\"#api/index.DateEvents\">DateEvents</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>Payload</code> the payload of the event, e.g. <code>DatasourceEvents[&#39;select&#39;]</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { DatasourceEvents, EventHandler } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst onSelect: EventHandler&lt;DatasourceEvents['select']&gt; = (data) =&gt; {\n    console.log('row', data.row, 'selected by', data.info);\n};\nconst off = datasource.on('select', onSelect);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"FieldType","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type FieldType = \"text\" | \"number\" | \"boolean\" | \"date\" | \"datetime\""],"doc":"<p>The type of a field. It decides how the datasource sorts, groups and filters the field, which\nformatter it gets by default, and how the grid shows and edits it.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>type</th>\n<th>value</th>\n<th>sorts / filters</th>\n<th>default formatter</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>&#39;text&#39;</code></td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td>as text</td>\n<td><code>&#39;text&#39;</code>, <a href=\"#api/index.TextFormatter\">TextFormatter</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;number&#39;</code></td>\n<td>number</td>\n<td>as numbers</td>\n<td><code>&#39;numberDot&#39;</code>, <a href=\"#api/index.NumberFormatterDot\">NumberFormatterDot</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;boolean&#39;</code></td>\n<td>boolean</td>\n<td>true / false</td>\n<td><code>&#39;boolean&#39;</code>, <a href=\"#api/index.BooleanFormatter\">BooleanFormatter</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;date&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>Date</code></td>\n<td>on the day, the time of day is ignored</td>\n<td><code>&#39;dateYYYYMMDD&#39;</code>, <a href=\"#api/index.DateFormatterYYYYMMDD\">DateFormatterYYYYMMDD</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;datetime&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>Date</code></td>\n<td>on the full timestamp</td>\n<td><code>&#39;datetimeYYYYMMDD&#39;</code>, <a href=\"#api/index.DateFormatterYYYYMMDDTHHMMSS\">DateFormatterYYYYMMDDTHHMMSS</a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>A field that is not listed in <code>fields</code> is <code>&#39;text&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    fields: {\n        age: 'number',\n        born: 'date', // 1990-05-17, filters match the whole day\n        lastLogin: 'datetime', // 2026-11-20T08:15:00\n        active: 'boolean'\n    }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["formatters"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"FilterExpression","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type FilterExpression = FilterGroup | FilterCondition"],"doc":"<p>A filter: one <a href=\"#api/index.FilterCondition\">FilterCondition</a>, or a <a href=\"#api/index.FilterGroup\">FilterGroup</a> of them. This is what\n<code>datasource.filter()</code> takes, <code>datasource.getFilter()</code> returns and the grid keeps in its state\n(<code>GridState.filter</code>). It is plain data, so it can be stored as JSON (a <code>Date</code> value comes back as\ntext, which a <code>date</code> / <code>datetime</code> field still reads).</p>\n<p>Build one with <a href=\"#api/index.and\">and</a>, <a href=\"#api/index.or\">or</a> and <a href=\"#api/index.where\">where</a>, or write the objects out.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { and, or, where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// a single condition\ndatasource.filter(where('balance', 'GREATER_THAN', 2500));\n\n// age &gt; 18 AND (a = 'x' OR a = 'y')\ndatasource.filter(and(where('age', 'GREATER_THAN', 18), or(where('a', 'EQUAL', 'x'), where('a', 'EQUAL', 'y'))));\n\n// no filter\ndatasource.filter(null);</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"FilterNode","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type FilterNode = FilterConditionNode | FilterGroupNode"],"doc":"<p>A node of the tree <code>datasource.getFilterTree()</code> returns: a <a href=\"#api/index.FilterGroupNode\">FilterGroupNode</a> or a\n<a href=\"#api/index.FilterConditionNode\">FilterConditionNode</a>. Tell them apart by <code>kind</code>.</p>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"FilterOperator","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type FilterOperator = \"EQUAL\" | \"LESS_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO\" | \"GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO\" | \"LESS_THAN\" | \"GREATER_THAN\" | \"BETWEEN\" | \"CONTAINS\" | \"NOT_EQUAL_TO\" | \"DOES_NOT_CONTAIN\" | \"BEGIN_WITH\" | \"END_WITH\" | \"IN\" | \"NOT_IN\" | \"IS_BLANK\" | \"IS_NOT_BLANK\""],"doc":"<p>How a <a href=\"#api/index.FilterCondition\">FilterCondition</a> compares the row&#39;s value with its <code>value</code>. The field&#39;s type (from\nthe datasource&#39;s <code>fields</code>, <code>&#39;text&#39;</code> when it is not listed) decides how the two are compared, and\nwhich operators the grid offers for it: see <a href=\"#api/index.operatorsFor\">operatorsFor</a>. The filtering guide has the exact\nrules of every operator for every type, written for a backend that has to filter the same way.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>EQUAL</code> / <code>NOT_EQUAL_TO</code> - the same / not the same. Text: the whole text, ignoring case unless\nthe condition is <code>caseSensitive</code> - <code>&#39;an&#39;</code> does not match <code>&#39;Ann&#39;</code> (use a wildcard, <code>&#39;an*&#39;</code>, or\n<code>CONTAINS</code>). <code>date</code>: the same day, <code>datetime</code>: the same second</li>\n<li><code>CONTAINS</code> / <code>DOES_NOT_CONTAIN</code>, <code>BEGIN_WITH</code>, <code>END_WITH</code> - text: has the value in it / has not,\nstarts with it, ends with it</li>\n<li><code>LESS_THAN</code>, <code>LESS_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO</code>, <code>GREATER_THAN</code>, <code>GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO</code> - number and\ndate: smaller / earlier, larger / later</li>\n<li><code>BETWEEN</code> - number and date: from <code>value[0]</code> to <code>value[1]</code>, both ends included: <code>[10, 20]</code>. A\nblank end is open, <code>[10, null]</code> is <code>GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO 10</code></li>\n<li><code>IN</code> / <code>NOT_IN</code> - one of a list / none of it: <code>value</code> is an array (or text with one value per\nline). <code>&#39;NULL&#39;</code> in the list matches a blank</li>\n<li><code>IS_BLANK</code> / <code>IS_NOT_BLANK</code> - the row value is blank / is not: null, undefined, <code>&#39;&#39;</code> or 0 (or an\ninvalid Date, in a date field). They take no <code>value</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>In a text value <code>*</code> and <code>%</code> are wildcards, any text: <code>where(&#39;name&#39;, &#39;EQUAL&#39;, &#39;per*2&#39;)</code> matches\n<code>person2</code>. <code>_</code> is one character, any - as in SQL <code>LIKE</code>: <code>&#39;p_mp&#39;</code> matches <code>pump</code> and <code>PUMP</code>, not\n<code>pmp</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>0 is blank.</strong> A row value of 0 counts as blank, on purpose: in ERP style data 0 and empty mean\nthe same. <code>IS_BLANK</code> matches a 0 (the number, in any field - the text <code>&#39;0&#39;</code> is not blank) and\n<code>IS_NOT_BLANK</code> leaves it out, and the header&#39;s value list (shown for text fields) puts a 0 under its\n&quot;Blank&quot; entry. The other way round, a blank row value of a number field compares as 0 -\n<code>where(&#39;age&#39;, &#39;LESS_THAN&#39;, 5)</code> matches the rows without an age - and of a boolean field as <code>false</code>.</p>\n<p>An operator the field&#39;s type does not offer (<code>CONTAINS</code> on a number, in a filter saved with v5)\nstill filters the way it did, see the guide&#39;s &quot;Operators a type does not offer&quot;.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndatasource.filter(where('age', 'GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO', 18));\ndatasource.filter(where('name', 'CONTAINS', 'son'));\ndatasource.filter(where('age', 'BETWEEN', [18, 30]));\ndatasource.filter(where('country', 'IN', ['Norway', 'Sweden']));\ndatasource.filter(where('email', 'IS_BLANK'));</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"GridConfig","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type GridConfig"],"doc":"<p>The grid&#39;s config: the options of each column (<code>columns</code>), where the columns go (<code>layout</code>), sizes\nand behaviour. It is what you write. What the user changes while working with the grid - column\norder and widths, sorting, grouping, filters - is the <a href=\"#api/index.GridState\">GridState</a>: read it with\n<code>gridInterface.getState()</code>, set it with <code>setState()</code>, and give the state the grid starts in as\n<code>initialState</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>It is plain JSON</strong>: no functions, so it can be stored - in a backend, say - and given back as it\nis. The functions of a grid (<code>isReadonly</code>, <code>cellClass</code>, <code>menus</code>) are <a href=\"#api/index.GridHooks\">GridHooks</a>, given next\nto the config: <code>createGrid(host, { config, datasource, hooks })</code>. A <code>Date</code> in <code>initialState</code>&#39;s\nfilter is the one value that does not survive JSON as it was: it comes back as its ISO text, see\n<a href=\"#api/index.GridState\">GridState</a>.</p>\n<p>To change an option while the grid is shown, use <code>gridInterface.updateConfig()</code>.</p>\n<p>The grid does not change the object you pass in: it keeps its own copy of <code>columns</code>, <code>layout</code> and\n<code>initialState</code>, the parts it changes while the user works.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { createGrid, Datasource, type GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ fields: { name: { validate: ['required'] }, age: 'number', born: 'date' } });\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    columns: {\n        name: { label: 'Name', placeholderFilter: 'search' },\n        age: { readonly: true }\n        // born is in the layout without an entry here: it gets the defaults\n    },\n    layout: {\n        left: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 150 }], // pinned left\n        center: [{ fields: ['age', 'born'], width: 100 }] // two fields stacked in one column\n    },\n    cellHeight: 22,\n    readonly: false,\n    initialState: { sorting: [{ attribute: 'name', ascending: true }] }\n};\n\nconst gridInterface = createGrid(document.getElementById('grid')!, { config, datasource });</code></pre>\n","samples":["basic-grid","column-layout"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"autoRemoveContextMenuOnScrollEvent","signatures":["autoRemoveContextMenuOnScrollEvent?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>closes the open menu (the right click menus, <code>openMenu()</code>, the date picker ...) when the grid is\nscrolled, default false. Leave it off where scrolling happens by accident, on a small touch screen</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"calculatedColumns","signatures":["calculatedColumns?: Record<string, CalculatedColumn>"],"doc":"<p>The calculated columns the grid starts with, by field name: columns whose values a formula\ncomputes from the other fields of the row - <code>{ total: { formula: &#39;{price} * {qty}&#39; } }</code>. Put their\nfields in the <code>layout</code>, give them <code>columns</code> options (a label, an aggregate, a format) as any field.\nSee <a href=\"#api/index.CalculatedColumn\">CalculatedColumn</a> and the guide &quot;Calculated columns&quot;.</p>\n<p>Part of the grid&#39;s state (<code>GridState.calculatedColumns</code>): the user adds, changes and removes them in\nthe grid config dialog, <code>getState()</code> has them. <code>resetState()</code> goes back to these (unless\n<code>initialState.calculatedColumns</code> is given); <code>updateConfig({ calculatedColumns })</code> shows new ones\nat once and makes them what <code>resetState()</code> goes back to.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    calculatedColumns: {\n        total: { formula: '{price} * {qty}', label: 'Total' },\n        daysLate: { formula: 'DAYS({due}, TODAY())', label: 'Days late' }\n    },\n    columns: { total: { aggregate: 'sum' } },\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['price', 'qty'], width: 80 }, { fields: ['total'], width: 90 }, { fields: ['daysLate'], width: 80 }] }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["calculated-columns"]},{"name":"cellHeaderLabelHeight","signatures":["cellHeaderLabelHeight?: number"],"doc":"<p>height of a header label cell in px, default <code>cellHeight</code>. Make it 2-3 times <code>cellHeight</code> for long\nlabels that wrap. <code>fitColumns()</code> measures the label on one line</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"cellHeight","signatures":["cellHeight?: number"],"doc":"<p>height of a cell in px, default 22. A row is a line of cells this high, or one per field of a\ncolumn with stacked fields. <code>gridInterface.fitRows()</code> makes a row as many lines high as its\nmultiline cells need: the first line of a cell this high, each line after it\n<code>multilineLineHeight</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"columns","signatures":["columns?: Record<string, ColumnConfig>"],"doc":"<p>The options of each column, keyed by the field name. A field in the <code>layout</code> without an entry\nhere gets the defaults. A field with an entry that is not in the layout is not shown, but the\nuser can add it from the column chooser.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"copyHeaders","signatures":["copyHeaders?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>a copy of more than one cell starts with a header line of the column labels - ranges (Ctrl+C) and\nthe row menu&#39;s Column / Row / Range copies - in the text and in the html table, so a table pasted\ninto Word or Excel has its headers. Default <code>true</code>; <code>false</code> copies the values only. A single cell\ncopies its value only. Pasted into the grid, a first line of the grid&#39;s column labels is skipped.\nSee the guide &quot;Selection and clipboard&quot;</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datePickerConfig","signatures":["datePickerConfig?: Partial<IDateConfig>"],"doc":"<p>the date picker of date cells and date header filters: only the fields to change. Of the\n<a href=\"#api/index.IDateConfig\">IDateConfig</a> the grid reads <code>showWeek</code> (default true), <code>isoWeek</code> (true), <code>weekStart</code> (1,\nmonday), <code>rowHeight</code> (22), <code>monthWidth</code> (230), <code>monthMargin</code> (10), <code>hideDimmedDates</code> (false),\n<code>showYearInMonth</code> (false) and <code>datepickerHeight</code> (282), and sets the rest itself. Its texts - the\nnames of the months and days, the buttons - are the grid&#39;s <code>texts</code> (<code>datePicker.*</code>)</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['born'], width: 120 }] },\n    datePickerConfig: { weekStart: 0, isoWeek: false } // weeks from sunday, the rest the defaults\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"detailForm","signatures":["detailForm?: DetailForm"],"doc":"<p>The detail form the grid starts with, default none (<code>{ show: false, fields: [] }</code>): a panel at the\nright of the rows with the current row as a form - a label and a value for each field of <code>fields</code>,\nin that order. A text of several lines (<code>FieldConfig.multiline</code>) gets a field tall enough to read\nit all. The cells&#39; values can be edited there too, see <a href=\"#api/index.DetailForm\">DetailForm</a>.</p>\n<p>Part of the grid&#39;s state (<code>GridState.detailForm</code>): the user turns it on, picks the fields and\ntheir order in the grid config dialog (the gear in the footer, tab <em>Detail form</em>), drags its width\nand collapses it, and <code>getState()</code> has what they did, to save. <code>resetState()</code> goes back to this one\n(unless <code>initialState.detailForm</code> is given). <code>expanded: false</code> starts it collapsed.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 150 }, { fields: ['city'], width: 120 }] },\n    // the notes are not in the layout: the form shows them, all their lines\n    detailForm: { show: true, fields: ['name', 'notes', 'city'], width: 320, minWidth: 200, maxWidth: 600 }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["detail-form"]},{"name":"dimRepeatedValues","signatures":["dimRepeatedValues?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>dims a cell when it repeats the value of the row above, so only the first row of a\nrun of equal values reads at full strength. Default = false.</p>\n<p>A cell always shows at full strength again at the start of a group, and blanks are\nnever dimmed. Can be toggled from the row context menu.</p>\n","samples":["misc-options"]},{"name":"edit","signatures":["edit?: EditPermissions"],"doc":"<p>What the user may do in an editable grid (<code>readonly: false</code>): add rows, change values, delete\nrows - any of them, default all three. A permission you give, not the user&#39;s: it is not part of\nthe state, and no menu or dialog changes it. <code>updateConfig({ edit })</code> changes it while the grid\nis shown - after a login check, say - and closes an open menu or editor. See\n<a href=\"#api/index.EditPermissions\">EditPermissions</a> for what each one stops.</p>\n<p>Anything but an object of <code>add</code>, <code>change</code> and <code>delete</code>, each <code>true</code>, <code>false</code> or left out, throws a\n<code>TypeError</code> when the grid is made or <code>updateConfig()</code> is given it: a misspelt permission would\nleave the user allowed without a word.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// the user adds rows and fills them in, the rows that were there stay as they are\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    readonly: false,\n    edit: { add: true, change: false, delete: false },\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 150 }] }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["edit-permissions"]},{"name":"editedMarker","signatures":["editedMarker?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>shows a marker in the top left corner of an edited cell, default <code>true</code>: a small triangle on a\ncell whose value differs from its original value (the datasource tracks it per field, see\n<code>getChanges()</code>). Not on a new row, every cell of it is new. Its tooltip shows the original\nvalue, and a click on it puts the original value back (<code>datasource.resetField()</code>, a step of the\nundo history) - in an editable grid.</p>\n<p><code>false</code> shows no marker. The cell element has the class <code>simple-html-cell-edited</code> either way,\nfor a look of your own. The colour is <code>--simple-html-grid-edited-color</code></p>\n<p>A field in conflict - the server changed it while the user had it edited, see\n<code>datasource.getConflicts()</code> - has the conflict marker instead, with or without this option: its\ncolour is <code>--simple-html-grid-conflict-color</code>, its tooltip has the server&#39;s value, a click takes it\n(in an editable grid). The cell element has the class <code>simple-html-cell-conflict</code></p>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"filterOnType","signatures":["filterOnType?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>the header filters filter as you type, default <code>false</code>: after a short pause in typing (300ms), no\nEnter needed - a number or date column when the text is a number or a date, not half typed. The\ndefault of every column, a column&#39;s own <code>filterOnType</code> wins; the user turns it on and off per\ncolumn (the operator choice of the header filter, Filter › in its menu, the grid config dialog),\nwhich is state: <code>GridState.headerFilters[field].filterOnType</code>. Not a boolean column, its checkbox\nfilters on a click. See the filtering guide, &quot;Filter as you type&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    filterOnType: true, // every header filter filters while typing\n    columns: { notes: { filterOnType: false } }, // but this one on Enter\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 150 }, { fields: ['notes'], width: 200 }] }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"filterOperatorIndicator","signatures":["filterOperatorIndicator?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>shows the operator of each header filter in its cell, default <code>true</code>: a small symbol beside the\ninput - on the right of a text filter (and a lookup column&#39;s), on the left of a number or date\nfilter - <code>=</code>, <code>≠</code>, <code>&lt;</code>, <code>≤</code>, <code>&gt;</code>, <code>≥</code>, <code>a..b</code> (between), <code>*a*</code> (contains), <code>!*a*</code> (does not\ncontain), <code>a*</code> (begins with), <code>*a</code> (ends with). Its tooltip names the operator. A click (a tap, F4\nin the filter) opens the operator choice under it: the operators of the filter menu&#39;s\nFilter › Operator ›, picking one does what Operator › does. A column that offers one operator only\nshows it, it can not be clicked. Not on a boolean column (a checkbox), nor on a column narrower\nthan 60px: the input keeps its room.</p>\n<p>The symbols are texts (<code>filter.indicator.&lt;FilterOperator&gt;</code>), the tooltip <code>filter.indicator.tooltip</code>.\n<code>false</code> shows the plain inputs, and F4 opens nothing: the operator is picked in the filter menu\nonly. A lookup&#39;s dropdown grid has it <code>false</code>. See the filtering guide, &quot;Header filters&quot;</p>\n","samples":["filtering"]},{"name":"footerHeight","signatures":["footerHeight?: number"],"doc":"<p>height of the footer in px, default 45: the row count, under it the filter (Clear and the chips) or\nthe button &quot;No filter&quot; that opens the filter editor. <code>0</code> hides it: no &quot;No filter&quot;, no stop of Tab</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"groupAggregates","signatures":["groupAggregates?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>shows the aggregates of each column that has some (<code>ColumnConfig.aggregate</code>) in the group rows,\ndefault <code>true</code>: in the column&#39;s place, over the group&#39;s rows - the rows of its sub groups and\nof collapsed groups included.</p>\n<p>A group row with aggregates has its name on a line of its own, and the aggregates on the lines\nunder it - a line for each function of a column (<code>aggregate: [&#39;sum&#39;, &#39;avg&#39;]</code> is two lines), so a\ngroup row is 1 + n lines, n the most a column needs. <code>false</code> shows the name only, one line, as\nwithout aggregates</p>\n","samples":["aggregates"]},{"name":"hideFilter","signatures":["hideFilter?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>hides the row of header filters, default false</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"hideLabels","signatures":["hideLabels?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>hides the row of header labels (the column names, click to sort), default false</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"importMenu","signatures":["importMenu?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>The import entries of the grid&#39;s menus, default <code>false</code>: <em>Import rows…</em> in the header menu\n(<code>header.import</code>) and <em>As new rows…</em> in the row menu&#39;s Paste › (<code>row.paste.newRows</code>). Both open the\nimport dialog - a CSV or Excel file picked or dropped, or rows pasted from a spreadsheet become new\nrows, see the import guide. Shown in an editable grid (<code>readonly: false</code>) where the user may add rows\n(<code>edit.add</code>).</p>\n<p>Off by default: a user adding many rows at once is for the app to allow. Without it\n<code>gridInterface.openImport()</code> opens the dialog from a button of your own, under the same rules.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    readonly: false,\n    importMenu: true,\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 150 }, { fields: ['born'], width: 110 }] }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["import"]},{"name":"initialState","signatures":["initialState?: Partial<GridState>"],"doc":"<p>The state the grid starts in, and <code>resetState()</code> goes back to: sorted, grouped, filtered ...\nWhat is left out starts empty (no sorting, no filter ...), the layout is <code>layout</code>.</p>\n<p>The grid applies it to the datasource when it is made: a filter, sort or grouping set on the\ndatasource before is replaced, and cleared when <code>initialState</code> leaves it out.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type GridConfig, where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 100 }, { fields: ['age'], width: 100 }] },\n    initialState: {\n        sorting: [{ attribute: 'age', ascending: false }],\n        filter: where('age', 'GREATER_THAN', 18),\n        headerFilters: { age: { value: 18, operator: 'GREATER_THAN' } } // what the header shows\n    }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["grid-state"]},{"name":"layout","signatures":["layout: GridLayout"],"doc":"<p>Where the columns go: pinned left, the scrolling center and pinned right. It is the layout the\ngrid starts with (unless <code>initialState.layout</code> is given) and <code>resetState()</code> goes back to. The\nuser changes it - drag/drop, pinning, the column chooser, resizing - those changes are in\n<code>getState().layout</code>.</p>\n","samples":["column-layout"]},{"name":"mergeHighlight","signatures":["mergeHighlight?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>the cells a merge changed flash once, default <code>true</code>: a cell whose value <code>datasource.upsert()</code>\nchanged gets the class <code>simple-html-cell-merged</code> when it is rendered in the second after, and a\ntint that fades out over that second (<code>--simple-html-grid-merged-color</code>). A field the user has\nedited is not changed by a merge - it is a conflict, the cell has the conflict marker. <code>false</code>: no\nflash. See the guide &quot;Live data&quot;</p>\n","samples":["live-data"]},{"name":"multilineLineHeight","signatures":["multilineLineHeight?: number"],"doc":"<p>the height in px of a line of text of a multiline cell, default <code>15</code>: in a row made taller\n(<code>gridInterface.fitRows()</code>) the lines of a cell&#39;s text after its first are this far apart - the\nfirst line is in the cell&#39;s input, <code>cellHeight</code> high. So the text reads as a paragraph, and a row\nof a note of three lines is <code>cellHeight + 2 * multilineLineHeight</code> high (52px by default). The\neditor of a multiline cell has the same line height, and so do the lines of aggregates under a\ngroup row&#39;s name and after the first of the totals row (<code>ColumnConfig.aggregate</code>).</p>\n<p>15 is about 1.35 times the default font size (11px). With a larger font\n(<code>--simple-html-grid-font-size</code>) make it larger too, as <code>cellHeight</code>: the grid needs it in px to\nplace the rows, it does not read the css.</p>\n<p>A whole number of 1 or more, anything else throws a <code>TypeError</code> when the grid is made or\n<code>updateConfig()</code> is given it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['notes'], width: 200 }] },\n    cellHeight: 28,\n    multilineLineHeight: 18 // for --simple-html-grid-font-size: 13px\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["multiline"]},{"name":"multilineTooltipLines","signatures":["multilineTooltipLines?: number"],"doc":"<p>the lines of a multiline cell&#39;s text its tooltip shows, default <code>5</code>: the first lines, then a\nline that says how many more there are (<code>… 7 more lines</code>, the text <code>cell.multiline.moreLines</code>).\nWhen only one line is left over, it is shown instead. The empty lines at the end of the text\nare left out, a line of more than 100 characters is cut with <code>…</code>. The tooltip of the marker of\nan edited cell shows the original value the same way.</p>\n<p>A whole number of 1 or more, anything else throws a <code>TypeError</code> when the grid is made or\n<code>updateConfig()</code> is given it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['notes'], width: 200 }] },\n    multilineTooltipLines: 10 // longer notes in the tooltip\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["multiline"]},{"name":"panelHeight","signatures":["panelHeight?: number"],"doc":"<p>height of the top panel (grouping) in px, default 25</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"placeholderRowCurrentEntityOnly","signatures":["placeholderRowCurrentEntityOnly?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>shows a column&#39;s <code>placeholderRow</code> on the current row (the current entity) only.\ndefault = true, so you need to set this to false to display on all rows</p>\n","samples":["required-placeholders"]},{"name":"readonly","signatures":["readonly?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>the whole grid is readonly, default <code>true</code>: no cell can be edited, and the row menu has no paste\nor clear. Set <code>false</code> to edit; the column&#39;s <code>readonly</code> and the <code>isReadonly</code> hook\n(<a href=\"#api/index.GridHooks\">GridHooks</a>) can still make cells readonly, and <code>edit</code> says which of adding, changing and\ndeleting rows the user may do</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rowStatus","signatures":["rowStatus?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>shows the state of each row on its row number, default <code>true</code>: an icon for a new row (+), an\nedited row (a pencil), a row marked for deletion (a trash can, the row number and the text of\nits cells struck through) and a row with an error (!, with the red bar). The tooltip and a\nscreen reader get the state as text. One icon: deleted wins, then an error, then new or edited.\nThe row numbers are a little wider, to make room for the icon.</p>\n<p><code>false</code> shows the plain row number. The classes <code>row-is-new</code>, <code>row-is-modified</code> and\n<code>row-is-deleted</code> around the number, and the error bar (<code>simple-html-row-error</code>), are there\neither way - for a look of your own. The colours are the theme&#39;s variables\n(<code>--simple-html-grid-new-color</code> ...), see the theming guide</p>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"selectSizeHeight","signatures":["selectSizeHeight?: number"],"doc":"<p>height of the column selector row under the header filters in px, default 18; 0 hides it. Its\nnumbers select columns (<code>gridInterface.getSelectedColumns()</code>), a right click opens the column menu</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"settingsButton","signatures":["settingsButton?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>shows the settings button, a gear at the right end of the footer, default <code>true</code>: it opens the\ngrid config dialog - each column&#39;s display format, a text column&#39;s template and link, applied\nto the state (<code>GridState.formats</code>), so <code>getState()</code> keeps what the user set. Its name and tooltip\nare the text <code>footer.settings</code>. Not in a footer of no height (<code>footerHeight: 0</code>); a lookup&#39;s\ndropdown grid has it <code>false</code>.</p>\n<p><code>false</code> hides the button only: the header menu still has <em>Column settings…</em> (<code>header.settings</code>,\ntake it out with the <code>menus</code> hook), and <code>gridInterface.openColumnSettings()</code> opens the dialog from\na button of your own. See the formatting guide, &quot;The grid config dialog&quot;</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"shortcutHelp","signatures":["shortcutHelp?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>the keyboard shortcuts help, default <code>true</code>: a dialog that lists the keys of the grid in groups -\nmoving around, selecting, editing, find, the menus - with a search, the keys as the platform names\nthem (⌘ on a Mac). The user opens it with <code>?</code> where the key types nothing (a readonly cell, a\ncheckbox, a column header, a row number), Ctrl+/ (Cmd+/) anywhere in the grid - also while typing in\na cell - and <em>Keyboard shortcuts…</em> in the header menu (<code>header.shortcuts</code>). Its texts are\n<code>shortcuts.*</code>, see the texts guide.</p>\n<p><code>false</code> turns its keys and the menu entry off - for an app with a help of its own, or one that uses\nthe keys itself. <code>gridInterface.openShortcutHelp()</code> still opens it. A lookup&#39;s dropdown grid has it\n<code>false</code>. See the accessibility guide, &quot;The keyboard shortcuts help&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 150 }] },\n    shortcutHelp: false // the app's own help button calls gridInterface.openShortcutHelp()\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"texts","signatures":["texts?: Texts"],"doc":"<p>The texts of this grid, by id: the ones to change. They win over the texts of the page\n(<a href=\"#api/index.setTexts\">setTexts</a>), which win over the defaults (<a href=\"#api/index.TEXTS\">TEXTS</a>, English). Plain JSON.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Every text the grid shows: the menus, the filter editor, the column chooser, the footer, the\ntooltips (ids ending with <code>.tooltip</code>) and the date picker. Not the texts the datasource makes -\nthe validation messages, <code>getFilterString()</code> and the name of the group of blank values: they are\nset with <code>setTexts()</code> only.</li>\n<li><code>updateConfig({ texts })</code> replaces them as a whole, and rebuilds the grid. A menu or the filter\neditor shows them the next time it opens.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For one language on the whole page, <code>setTexts()</code> is enough: this is for a grid that differs.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 150 }] },\n    texts: {\n        'row.copy': 'Kopier',\n        'filterEditor.addCondition.tooltip': 'Legg til betingelse'\n    }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["translation"]},{"name":"tooltips","signatures":["tooltips?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>renders the built in tooltip, default = true: on the buttons and icons of the filter editor,\nand the validation messages on a cell with an error and on its row selector</p>\n<p>the <code>data-tooltip</code> attribute is always written to the elements, also when this is\nfalse, so you can hook up your own tooltip library instead. The texts of the tooltips are\ntexts like the others, their ids end with <code>.tooltip</code>: see <code>texts</code></p>\n","samples":["tooltips","validation"]},{"name":"totalsRow","signatures":["totalsRow?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>shows the totals row under the rows, default <code>false</code>: the aggregate of each column that has one\n(<code>ColumnConfig.aggregate</code>), over the rows the filter lets through - when grouped, the rows of\ncollapsed groups too. &quot;Total&quot; at the left (the text <code>aggregate.total</code>). It follows the columns\nwhen they scroll sideways, and the values follow the filter and every change of a row: an edit,\nundo, <code>upsert()</code>. The horizontal scrollbar is between the rows and the totals row. As many lines\nas the column with the most functions needs.</p>\n<p>Part of the grid&#39;s state (<code>GridState.totalsRow</code>): the header menu turns it on and off</p>\n","samples":["aggregates"]},{"name":"typeFormats","signatures":["typeFormats?: TypeFormats"],"doc":"<p>the formats of the columns by type: how every <code>date</code>, <code>datetime</code> and <code>number</code> column shows its\nvalues when it has no date or number format of its own - <code>{ date: &#39;norwegian&#39;, number: { decimals: 2 } }</code>.\nThe grid&#39;s state (<code>GridState.typeFormats</code>): the user changes it on the Defaults tab of the grid\nconfig dialog, <code>getState()</code> and the views keep it. A type left out shows the field&#39;s formatter. See\n<a href=\"#api/index.TypeFormats\">TypeFormats</a>. A format a type does not take throws a <code>TypeError</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"views","signatures":["views?: GridView[]"],"doc":"<p>The named views the grid starts with, see <a href=\"#api/index.GridView\">GridView</a>: &quot;My open orders&quot;, &quot;Late deliveries&quot; -\neach a snapshot of the state under a name. The user switches between them with the views button\nat the left end of the footer (<code>viewsButton</code>), and saves, renames and deletes their own there. A\nview with <code>readonly: true</code> is yours - shared by the company, say - the user can apply it and save\nit as a view of their own, not change it. The view with <code>default: true</code> is applied when the grid is\nmade, on top of <code>initialState</code>.</p>\n<p>The grid keeps the list (<code>gridInterface.getViews()</code>) and sends <code>views-change</code> with it when the user\nchanges it: store it there - in a backend, say - and give it back here next time. Or let the grid\nkeep it in the browser, <code>viewsStorageKey</code>. Given, the views button is shown.</p>\n<p><code>updateConfig({ views })</code> makes the list again, as when the grid is made (with the stored views of\n<code>viewsStorageKey</code>); <code>setViews()</code> replaces it. A list that is not one of views - an id or a name\nthat is no text, a state that is no object, two views of one id, two defaults - throws a\n<code>TypeError</code> when the grid is made or <code>updateConfig()</code> is given it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type GridConfig, where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['company'], width: 150 }, { fields: ['country'], width: 120 }] },\n    views: [\n        {\n            id: 'norway',\n            name: 'Norway',\n            state: { filter: where('country', 'EQUAL', 'Norway'), headerFilters: { country: { value: 'Norway' } } },\n            readonly: true\n        }\n    ],\n    // the user's own views are kept in localStorage, the shared one above comes from here every time\n    viewsStorageKey: 'orders-grid-views'\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["views"]},{"name":"viewsButton","signatures":["viewsButton?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>shows the views button at the left end of the footer, on the line of the filter: the name of the\nview shown - &quot;Standard&quot; when none is (the config&#39;s state) - with a <code>*</code> after it when the state\nchanged since it was applied or saved. A click opens the views menu: the views to switch to, and\nSave, Save as new view…, Revert, Rename…, Delete and Default view. Default <code>true</code> when <code>views</code> or\n<code>viewsStorageKey</code> is given, else <code>false</code>. Not in a footer of no height (<code>footerHeight: 0</code>).</p>\n<p><code>false</code> hides it: the views and <code>gridInterface.applyView()</code>, <code>saveViewAs()</code> ... still work, for a\nviews control of your own</p>\n","samples":["views"]},{"name":"viewsStorageKey","signatures":["viewsStorageKey?: string"],"doc":"<p>Keeps the user&#39;s views in the browser&#39;s localStorage under this key, the ready way to keep them\nwhen there is no backend for them: read when the grid is made, written every time the list\nchanges. Stored are the views that are not <code>readonly</code> and which view is the default; the readonly\nviews come from <code>views</code> every time. Once the user has saved one, the stored views are the user&#39;s -\na view of <code>views</code> that is not readonly and was deleted stays deleted.</p>\n<p>The browser can refuse - blocked storage, a private window that keeps nothing: the grid starts\nwith <code>views</code>, and a view saved stays until the page is left (a warning in the console). Something\nstored that is no list of views is passed by. Given, the views button is shown.</p>\n<p>Put a version in the key and change it when the columns of the config change much: a view keeps\nthe layout it was saved with, see the state guide.</p>\n","samples":["views"]}]}]},{"name":"IconSetName","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type IconSetName = \"arrows\" | \"traffic\" | \"flags\" | \"symbols\""],"doc":"<p>The icons of an icon set, <code>IconSetFormat.set</code>: three each - the icon of the high values, of the middle\nones and of the low ones. Each is drawn in the icon colours of the theme, green, amber and red\n(<code>--simple-html-grid-icon-green-color</code> ...):</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>set</th>\n<th>high</th>\n<th>middle</th>\n<th>low</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>&#39;arrows&#39;</code></td>\n<td>▲ green</td>\n<td>► amber</td>\n<td>▼ red</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;traffic&#39;</code></td>\n<td>● green</td>\n<td>● amber</td>\n<td>● red</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;flags&#39;</code></td>\n<td>⚑ green</td>\n<td>⚑ amber</td>\n<td>⚑ red</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;symbols&#39;</code></td>\n<td>✓ green</td>\n<td>! amber</td>\n<td>✕ red</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { IconSetName } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst lights: IconSetName = 'traffic';</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"ImportCell","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type ImportCell = string | number | boolean | Date | null"],"doc":"<p>A value of a cell as the import reads it from a file: text, a number, a boolean or a <code>Date</code> - or <code>null</code>\nfor an empty cell. A CSV file gives text only, an .xlsx file each type its cells have.</p>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"ImportFileProblem","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type ImportFileProblem = \"tooLarge\" | \"xls\" | \"broken\" | \"unsupported\""],"doc":"<p>Why a file can not be imported, <a href=\"#api/index.ImportFileError\">ImportFileError</a>&#39;s <code>problem</code>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&#39;tooLarge&#39;</code>: over one of the <a href=\"#api/index.IMPORT_LIMITS\">IMPORT_LIMITS</a></li>\n<li><code>&#39;xls&#39;</code>: an Excel 97-2003 workbook (.xls, a binary format): save it as .xlsx or CSV</li>\n<li><code>&#39;broken&#39;</code>: neither CSV nor an .xlsx workbook, or damaged: a ZIP that does not hold a workbook, a\npart that is not well-formed XML, a ZIP that is encrypted or uses ZIP64, data that does not inflate\nto its size and CRC</li>\n<li><code>&#39;unsupported&#39;</code>: the browser can not inflate the parts of an .xlsx file - it has no\n<code>DecompressionStream(&#39;deflate-raw&#39;)</code> (Chrome 103, Firefox 113, Safari 16.4 have it). CSV works there</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"Lookup","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type Lookup = LookupFromDatasource | LookupFromGridInterface"],"doc":"<p>A list to pick a cell&#39;s value from, for a column&#39;s <code>editor</code> (<a href=\"#api/index.ColumnEditor\">ColumnEditor</a>): the rows to pick\nfrom, the field of a row that is stored in the cell, and the field the user sees. Register it with\n<a href=\"#api/index.registerLookup\">registerLookup</a> under an id, the column names the id.</p>\n<p>Either a datasource of its own - the rows, and for the dropdown grid (<code>type: &#39;grid&#39;</code>) the\n<a href=\"#api/index.GridConfig\">GridConfig</a> of the grid in it - or a <a href=\"#api/index.GridInterface\">GridInterface</a> you made, shown as it is.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, GridInterface, type Lookup } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst countries = new Datasource();\ncountries.setData([{ code: 'NO', name: 'Norway' }, { code: 'SE', name: 'Sweden' }]);\n\n// the cell stores 'NO' and shows 'Norway'\nconst fromRows: Lookup = { datasource: countries, valueField: 'code', labelField: 'name' };\n\n// a dropdown grid with these columns\nconst withColumns: Lookup = {\n    datasource: countries,\n    valueField: 'code',\n    labelField: 'name',\n    config: { layout: { center: [{ fields: ['code'], width: 60 }, { fields: ['name'], width: 160 }] } }\n};\n\n// a grid interface of your own: its config, its hooks\nconst customers = new GridInterface({ layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 200 }] } }, new Datasource());\nconst fromInterface: Lookup = { gridInterface: customers, valueField: 'id', labelField: 'name' };</code></pre>\n","samples":["lookups"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"MenuEntry","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type MenuEntry = MenuItem | MenuSubmenu | MenuSection | MenuSeparator | MenuBlock"],"doc":"<p>One entry of a menu: an item to click, a submenu, a section header, a separator line, or a block\n(an element shown as it is). The grid&#39;s own menus are lists of these, see <a href=\"#api/index.GridMenus\">GridMenus</a> to\nchange them, and <code>gridInterface.openMenu()</code> opens a menu of your own.</p>\n<p>Every entry has an <code>id</code>. The ids of the grid&#39;s own entries are listed in <a href=\"#api/index.MENU_IDS\">MENU_IDS</a>; give\nyours ids that do not clash with them.</p>\n<p>An entry with a <code>visible</code> callback that returns <code>false</code> is left out. A section header or separator\nis shown as long as it is in the list: hide it together with the entries under it. A submenu with\nno item, submenu or block left to show is left out too.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { MenuEntry } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const pick: (fruit: string | null) =&gt; void;\ndeclare const event: MouseEvent;\n\nconst entries: MenuEntry[] = [\n    { type: 'section', id: 'fruit', label: 'Pick a fruit:' },\n    { id: 'fruit.apple', label: 'Apple', action: () =&gt; pick('Apple') },\n    { id: 'fruit.banana', label: 'Banana', action: () =&gt; pick('Banana') },\n    {\n        type: 'submenu',\n        id: 'fruit.more',\n        label: 'More',\n        entries: [\n            { id: 'fruit.kiwi', label: 'Kiwi', action: () =&gt; pick('Kiwi') },\n            { id: 'fruit.mango', label: 'Mango', action: () =&gt; pick('Mango') }\n        ]\n    },\n    { type: 'separator', id: 'fruit.separator' },\n    { id: 'fruit.none', label: 'None', hint: 'clears the cell', action: () =&gt; pick(null) }\n];\ngridInterface.openMenu(event, entries);</code></pre>\n","samples":["context-menu"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"ModifiedEntity","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type ModifiedEntity<T> = Partial<T> & { __KEY?: string | number }"],"doc":"<p>One edited row in <a href=\"#api/index.Changes\">Changes</a>: the row&#39;s key and the fields whose value differs from the\noriginal, with their new value.</p>\n<p>The key is under the name of the key field (<code>id</code> with <code>new Datasource({ key: &#39;id&#39; })</code>), or under\n<code>__KEY</code> when the datasource has no key - then it is a generated negative number, a server can not\nuse it.</p>\n<p>A field edited back to its original value is not in it, and a row with no field left that\ndiffers is not edited. When a value differs depends on the field&#39;s type, see <a href=\"#api/index.Changes\">Changes</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ninterface Person {\n    id: number;\n    name: string;\n    city: string;\n}\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource&lt;Person&gt;({ key: 'id' });\ndatasource.setData([{ id: 7, name: 'Ann', city: 'Oslo' }]);\ndatasource.getDataRows()[0].city = 'Bergen';\n\ndatasource.getChanges().modifiedEntities; // [{ id: 7, city: 'Bergen' }]</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"PaletteColor","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type PaletteColor = \"red\" | \"orange\" | \"amber\" | \"yellow\" | \"lime\" | \"green\" | \"teal\" | \"cyan\" | \"blue\" | \"indigo\" | \"purple\" | \"pink\" | \"brown\" | \"grey\""],"doc":"<p>A colour of the palette of the colour rules (<a href=\"#api/index.ColorRule\">ColorRule</a>): the text colour or the background\nof a cell. Each is a css variable of the theme, a colour for light and one for dark, kept readable:\nthe text colours have 4.5:1 to the rows, the selected rows and the backgrounds of the palette, the\ngrid&#39;s text has 4.5:1 to the backgrounds. A colour of your own is a custom colour, <code>#rrggbb</code> (see\n<a href=\"#api/index.RuleColor\">RuleColor</a>). See the theming guide, &quot;Colour rules&quot;.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>colour</th>\n<th>text</th>\n<th>background</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>&#39;red&#39;</code></td>\n<td>dark red, light in dark mode</td>\n<td>light red, dark in dark mode</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;orange&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;amber&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;yellow&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;lime&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;green&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;teal&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;cyan&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;blue&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;indigo&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;purple&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;pink&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;brown&#39;</code></td>\n<td>the same</td>\n<td>the same</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;grey&#39;</code></td>\n<td>quiet text</td>\n<td>a grey background</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { ColorRule, PaletteColor } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst warning: PaletteColor = 'amber';\nconst rule: ColorRule = { operator: 'EQUAL', value: 'waiting', background: warning };</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"RuleColor","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type RuleColor = PaletteColor | `#${string}`"],"doc":"<p>A colour of a colour rule: a colour of the palette (<a href=\"#api/index.PaletteColor\">PaletteColor</a>), or a custom colour - <code>#</code> and\nsix hex digits, <code>&#39;#ff8800&#39;</code>, nothing else.</p>\n<p>A custom colour is the same in light and in dark, so the grid keeps it readable: a custom background\nwithout a text colour gets black or white text, whichever reads better on it; a custom text colour is\nthe colour picked in light mode and made lighter in dark mode until it has 4.5:1 to the rows. The grid\nconfig dialog warns when a custom text colour has less than 4.5:1 to the light rows or to its custom\nbackground. It reaches the page as the value of a css custom property, never as css text.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { ColorRule, RuleColor } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst brand: RuleColor = '#0f766e';\nconst rule: ColorRule = { operator: 'EQUAL', value: 'vip', background: brand }; // white text on it</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"RuleWeek","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type RuleWeek = \"iso\" | \"us\""],"doc":"<p>The weeks of a colour rule on a date (<code>ColorRule.week</code>):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&#39;iso&#39;</code> - ISO 8601: a week starts on Monday, week 1 has the year&#39;s first Thursday</li>\n<li><code>&#39;us&#39;</code> - a week starts on Sunday, week 1 has January 1 (Excel&#39;s <code>WEEKNUM</code>)</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"SelectionMode","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type SelectionMode = \"none\" | \"single\" | \"multiple\""],"doc":"<p>How rows can be selected:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&#39;multiple&#39;</code> - many rows: ctrl+click adds a row, shift+click a range (the default)</li>\n<li><code>&#39;single&#39;</code> - one row at a time</li>\n<li><code>&#39;none&#39;</code> - no selection. Clicking a row still makes it the current entity</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>selectAll()</code> (and a click on the grid&#39;s top left corner) selects only in <code>&#39;multiple&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p>The datasource owns it: set it with <code>DatasourceOptions.selectionMode</code> or\n<code>datasource.setSelectionMode()</code>. A grid reads it from its datasource, it has no option of its own\n(v5&#39;s <code>GridConfig.selectionMode</code> is removed).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ key: 'id', selectionMode: 'single' });\ndatasource.setSelectionMode('none'); // later, also while it is shown in a grid</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"SourceColumn","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type SourceColumn = ColumnConfig & { field: string }"],"doc":"<p>A column the source of the rows has now - a database view, an API - as <a href=\"#api/index.reconcileColumns\">reconcileColumns</a> and\n<code>gridInterface.updateColumns()</code> take it: its field and the options of its column (a\n<a href=\"#api/index.ColumnConfig\">ColumnConfig</a>: label, readonly, operator ...).</p>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"TextId","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type TextId = \"row.copy\" | \"row.copy.cell\" | \"row.copy.column\" | \"row.copy.column.hint\" | \"row.copy.row\" | \"row.copy.row.hint\" | \"row.copy.selectedColumns\" | \"row.copy.selectedColumns.hint\" | \"row.copy.range\" | \"row.filter\" | \"row.filter.replace\" | \"row.filter.replace.hint\" | \"row.filter.add\" | \"row.filter.add.hint\" | \"row.view\" | \"row.view.dimRepeatedValues\" | \"row.view.changedOnly\" | \"row.paste\" | \"row.paste.current\" | \"row.paste.cell\" | \"row.paste.cell.hint\" | \"row.paste.range\" | \"row.paste.fillDown\" | \"row.paste.fillDown.hint\" | \"row.paste.fillDown.hint.mac\" | \"row.paste.newRows\" | \"row.clear\" | \"row.clear.current\" | \"row.clear.cell\" | \"row.clear.cell.hint\" | \"row.clear.range\" | \"row.delete\" | \"row.delete.row\" | \"row.delete.rows\" | \"row.delete.rows.hint\" | \"row.delete.undo\" | \"row.delete.undo.hint\" | \"row.edit\" | \"row.edit.undo\" | \"row.edit.undo.hint\" | \"row.edit.undo.hint.mac\" | \"row.edit.redo\" | \"row.edit.redo.hint\" | \"row.edit.redo.hint.mac\" | \"row.edit.revertCell\" | \"row.edit.revertRow\" | \"row.edit.revertRows\" | \"row.edit.revertRows.hint\" | \"row.size\" | \"row.size.fitColumn\" | \"row.size.fitRow\" | \"row.size.fitRows\" | \"row.size.fitRows.hint\" | \"row.size.fitAllRows\" | \"row.size.resetRow\" | \"row.size.resetAllRows\" | \"row.export\" | \"row.export.excel\" | \"row.export.excelSelected\" | \"row.select\" | \"row.select.row\" | \"row.select.rowsTo\" | \"row.select.allRows\" | \"row.select.rangeTo\" | \"row.select.addCell\" | \"row.select.clear\" | \"header.column.pin\" | \"header.column.pinLeft\" | \"header.column.pinLeftCopy\" | \"header.column.pinRight\" | \"header.column.pinRightCopy\" | \"header.column.unpin\" | \"header.column.hide\" | \"header.column.removeSorting\" | \"header.column.chooser\" | \"header.size\" | \"header.size.column\" | \"header.size.all\" | \"header.size.resetColumn\" | \"header.size.resetAll\" | \"header.aggregate\" | \"header.aggregate.sum\" | \"header.aggregate.avg\" | \"header.aggregate.min\" | \"header.aggregate.max\" | \"header.aggregate.count\" | \"header.aggregate.totalsRow\" | \"header.format\" | \"header.format.default\" | \"header.format.date.iso\" | \"header.format.date.norwegian\" | \"header.format.date.norwegianShort\" | 